 participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.</p>\n<p>Other duties as assigned or needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Should Apply?</strong></p>\n<p>We are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ideal candidates will have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning</li>\n<li>Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve</li>\n<li>Programming experience</li>\n<li>Appetite for risk-taking</li>\n<li>Demonstrated interest in financial markets</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reliable and predictable availability required.</p>\n<p>INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.</p>\n<p>The estimated base salary for this role is $300,000 per year.</p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["quant"],"role_matches":["Quantitative"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Quantitative"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:8027922","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"8027922","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"8595fd9f5d4925d4143f149e207f9f35ae6ac07a43b831598a5098304e6e69c5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus Quantitative Trader (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8027922","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8027922","locations":[{"label":"Hong Kong, Shanghai"},{"label":"Hong Kong"},{"label":"China"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Front Office "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3480179,"first_published_at":"2026-08-24T03:42:46-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T03:42:46-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incentivizing collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nOur trading teams are each comprised of a dynamic group of traders, quantitative researchers, and engineers who work together to examine the global markets, seeking to understand the complexities of various traded products and exchanges. They leverage their impeccable statistical analysis and data mining skills, using the results of their research to make forecasts and develop profitable predictive trading models.\n\n-------------------------------\n*Candidates should be interested in working in Hong Kong or Shanghai for their full-time job after graduation.\n-------------------------------\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nThe quant trading internship is an intensive 10-week program focused on enhancing your trading aptitude and understanding of financial markets, as well as helping you experience what it’s like to be a full-time quant trader at Jump.\n\nAt Jump, our people contribute to trading teams in the following roles, or a blend of all three: quant trader, quant researcher, and quant developer. During our internship you will get training in all of these areas, with a focus in trading and financial markets. Topics include trading strategies and intuition, market mechanics, statistics, and our research process for signal generation.\n\nYou will have the opportunity to work with our trading teams on meaningful projects with real impact while receiving daily 1:1 mentorship from experienced quant traders, researchers, and developers. You will also participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.\n\nOther duties as assigned or needed.\n\nWho Should Apply?\n\nWe are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.\n\nIdeal candidates will have:\n\n- Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning\n\n- Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve\n\n- Programming experience\n\n- Appetite for risk-taking\n\n- Demonstrated interest in financial markets\n\nReliable and predictable availability required","description_html":"<p>Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incentivizing collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"2993\">Our trading teams are each comprised of a dynamic group of traders, quantitative researchers, and engineers who work together to examine the global markets, seeking to understand the complexities of various traded products and exchanges. They leverage their impeccable statistical analysis and data mining skills, using the results of their research to make forecasts and develop profitable predictive trading models.<br><br><em>-------------------------------</em><br><em>*Candidates should be interested in working in Hong Kong or Shanghai for their full-time job after graduation.</em><br><em>-------------------------------</em></p>\n<p><strong>About the Role:</strong></p>\n<p>The quant trading internship is an intensive 10-week program focused on enhancing your trading aptitude and understanding of financial markets, as well as helping you experience what it’s like to be a full-time quant trader at Jump.</p>\n<p>At Jump, our people contribute to trading teams in the following roles, or a blend of all three: quant trader, quant researcher, and quant developer. During our internship you will get training in all of these areas, with a focus in trading and financial markets. Topics include trading strategies and intuition, market mechanics, statistics, and our research process for signal generation.</p>\n<p>You will have the opportunity to work with our trading teams on meaningful projects with real impact while receiving daily 1:1 mentorship from experienced quant traders, researchers, and developers. You will also participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.</p>\n<p>Other duties as assigned or needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Should Apply?</strong></p>\n<p>We are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ideal candidates will have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning</li>\n<li>Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve</li>\n<li>Programming experience&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Appetite for risk-taking</li>\n<li>Demonstrated interest in financial markets</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reliable and predictable availability required</p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T08:29:29.538Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["quant"],"role_matches":["Quantitative"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Quantitative"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:8027941","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"8027941","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"926551d2ab8fb09ebe950578fbe6ba500fa2d4ac6d4837f9679987ea21f8d552","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus Quantitative Trader (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8027941","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8027941","locations":[{"label":"Singapore"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Front Office "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3480191,"first_published_at":"2026-08-03T03:00:24-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-18T18:43:28-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incentivizing collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nOur trading teams are each comprised of a dynamic group of traders, quantitative researchers, and engineers who work together to examine the global markets, seeking to understand the complexities of various traded products and exchanges. They leverage their impeccable statistical analysis and data mining skills, using the results of their research to make forecasts and develop profitable predictive trading models.\n\n-------------------------------\n*Candidates should be interested in working in Singapore for their full-time job after graduation.\n\n*Timing of application consideration and interviews will vary to accommodate university timelines.\n-------------------------------\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nThe quant trading internship is an intensive 10-week program focused on enhancing your trading aptitude and understanding of financial markets, as well as helping you experience what it’s like to be a full-time quant trader at Jump.\n\nAt Jump, our people contribute to trading teams in the following roles, or a blend of all three: quant trader, quant researcher, and quant developer. During our internship you will get training in all of these areas, with a focus in trading and financial markets. Topics include trading strategies and intuition, market mechanics, statistics, and our research process for signal generation.\n\nYou will have the opportunity to work with our trading teams on meaningful projects with real impact while receiving daily 1:1 mentorship from experienced quant traders, researchers, and developers. You will also participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.\n\nOther duties as assigned or needed.\n\nWho Should Apply?\n\nWe are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.\n\nIdeal candidates will have:\n\n- Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning\n\n- Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve\n\n- Programming experience\n\n- Appetite for risk-taking\n\n- Demonstrated interest in financial markets\n\nReliable and predictable availability required.","description_html":"<p>Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incentivizing collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"2993\">Our trading teams are each comprised of a dynamic group of traders, quantitative researchers, and engineers who work together to examine the global markets, seeking to understand the complexities of various traded products and exchanges. They leverage their impeccable statistical analysis and data mining skills, using the results of their research to make forecasts and develop profitable predictive trading models.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"2993\">-------------------------------<br>*Candidates should be interested in working in Singapore for their full-time job after graduation.</p>\n<p>*Timing of application consideration and interviews will vary to accommodate university timelines.<br>-------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>About the Role:</strong></p>\n<p>The quant trading internship is an intensive 10-week program focused on enhancing your trading aptitude and understanding of financial markets, as well as helping you experience what it’s like to be a full-time quant trader at Jump.</p>\n<p>At Jump, our people contribute to trading teams in the following roles, or a blend of all three: quant trader, quant researcher, and quant developer. During our internship you will get training in all of these areas, with a focus in trading and financial markets. Topics include trading strategies and intuition, market mechanics, statistics, and our research process for signal generation.</p>\n<p>You will have the opportunity to work with our trading teams on meaningful projects with real impact while receiving daily 1:1 mentorship from experienced quant traders, researchers, and developers. You will also participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.</p>\n<p>Other duties as assigned or needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Should Apply?</strong></p>\n<p>We are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ideal candidates will have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning</li>\n<li>Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve</li>\n<li>Programming experience</li>\n<li>Appetite for risk-taking</li>\n<li>Demonstrated interest in financial markets</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reliable and predictable availability required.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["quant"],"role_matches":["Quantitative"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Quantitative"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:8050772","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"8050772","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"1b13265dccaf546da16c7324ce9cf15428453ec7c932dd6d598d0edcc650a5c7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus Quantitative Trader (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8050772","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8050772","locations":[{"label":"London; Amsterdam"},{"label":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands"},{"label":"London, United Kingdom"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Front Office "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3489289,"first_published_at":"2026-07-13T08:37:03-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-07-24T20:00:03-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nOur trading teams are each comprised of a dynamic group of traders, quantitative researchers, and engineers who work together to examine the global markets, seeking to understand the complexities of various traded products and exchanges. They leverage their impeccable statistical analysis and data mining skills, using the results of their research to make forecasts and develop profitable predictive trading models.\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nThe quant trading internship is an intensive 10-week program focused on enhancing your trading aptitude and understanding of financial markets, as well as helping you experience what it’s like to be a full-time quant trader at Jump.\n\nAt Jump, our people contribute to trading teams in the following roles, or a blend of all three: quant trader, quant researcher, and quant developer. During our internship you will get training in all of these areas, with a focus in trading and financial markets. Topics include trading strategies and intuition, market mechanics, statistics, and our research process for signal generation.\n\nYou will have the opportunity to work with our trading teams on meaningful projects with real impact while receiving daily 1:1 mentorship from experienced quant traders, researchers, and developers. You will also participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.\n\nOther duties as assigned or needed.\n\nWho Should Apply?\n\nWe are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.\n\nIdeal candidates will have:\n\n- Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning\n\n- Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve\n\n- Programming experience\n\n- Appetite for risk-taking\n\n- Demonstrated interest in financial markets\n\nReliable and predictable availability required.\n\nINTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.","description_html":"<p>Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"2993\">Our trading teams are each comprised of a dynamic group of traders, quantitative researchers, and engineers who work together to examine the global markets, seeking to understand the complexities of various traded products and exchanges. They leverage their impeccable statistical analysis and data mining skills, using the results of their research to make forecasts and develop profitable predictive trading models.</p>\n<p><strong>About the Role:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>The quant trading internship is an intensive 10-week program focused on enhancing your trading aptitude and understanding of financial markets, as well as helping you experience what it’s like to be a full-time quant trader at Jump.</p>\n<p>At Jump, our people contribute to trading teams in the following roles, or a blend of all three: quant trader, quant researcher, and quant developer. During our internship you will get training in all of these areas, with a focus in trading and financial markets. Topics include trading strategies and intuition, market mechanics, statistics, and our research process for signal generation.</p>\n<p>You will have the opportunity to work with our trading teams on meaningful projects with real impact while receiving daily 1:1 mentorship from experienced quant traders, researchers, and developers. You will also participate in mock trading sessions, poker training, and other modules designed to improve probabilistic thinking, risk-taking, and trader mindset.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Other duties as assigned or needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Should Apply?</strong></p>\n<p>We are seeking the sharpest analytical minds from top undergraduate and graduate programs.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ideal candidates will have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Outstanding skills in probabilistic thinking and mathematical reasoning</li>\n<li>Competitive spirit and uncommon drive to learn and improve</li>\n<li>Programming experience&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Appetite for risk-taking</li>\n<li>Demonstrated interest in financial markets&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reliable and predictable availability required.</p>\n<p>INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.</p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["quant"],"role_matches":["Quantitative"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Quantitative"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:7975026","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"7975026","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"08a24f1f91895613e2c013adb0cdaf9b6ea3c5b4f6c00c84bea11fd4e23fbdd4","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus Software Engineer (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=7975026","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=7975026","locations":[{"label":"London"},{"label":"London, United Kingdom"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Core Development "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3461429,"first_published_at":"2026-07-13T08:37:21-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-18T18:18:12-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nCore Development is a global team of technologists who architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform. From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage software & hardware engineering, data science and research, to deliver the infrastructure and tools that drive our trading and business needs.\n\nSoftware Engineering Internship (London)\n\n*NOTE - We accept students needing placements or otherwise extended internships. We also allow internships to take place during a non-summer term (for example - the winter, spring, or fall months) if preferable when it makes sense.\n\nWhat you will do:\n\nOur software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience within our core development team that designs, codes, tests, and maintains our distributed trading system.\n\nYou will learn the fundamentals of a large-scale, high-performance infrastructure; sharpen your C++/Python programming skills; and see what it’s like to work as a full-time software engineer at Jump. Throughout your internship you will take on projects targeted for production, which go through our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. May include other duties as assigned or needed.\n\nYou will be working side by side with our experienced software engineers where you will receive continuous feedback and coaching from a dedicated mentor throughout the summer.\n\nOur internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time opportunities at Jump.\n\nSkills you will need:\n\n- Experience with C++ programming on Linux\n\n-\n\n- Experience with command line on Linux\n\n-\n\n- Experience with Git/version control\n\n- Experience with Python programming on Linux\n\n- Strong understanding of data structures and threading models\n\n- Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily\n\n- Passion for solving complex problems using both novel and state of the art commercial solutions\n\n- Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, operating systems -- to produce extremely high-performance software\n\n- Reliable and predictable availability\n\n* No finance or economics study or work experience required\n\nAlso helpful, but not required:\n\n- Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus\n\n- Advanced coursework in algorithms, network programming, operating systems, compilers\n\n- Experience in Rust\n\n- Claude Code in a real work environment\n\n- Experience with any of the following: gRPC, kafka, redpanda, eBPF, dpdk, Clickhouse, FastAPI, Kubernetes, Pandas, SQL, MySQL, DuckDB or the Arrow ecosystem\n\nINTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.","description_html":"<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply&nbsp;cutting edge&nbsp;research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by&nbsp;incenting&nbsp;collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Core Development is a global team of technologists who&nbsp;architect, build and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;our world-class trading platform. From&nbsp;optimizing&nbsp;our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we&nbsp;leverage&nbsp;software &amp; hardware engineering, data&nbsp;science&nbsp;and research, to deliver the infrastructure and tools that drive our trading and business needs.</span>&nbsp;<br><br></p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Software Engineering Internship (London)</span></strong><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">*NOTE - We accept students needing placements or otherwise extended internships. We also allow internships to take place during a non-summer term (for example - the winter, spring, or fall months) if preferable when it makes sense.</span></em></strong><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong>What you will do:</strong></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Our software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience within our core development team that designs, codes, tests, and&nbsp;maintains&nbsp;our distributed trading system.&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">You will learn the fundamentals of a large-scale, high-performance infrastructure; sharpen your C++/Python programming skills; and see what&nbsp;it’s&nbsp;like to work as a full-time software engineer at Jump. Throughout your internship you will take on projects targeted for production, which go through our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. May include other duties as assigned or needed.&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">You will be working side by side with our experienced software engineers&nbsp;where you will&nbsp;receive&nbsp;continuous&nbsp;feedback and coaching from a dedicated mentor throughout the summer.&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Our internship program is the primary way we&nbsp;identify&nbsp;top young software engineers for our core development team, and&nbsp;it’s&nbsp;a proven path for earning full-time opportunities at Jump.&nbsp;</span> <em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">&nbsp;</span></em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Skills you will need:&nbsp;</span></strong><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience with C++ programming on Linux</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"o\" data-font=\"Courier New\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:1440,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Courier New&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[9675],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;o&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"2\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience with command line on Linux</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"o\" data-font=\"Courier New\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:1440,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Courier New&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[9675],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;o&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"2\" data-aria-level=\"2\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience with Git/version control</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"2\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience with Python programming on Linux</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"3\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Strong understanding of data structures and threading models</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"4\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"5\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Passion for solving complex problems using both novel and&nbsp;state of the art&nbsp;commercial solutions</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"6\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking,&nbsp;operating systems&nbsp;-- to produce extremely high-performance software</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"7\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Reliable and predictable availability</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">* No finance or economics study or work experience&nbsp;required</span></em><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">&nbsp; Also helpful, but not&nbsp;required:</span></strong><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"2\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus</span></li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"2\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\">Advanced coursework in algorithms, network programming, operating systems, compilers</li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"2\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\">Experience in Rust</li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"2\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\">Claude Code in a real work environment</li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"2\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\">Experience with any of the following: gRPC, kafka, redpanda, eBPF, dpdk, Clickhouse, FastAPI, Kubernetes, Pandas, SQL, MySQL, DuckDB or the Arrow ecosystem<span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.</span></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:8002989","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"8002989","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"56efea9435999f764995a22953976b4066ef5bb384683c3c015c5378ed630472","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus Software Engineer (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8002989","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8002989","locations":[{"label":"Chicago"},{"label":"Chicago, IL, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Core Development "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3470043,"first_published_at":"2026-07-08T17:35:32-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-08T01:01:43-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nCore Development is a global team of technologists who lean into the cutting edge of agentic development to architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage the latest agentic tools to deliver the infrastructure that drives our trading and business needs.\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\n\nOur software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience with our technology team that designs, codes, tests, and maintains our distributed trading system and one of the world’s largest supercomputers.\n\nYou will be working side by side with our experienced software engineers and will receive ongoing coaching from a dedicated mentor throughout the summer. Our internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time opportunities at Jump.\n\nOver the course of the summer, you will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. You will apply your programming and analysis skills to contribute to our real-time large-scale, high-performance trading platform and related infrastructure.\n\nOther duties as assigned or needed\n\nSkills You’ll Need:\n\n- Hands-on experience and a high level of proficiency in one or more of the following:\n\n- C++ development on Linux platform\n\n- Python development on Linux platform\n\n- Strong understanding of data structures and threading models\n\n- Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily\n\n- Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build optimal solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries\n\n- Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, OS design -- to produce extremely high-performance software\n\n- Reliable and predictable availability\n\nAlso Helpful, but Not Required:\n\n- Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus\n\n- Advanced coursework in algorithms, network programming, operating systems, compilers\n\n- Experience with AI tools like Claude Code in a real work environment\n\n* No finance or economics study or work experience required\n\nINTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply. We accept students eligible for CPT/OPT and we sponsor work visas for full-time positions\n\nThe estimated base salary for this role is $250,000 per year.","description_html":"<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"1448\">Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"1448\">Core Development is a global team of technologists who lean into the cutting edge of agentic development to architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage the latest agentic tools to deliver the infrastructure that drives our trading and business needs.</p>\n<p><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></p>\n<p>Our software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience with our technology team that designs, codes, tests, and maintains our distributed trading system and one of the world’s largest supercomputers.</p>\n<p>You will be working side by side with our experienced software engineers and will receive ongoing coaching from a dedicated mentor throughout the summer. Our internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time opportunities at Jump.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Over the course of the summer, you will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. You will apply your programming and analysis skills to contribute to our real-time large-scale, high-performance trading platform and related infrastructure.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Other duties as assigned or needed</p>\n<p><strong>Skills You’ll Need:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hands-on experience and a high level of proficiency in one or more of the following:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>C++ development on Linux platform</li>\n<li>Python development on Linux platform</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Strong understanding of data structures and threading models</li>\n<li>Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily</li>\n<li>Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build optimal solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries</li>\n<li>Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, OS design -- to produce extremely high-performance software&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Reliable and predictable availability&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Also Helpful, but Not Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus</li>\n<li>Advanced coursework in algorithms, network programming, operating systems, compilers&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Experience with AI tools like Claude Code in a real work environment</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>* No finance or economics study or work experience required</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply. We accept students eligible for CPT/OPT and we sponsor work visas for full-time positions</p>\n<p>The estimated base salary for this role is $250,000 per year.</p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:7974943","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"7974943","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"2fb57cef9f071095b84aa8d414f19498e91b0260eaa5b2bef731cd612e8f7663","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus UI Software Engineer (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=7974943","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=7974943","locations":[{"label":"London"},{"label":"London, United Kingdom"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Core Development "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3461391,"first_published_at":"2026-07-13T08:37:46-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-18T18:14:45-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nJump Trading has a global team of technologists who architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform. From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage software & hardware engineering, sophisticated front-end technologies, data science and research, to deliver the infrastructure and tools that drive our trading and business needs.\n\nNOTE - We accept students needing placements or otherwise extended internships. We also allow internships to take place during a non-summer term (for example - the winter, spring, or fall months) if preferable when it makes sense.\n\nWhat you will do:\n\nOur Web Dev / UI software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience at Jump Trading.\n\nDuring your internship, you will use advanced Typescript, Python, and modern Web frameworks to build Web-based applications that interact with several components of our real-time trading platform.\n\nOur internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time or return internship opportunities at Jump Trading in London.\n\nYou will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. May also include other duties as assigned or needed.\n\nSkills you will need:\n\n- Hands-on experience and a high level of proficiency in one or more of the following:\n\n- Web development using Python and Typescript\n\n- Python development on Linux platform\n\n- Strong understanding of data structures, algorithms, and threading models\n\n- Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily\n\n- Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build optimal solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries\n\n- Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, OS design -- to produce extremely high-performance software\n\n- Reliable and predictable availability\n\nAlso helpful, but not required:\n\n- Comfort in React\n\n- Claude Code in a real work environment\n\n- Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus\n\n* No finance or economics study or work experience required\n\nINTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.","description_html":"<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply&nbsp;cutting edge&nbsp;research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by&nbsp;incenting&nbsp;collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>Jump Trading has a global team of technologists who architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform. From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage software &amp; hardware engineering, sophisticated front-end technologies, data science and research, to deliver the infrastructure and tools that drive our trading and business needs.</p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">NOTE - We accept students needing placements or otherwise extended internships. We also allow internships to take place during a non-summer term (for example - the winter, spring, or fall months) if preferable when it makes sense.&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\n<p><strong>What you will do:</strong></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Our Web Dev / UI software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience at Jump Trading.</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">During your internship, you will use advanced Typescript, Python, and modern Web frameworks to build Web-based applications that interact with several components of our real-time trading platform.</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Our internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time or return internship opportunities at Jump Trading in London.</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">You will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. May also include other duties as assigned or needed.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Skills you will need:</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Hands-on experience and a high level of proficiency in one or more of the following:</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"o\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:1440,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[9675],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;o&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"2\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Web development using Python and Typescript&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"o\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:1440,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[9675],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;o&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"2\" data-aria-level=\"2\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Python development on Linux platform</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"2\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Strong understanding of data structures, algorithms, and threading models</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"3\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily</span></li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"3\" data-aria-level=\"1\">Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build optimal solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"4\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, OS design -- to produce extremely high-performance software</span></li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"5\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Reliable and predictable availability</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Also helpful, but not required:</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"6\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Comfort in React</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"7\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Claude Code in a real work environment</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"1\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"8\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\">* No finance or economics study or work experience required</span></span></p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.&nbsp;</span></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:jumptrading:8003019","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"jumptrading","job_id":"8003019","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/jumptrading/jobs","response_hash":"910dda4548423f239938a6175db38b8f7b0a945f0005164fa0eb4bb76d5ac72b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Jump Trading","slug":"jump-trading","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Campus UI Software Engineer (Intern)","canonical_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8003019","apply_url":"https://www.jumptrading.com/hr/job?gh_jid=8003019","locations":[{"label":"Chicago"},{"label":"Chicago, IL, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Core Development "],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3470057,"first_published_at":"2026-07-08T17:35:13-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-14T11:41:55-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.\n\nJump Trading has a global team of technologists who architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform. From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage software & hardware engineering, sophisticated front-end technologies, data science and research, to deliver the infrastructure and tools that drive our trading and business needs.\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\n\nOur Web Dev / UI software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience at Jump Trading.\n\nDuring your internship, you will use advanced Typescript, Python, and modern Web frameworks to build Web-based applications that interact with several components of our real-time trading platform.\n\nOur internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time or return internship opportunities at Jump Trading in Chicago.\n\nYou will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies.\n\nOther duties as assigned or needed\n\nSkills You’ll Need:\n\n- Hands-on experience and a high level of proficiency in one or more of the following:\n\n- Web development using Python and Typescript\n\n- Python development on Linux platform\n\n- Strong understanding of data structures, algorithms, and threading models\n\n- Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily\n\n- Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build optimal solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, OS design -- to produce extremely high-performance software  \n\n- Reliable and predictable availability\n\nAlso helpful, but not required:\n\n- Comfort in React\n\n- Claude code in a real work environment\n\n- Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus\n\n* No finance or economics study or work experience required\n\nINTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply. We accept students eligible for CPT/OPT and we sponsor work visas for full-time positions.\n\nThe estimated base salary for this role is $250,000 per year.","description_html":"<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"1448\">Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"1448\">Jump Trading has a global team of technologists who architect, build and maintain our world-class trading platform. From optimizing our core trading engine to building custom hardware, we leverage software &amp; hardware engineering, sophisticated front-end technologies, data science and research, to deliver the infrastructure and tools that drive our trading and business needs.</p>\n<p><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></p>\n<p>Our Web Dev / UI software engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience at Jump Trading.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>During your internship, you will use advanced Typescript, Python, and modern Web frameworks to build Web-based applications that interact with several components of our real-time trading platform.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Our internship program is the primary way we identify top young software engineers for our core development team, and it’s a proven path for earning full-time or return internship opportunities at Jump Trading in Chicago.</p>\n<p>You will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Other duties as assigned or needed</p>\n<p><strong>Skills You’ll Need:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hands-on experience and a high level of proficiency in one or more of the following:&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Web development using Python and Typescript&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Python development on Linux platform&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of data structures, algorithms, and threading models&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build optimal solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as hardware, networking, OS design -- to produce extremely high-performance software  &nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Reliable and predictable availability&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Also helpful, but not required:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Comfort in React&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Claude code in a real work environment&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Past internship or job experience in a software development role is a plus&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>* No finance or economics study or work experience required</p>\n<p>INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply. We accept students eligible for CPT/OPT and we sponsor work visas for full-time positions.</p>\n<p>The estimated base salary for this role is $250,000 per year.</p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Employment Type":"Jump Trading - Intern"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","Campus"],"positive_matches":["Intern","Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:nvidia-nvidiaexternalcareersite:/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023639","source":{"type":"workday","board":"nvidia-NVIDIAExternalCareerSite","job_id":"/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023639","source_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/nvidia/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/jobs","response_hash":"0f064c66239c77ffd2e9ffef0eef2bab53b4ba26740c81244f3abde8e6e39919","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:48:46.459Z"},"company":{"name":"NVIDIA","slug":"nvidia","lists":["ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Deep Learning Software Engineering Intern, Test Development - 2027","canonical_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023639","apply_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023639","locations":[{"label":"China, Shanghai"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"JR2023639","internal_job_id":"ba11c49d95681017c95f83ab4e500000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"We are now looking for a Deep Learning Software Test Development Engineering Intern.\n \nThe position is in NVIDIA Deep Learning Software Quality Assurance team that defines, develops and performs tests to validate robustness and measure the performance of NVIDIA‘s Deep Learning software and GPU Infrastructure for autonomous driving, healthcare, speech recognition, natural language processing, and a wide variety of other AI scenarios. This team collaborates with multiple AI product teams to develop new products; derive and improve complex test plans; and improve our workflow processes for a diverse range of GPU computing platforms. You should grow with being in the critical path supporting developers working for billion-dollar business lines as well as intimately understanding the values of responsiveness, thoroughness and teamwork. You should constantly foster and implement efficiency improvements across your domain. Join the team which is building software which will be used by the entire world!\n \nWhat you’ll be doing:\n- GPU Software testing and test automation improvement for NVIDIA Deep Learning Software products, such as Edge-LLM, TensorRT, NVIDIA optimized Frameworks (E.g. TensorFlow, PyTorch, MxNET, etc.)\n\n- Be responsible for functionality, compatibility, and performance tests in DL SW stack release.\n\n- Work with development teams to triage issues, root cause analysis, verify fixes, define new tests, improve test plans. \n\n- Utilize AI-powered tools to improve efficiency and quality, including test case/plan/script generation, defect detection, CBTP, bug fixing and day to day assistance.  \n\n \nWhat we need to see: \n- Pursuing MS or higher degree in CS/EE/CE.\n\n- Scripting language (Python, Perl, bash), Linux knowledge is required.\n\n- Experiences in C/C++ programming is a plus.\n\n- Familiarity any Deep Learning Framework is a strong plus.\n\n- Good communication skills, fluent oral and written English.\n\n- Experience with AI tools. \n\n \nWays to stand out from the crowd:\n- Familiarity working with NVIDIA GPU hardware is a strong plus.\n\n- Background with NVIDIA GPU Computing (CUDA) is a strong plus.\n\n- Proven success in leveraging AI tools to significantly improve efficiency, streamline workflows or enhance process automation.\n\n \nNVIDIA is committed to fostering a diverse work environment and proud to be an equal opportunity employer. As we highly value diversity in our current and future employees, we do not discriminate (including in our hiring and promotion practices) based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status or any other characteristic protected by law.","description_html":"<p><span>We are now looking for a Deep Learning Software Test Development Engineering Intern.</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span>The position is in NVIDIA Deep Learning Software Quality Assurance team that defines, develops and performs tests to validate robustness and measure the performance of NVIDIA‘s Deep Learning software and GPU Infrastructure for autonomous driving, healthcare, speech recognition, natural language processing, and a wide variety of other AI scenarios. This team collaborates with multiple AI product teams to develop new products; derive and improve complex test plans; and improve our workflow processes for a diverse range of GPU computing platforms. You should grow with being in the critical path supporting developers working for billion-dollar business lines as well as intimately understanding the values of responsiveness, thoroughness and teamwork. You should constantly foster and implement efficiency improvements across your domain. Join the team which is building software which will be used by the entire world!</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span><b>What you’ll be doing:</b></span></p><ul><li><p><span>GPU Software testing and test automation improvement for NVIDIA Deep Learning Software products, such as Edge-LLM, TensorRT, NVIDIA optimized Frameworks (E.g. TensorFlow, PyTorch, MxNET, etc.)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Be responsible for functionality, compatibility, and performance tests in DL SW stack release.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Work with development teams to triage issues, root cause analysis, verify fixes, define new tests, improve test plans. </span></p></li><li><p><span>Utilize AI-powered tools to improve efficiency and quality, including test case/plan/script generation, defect detection, CBTP, bug fixing and day to day assistance.  </span></p></li></ul><p><span> </span></p><p><span><b>What we need to see: </b></span></p><ul><li><p><span>Pursuing MS or higher degree in CS/EE/CE.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Scripting language (Python, Perl, bash), Linux knowledge is required.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experiences in C/C&#43;&#43; programming is a plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Familiarity any Deep Learning Framework is a strong plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Good communication skills, fluent oral and written English.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with AI tools. </span></p></li></ul><p><span> </span></p><p><span><b>Ways to stand out from the crowd:</b></span></p><ul><li><p><span>Familiarity working with NVIDIA GPU hardware is a strong plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Background with NVIDIA GPU Computing (CUDA) is a strong plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Proven success in leveraging AI tools to significantly improve efficiency, streamline workflows or enhance process automation.</span></p></li></ul><p><span> </span></p><p><span>NVIDIA is committed to fostering a diverse work environment and proud to be an equal opportunity employer. As we highly value diversity in our current and future employees, we do not discriminate (including in our hiring and promotion practices) based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status or any other characteristic protected by law.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"China","id":"6cb77610a8a543aea2d6bc10457e35d4"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:48:46.459Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":"2027","tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineering"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","2027"],"positive_matches":["Intern","2027"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:nvidia-nvidiaexternalcareersite:/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023641","source":{"type":"workday","board":"nvidia-NVIDIAExternalCareerSite","job_id":"/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023641","source_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/nvidia/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/jobs","response_hash":"19188018e4c28fcbe23c2252c893a654b7458a02f0cd0424fcf8058782cb04f5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:48:46.459Z"},"company":{"name":"NVIDIA","slug":"nvidia","lists":["ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Deep Learning Software Engineering Intern, Test Development - 2027","canonical_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023641","apply_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023641","locations":[{"label":"China, Shanghai"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"JR2023641","internal_job_id":"ebd12953512a10357b5087b611ac0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Deep Learning SWQA Mobile team has permission to open 1 intern Req. Looking for full time interns to help on cuDNN, TensorRT, DL FW, TensorRT Model Connect or DL Mobile SWQA projects in the next 12+ months.\n \nWe are now looking for a Deep Learning Software Test Development Engineering Intern. The position is in NVIDIA Deep Learning Software Quality Assurance team that defines, develops and performs tests to validate robustness and measure the performance of NVIDIA‘s Deep Learning software and GPU Infrastructure for autonomous driving, healthcare, speech recognition, natural language processing, and a wide variety of other AI scenarios. This team collaborates with multiple AI product teams to develop new products; derive and improve complex test plans; and improve our workflow processes for a diverse range of GPU computing platforms. You should grow with being in the critical path supporting developers working for billion-dollar business lines as well as intimately understanding the values of responsiveness, thoroughness and teamwork. You should constantly foster and implement efficiency improvements across your domain. Join the team which is building software which will be used by the entire world!\n \nWhat you’ll be doing:\n- GPU Software testing and test automation improvement for NVIDIA Deep Learning Software products, such as cuDNN, TensorRT, NVIDIA optimized Frameworks (E.g. TensorFlow, PyTorch, MxNET, etc.)\n\n- Be responsible for functionality, compatibility, and performance tests in DL SW stack release.\n\n- Work with development teams to triage issues, root cause analysis, verify fixes, define new tests, improve test plans. \n\n- Utilize AI-powered tools to improve efficiency and quality, including test case/plan/script generation, defect detection, CBTP, bug fixing and day to day assistance.  \n\n \nWhat we need to see: \n- Pursuing MS or higher degree in CS/EE/CE.\n\n- Scripting language (Python, Perl, bash), Linux knowledge is required.\n\n- Experiences in C/C++ programming is a plus.\n\n- Familiarity any Deep Learning Framework is a strong plus.\n\n- Good communication skills, fluent oral and written English.\n\n- Experience with AI tools. \n\n \nWays to stand out from the crowd:\n- Familiarity working with NVIDIA GPU hardware is a strong plus.\n\n- Background with NVIDIA GPU Computing (CUDA) is a strong plus.\n\n- Proven success in leveraging AI tools to significantly improve efficiency, streamline workflows or enhance process automation.\n\n \nNVIDIA is committed to fostering a diverse work environment and proud to be an equal opportunity employer. As we highly value diversity in our current and future employees, we do not discriminate (including in our hiring and promotion practices) based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status or any other characteristic protected by law.","description_html":"<p><span><span><span>Deep Learning SWQA Mobile team has permission to open 1 intern Req. Looking for full time interns to help on cuDNN, TensorRT, DL FW, TensorRT Model Connect or DL Mobile SWQA projects in the next 12&#43; months.</span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span> </span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span>We are now looking for a Deep Learning Software Test Development Engineering Intern. </span></span></span><span><span><span>The position is in NVIDIA Deep Learning Software Quality Assurance team that defines, develops and performs tests to validate robustness and measure the performance of NVIDIA‘s Deep Learning software and GPU Infrastructure for autonomous driving, healthcare, speech recognition, natural language processing, and a wide variety of other AI scenarios. This team collaborates with multiple AI product teams to develop new products; derive and improve complex test plans; and improve our workflow processes for a diverse range of GPU computing platforms. You should grow with being in the critical path supporting developers working for billion-dollar business lines as well as intimately understanding the values of responsiveness, thoroughness and teamwork. You should constantly foster and implement efficiency improvements across your domain. Join the team which is building software which will be used by the entire world!</span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span> </span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span><b>What you’ll be doing:</b></span></span></span></p><ul><li><p><span><span><span>GPU Software testing and test automation improvement for NVIDIA Deep Learning Software products, such as cuDNN, TensorRT, NVIDIA optimized Frameworks (E.g. TensorFlow, PyTorch, MxNET, etc.)</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Be responsible for functionality, compatibility, and performance tests in DL SW stack release.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Work with development teams to triage issues, root cause analysis, verify fixes, define new tests, improve test plans. </span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Utilize AI-powered tools to improve efficiency and quality, including test case/plan/script generation, defect detection, CBTP, bug fixing and day to day assistance.  </span></span></span></p></li></ul><p><span><span><span> </span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span><b>What we need to see: </b></span></span></span></p><ul><li><p><span><span><span>Pursuing MS or higher degree in CS/EE/CE.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Scripting language (Python, Perl, bash), Linux knowledge is required.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Experiences in C/C&#43;&#43; programming is a plus.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Familiarity any Deep Learning Framework is a strong plus.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Good communication skills, fluent oral and written English.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Experience with AI tools. </span></span></span></p></li></ul><p><span><span><span> </span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span><b>Ways to stand out from the crowd:</b></span></span></span></p><ul><li><p><span><span><span>Familiarity working with NVIDIA GPU hardware is a strong plus.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Background with NVIDIA GPU Computing (CUDA) is a strong plus.</span></span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span><span>Proven success in leveraging AI tools to significantly improve efficiency, streamline workflows or enhance process automation.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p><span><span><span> </span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span>NVIDIA is committed to fostering a diverse work environment and proud to be an equal opportunity employer. As we highly value diversity in our current and future employees, we do not discriminate (including in our hiring and promotion practices) based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status or any other characteristic protected by law.</span></span></span><span><span><span> </span></span></span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"China","id":"6cb77610a8a543aea2d6bc10457e35d4"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:48:46.459Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":"2027","tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineering"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","2027"],"positive_matches":["Intern","2027"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:nvidia-nvidiaexternalcareersite:/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023656","source":{"type":"workday","board":"nvidia-NVIDIAExternalCareerSite","job_id":"/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023656","source_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/nvidia/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/jobs","response_hash":"df05367560ffff8dc4b6d3a3b8a40e109e8ffbfd482d0c3b95daf13696116cc6","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:48:46.459Z"},"company":{"name":"NVIDIA","slug":"nvidia","lists":["ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Deep Learning Software Engineering Intern, Test Development - 2027","canonical_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023656","apply_url":"https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/China-Shanghai/Deep-Learning-Software-Engineering-Intern--Test-Development---2027_JR2023656","locations":[{"label":"China, Shanghai"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"JR2023656","internal_job_id":"be21dd777426103526be72217e0e0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"We are now looking for a Deep Learning Software Test Development Engineer  Intern !\n\nThe position is in NVIDIA Deep Learning Software Quality Assurance team that defines, develops and performs tests to validate robustness and measure the performance of NVIDIA‘s Deep Learning software and GPU Infrastructure for autonomous driving, healthcare, speech recognition, natural language processing, and a wide variety of other AI scenarios. This team collaborates with multiple AI product teams to develop new products; derive and improve complex test plans; and improve our workflow processes for a diverse range of GPU computing platforms. You should grow with being in the critical path supporting developers working for billion-dollar business lines as well as intimately understanding the values of responsiveness, thoroughness and teamwork. You should constantly foster and implement efficiency improvements across your domain. Join the team which is building software which will be used by the entire world!\n\nWhat you’ll be doing:\n- Be responsible for functionality, compatibility, and performance tests in NVIDIA AI SW stack release.\n\n- Develop, maintain, and improve test automation infrastructure with using AI tools. Use AI to improve quality and productivity across QA End-to-End workflow.\n\n- Work with development teams to triage issues, root cause analysis, verify fixes, define new tests, improve test plans.\n\nWhat we need to see:\n- Pursuing MS or higher degree in CS/EE/CE or a related field .\n\n- Proven success in leveraging AI tools to significantly improve efficiency, streamline workflows or enhance process automation.\n\n- Good python, C++ programming skillset, Linux knowledge is required.\n\n- Experience in software development with popular AI models is a strong plus.\n\n- Good communication skills, fluent oral and written English.\n\nWays to stand out from the crowd:\n- Be familiar with deep neural network training, inference, optimization in typical DL Frameworks.\n\n- Background with NVIDIA GPU Computing (CUDA) is a strong plus.\n\nWith highly competitive salaries and a comprehensive benefits package, NVIDIA is widely considered to be one of the technology world’s most desirable employers. We have some of the most brilliant and talented people in the world working for us. If you're creative, autonomous and love a challenge, we want to hear from you. Come, join our AI Software QA Test development team, and help build the real-time, cost-effective computing platform driving our success in the exciting and quickly growing field of AI.\n\n#deeplearning","description_html":"<p>We are now looking for a Deep Learning Software Test Development Engineer <span>Intern</span>!</p><p></p><p>The position is in NVIDIA Deep Learning Software Quality Assurance team that defines, develops and performs tests to validate robustness and measure the performance of NVIDIA‘s Deep Learning software and GPU Infrastructure for autonomous driving, healthcare, speech recognition, natural language processing, and a wide variety of other AI scenarios. This team collaborates with multiple AI product teams to develop new products; derive and improve complex test plans; and improve our workflow processes for a diverse range of GPU computing platforms. You should grow with being in the critical path supporting developers working for billion-dollar business lines as well as intimately understanding the values of responsiveness, thoroughness and teamwork. You should constantly foster and implement efficiency improvements across your domain. Join the team which is building software which will be used by the entire world!</p><p></p><p><b>What you’ll be doing:</b></p><ul><li><p>Be responsible for functionality, compatibility, and performance tests in NVIDIA AI SW stack release.</p></li><li><p>Develop, maintain, and improve test automation infrastructure with using AI tools. <span>Use AI to improve quality and productivity across QA End-to-End workflow.</span></p></li><li><p>Work with development teams to triage issues, root cause analysis, verify fixes, define new tests, improve test plans.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>What we need to see:</b></p><ul><li><p>Pursuing MS or higher degree in CS/EE/CE <span>or a related field</span>.</p></li><li><p>Proven success in leveraging AI tools to significantly improve efficiency, streamline workflows or enhance process automation.</p></li><li><p>Good python, C&#43;&#43; programming skillset, Linux knowledge is required.</p></li><li><p>Experience in software development with popular AI models is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p>Good communication skills, fluent oral and written English.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Ways to stand out from the crowd:</b></p><ul><li><p>Be familiar with deep neural network training, inference, optimization in typical DL Frameworks.</p></li><li><p>Background with NVIDIA GPU Computing (CUDA) is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>With highly competitive salaries and a comprehensive benefits package, NVIDIA is widely considered to be one of the technology world’s most desirable employers. We have some of the most brilliant and talented people in the world working for us. If you&#39;re creative, autonomous and love a challenge, we want to hear from you. Come, join our AI Software QA Test development team, and help build the real-time, cost-effective computing platform driving our success in the exciting and quickly growing field of AI.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>#deeplearning","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"China","id":"6cb77610a8a543aea2d6bc10457e35d4"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:48:46.459Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"target","score":12,"level":"intern","term":"2027","tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineering"],"early_career_matches":["Intern","2027"],"positive_matches":["Intern","2027"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-infra","research"]}}
