{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"pinpoint:wolve:525572","source":{"type":"pinpoint","board":"wolve","job_id":"525572","source_url":"https://wolve.pinpointhq.com/postings.json","response_hash":"c40b81ac413fdcfdce3689150d3d10b7930efd60a29f8eb1d46b88e92a142ada","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Wolverine Trading","slug":"wolverine-trading","lists":["quant","software"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer – N-Tiered Software Developer","canonical_url":"https://careers.wolve.com/en/postings/ce3f9cb7-4219-4676-8241-5c8b7903d4c6","apply_url":"https://careers.wolve.com/en/postings/ce3f9cb7-4219-4676-8241-5c8b7903d4c6","locations":[{"label":"Chicago, IL","city":"Chicago","region":"Illinois","country":null,"remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":"525572","first_published_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Join a small, talented team of developers at Wolverine Asset Management to solve the business's problems with technology. You'll play a key part in building new applications and extending existing functionality, gaining valuable experience while helping us pursue the best coding patterns and practices. Knowledge of finance or trading is a plus, but not required.\n\n- Perform full-stack development of primarily desktop applications using .NET technologies and SQL Server, working alongside developers and traders in a dynamic environment\n- Design, develop, and support applications that solve real business problems, applying strong troubleshooting skills to resolve software issues\n- Implement and uphold best practices for software engineering policies and procedures\n\n- A bachelor's degree in computer science/engineering (or equivalent practical experience) and working knowledge of an object-oriented language such as C# or Java, plus SQL Server or a comparable relational database\n- A solid grasp of software development methodologies and of requirements gathering, testing, and implementation from both technical and business perspectives; experience with WPF and/or Windows Forms is preferred\n- A proactive, self-motivated problem solver who thrives on a team, contributes confidently in planning sessions, and keeps the end-user experience front of mind\n\nOur flat organizational structure promotes teamwork across the Firm and offers easy access to senior staff. While we work exceptionally well as a team in the office, our bonds are further strengthened through company events, activities and giving back. Volleyball, soccer, hockey, 5K runs, picnic, parties, and trivia nights provide friendly competition and build better relationships. By getting out of our usual environment and doing out-of-the-ordinary things together, we foster creativity and broaden our imaginations to accomplish new challenges.\n\nBenefits:\n- Highly competitive salary & bonus opportunity\n- Generous paid time off and flexible scheduling\n- 100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, life, and disability benefits for single coverage\n- Generous Paid Parental Leave\n- Retirement Plans: 401K and Roth 401K\n- Profit sharing plan\n- Long- and short-term disability\nAdditional Perks:\n- Free breakfast and lunch from our in-house kitchen with rotating menus (including snacks!)\n- On-site gym with a subsidized membership\n- Frequent company outings\n- Opportunity to give back to organizations that help individuals in need in the Chicagoland area\nProfessional Development:\n- In-house education team – classes and resources are offered for continuous learning opportunities\n- Mentorship Program through your first six months of employment\nThe base compensation range for this role is approximately $80,000-$120,000 contingent on experience. Wolverine's total compensation model includes base salary and an annual discretionary bonus.","description_html":"<div><!--block-->Join a small, talented team of developers at Wolverine Asset Management to solve the business's problems with technology. You'll play a key part in building new applications and extending existing functionality, gaining valuable experience while helping us pursue the best coding patterns and practices. Knowledge of finance or trading is a plus, but not required.</div>\n<ul><li><!--block-->Perform full-stack development of primarily desktop applications using .NET technologies and SQL Server, working alongside developers and traders in a dynamic environment</li><li><!--block-->Design, develop, and support applications that solve real business problems, applying strong troubleshooting skills to resolve software issues</li><li><!--block-->Implement and uphold best practices for software engineering policies and procedures</li></ul>\n<ul><li><!--block-->A bachelor's degree in computer science/engineering (or equivalent practical experience) and working knowledge of an object-oriented language such as C# or Java, plus SQL Server or a comparable relational database</li><li><!--block-->A solid grasp of software development methodologies and of requirements gathering, testing, and implementation from both technical and business perspectives; experience with WPF and/or Windows Forms is preferred</li><li><!--block-->A proactive, self-motivated problem solver who thrives on a team, contributes confidently in planning sessions, and keeps the end-user experience front of mind</li></ul>\n<div><!--block-->Our flat organizational structure promotes teamwork across the Firm and offers easy access to senior staff. While we work exceptionally well as a team in the office, our bonds are further strengthened through company events, activities and giving back. Volleyball, soccer, hockey, 5K runs, picnic, parties, and trivia nights provide friendly competition and build better relationships. By getting out of our usual environment and doing out-of-the-ordinary things together, we foster creativity and broaden our imaginations to accomplish new challenges.</div><div><!--block-->&nbsp;</div><div><!--block--><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li><!--block-->Highly competitive salary &amp; bonus opportunity</li><li><!--block-->Generous paid time off and flexible scheduling</li><li><!--block-->100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, life, and disability benefits for single coverage</li><li><!--block-->Generous Paid Parental Leave</li><li><!--block-->Retirement Plans: 401K and Roth 401K</li><li><!--block-->Profit sharing plan</li><li><!--block-->Long- and short-term disability&nbsp;</li></ul><div><!--block--><strong>Additional Perks:</strong></div><ul><li><!--block-->Free breakfast and lunch from our in-house kitchen with rotating menus (including snacks!)</li><li><!--block-->On-site gym with a subsidized membership</li><li><!--block-->Frequent company outings</li><li><!--block-->Opportunity to give back to organizations that help individuals in need in the Chicagoland area</li></ul><div><!--block--><strong>Professional Development:</strong></div><ul><li><!--block-->In-house education team – classes and resources are offered for continuous learning opportunities</li><li><!--block-->Mentorship Program through your first six months of employment</li></ul><div><!--block-->The base compensation range for this role is approximately $80,000-$120,000 contingent on experience. Wolverine's total compensation model includes base salary and an annual discretionary bonus.</div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"reporting_to":""},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T08:02:38.273Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":8,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer","Software Developer","Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["quant","software"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:akunacapital:7986086","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"akunacapital","job_id":"7986086","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/akunacapital/jobs","response_hash":"e5a709fac40e36dd2ad5e8e9b765be8a1b28d9bf3208dc40b1e7c84ae72d475e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Akuna Capital","slug":"akuna-capital","lists":["quant"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Expression of Interest: 2027 Trading Sneak Peek Weeks","canonical_url":"https://www.akunacapital.com/careers/job/7986086?gh_jid=7986086","apply_url":"https://www.akunacapital.com/careers/job/7986086/?gh_jid=7986086","locations":[{"label":"Chicago"},{"label":"Chicago, Illinois, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"intern","departments":["Trading"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":3465474,"first_published_at":"2026-07-19T19:52:34-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-07-19T19:52:34-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Register your interest for our 2027 Trading Sneak Peek Weeks!\n\nThank you for your interest in Akuna's Trading internship! We are excited to share that we will be hosting multiple Trading Sneak Peek Weeks throughout 2027, rather than a traditional summer internship. These one-week micro-internships are designed to provide an accelerated, hands-on introduction to the tools, skills, and knowledge our trading teams use to drive success every day. With this new format, we are excited to welcome even more trading-focused interns to our office in 2027! By submitting this application, you’ll be added to our list of interested candidates and will be notified as soon as the roles goes live.\n\nAbout Akuna:  \n\nAkuna Capital is an innovative trading firm with a strong focus on collaboration, cutting-edge technology, data driven solutions, and automation. We specialize in providing liquidity as an options market-maker – meaning we are committed to providing competitive quotes that we are willing to both buy and sell. To do this successfully, we design and implement our own low latency technologies, trading strategies and mathematical models.   \n\nOur Founding Partners first conceptualized Akuna in their hometown of Sydney. They opened the firm’s first office in 2011 in the heart of the derivatives industry and the options capital of the world – Chicago. Today, Akuna is proud to operate from additional offices in Sydney, Shanghai, London and Singapore.  \n\nWhat you’ll do as a Trading Sneak Peek Week Participant:\n\nAs a Trading Sneak Peek Week participant , you will be enrolled in a crash course on the exciting world of options. You’ll start the week collaborating with our dedicated trader trainers, as they teach you risk management, game theory, and optimal decision making. Outside the classroom, you’ll have the opportunity to apply your knowledge in real time. Does mastering the educational trading games and simulations used by our entry-level traders sound like fun? Would you like to shadow our trading desks to learn about Akuna's unique approach to acting as a global liquidity provider/market maker? If your answer is yes, Sneak Peek Week is right for you!\n\nAdditional program perks :  \n\n- AkunaU lectures from the firm’s leaders  \n\n- Roundtable networking sessions\n\n- Fun events dedicated to showcasing our firm and the beauty of Chicago  \n\n- Transportation and accommodation provided by Akuna    \n\n- Competitive stipend  \n\nQualities that make great candidates:  \n\n- Graduating between December 2027 – August 2028\n\n- Pursuing a BS/MS/ PhD in engineering, economics, statistics, mathematics, computer science, actuarial science or a related/equivalent field  \n\n- Able to attend program in person at Akuna’s Chicago headquarters\n\n- Entrepreneurial self-starter ready to work in a fast paced, collaborative, team environment  \n\n- Strong math, numerical, and quantitative skills  \n\n- Demonstrable interest in trading and the financial markets   \n\n- Legal authorization to work in the U.S. is required on the first day of employment including F-1 students using OPT or STEM  \n\nIn addition to technical skillsets, Akuna values the unique perspectives people can bring to the table to collaboratively solve complex problems and drive Akuna forward. We want everyone to feel empowered to apply. We welcome your application and encourage you to take the first steps toward your future with us!\n\nIn accordance with Illinois Equal Pay Act, the total pay for this one-week program is $2,250. The total pay herein was determined in good faith by Akuna Capital LLC.","description_html":"<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&quot;ObjectId&quot;:&quot;c599367a-ea1b-4805-b256-0671c01bc1c5|105&quot;,&quot;ClassId&quot;:1073872969,&quot;Properties&quot;:[469775450,&quot;normaltextrun&quot;,201340122,&quot;1&quot;,134233614,&quot;true&quot;,469778129,&quot;normaltextrun&quot;,335572020,&quot;1&quot;,469778324,&quot;Default Paragraph Font&quot;]}\">Register your interest for our 2027 Trading Sneak Peek Weeks!&nbsp;</span></span></strong></p>\n<p>Thank you for your interest in Akuna's Trading internship! We are excited to share that we will be hosting multiple Trading Sneak Peek Weeks throughout 2027, rather than a traditional summer internship. These one-week micro-internships are designed to provide an accelerated, hands-on introduction to the tools, skills, and knowledge our trading teams use to drive success every day. With this new format, we are excited to welcome even more trading-focused interns to our office in 2027!<span data-contrast=\"auto\"> By submitting this application, you’ll be added to our list of interested candidates and will be notified as soon as the roles goes live.<br></span></p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&quot;ObjectId&quot;:&quot;c599367a-ea1b-4805-b256-0671c01bc1c5|105&quot;,&quot;ClassId&quot;:1073872969,&quot;Properties&quot;:[469775450,&quot;normaltextrun&quot;,201340122,&quot;1&quot;,134233614,&quot;true&quot;,469778129,&quot;normaltextrun&quot;,335572020,&quot;1&quot;,469778324,&quot;Default Paragraph Font&quot;]}\">About Akuna:</span></span></strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"eop\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&quot;ObjectId&quot;:&quot;c599367a-ea1b-4805-b256-0671c01bc1c5|106&quot;,&quot;ClassId&quot;:1073872969,&quot;Properties&quot;:[469775450,&quot;eop&quot;,201340122,&quot;1&quot;,134233614,&quot;true&quot;,469778129,&quot;eop&quot;,335572020,&quot;1&quot;,469778324,&quot;Default Paragraph Font&quot;]}\"> </span></span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">Akuna Capital is an innovative trading firm with a strong focus on collaboration,&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">cutting-edge</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\"> technology, data driven solutions, and automation. We specialize in providing liquidity as an options market-maker – meaning we are committed to providing competitive quotes that we are willing to both buy and sell. To do this successfully, we design and implement our own low latency technologies, trading strategies and mathematical models. </span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"eop\"> </span></span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">Our Founding Partners first conceptualized Akuna in their hometown of Sydney. They opened the firm’s first office in 2011 in the heart of the derivatives industry and the options capital of the world – Chicago. Today, Akuna is proud to </span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">operate</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\"> from </span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">additional</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\"> offices in Sydney, </span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">Shanghai,</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\"> London and Singapore.</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"eop\"> </span></span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">What you’ll do as a Trading Sneak Peek Week Participant:</span></strong></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">As a Trading Sneak Peek Week participant</span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">, you will be enrolled in a crash course on the exciting world of options. You’ll start the week collaborating with our dedicated trader trainers, as they teach you risk management, game theory, and optimal decision making. Outside the classroom, you’ll have the opportunity to apply your knowledge in real time. Does mastering the educational trading games and simulations used by our entry-level traders sound like fun? Would you like to shadow our trading desks to learn about Akuna's unique approach to acting as a global liquidity provider/market maker? If your answer is yes, Sneak Peek Week is right for you!&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:160,&quot;335559740&quot;:259}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">Additional</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\"> program </span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">perks</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">:</span></span></strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"eop\"> </span></span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"6\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559684&quot;:-2,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"1\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">AkunaU</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\"> lectures from the firm’s leaders</span><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"eop\"> </span></span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"6\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559684&quot;:-2,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\" data-aria-posinset=\"2\" data-aria-level=\"1\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"normaltextrun\">Roundtable networking sessions</span></span></li>\n<li data-leveltext=\"\" data-font=\"Symbol\" data-listid=\"6\" data-list-defn-props=\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559684&quot;:-2,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&q