r contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p>Experience with REST APIs, webhooks, and automation middleware</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating enterprise systems, such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of AI and ML workflows leveraging existing AI and ML tools</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI/CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </p></li><li><p>Experience with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","data"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer","Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0244749","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0244749","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"ac7cdf0553459a1582f3cf2955702cb35ad48f150149b79f6426bb08d9709316","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0244749","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0244749","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244749","internal_job_id":"6c9b0fa821f61002080e869c9b720000","first_published_at":"2026-07-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the develop ment of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n- Experience develop ing predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources  \n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n- Experience integrating enterprise systems, such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms\n- Knowledge of AI and ML workflows leveraging existing AI and ML tools\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience in the develop ment of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI / CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL \n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n- Experience with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n- Master's degree \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership <span>skills</span> and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the <span>develop</span>ment of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </li><li><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </li><li><span>Experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </li><li><span>Experience</span> integrating enterprise systems, such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> AI and ML workflows leveraging existing AI and ML tools</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> in the <span>develop</span>ment of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI<span>/</span>CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL </li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","data"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer","Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0246671","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0246671","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"edc05f408cb1fd2f54b0c9c83a7709486a0c5308f95348a703a4f992619df5f8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0246671","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0246671","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246671","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d0100115313bdb7bf50000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  \n\n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n\n- Experience integrating enterprise systems such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms\n\n- Knowledge of AI and ML workflows leveraging existing AI and ML tools\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI / CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL \n\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- Master's degree\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.   \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating enterprise systems such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AI and ML workflows leveraging existing AI and ML tools</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI<span>/</span>CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span>  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","data"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer","Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0247551","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0247551","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"b0467864703546882c7a531b482a35beb16520b876c474b12a2f4cd58c903a93","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0247551","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/AI-ML-Engineer-and-Data-Scientist_R0247551","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247551","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a1001faed5c830e1e0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- 3+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, data mining, and full stack analytic processes  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources  \n\n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n\n- Experience with REST APIs, webhooks, and automation middleware\n\n- Experience integrating enterprise systems, such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms\n\n- Ability to travel to OCONUS locations up to 20% of the time\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI/CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL \n\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- Master's degree \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer and Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, data mining, and full stack analytic processes  </p></li><li><p>Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p>Experience with REST APIs, webhooks, and automation middleware</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating enterprise systems, such as Jira, Confluence, APIs, or in-house platforms</p></li><li><p>Ability to travel to OCONUS locations up to 20% of the time</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging CDS, Gitlab, CI/CD, Argo CD, R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </p></li><li><p>Experience with visualization packages, including Palantir, Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","data"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer","Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7b1a863dcba9099c2b343928dc4aaaeff40df5f2ac03a8b69687f4ced3128ba8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Applied AI Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"},{"label":"Reston, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246156","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb401001a02400efc3a90000","first_published_at":"2026-08-06","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Applied AI Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experience d engineer, you know that artifi cia l intelligence (AI) is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support an enterprise-wide application and data capability. As an AI engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.\n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a large community of AI engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and MLOps engineers to deliver world class solutions, including processing data and information at a massive scale. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI and ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for our national security customers.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience in sof tware engineering, applied AI and ML, or full-stack development, including AI integrations\n- Experience rapidly prototyping, developing, and iterating on use-case-specific AI solutions such as chat systems, user-facing applications, and domain-specific copilots\n- Experience conducting comprehensive evaluation and tuning of AI outputs, including refining prompts, optimizing retrieval logic, and implementing custom heuristics\n- Experience with Python and building API endpoints such as FastAPI or Flask, or rapid UI frameworks such as Streamlit or Gradio, to demonstrate AI capabilities\n- Ability to work closely with mission integration teams and product stakeholders to translate mission needs into refined, business-facing AI capabilities\n- Ability to pivot quickly between different domains and use cases, adapting AI solutions to various operational requirements\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with human-in-the-loop ( HITL ) evaluation, AI red teaming, or assessing conversational interfaces for safety and hallucination mitigation\n- Experience with front-end development technologies such as React or TypeScript, to support end-to-end user-facing product delivery\n- Experience deploying and managing analytical dashboards or mechanisms to track user interactions and model performance\n- Knowledge of user experience ( UX ) best practices, including conversational AI and generative interfaces\n- Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Applied AI Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d engineer, you know that artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence (AI) is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support an enterprise-wide application and data capability. As an AI engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a large community of AI engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and MLOps engineers to deliver world class solutions, including processing data and information at a massive scale. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI and ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for our national security customers.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, applied AI and ML, or full-stack development, including AI integrations</li><li><span>Experience</span> rapidly prototyping, developing, and iterating on use-case-specific AI solutions such as chat systems, user-facing applications, and domain-specific copilots</li><li><span>Experience</span> conducting comprehensive evaluation and tuning of AI outputs, including refining prompts, optimizing retrieval logic, and implementing custom heuristics</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python and building API endpoints such as FastAPI or Flask, or rapid UI frameworks such as Streamlit or Gradio, to demonstrate AI capabilities</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work closely with mission integration teams and product stakeholders to translate mission needs into refined, business-facing AI capabilities</li><li><span>Ability to</span> pivot quickly between different domains and use cases, adapting AI solutions to various operational requirements</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with human-in-the-loop <span>(</span>HITL<span>)</span> evaluation, AI red teaming, or assessing conversational interfaces for safety and hallucination mitigation</li><li><span>Experience</span> with front-end development technologies such as React or TypeScript, to support end-to-end user-facing product delivery</li><li><span>Experience</span> deploying and managing analytical dashboards or mechanisms to track user interactions and model performance</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> user <span>experience</span> <span>(</span>UX<span>)</span> best practices, including conversational AI and generative interfaces</li><li>Security&#43; <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 18 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["AI Engineer","Applied AI"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Applied"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0240233","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0240233","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7c650546823c6994e207a77e3156f5712ae8737d7ef4babf09b327a6eef7fbcb","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer and Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0240233","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0240233","locations":[{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240233","internal_job_id":"31c17c05798f1001f5dd3f43378e0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-07","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer and Developer The Opportunity: \nAs a back-end develop er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a develop er like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a back-end develop er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution develop ed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 4+ years of experience designing, modifying, develop ing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications  \n- 4+ years of experience designing, optimizing, and maintaining NoSQL databases\n- Experience with Python coding\n- Experience with end-to-end design, scoping, and implementation of AWS-based tools\n- Experience with API develop ment\n- Experience in EO / IR image processing, data exploitation, or analysis algorithm develop ment\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment \n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n- Bachelor’s degree and 4+ years of experience in sof tware engineering, or Master's degree and 2+ years of experience in sof tware engineering\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with container technology, including Docker or podman\n- Experience with Python coding for AI / ML solutions such as PyTorch and TensorFlow\n- Experience working with Agentic workflows and LLMs, such as Claude or GPT\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer and Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a back-end <span>develop</span>er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a <span>develop</span>er like you with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a back-end <span>develop</span>er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution <span>develop</span>ed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, <span>develop</span>ing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications  </li><li>4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, optimizing, and maintaining NoSQL databases</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python coding</li><li><span>Experience</span> with end-to-end design, scoping, and implementation of AWS-based tools</li><li><span>Experience</span> with API <span>develop</span>ment</li><li><span>Experience</span> in EO<span>/</span>IR image processing, data exploitation, or analysis algorithm <span>develop</span>ment</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </li><li><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> and 4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, or <span>Master&#39;s degree</span> and 2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with container technology, including Docker or podman</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python coding for AI<span>/</span>ML solutions such as PyTorch and TensorFlow</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with Agentic workflows and LLMs, such as Claude or GPT</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 17 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer","Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Dayton-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0243825","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Dayton-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0243825","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8079f6413b27728d730ee8706957ac1adacaa57c0941a90e40b83b2935d079fd","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer and Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0243825","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Software-Engineer-and-Developer_R0243825","locations":[{"label":"Dayton, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243825","internal_job_id":"186c347b6c0e1000ca31e6bd0e590000","first_published_at":"2026-07-06","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer and Developer The Opportunity: \nJoin us in shaping the future of our systems. We’re seeking a motivated Software Engineer to help design, implement, and enhance modern solutions within an agile development environment. In this role, you’ll contribute to system modernization efforts through hands-on development, ongoing maintenance, and proactive problem-solving. You’ll apply your functional expertise and industry knowledge to address a range of technical challenges of moderate scope and complexity. Working both independently and collaboratively, you’ll help deliver reliable, scalable solutions while also supporting and guiding junior team members as needed.\n\nIf you’re passionate about building better systems and making meaningful technical contributions, we invite you to grow with us.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 4+ years of experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing software programming applications  \n\n- 4+ years of experience building and maintaining automated data pipelines to support AI and ML workflows\n\n- Experience with Python coding\n\n- Experience with managing infrastructure, such as cloud or on-prem, and containerization in support of secure workflows\n\n- Experience with building workflows for real-time trend and anomaly analysis processing and data exploitation\n\n- Experience in creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment \n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- Bachelor’s degree and 4+ years of experience in software engineering, or Master's degree and 2+ years of experience in software engineering\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with container technology, including Docker or Podman\n\n- Experience with Python coding for AI and ML solutions, such as PyTorch and TensorFlow\n\n- Experience working with Agentic workflows and LLMs, such as Claude or GPT\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer and Developer<div><p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Join us in shaping the future of our systems. We’re seeking a motivated Software Engineer to help design, implement, and enhance modern solutions within an agile development environment. In this role, you’ll contribute to system modernization efforts through hands-on development, ongoing maintenance, and proactive problem-solving. You’ll apply your functional expertise and industry knowledge to address a range of technical challenges of moderate scope and complexity. Working both independently and collaboratively, you’ll help deliver reliable, scalable solutions while also supporting and guiding junior team members as needed.</p><p></p><p>If you’re passionate about building better systems and making meaningful technical contributions, we invite you to grow with us.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing software programming applications  </span></p></li><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience building and maintaining automated data pipelines to support AI and ML workflows </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Python coding </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with managing infrastructure, such as cloud or on-prem, and containerization in support of secure workflows</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with building workflows for real-time trend and anomaly analysis processing and data exploitation</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience in creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </span></p></li><li><p><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree and 4&#43; years of experience in software engineering, or Master&#39;s degree and 2&#43; years of experience in software engineering</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with container technology, including Docker or Podman</p></li><li><p>Experience with Python coding for AI and ML solutions, such as PyTorch and TensorFlow</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Agentic workflows and LLMs, such as Claude or GPT</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance: </b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer","Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"smartrecruiters:boschgroup:744000137380229","source":{"type":"smartrecruiters","board":"BoschGroup","job_id":"744000137380229","source_url":"https://api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/BoschGroup/postings","response_hash":"adc2a6cdc69f5f337b53dc9f1b0109e2604bcbbbcc05a2cef30fce0dda69deed","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Bosch","slug":"bosch","lists":["research","robotics"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"[SO] Web Apps AI Engineer (Full-Stack + LLM/ AI)","canonical_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/BoschGroup/744000137380229--so-web-apps-ai-engineer-full-stack-llm-ai-","apply_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/BoschGroup/744000137380229--so-web-apps-ai-engineer-full-stack-llm-ai-?oga=true","locations":[{"label":"Ho Chi Minh city, , Vietnam","city":"Ho Chi Minh city","region":null,"country":"vn","remote":false,"hybrid":false}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Information Technology"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"REF262822J","internal_job_id":"b4ca4840-024a-4c08-a4b1-c94f309e6583","first_published_at":"2026-07-13T07:26:34.366Z","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"The Bosch Group is a leading global supplier of technology and services. Its operations are divided into four business sectors: Mobility, Industrial Technology, Consumer Goods, and Energy and Building Technology. With technology that is “Invented for life,” Bosch wants to help improve quality of life and conserve natural resources.  \nThe Bosch Group comprises Robert Bosch GmbH and its roughly 490 subsidiary and regional companies in over 60 countries. Including sales and service partners, Bosch’s global manufacturing, engineering, and sales network covers nearly every country in the world. Bosch’s innovative strength is key to the company’s further development.  \nBosch Global Software Technologies Company Limited (BGSV)   is 100% owned subsidiary of Robert Bosch GmbH, offering end-to-end Engineering, IT, and Business Solutions.   \nStarting its operation from 2010 at Etown 2 in HCMC, BGSV is the first software development center of Bosch in Southeast Asia. BGSV nowadays have over 4,000 associates, with a global footprint and presence in the US, Europe, and the Asia Pacific region. With our unique ability to offer end-to-end solutions that connect sensors, software, and services, we enable businesses to move from the traditional to digital or improve businesses by introducing a digital element in their products and processes.  \nBGSV currently operates from three offices located at the following addresses:  \n1. Etown Building – 364 Cong Hoa Street, Ward 13, Tan Binh District, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam  \n2. OfficeHaus Building – 32 Tan Thang Street, Son Ky Ward, Tan Phu District, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam  \n3.  Capital Place Building – 29 Lieu Giai Street, Ngoc Khanh Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam  \n\nAbout department: SO\nAs an in-house service provider, SO department supports the Bosch Group in areas including  Supply Chain Management ,  Project Management ,  Data Security ,  L1/L2 IT Support ,  Human Resources Shared Services ,  Web Content Management ,  Quality Management  as well as  Translation/Interpreter  services. \n\nWe pool administrative tasks and ensure efficient processes and improve the entire service chain using automation solutions such as  RPA  and  AI .\n\nThrough the various sections and topics listed here, we aim to introduce to the customers from all around the world to get to know about our  Overview ,  Services , our  Competencies ,  Tools & Process  and  Expertise  as we deliver excellence together as one team.\nKey Responsibilities:\nWe are seeking a highly skilled AI Engineer with Full-Stack Development capabilities who has hands-on experience with Large Language Models (LLMs) to join our dynamic team. You will be responsible for designing, developing, and deploying AI-driven applications that combine advanced machine learning with robust front-end and back-end architectures\nFull-Stack Development\n- Develop and maintain scalable web applications using modern front-end frameworks (React, Vue, etc.) and back-end technologies (Node.js, Python/FastAPI, etc.).\n- Design APIs and services to interface with ML models and data pipelines.\n- Integrate cloud services and manage infrastructure using AWS/GCP/Azure.\n- Ensure performance, responsiveness, and security across platforms\nAI/ML Engineering\n- Design, fine-tune, and optimize LLM for specific use cases (e.g., chatbots, summarization, document processing).\n- Work with vector databases and embedding models for semantic search and retrieval.\n- Build RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) pipelines and LLMOps workflows.\n- Implement AI safety, prompt engineering, and performance monitoring.\n\n- Bachelor’s or Master’s in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a related field.\n- 3+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering and full-stack development.\n- Strong knowledge of: - Back-end: Node.js, FastAPI, Flask\n- Front-end: React, Next.js, Vue\n- Programming: Python, JavaScript/TypeScript\n- LLMs (OpenAI GPT, Hugging Face Transformers, LangChain/LlamaIndex)\n- ML Frameworks: PyTorch, TensorFlow, Hugging Face…\n- Databases: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, and vector databases (e.g., FAISS, Pinecone)\n\n- Experience with Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Git, Agile\n\n- Fluent in English communication (written & verbal)\n\nWHY   BOSCH?\nBecause we don't just follow trends, we  create  them.\nBecause together we turn ideas into reality, working every day to make the world of tomorrow a better place.\nDo you have high standards when it comes to your job? So do we. At Bosch, you will discover more than just work.\nBenefits and Career Opportunities\n- Working in one of the  Best Places to Work in Vietnam and Top 30 of the  Most Innovative Companies  all over the world\n- Join a dynamic and fast-growing global company ( English-speaking  environment)\n- Engage in our diverse training programs which surely help strengthen both your personal and professionalism\n- 13th-month  salary bonus + attractive  performance bonus  (you'll love it!) + annual performance appraisal\n- 100% monthly salary  and  mandatory social insurances  in 2-month probation\n- Meal, Commuting and Parking allowance\n- Premium health insurance for you and  02 family members\n- 15++ days of annual leave  + 1 day of birthday leave\n- Flexible working time\n- Free in-house entertainment facilities and sport activities : football, badminton, yoga, Aerobics….\n- Vibrant culture : Enjoy team-building events, company trips, year-end parties, tech talks, charity & CSR initiatives\n- Onsite opportunities : short-term and long-term assignments","description_html":"<p><strong><em>The Bosch Group</em></strong><em> is a leading global supplier of technology and services. Its operations are divided into four business sectors: Mobility, Industrial Technology, Consumer Goods, and Energy and Building Technology. With technology that is “Invented for life,” Bosch wants to help improve quality of life and conserve natural resources.</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em>The Bosch Group comprises </em><strong><em>Robert Bosch GmbH</em></strong><em><strong> </strong>and its roughly 490 subsidiary and regional companies in over 60 countries. Including sales and service partners, Bosch’s global manufacturing, engineering, and sales network covers nearly every country in the world. Bosch’s innovative strength is key to the company’s further development.</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em><strong>Bosch Global Software Technologies Company Limited (BGSV)</strong> </em><em>is 100% owned subsidiary of Robert Bosch GmbH, offering end-to-end Engineering, IT, and Business Solutions.&#xa0;</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em>Starting its operation from 2010 at Etown 2 in HCMC, BGSV is the first software development center of Bosch in Southeast Asia. BGSV nowadays have over 4,000 associates, with a global footprint and presence in the US, Europe, and the Asia Pacific region. With our unique ability to offer end-to-end solutions that connect sensors, software, and services, we enable businesses to move from the traditional to digital or improve businesses by introducing a digital element in their products and processes.</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em>BGSV currently operates from </em><strong><em>three offices</em></strong><em><strong> </strong>located at the following addresses:</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em>1. </em><strong><em>Etown Building</em></strong><em> – 364 Cong Hoa Street, Ward 13, Tan Binh District, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em>2. </em><strong><em>OfficeHaus Building</em></strong><em> – 32 Tan Thang Street, Son Ky Ward, Tan Phu District, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam</em>&#xa0;</p><p><em>3. </em><strong><em>Capital Place Building</em></strong><em> – 29 Lieu Giai Street, Ngoc Khanh Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam</em>&#xa0;</p>\n<p><strong><u>About department: </u>SO</strong></p><p>As an in-house service provider, SO department supports the Bosch Group in areas including&#xa0;<strong>Supply Chain Management</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Project Management</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Data Security</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>L1/L2 IT Support</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Human Resources Shared Services</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Web Content Management</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Quality Management</strong>&#xa0;as well as&#xa0;<strong>Translation/Interpreter&#xa0;</strong>services.&#xa0;<br>\n<br>\nWe pool administrative tasks and ensure efficient processes and improve the entire service chain using automation solutions such as&#xa0;<strong>RPA</strong>&#xa0;and&#xa0;<strong>AI</strong>.<br>\n<br>\nThrough the various sections and topics listed here, we aim to introduce to the customers from all around the world to get to know about our&#xa0;<strong>Overview</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Services</strong>, our&#xa0;<strong>Competencies</strong>,&#xa0;<strong>Tools &amp; Process</strong>&#xa0;and&#xa0;<strong>Expertise</strong>&#xa0;as we deliver excellence together as one team.</p><p><u><strong>Key Responsibilities: </strong></u></p><p>We are seeking a highly skilled <strong>AI Engineer with Full-Stack Development </strong>capabilities who has hands-on experience with Large Language Models (LLMs) to join our dynamic team. You will be responsible for designing, developing, and deploying AI-driven applications that combine advanced machine learning with robust front-end and back-end architectures</p><p><u>Full-Stack Development</u></p><ul><li>Develop and maintain scalable web applications using modern front-end frameworks (React, Vue, etc.) and back-end technologies (Node.js, Python/FastAPI, etc.).</li><li>Design APIs and services to interface with ML models and data pipelines.</li><li>Integrate cloud services and manage infrastructure using AWS/GCP/Azure.</li><li>Ensure performance, responsiveness, and security across platforms</li></ul><p><u>AI/ML Engineering</u></p><ul><li>Design, fine-tune, and optimize LLM for specific use cases (e.g., chatbots, summarization, document processing).</li><li>Work with vector databases and embedding models for semantic search and retrieval.</li><li>Build RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) pipelines and LLMOps workflows.</li><li>Implement AI safety, prompt engineering, and performance monitoring.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Bachelor’s or Master’s in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a related field.</li><li>3+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering and full-stack development.</li><li>Strong knowledge of:<ul><li><strong>Back-end:</strong> Node.js, FastAPI, Flask</li><li><strong>Front-end:</strong> React, Next.js, Vue</li><li><strong>Programming: </strong>Python, JavaScript/TypeScript</li><li><strong>LLMs </strong>(OpenAI GPT, Hugging Face Transformers, LangChain/LlamaIndex)</li><li><strong>ML Frameworks:</strong> PyTorch, TensorFlow, Hugging Face…</li><li><strong>Databases: </strong>PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, and vector databases (e.g., FAISS, Pinecone)</li></ul></li><li><p>Experience with Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Git, Agile</p></li><li><p><strong>Fluent in English</strong> communication (written &amp; verbal)</p></li></ul>\n<p><em><strong>WHY</strong>&#xa0;<strong>BOSCH?</strong></em></p><p><em>Because we don't just follow trends, we&#xa0;<strong>create&#xa0;</strong>them.</em></p><p><em>Because together we turn ideas into reality, working every day to make the world of tomorrow a better place.</em></p><p><em>Do you have high standards when it comes to your job? So do we. At Bosch, you will discover more than just work.</em></p><p><em><strong>Benefits and Career Opportunities</strong></em></p><ul><li><em>Working in one of the&#xa0;<strong>Best Places to Work </strong>in Vietnam and&#xa0;Top 30 of the&#xa0;<strong>Most Innovative Companies</strong>&#xa0;all over the world</em></li><li><em>Join a dynamic and fast-growing global company (<strong>English-speaking</strong>&#xa0;environment)</em></li><li><em>Engage in our <strong>diverse training programs</strong> which surely help strengthen both your personal and professionalism</em></li><li><em><strong>13th-month&#xa0;</strong>salary bonus + attractive&#xa0;<strong>performance bonus&#xa0;</strong>(you'll love it!) + annual performance appraisal</em></li><li><em><strong>100% monthly&#xa0;salary</strong>&#xa0;and&#xa0;<strong>mandatory social insurances</strong>&#xa0;in 2-month probation</em></li><li><em><strong>Meal,</strong> <strong>Commuting </strong>and<strong> Parking </strong>allowance</em></li><li><em>Premium health insurance for you and&#xa0;<strong>02 family members</strong></em></li><li><em><strong>15++ days of annual leave&#xa0;</strong>+ 1 day of birthday leave</em></li><li><em><strong>Flexible </strong>working time</em></li><li><em>Free in-house entertainment facilities and <strong>sport activities</strong>: football, badminton, yoga, Aerobics….</em></li><li><em><strong>Vibrant culture</strong>: Enjoy team-building events, company trips, year-end parties, tech talks, charity &amp; CSR initiatives</em></li><li><em><strong>Onsite opportunities</strong>: short-term and long-term assignments</em></li></ul>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"experience_level":"Associate","industry":"Automotive","Contract type":"Limited","Tariff Area":"Vietnam Local Grades","Legal Entity(acronym)":"BGSV","Working Location":"Ho Chi Minh City","Global Salary Level":"Experienced/ Middle Tariff","Working hours":"Full-time","Legal Entity":"Bosch Global Software Technologies Company Limited","Position type":"Professional","Country/Region":"Vietnam","Brands":"Bosch Group","Working Country":"Vietnam","Local Grade":"VN_L51","Division":"SO"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["AI Engineer","LLM"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","LLM"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["research","robotics"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"smartrecruiters:boschgroup:744000138985411","source":{"type":"smartrecruiters","board":"BoschGroup","job_id":"744000138985411","source_url":"https://api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/BoschGroup/postings","response_hash":"51b027a87c1e44496fcfad367c2283266b931535632e91cb8df644fd6dc2ff58","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Bosch","slug":"bosch","lists":["research","robotics"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI Research Scientist - GenAI","canonical_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/BoschGroup/744000138985411-ai-research-scientist-genai","apply_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/BoschGroup/744000138985411-ai-research-scientist-genai?oga=true","locations":[{"label":"Pittsburgh, PA, United States","city":"Pittsburgh","region":"PA","country":"us","remote":false,"hybrid":true}],"workplace_type":"hybrid","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"REF281786T","internal_job_id":"5862ae33-ca66-425a-bacd-c67f0124301a","first_published_at":"2026-07-22T03:40:34.358Z","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"We Are Bosch.\nAt Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our areas of activity are every bit as diverse as our outstanding Bosch teams around the world. Their creativity is the key to innovation through connected living, mobility, or industry.\nLet’s grow together, enjoy more, and inspire each other.  Work #LikeABosch \n- Reinvent yourself:  At Bosch, you will evolve.\n- Discover new directions:  At Bosch, you will find your place.\n- Balance your life:  At Bosch, your job matches your lifestyle.\n- Celebrate success:  At Bosch, we celebrate you.\n- Be yourself:  At Bosch, we value values.\n- Shape tomorrow:  At Bosch, you change lives.\nDo you want beneficial technologies being shaped your ideas? Whether in the areas of mobility solutions, consumer goods, industrial technology or energy and building technology - with us, you will have the chance to improve quality of life all across the globe. Welcome to Bosch.\n\nAs a part of the global research, our AI research in Pittsburgh focuses on Multimodal Foundation Models, AI-based Sensing, Driving assistance, agentic AI, and efficient GenAI. We develop scalable, intelligent, and trustworthy AI solutions for Bosch products and services in application areas such as advanced manufacturing, smart home and building solutions, advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS), robust AI systems, and AI-based simulators.\nOriginating from Bosch AI research in Pittsburgh, we are responsible for pushing the boundaries of multimodal foundation models and GenAI through key innovations to solve complex industry problems, and shape the future of Bosch products and services for both internal and external users. We work with internal partners of different Bosch business units to transfer our solutions into future products. We also actively collaborate with leading groups in academia and industry to promote research ideas and publish research findings in internationally renowned conferences and journals such as ICML, ICLR, ICRA, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, etc.)\n- Conduct research on multimodal foundation models, agentic AI, robustness and efficient GenAI to address academic and industrial challenges.\n- Work with an international team of experts to transfer and apply Bosch in-house AI innovations and 3rd-party solutions to Bosch AI products and services, building systems that can advance manufacturing, energy solutions, AI-based sensing, driving assistance, etc.\n- Stay abreast of the latest technological innovations and market trends by attending academic conferences, technical events, and seminars.\n- Offer expert insights to the management team in relevant technology sectors, aiding in strategic planning, R&D trajectory, and investment decisions.\nDocument and disseminate research findings through high-caliber publications and/or patent submissions.\n\nBasic Qualifications\n- Ph.D. in Computer Science or Engineering, or a related discipline or master’s degree with 3+ years industry experience (multimodal foundation model related) after graduation.\n- 4+ years of research experience or equivalent graduate research experience on multimodal foundation models, agentic AI, robust and efficient GenAI\n- In-depth experiences in foundation models, with work in at least two of the following areas: time-series data analysis, LLMs, VLMs/MMLMs, inference efficiency, deployment of large models, robustness\n- Proficiency in one or more programming languages commonly used in systems research (e.g., Python, C++) and hands on experience with AI libraries.\n- Publication record in top venues including ICML, ICLR, ICRA, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, etc.\n- Strong interpersonal, communication, and teamwork capabilities.\n\n \nPreferred Qualifications\n- Strong background in math, statistics, computational modeling\n- 3+ years experiences in industrial research\n- Hands-on experience in product development in the above-mentioned areas for consumer/enterprise markets.\n- Experience in leading R&D project & team dealing with international customers.\n- Leadership skills with excellent English communication & teamwork skills.\n\nEqual Opportunity Employer, including disability / veterans.\nPlease note that employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a drug screen and background check. Candidates who have been offered the position must pass both screenings before their start date. \nFor more information on our culture and benefits, please visit:\nCulture and Benefits | Bosch in the USA","description_html":"<p><strong>We Are Bosch.</strong></p><p>At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our areas of activity are every bit as diverse as our outstanding Bosch teams around the world. Their creativity is the key to innovation through connected living, mobility, or industry.</p><p>Let’s grow together, enjoy more, and inspire each other.&#xa0;<strong>Work #LikeABosch&#xa0;</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Reinvent yourself:&#xa0;</strong>At Bosch, you will evolve.</li><li><strong>Discover new directions:</strong>&#xa0;At Bosch, you will find your place.</li><li><strong>Balance your life:</strong>&#xa0;At Bosch, your job matches your lifestyle.</li><li><strong>Celebrate success:</strong>&#xa0;At Bosch, we celebrate you.</li><li><strong>Be yourself:</strong>&#xa0;At Bosch, we value values.</li><li><strong>Shape tomorrow:</strong>&#xa0;At Bosch, you change lives.</li></ul><p>Do you want beneficial technologies being shaped your ideas? Whether in the areas of mobility solutions, consumer goods, industrial technology or energy and building technology - with us, you will have the chance to improve quality of life all across the globe. Welcome to Bosch.</p>\n<p>As a part of the global research, our AI research in Pittsburgh focuses on Multimodal Foundation Models, AI-based Sensing, Driving assistance, agentic AI, and efficient GenAI. We develop scalable, intelligent, and trustworthy AI solutions for Bosch products and services in application areas such as advanced manufacturing, smart home and building solutions, advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS), robust AI systems, and AI-based simulators.</p><p>Originating from Bosch AI research in Pittsburgh, we are responsible for pushing the boundaries of multimodal foundation models and GenAI through key innovations to solve complex industry problems, and shape the future of Bosch products and services for both internal and external users. We work with internal partners of different Bosch business units to transfer our solutions into future products. We also actively collaborate with leading groups in academia and industry to promote research ideas and publish research findings in internationally renowned conferences and journals such as ICML, ICLR, ICRA, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, etc.)</p><ul><li>Conduct research on multimodal foundation models, agentic AI, robustness and efficient GenAI to address academic and industrial challenges.</li><li>Work with an international team of experts to transfer and apply Bosch in-house AI innovations and 3rd-party solutions to Bosch AI products and services, building systems that can advance manufacturing, energy solutions, AI-based sensing, driving assistance, etc.</li><li>Stay abreast of the latest technological innovations and market trends by attending academic conferences, technical events, and seminars.</li><li>Offer expert insights to the management team in relevant technology sectors, aiding in strategic planning, R&amp;D trajectory, and investment decisions.</li></ul><p>Document and disseminate research findings through high-caliber publications and/or patent submissions.</p>\n<p><strong>Basic Qualifications</strong></p><ul><li>Ph.D. in Computer Science or Engineering, or a related discipline or master’s degree with 3+ years industry experience (multimodal foundation model related) after graduation.</li><li>4+ years of research experience or equivalent graduate research experience on multimodal foundation models, agentic AI, robust and efficient GenAI</li><li>In-depth experiences in foundation models, with work in at least two of the following areas: time-series data analysis, LLMs, VLMs/MMLMs, inference efficiency, deployment of large models, robustness</li><li>Proficiency in one or more programming languages commonly used in systems research (e.g., Python, C++) and hands on experience with AI libraries.</li><li>Publication record in top venues including ICML, ICLR, ICRA, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, etc.</li><li>Strong interpersonal, communication, and teamwork capabilities.<br>\n&#xa0;</li></ul><p><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul><li>Strong background in math, statistics, computational modeling</li><li>3+ years experiences in industrial research</li><li>Hands-on experience in product development in the above-mentioned areas for consumer/enterprise markets.</li><li>Experience in leading R&amp;D project &amp; team dealing with international customers.</li><li>Leadership skills with excellent English communication &amp; teamwork skills.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability / veterans.</strong></p><p><strong><em>Please note that employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a drug screen and background check. Candidates who have been offered the position must pass both screenings before their start date.&#xa0;</em></strong></p><p>For more information on our culture and benefits, please visit:</p><p><a href=\"https://www.bosch.us/careers/why-bosch/culture-and-benefits/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Culture and Benefits | Bosch in the USA</a></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"experience_level":"Mid-Senior Level","industry":"Research","Contract type":"Unlimited","Tariff Area":"United States Local Grades","Legal Entity(acronym)":"RBUS","Working Location":"Pittsburgh, PA","Global Salary Level":"Experienced/ Middle Tariff","Direct Or Indirect":"Indirect","Working hours":"Full-time","Legal Entity":"Robert Bosch LLC","Division full name":"CR","Position type":"Professional","Country/Region":"United States","Brands":"Bosch Group","Working Country":"United States","Local Grade":"US_E3","Division":"CR"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["GenAI","Research Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","GenAI"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["research","robotics"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"smartrecruiters:boschgroup:744000144027727","source":{"type":"smartrecruiters","board":"BoschGroup","job_id":"744000144027727","source_url":"https://api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/BoschGroup/postings","response_hash":"99c346d6e230a2c71970e006cdc9511296121e8a3aeeb1fa59227da8a0a91a86","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Bosch","slug":"bosch","lists":["research","robotics"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Applied AI Engineer (f/m/div.)","canonical_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/BoschGroup/744000144027727-applied-ai-engineer-f-m-div-","apply_url":"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/BoschGroup/744000144027727-applied-ai-engineer-f-m-div-?oga=true","locations":[{"label":"Braga, , Portugal","city":"Braga","region":null,"country":"pt","remote":false,"hybrid":true}],"workplace_type":"hybrid","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"REF292955M","internal_job_id":"e064e6c5-c36b-4019-b6cc-6259540d8768","first_published_at":"2026-08-18T09:50:30.441Z","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"The Bosch Group has more than 400 000 employees around the world, present in 60 countries, and we are proud to impact people’s lives and to work towards a more sustainable future.\nBosch Car Multimedia, S.A. belongs to the Automotive Electronics division and is focused on making the vehicles our third living space. The company' success lies in its highly specialized and innovative team, and on the technological know-how which makes Bosch the leading supplier in the automotive market.\nAt the Bosch Research & Development Center in Braga, more than 350 engineers develop car multimedia solutions and the most innovative localization, perception and safety sensors that are helping to shape connected and autonomous mobility. From hardware to software to physics, we have all kinds of opportunities waiting for you.\nAt Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. Bosch is an employer that values diversity and equal opportunities. We welcome applications from people with disabilities and we can provide reasonable accommodations during the recruitment process and in the performance of professional activity. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential.\n\nAs a GenAI Engineer , you design, prototype, and implement AI agents that support engineering workflows across Bosch. You translate complex engineering use cases into intelligent, reliable, and compliant GenAI solutions that accelerate innovation.\nYour contribution to something big:\n- Designing and implementing GenAI agents that support engineering tasks such as requirements analysis, documentation assistance, test interpretation, and failure analysis.\n- Building AI pipelines using LLMs, embeddings, vector databases, and domain‑specific knowledge sources.\n- Integrating AI agents with engineering tools, databases, and repositories (e.g., PLM systems, test data platforms, document repositories).\n- Developing Retrieval‑Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines for structured and semi‑structured engineering data.\n- Ensuring agent reliability, traceability, and safe behavior in regulated engineering environments.\n- Collaborating with domain experts to evaluate usability, performance, and fit for purpose.\n- Documenting architectures, APIs, integration points, and operational guidelines.\n- Working closely with security and compliance teams to ensure responsible and compliant AI usage.\n\nWhat distinguishes you:  \nEducation:  Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or a comparable field.\nExperience:\n- Experience in GenAI development, agent orchestration, or AI‑assisted tooling.\n- Solid software engineering background (Python preferred; experience with APIs and microservices).\n- Familiarity with structured and semi‑structured data formats (JSON, PDFs, engineering documentation, etc.).\nKnow‑how:\n- Understanding of LLM integration patterns, embeddings, and vector stores.\n- Knowledge of agent frameworks (e.g., LangChain, LlamaIndex, OpenAI Agents, CrewAI, Swarm, MCP).\n- Nice to have: experience with MLOps, AI observability, evaluation frameworks, or model deployment.\n- Nice to have: familiarity with PLM systems, engineering workflows, or compliance standards in automotive/industrial environments.\nWorking Style & Methods:\n- Structured, reliable, and solution‑oriented working style.\n- Ability to collaborate with cross‑functional engineering teams.\n- Comfortable working in iterative, experimental environments.\nPersonality:\n- Curious, proactive, and eager to explore new technologies.\n- Strong communication skills and a collaborative mindset.\n- Open to learning and working with diverse teams and perspectives.\nLanguages:  Proficient in English.\n\nWork #LikeABosch includes: \n⚖️ Flexible work conditions\n🔀 Hybrid work system\n🌐 Exchange with colleagues around the world\n🛡️  Health insurance\n🧑‍⚕️  Medical office (psychology and general clinic) & Social Services Office on site\n📚 Training opportunities (p.e., technical training, foreign languages training) & certifications\n📈 Opportunities for career progression and continuous professional development\n💲 Access to great discounts in partnerships and Bosch products\n🏋️ Sports and health related activities\n💰 Flexible benefits platform\n🚉 Great access to public transports\n🚌 Free transport from Porto\n🅿️ Free parking lot\n🍽️ Canteen\n \nSuccess stories don´t just happen. They are made...\nMake it happen. We are looking forward to your application!","description_html":"<p>The Bosch Group has more than 400 000 employees around the world, present in 60 countries, and we are proud to impact people’s lives and to work towards a more sustainable future.</p><p>Bosch Car Multimedia, S.A. belongs to the Automotive Electronics division and is focused on making the vehicles our third living space. The company' success lies in its highly specialized and innovative team, and on the technological know-how which makes Bosch the leading supplier in the automotive market.</p><p>At the Bosch Research &amp; Development Center in Braga, more than 350 engineers develop car multimedia solutions and the most innovative localization, perception and safety sensors that are helping to shape connected and autonomous mobility. From hardware to software to physics, we have all kinds of opportunities waiting for you.</p><p>At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. Bosch is an employer that values diversity and equal opportunities. We welcome applications from people with disabilities and we can provide reasonable accommodations during the recruitment process and in the performance of professional activity. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential.</p>\n<p>As a <strong>GenAI Engineer</strong>, you design, prototype, and implement AI agents that support engineering workflows across Bosch. You translate complex engineering use cases into intelligent, reliable, and compliant GenAI solutions that accelerate innovation.</p><p><strong>Your contribution to something big:</strong></p><ul><li>Designing and implementing GenAI agents that support engineering tasks such as requirements analysis, documentation assistance, test interpretation, and failure analysis.</li><li>Building AI pipelines using LLMs, embeddings, vector databases, and domain‑specific knowledge sources.</li><li>Integrating AI agents with engineering tools, databases, and repositories (e.g., PLM systems, test data platforms, document repositories).</li><li>Developing Retrieval‑Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines for structured and semi‑structured engineering data.</li><li>Ensuring agent reliability, traceability, and safe behavior in regulated engineering environments.</li><li>Collaborating with domain experts to evaluate usability, performance, and fit for purpose.</li><li>Documenting architectures, APIs, integration points, and operational guidelines.</li><li>Working closely with security and compliance teams to ensure responsible and compliant AI usage.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>What distinguishes you:</strong>&#xa0;</p><p><strong>Education:&#xa0;</strong>Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or a comparable field.</p><p><strong>Experience:</strong></p><ul><li>Experience in GenAI development, agent orchestration, or AI‑assisted tooling.</li><li>Solid software engineering background (Python preferred; experience with APIs and microservices).</li><li>Familiarity with structured and semi‑structured data formats (JSON, PDFs, engineering documentation, etc.).</li></ul><p><strong>Know‑how:</strong></p><ul><li>Understanding of LLM integration patterns, embeddings, and vector stores.</li><li>Knowledge of agent frameworks (e.g., LangChain, LlamaIndex, OpenAI Agents, CrewAI, Swarm, MCP).</li><li>Nice to have: experience with MLOps, AI observability, evaluation frameworks, or model deployment.</li><li>Nice to have: familiarity with PLM systems, engineering workflows, or compliance standards in automotive/industrial environments.</li></ul><p><strong>Working Style &amp; Methods:</strong></p><ul><li>Structured, reliable, and solution‑oriented working style.</li><li>Ability to collaborate with cross‑functional engineering teams.</li><li>Comfortable working in iterative, experimental environments.</li></ul><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><ul><li>Curious, proactive, and eager to explore new technologies.</li><li>Strong communication skills and a collaborative mindset.</li><li>Open to learning and working with diverse teams and perspectives.</li></ul><p><strong>Languages:&#xa0;</strong>Proficient in English.</p>\n<p><strong>Work #LikeABosch includes:&#xa0;</strong></p><p>⚖️ Flexible work conditions</p><p>🔀 Hybrid work system</p><p>🌐 Exchange with colleagues around the world</p><p>🛡️&#xa0;&#xa0;Health insurance</p><p>🧑‍⚕️&#xa0;&#xa0;Medical office (psychology and general clinic) &amp;&#xa0;Social Services Office&#xa0;on site</p><p>📚 Training opportunities (p.e., technical training, foreign languages training) &amp; certifications</p><p>📈 Opportunities for career progression and continuous professional development</p><p>💲 Access to great discounts in partnerships and Bosch products</p><p>🏋️ Sports and health related activities</p><p>💰 Flexible benefits platform</p><p>🚉 Great access to public transports</p><p>🚌 Free transport from Porto</p><p>🅿️ Free parking lot</p><p>🍽️ Canteen</p><p>&#xa0;</p><p><strong>Success stories don´t just happen. They are made...</strong></p><p><strong>Make it happen. We are looking forward to your application!</strong></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"experience_level":"Associate","industry":"Computer Software","Contract type":"According to Arrangement","Tariff Area":"Portugal Local Grades","Legal Entity(acronym)":"RBPB","Working Location":"Braga","Global Salary Level":"Others","Direct Or Indirect":"Indirect","Working hours":"Full-time","Legal Entity":"Bosch Car Multimedia Portugal","Division full name":"Cross-Domain Computing Solutions","Position type":"Professional","Country/Region":"Portugal","Brands":"Bosch Group","Working Country":"Portugal","Local Grade":"PT_Tariff","Division":"XC"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["AI Engineer","Applied AI"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Applied"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["research","robotics"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:brex:8523177002","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"brex","job_id":"8523177002","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/brex/jobs","response_hash":"9cc2aa7eac0e0e63b98f3e86c73127e68d2fd87611475e84b16c25c188d13219","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Brex","slug":"brex","lists":["finance-ai","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer, Forward Deployed Agent Builder","canonical_url":"https://www.brex.com/careers/8523177002?gh_jid=8523177002","apply_url":"https://www.brex.com/careers/8523177002?gh_jid=8523177002","locations":[{"label":"New York, New York, United States"},{"label":"United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"1792","internal_job_id":6404209002,"first_published_at":"2026-04-24T12:54:43-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-06-10T13:59:16-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Why join us\n\nBrex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world's best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.\n\nWorking at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.\n\nEngineering at Brex\n\nEngineering at Brex is about building systems that scale with speed and intention. Our teams span Software, Data, Security, and IT, and operate with high autonomy and deep collaboration. We tackle hard technical problems, own our outcomes, and push for excellence at every level — from architecture to deployment. It’s an environment where engineering is a craft, and builders become leaders.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nWe're building AI agents to automate and augment internal functions at Brex, and we're looking for a hands-on builder to help us do it. You'll embed with teams across the company to understand how they actually work, then design, build, and ship agents that deliver real outcomes. You'll work on top of existing models and frameworks, wiring together tools, MCPs, and internal systems into agentic workflows. This is a technical role where you'll spend most of your time building, shipping, and iterating alongside the people whose work you're automating.\n\nWhere you’ll work\n\nThis role will be based in our New York City office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- Embed with partner teams to deeply understand workflows, including shadowing and learning different job functions.\n\n- Scope, design, and deploy agents that take over real workflows across internal orgs.\n\n- Integrate agents with internal systems, APIs, and data sources.\n\n- Define evaluation frameworks, success metrics, and feedback loops to measure and improve agent performance.\n\n- Build shared tooling and contribute to playbooks that accelerate deployments, while owning reliability, adoption, and business impact.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- 4+ years in engineering, technical product/program management, applied AI, or a similar technical role, with a track record of shipping AI/automation systems to production.\n\n- Hands-on experience building with LLMs, agent frameworks, and tool-use patterns (e.g., MCP, function calling, RAG) across the full stack (data, APIs, orchestration, product).\n\n- Experience designing and optimizing SQL and/or NoSQL databases, including data modeling, query performance tuning, and schema design.\n\n- Strong ability to decompose human workflows into scalable, agentic systems, grounded in a deep curiosity for how people work.\n\n- High ownership and cross-functional influence, with the ability to quickly build trust across teams and seniority levels.\n\nBonus points\n\n- Experience automating back-office functions rather than just customer-facing AI features.\n\n- Experience with OpenClaw, Hermes, or other general-purpose agent harnesses.\n\nCompensation:\n\nThe expected salary range for this role is $152,000 - $240,000. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.\nPlease be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a brex.com domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p><strong>Why join us</strong></p>\n<p>Brex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world's best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.</p>\n<p>Working at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.</p></div><p><strong>Engineering at Brex</strong></p>\n<p>Engineering at Brex is about building systems that scale with speed and intention. Our teams span Software, Data, Security, and IT, and operate with high autonomy and deep collaboration. We tackle hard technical problems, own our outcomes, and push for excellence at every level — from architecture to deployment. It’s an environment where engineering is a craft, and builders become leaders.</p>\n<p><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p>\n<p>We're building AI agents to automate and augment internal functions at Brex, and we're looking for a hands-on builder to help us do it. You'll embed with teams across the company to understand how they actually work, then design, build, and ship agents that deliver real outcomes. You'll work on top of existing models and frameworks, wiring together tools, MCPs, and internal systems into agentic workflows. This is a technical role where you'll spend most of your time building, shipping, and iterating alongside the people whose work you're automating.</p>\n<p><strong>Where you’ll work</strong></p>\n<p>This role will be based in our New York City office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!</p>\n<p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Embed with partner teams to deeply understand workflows, including shadowing and learning different job functions.</li>\n<li>Scope, design, and deploy agents that take over real workflows across internal orgs.</li>\n<li>Integrate agents with internal systems, APIs, and data sources.</li>\n<li>Define evaluation frameworks, success metrics, and feedback loops to measure and improve agent performance.</li>\n<li>Build shared tooling and contribute to playbooks that accelerate deployments, while owning reliability, adoption, and business impact.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>4+ years in engineering, technical product/program management, applied AI, or a similar technical role, with a track record of shipping AI/automation systems to production.</li>\n<li>Hands-on experience building with LLMs, agent frameworks, and tool-use patterns (e.g., MCP, function calling, RAG) across the full stack (data, APIs, orchestration, product).</li>\n<li>Experience designing and optimizing SQL and/or NoSQL databases, including data modeling, query performance tuning, and schema design.</li>\n<li>Strong ability to decompose human workflows into scalable, agentic systems, grounded in a deep curiosity for how people work.</li>\n<li>High ownership and cross-functional influence, with the ability to quickly build trust across teams and seniority levels.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bonus points</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience automating back-office functions rather than just customer-facing AI features.</li>\n<li>Experience with OpenClaw, Hermes, or other general-purpose agent harnesses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compensation:</strong></p>\n<p>The expected salary range for this role is $152,000 - $240,000. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><em>Please be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"http://brex.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://brex.com\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">brex.com</a>&nbsp;domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.</em></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Job Post Department":"Engineering"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer","Forward Deployed"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","Agent"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["finance-ai","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:brex:8523203002","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"brex","job_id":"8523203002","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/brex/jobs","response_hash":"8b181f2c99f3b2f31ca403f5b9652d65a84a167c4955eba7c4135d83aa976221","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Brex","slug":"brex","lists":["finance-ai","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer, Forward Deployed Agent Builder","canonical_url":"https://www.brex.com/careers/8523203002?gh_jid=8523203002","apply_url":"https://www.brex.com/careers/8523203002?gh_jid=8523203002","locations":[{"label":"San Francisco, California, United States"},{"label":"United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"1792","internal_job_id":6404209002,"first_published_at":"2026-04-27T15:29:45-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-06-10T13:59:16-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Why join us\n\nBrex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world's best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.\n\nWorking at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.\n\nEngineering at Brex\n\nEngineering at Brex is about building systems that scale with speed and intention. Our teams span Software, Data, Security, and IT, and operate with high autonomy and deep collaboration. We tackle hard technical problems, own our outcomes, and push for excellence at every level — from architecture to deployment. It’s an environment where engineering is a craft, and builders become leaders.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nWe're building AI agents to automate and augment internal functions at Brex, and we're looking for a hands-on builder to help us do it. You'll embed with teams across the company to understand how they actually work, then design, build, and ship agents that deliver real outcomes. You'll work on top of existing models and frameworks, wiring together tools, MCPs, and internal systems into agentic workflows. This is a technical role where you'll spend most of your time building, shipping, and iterating alongside the people whose work you're automating.\n\nWhere you’ll work\n\nThis role will be based in our San Francisco office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- Embed with partner teams to deeply understand workflows, including shadowing and learning different job functions.\n\n- Scope, design, and deploy agents that take over real workflows across internal orgs.\n\n- Integrate agents with internal systems, APIs, and data sources.\n\n- Define evaluation frameworks, success metrics, and feedback loops to measure and improve agent performance.\n\n- Build shared tooling and contribute to playbooks that accelerate deployments, while owning reliability, adoption, and business impact.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- 4+ years in engineering, technical product/program management, applied AI, or a similar technical role, with a track record of shipping AI/automation systems to production.\n\n- Hands-on experience building with LLMs, agent frameworks, and tool-use patterns (e.g., MCP, function calling, RAG) across the full stack (data, APIs, orchestration, product).\n\n- Experience designing and optimizing SQL and/or NoSQL databases, including data modeling, query performance tuning, and schema design.\n\n- Strong ability to decompose human workflows into scalable, agentic systems, grounded in a deep curiosity for how people work.\n\n- High ownership and cross-functional influence, with the ability to quickly build trust across teams and seniority levels.\n\nBonus points\n\n- Experience automating back-office functions rather than just customer-facing AI features.\n\n- Experience with OpenClaw, Hermes, or other general-purpose agent harnesses.\n\nCompensation:\n\nThe expected salary range for this role is $152,000 - $240,000. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.\nPlease be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a brex.com domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p><strong>Why join us</strong></p>\n<p>Brex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world's best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.</p>\n<p>Working at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.</p></div><p><strong>Engineering at Brex</strong></p>\n<p>Engineering at Brex is about building systems that scale with speed and intention. Our teams span Software, Data, Security, and IT, and operate with high autonomy and deep collaboration. We tackle hard technical problems, own our outcomes, and push for excellence at every level — from architecture to deployment. It’s an environment where engineering is a craft, and builders become leaders.</p>\n<p><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p>\n<p>We're building AI agents to automate and augment internal functions at Brex, and we're looking for a hands-on builder to help us do it. You'll embed with teams across the company to understand how they actually work, then design, build, and ship agents that deliver real outcomes. You'll work on top of existing models and frameworks, wiring together tools, MCPs, and internal systems into agentic workflows. This is a technical role where you'll spend most of your time building, shipping, and iterating alongside the people whose work you're automating.</p>\n<p><strong>Where you’ll work</strong></p>\n<p>This role will be based in our San Francisco office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!</p>\n<p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Embed with partner teams to deeply understand workflows, including shadowing and learning different job functions.</li>\n<li>Scope, design, and deploy agents that take over real workflows across internal orgs.</li>\n<li>Integrate agents with internal systems, APIs, and data sources.</li>\n<li>Define evaluation frameworks, success metrics, and feedback loops to measure and improve agent performance.</li>\n<li>Build shared tooling and contribute to playbooks that accelerate deployments, while owning reliability, adoption, and business impact.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>4+ years in engineering, technical product/program management, applied AI, or a similar technical role, with a track record of shipping AI/automation systems to production.</li>\n<li>Hands-on experience building with LLMs, agent frameworks, and tool-use patterns (e.g., MCP, function calling, RAG) across the full stack (data, APIs, orchestration, product).</li>\n<li>Experience designing and optimizing SQL and/or NoSQL databases, including data modeling, query performance tuning, and schema design.</li>\n<li>Strong ability to decompose human workflows into scalable, agentic systems, grounded in a deep curiosity for how people work.</li>\n<li>High ownership and cross-functional influence, with the ability to quickly build trust across teams and seniority levels.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bonus points</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience automating back-office functions rather than just customer-facing AI features.</li>\n<li>Experience with OpenClaw, Hermes, or other general-purpose agent harnesses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compensation:</strong></p>\n<p>The expected salary range for this role is $152,000 - $240,000. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><em>Please be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"http://brex.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://brex.com\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">brex.com</a>&nbsp;domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.</em></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Job Post Department":"Engineering"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer","Forward Deployed"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","Agent"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["finance-ai","ai-ml"]}}
