nities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d AI engineer, you know that AI systems are critical to understanding and processing massive datasets in an organization. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support optimizing organizational efficiency. As an AI Developer on our Air Power team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.   </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying cutting-edge Agentic frameworks. You’ll be part of a large community of AI professionals across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and product owners to deliver world-class solutions to transform how the Air Force manages its day-to-day business. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of Agentic Frameworks.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> building production-grade <span>sof</span>tware in Python, TypeScript, or Java with APIs and data services, including FastAPI, Flask, REST, GraphQL, or SQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing and deploying AI-enabled applications such as LLMs, RAG, and agentic workflows to solve mission problems</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> design event-driven integrations and workflow automation such as asynchronous messaging or audit logging to move from insight to action</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> implement MLOps or DevSecOps practices such as CI<span>/</span>CD, containerization, automated testing, or model evaluation</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in Mathematics, Computer Science, <span>Sof</span>tware Engineering, or Data Science</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with geospatial or 3D data, including point clouds, LiDAR, or photogram<span>met</span>ry, or digital-twin or facility and asset data models</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating sensor streams or IoT tele<span>met</span>ry and edge-to-cloud data flows such as Kafka, NATS, RabbitMQ, or <span>equivalent</span> for asset monitoring and situational awareness</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> deploying <span>sof</span>tware and data or ML pipelines in disconnected, air-gapped, or classified environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with cross-domain data handling constraints</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with RMF or STIG-aligned delivery</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI-assisted <span>sof</span>tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns to increase delivery velocity responsibly</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 11 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/AI-Developer_R0245641","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/AI-Developer_R0245641","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"65415d2fbf6147ec02472269223b3525d6bbd24a514dd99283e77e3c6c701b06","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/AI-Developer_R0245641","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/AI-Developer_R0245641","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"},{"label":"Fort Meade, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245641","internal_job_id":"fe4132e52a921001631db2d321fe0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-29","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI Developer The Opportunity:\nAs an experience d AI engineer, you know that AI systems are critical to understanding and processing massive datasets in an organization. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support optimizing organizational efficiency. As an AI Developer on our Air Power team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.\n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying cutting-edge Agentic frameworks. You’ll be part of a large community of AI professionals across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and product owners to deliver world-class solutions to transform how the Air Force manages its day-to-day business. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of Agentic Frameworks.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience building production-grade sof tware in Python, TypeScript, or Java with APIs and data services, including FastAPI, Flask, REST, GraphQL, or SQL\n\n- Experience developing and deploying AI-enabled applications such as LLMs, RAG, and agentic workflows to solve mission problems\n\n- Experience building secure data foundations on enterprise cloud platforms such as AWS, governed ingest and file exchange, data catalog and met adata, and data mesh-style data products to enable reuse across teams and bases\n\n- Ability to design event-driven integrations and workflow automation such as asynchronous messaging or audit logging to move from insight to action\n\n- Ability to implement MLOps or DevSecOps practices such as CI / CD, containerization, automated testing, or model evaluation\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience working with geospatial or 3D data, including point clouds, LiDAR, or photogram met ry, or digital-twin or facility and asset data models\n\n- Experience integrating sensor streams or IoT tele met ry and edge-to-cloud data flows such as Kafka, NATS, RabbitMQ, or equivalent for asset monitoring and situational awareness\n\n- Experience deploying sof tware and data or ML pipelines in disconnected, air-gapped, or classified environments\n\n- Experience with cross-domain data handling constraints\n\n- Experience with RMF or STIG-aligned delivery\n\n- Experience with AI-assisted sof tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns to increase delivery velocity responsibly\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d AI engineer, you know that AI systems are critical to understanding and processing massive datasets in an organization. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support optimizing organizational efficiency. As an AI Developer on our Air Power team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying cutting-edge Agentic frameworks. You’ll be part of a large community of AI professionals across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and product owners to deliver world-class solutions to transform how the Air Force manages its day-to-day business. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of Agentic Frameworks.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> building production-grade <span>sof</span>tware in Python, TypeScript, or Java with APIs and data services, including FastAPI, Flask, REST, GraphQL, or SQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing and deploying AI-enabled applications such as LLMs, RAG, and agentic workflows to solve mission problems</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building secure data foundations on enterprise cloud platforms such as AWS, governed ingest and file exchange, data catalog and <span>met</span>adata, and data mesh-style data products to enable reuse across teams and bases</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> design event-driven integrations and workflow automation such as asynchronous messaging or audit logging to move from insight to action</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> implement MLOps or DevSecOps practices such as CI<span>/</span>CD, containerization, automated testing, or model evaluation</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with geospatial or 3D data, including point clouds, LiDAR, or photogram<span>met</span>ry, or digital-twin or facility and asset data models</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating sensor streams or IoT tele<span>met</span>ry and edge-to-cloud data flows such as Kafka, NATS, RabbitMQ, or <span>equivalent</span> for asset monitoring and situational awareness</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> deploying <span>sof</span>tware and data or ML pipelines in disconnected, air-gapped, or classified environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with cross-domain data handling constraints</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with RMF or STIG-aligned delivery</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI-assisted <span>sof</span>tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns to increase delivery velocity responsibly</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 26 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0230233","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0230233","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"49061b91db776165cf1ca2b1c8e2bd67da9544b354d6ceb27db1e3e16620bbdf","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0230233","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0230233","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0230233","internal_job_id":"780f9668fae11001628dcedce5740000","first_published_at":"2026-06-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an artificial intelligence (AI) sof tware engineer, you know that good sof tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation—we’re looking for a sof tware engineer like you to create AI and machine learning solutions that help solve the world's toughest problems.\n\nOn our team, you’ll create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nReady to transform systems for the better with AI technology?\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- 4+ years of experience building production-grade applications using languages, including Python, Rus t, Go, Scala, or Java\n\n- 2+ years of experience building or maintaining production-grade RESTful APIs or sof tware interfaces\n\n- 1+ years of experience designing, configuring, and implementing sof tware systems in production environments \n\n- Experience with CI / CD tools, including GitLab CI or Jenkins, and source control systems, including Git\n\n- Experience working with Agentic AI solutions\n\n- Experience with Linux systems, networking, and containerization, including Docker or Podman\n\n- Knowledge of federal cybersecurity best practices and standards, secure coding, and compliance requirements\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in a CS or Engineering field and 4+ years of experience with sof tware engineering, or 9+ years of experience with sof tware engineering in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with AWS services and emulation environments, including LocalStack\n\n- Experience with secure on-prem deployments leveraging hypervisors, including ESXi\n\n- Experience with Ansible for configuration management and infrastructure automation\n\n- Experience integrating with SIEMs, firewalls, or endpoint protection systems\n\n- Knowledge of orchestration tools such as Kubernetes, including on-prem or air-gapped\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Security+, Linux+, or DevOps related Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b><br />As an artificial intelligence (AI) <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know that good <span>sof</span>tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation—we’re looking for a <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to create AI and machine learning solutions that help solve the world&#39;s toughest problems.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Ready to transform systems for the better with AI technology?</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>4&#43; years of experience building production-grade applications using languages, including Python, <span>Rus</span>t, Go, Scala, or Java</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience building or maintaining production-grade RESTful APIs or <span>sof</span>tware interfaces</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience designing, configuring, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware systems in production environments </p></li><li><p>Experience with CI<span>/</span>CD tools, including GitLab CI or Jenkins, and source control systems, including Git</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Agentic AI solutions</p></li><li><p>Experience with Linux systems, networking, and containerization, including Docker or Podman</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of federal cybersecurity best practices and standards, secure coding, and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in a CS or Engineering field and 4&#43; years of experience with <span>sof</span>tware engineering, or 9&#43; years of experience with <span>sof</span>tware engineering in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with AWS services and emulation environments, including LocalStack</p></li><li><p>Experience with secure on-prem deployments leveraging hypervisors, including ESXi</p></li><li><p>Experience with Ansible for configuration management and infrastructure automation</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating with SIEMs, firewalls, or endpoint protection systems</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of orchestration tools such as Kubernetes, including on-prem or air-gapped</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Security&#43;, Linux&#43;, or DevOps <span>related</span> Certification</p></li></ul><p><br /><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","AI"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0247491","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0247491","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7195440c9035e54119d70c2945ff06db3f067ea313e38e2c868aa6d0b7052d4c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0247491","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/AI-Software-Engineer_R0247491","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247491","internal_job_id":"71f6309939971001ab0df5ebd3440000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an artificial intelligence (AI)   sof tware engineer, you know that good   sof tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation—we’re looking for a   sof tware engineer like you to create AI and machine learning solutions that help solve the world's toughest problems.\n\nOn our team, you’ll create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nReady to transform systems for the better with AI technology?\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.   \n\nYou Have:  \n- 4+ years of experience writing production-grade applications in a programming language such as Python, Javascript, Rust, or Go\n\n- 2+ years of experience in a frontend framework such as React or Angular\n\n- 1+ years of experience building or maintaining RESTful APIs or software interfaces\n\n- 1+ years of experience designing, configuring, and implementing software systems in production environments \n\n- Experience with CI/CD tools, including GitLab CI or Jenkins, and source control systems, including Git\n\n- Experience working with Agentic AI solutions\n\n- Experience with Linux systems, networking, and containerization, including Docker or Podman\n\n- Knowledge of federal cybersecurity best practices and standards, secure coding, and compliance requirements\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in a CS or Engineering field and 4+ years of experience with software engineering, or 6+ years of experience with software engineering in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with AWS services and emulation environments, including LocalStack\n\n- Experience with secure on-prem deployments leveraging hypervisors, including ESXi\n\n- Experience integrating with SIEMs, firewalls, or endpoint protection systems\n\n- Knowledge of orchestration tools such as Kubernetes, including on-prem or air-gapped\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Security+, Linux+, Kubernetes CKAD, AWS Solutions Architect, or a related Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b><br />As an artificial intelligence (AI)<span> </span><span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know that good<span> </span><span>sof</span>tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation—we’re looking for a<span> </span><span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to create AI and machine learning solutions that help solve the world&#39;s toughest problems.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Ready to transform systems for the better with AI technology?</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. <span class=\"emphasis\"> </span></p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p>4&#43; years of experience writing production-grade applications in a programming language such as Python, Javascript, Rust, or Go</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in a frontend framework such as React or Angular</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience building or maintaining RESTful APIs or software interfaces</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience designing, configuring, and implementing software systems in production environments </p></li><li><p>Experience with CI/CD tools, including GitLab CI or Jenkins, and source control systems, including Git</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Agentic AI solutions</p></li><li><p>Experience with Linux systems, networking, and containerization, including Docker or Podman</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of federal cybersecurity best practices and standards, secure coding, and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in a CS or Engineering field and 4&#43; years of experience with software engineering, or 6&#43; years of experience with software engineering in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with AWS services and emulation environments, including LocalStack</p></li><li><p>Experience with secure on-prem deployments leveraging hypervisors, including ESXi</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating with SIEMs, firewalls, or endpoint protection systems</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of orchestration tools such as Kubernetes, including on-prem or air-gapped</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Security&#43;, Linux&#43;, Kubernetes CKAD, AWS Solutions Architect, or a related Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer","AI"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-Solution-Developer_R0229078","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-Solution-Developer_R0229078","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3e6456d258ac8e242bcbabbc44cfdc92d927d1cd1281f4f99c5356ffbdd615cd","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI Solution Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-Solution-Developer_R0229078","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-Solution-Developer_R0229078","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0229078","internal_job_id":"c305361aec8a1000c7f5e11bb3c60000","first_published_at":"2026-07-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI Solution Developer Key Role:\nDesigns and implements effective AI solution architecture or strategy utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and methods to address clients' business problems and needs, while complying with the organization’s strategies and business goals, and key ethical considerations. Applies advanced consulting, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develops innovative solutions to complex problems. Works without considerable direction. Mentors and may supervise team members.\n\nBasic Qualifications:\n- 6+ years of experience implementing enterprise IT systems, applications, and infrastructure\n\n- 4+ years of experience in AI and Data Science using Python programming and big data technologies, including Hive, Q, Bedrock, PySpark, Synapse, or Databricks\n\n- Experience with the Amazon AI product tool suite - Sage Maker studio, as well as Bedrock\n\n- Experience in architecting and implementing a highly available, scalable, and resilient enterprise cloud environment\n\n- Experience leading architecture, platform engineering, and development teams on enterprise cloud engagements\n\n- Experience in training LLMs\n\n- Knowledge of Big Data solutions and data migration technologies, and processes \n\n- Ability to deploy a production application to an AWS cloud environment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph \n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nAdditional Qualifications:\n- Experience providing technical guidance to architects and engineers\n\n- Experience working in GCP or Microsoft Azure\n\n- Knowledge of security and compliance requirements for cloud-based solutions, network architecture, and security principles\n\n- Security, Cloud, or Software Development Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI Solution Developer<p><b>Key Role:</b></p><p>Designs and implements effective AI solution architecture or strategy utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and methods to address clients&#39; business problems and needs, while complying with the organization’s strategies and business goals, and key ethical considerations. Applies advanced consulting, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develops innovative solutions to complex problems. Works without considerable direction. Mentors and may supervise team members.</p><p></p><p><b>Basic Qualifications:</b></p><ul><li><p>6&#43; years of experience implementing enterprise IT systems, applications, and infrastructure</p></li><li><p>4&#43; years of experience in AI and Data Science using Python programming and big data technologies, including Hive, Q, Bedrock, PySpark, Synapse, or Databricks</p></li><li><p>Experience with the Amazon AI product tool suite - Sage Maker studio, as well as Bedrock</p></li><li><p>Experience in architecting and implementing a highly available, scalable, and resilient enterprise cloud environment</p></li><li><p>Experience leading architecture, platform engineering, and development teams on enterprise cloud engagements</p></li><li><p>Experience in training LLMs</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Big Data solutions and data migration technologies, and processes </p></li><li><p>Ability to deploy a production application to an AWS cloud environment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Additional Qualifications:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience providing technical guidance to architects and engineers</p></li><li><p>Experience working in GCP or Microsoft Azure</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of security and compliance requirements for cloud-based solutions, network architecture, and security principles</p></li><li><p>Security, Cloud, or Software Development Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0245425","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0245425","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4731d08c8d797cea834241be62184a61928d98e4557ff8f979f77541f3ed3180","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0245425","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0245425","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245425","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d01000b4b06f42aa170000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity:\nData scientists and intelligence analysts rely on multi‑step workflows that are time‑sensitive, detail‑rich, and critical to national security. As an AI/ML Engineer, you will work directly with mission users to capture these workflows, document operational decision points, and translate them into effective AI‑enabled capabilities.\n\nYou will design and implement solutions that may include LLM‑powered workflows, agent‑based automation, or hybrid approaches depending on mission needs. Your work will streamline analytical tasks, improve data accessibility, and support rapid, informed decision‑making in high‑tempo environments.\n\nYou’ll collaborate with operators, analysts, developers, and mission leadership to ensure solutions integrate cleanly with existing systems, perform reliably in production, and adhere to the security and governance expectations of classified environments.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience capturing user workflows and translating them into structured process maps, automation requirements, or executable logic\n\n- Experience designing or implementing LLM‑based or agentic workflows, including multi‑step reasoning, tool integrations, and orchestration\n\n- Experience integrating AI systems with APIs, enterprise data stores, or mission platforms\n\n- Experience with programming languages such as Python\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor’s degree and 5+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering, data science, or software engineering within cyber, intelligence, or national security environments, Master's degree and 3+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering, data science, or software engineering within cyber, intelligence, or national security environments, or 10+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering, data science, or software engineering within cyber, intelligence, or national security environments in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience engineering AI capabilities in on‑premise or multi‑classification environments\n\n- Experience with ML frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, vLLM, or llama.cpp\n\n- Experience with AWS or Azure, including work in restricted or classified environments\n\n- Experience with AI or LLM development frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, PydanticAI, or CrewAI\n\n- Experience with cyber or intelligence workflows, operational data types, or mission‑oriented analytical processes\n\n- Master’s degree in AI, ML, Data Science, Cybersecurity, or Engineering\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b><br />Data scientists and intelligence analysts rely on multi‑step workflows that are time‑sensitive, detail‑rich, and critical to national security. As an AI/ML Engineer, you will work directly with mission users to capture these workflows, document operational decision points, and translate them into effective AI‑enabled capabilities.</p><p></p><p>You will design and implement solutions that may include LLM‑powered workflows, agent‑based automation, or <span>hybrid</span> approaches depending on mission needs. Your work will streamline analytical tasks, improve data accessibility, and support rapid, informed decision‑making in high‑tempo environments.</p><p></p><p>You’ll collaborate with operators, analysts, developers, and mission leadership to ensure solutions integrate cleanly with existing systems, perform reliably in production, and adhere to the security and governance expectations of classified environments.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> capturing user workflows and translating them into structured process maps, automation requirements, or executable logic</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing or implementing LLM‑based or agentic workflows, including multi‑step reasoning, tool integrations, and orchestration</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating AI systems with APIs, enterprise data stores, or mission platforms</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with programming languages such as Python</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree and 5&#43; years of experience in AI/ML engineering, data science, or software engineering within cyber, intelligence, or national security environments, Master&#39;s degree and 3&#43; years of experience in AI/ML engineering, data science, or software engineering within cyber, intelligence, or national security environments, or 10&#43; years of experience in AI/ML engineering, data science, or software engineering within cyber, intelligence, or national security environments in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> engineering AI capabilities in on‑premise or multi‑classification environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with ML frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, vLLM, or llama.cpp</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AWS or Azure, including work in restricted or classified environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI or LLM development frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, PydanticAI, or CrewAI</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with cyber or intelligence workflows, operational data types, or mission‑oriented analytical processes</p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span> in AI, ML, Data Science, Cybersecurity, or Engineering</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Dayton-OH/AI-ML-Engineer_R0246722-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Dayton-OH/AI-ML-Engineer_R0246722-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"ff2a2bd7431141acf220afb50f513fbb08878cea2d104fe77406b08428a6f710","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/AI-ML-Engineer_R0246722-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/AI-ML-Engineer_R0246722-1","locations":[{"label":"Dayton, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246722","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a1000cc3fc63962c70001","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experienced engineer, you know that building reliable and scalable AI systems requires far more than just model development—it demands strong software engineering practices, automation, and seamless integration across complex environments. Your ability to design and maintain robust AI and ML pipelines, automate workflows, and integrate AI capabilities into production systems makes you an essential part of delivering resilient, mission-focused solutions. We need your technical expertise and problem‑solving mindset to support the development and operationalization of AI capabilities that directly enhance mission performance and decision‑making. As an AI and ML engineer on our national security team, you’ll build, test, deploy, and operate software end‑to‑end AI pipelines that keep mission systems running securely and efficiently. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience with data science, ML engineering, software engineering, data research, or data analytics \n\n- Experience building and deploying AI and ML solutions into production \n\n- Experience implementing document RAG and Graph RAG solutions \n\n- Experience building applications leveraging LLMs for automation tasks such as text summarization or customized reports, including with multi-agent solutions \n\n- Experience adapting and fine-tuning open-source models \n\n- Experience with object-oriented Python programming and best practices \n\n- Experience with containerization technology such as Docker, Helm, or Kubernetes \n\n- Ability to create solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree and 3+ years of experience with AI and ML, or 6+ years of experience with AI and ML in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with databases such as Qdrant, Milvus, or Elasticsearch \n\n- Experience with Elasticsearch index \n\n- Experience with relational databases such as Postgres \n\n- Experience with on-prem compute \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\nClearance : \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As an experienced engineer, you know that building reliable and scalable AI systems requires far more than just model development—it demands strong software engineering practices, automation, and seamless integration across complex environments. Your ability to design and maintain robust AI and ML pipelines, automate workflows, and integrate AI capabilities into production systems makes you an essential part of delivering resilient, mission-focused solutions. We need your technical expertise and problem‑solving mindset to support the development and operationalization of AI capabilities that directly enhance mission performance and decision‑making. As an AI and ML engineer on our national security team, you’ll build, test, deploy, and operate software end‑to‑end AI pipelines that keep mission systems running securely and efficiently. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with data science, ML engineering, software engineering, data research, or data analytics </p></li><li><p>Experience building and deploying AI and ML solutions into production </p></li><li><p>Experience implementing document RAG and Graph RAG solutions </p></li><li><p>Experience building applications leveraging LLMs for automation tasks such as text summarization or customized reports, including with multi-agent solutions </p></li><li><p>Experience adapting and fine-tuning open-source models </p></li><li><p>Experience with object-oriented Python programming and best practices </p></li><li><p>Experience with containerization technology such as Docker, Helm, or Kubernetes </p></li><li><p>Ability to create solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree and 3&#43; years of experience with AI and ML, or 6&#43; years of experience with AI and ML in<span> lieu of a degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with databases such as Qdrant, Milvus, or Elasticsearch </p></li><li><p>Experience with Elasticsearch index </p></li><li><p>Experience with relational databases such as Postgres </p></li><li><p>Experience with on-prem compute </p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance</b>: </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Meade-MD/AI-ML-Engineer_R0241767","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Meade-MD/AI-ML-Engineer_R0241767","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"12174041c0ee81418aed5e5719b91eb95643966b6c8c19798841d7bcad9a5fcf","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/AI-ML-Engineer_R0241767","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/AI-ML-Engineer_R0241767","locations":[{"label":"Fort Meade, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241767","internal_job_id":"8d303c4688181001a1b03386f8c90000","first_published_at":"2026-07-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experienced engineer, you know that building reliable and scalable AI systems requires far more than just model development—it demands strong software engineering practices, automation, and seamless integration across complex environments. Your ability to design and   maintain   robust AI/ML pipelines, automate workflows, and integrate AI capabilities into production systems makes you an essential part of delivering resilient, mission-focused solutions. We need your technical   expertise   and problem‑solving mindset to support the development and operationalization of AI capabilities that directly enhance mission performance and decision‑making. As an AI and ML engineer on our national security team,   you’ll   build, test, deploy, and   operate  software end ‑to‑end AI pipelines that keep mission systems running securely and efficiently.  \n\nIn this role,   you’ll   guide the development of mission‑critical AI solutions by building reproducible pipelines, applying automation best practices, and introducing emerging tools that enhance performance and reliability.   You’ll   collaborate with a cross‑functional team of AI Model Engineers, Data Engineers, Cloud Architects, and ISSEs to align AI and ML workflows with infrastructure and security requirements, ensuring seamless integration into production and mission systems.   You’ll   contribute to solutions that   optimize   data flow, automate operational workflows, ensure monitoring and observability, and support resilient mission execution across hybrid compute environments. Your engineering skills and experience with modern AI and ML frameworks will help clients navigate evolving toolchains, deployment patterns, and operational considerations for scalable AI systems.  \n\nWork with us to build reliable AI pipelines, modernize mission workflows, and define AI and ML strategy.\n \n\nJoin us. The world   can’t   wait.   \n\nYou Have:      \n\n- 6+ years of experience with software engineering\n\n- Experience with Python\n\n- Experience developing and   maintaining   AI and ML pipelines for model training, validation, and deployment\n\n- Experience integrating AI and ML capabilities into production systems and mission workflows\n\n- Experience implementing monitoring and observability solutions for model performance, resource   utilization , and system health\n\n- Knowledge of hybrid compute environments such as cloud and on‑prem\n\n- Ability to automate workflows and build reproducible, scalable, and efficient ML and AI systems\n\n- Ability to collaborate with cross‑functional teams, such as AI Model Engineers, Data Engineers, Cloud Architects, or ISSE, to align workflows with infrastructure and security requirement\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS diploma or GED and 6+ years of experience with­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­ software engineering or AI system development, or Bachelor’s degree and 4+ years of experience with software engineering or AI system development\n\nNice If You Have:    \n\n- 10+ years of experience with software engineering\n\n- Experience with Rust for systems‑level or high‑performance components\n\n- Experience evaluating or adopting emerging AI and ML frameworks, libraries, or toolchains\n\n- Experience with containerization or orchestration technologies such as Docker or Kubernetes\n\n- Experience in cloud services relevant to AI and ML such as AWS   or   Azure\n\n- Knowledge of CI/CD for ML pipelines or infrastructure‑as‑code such as Terraform or CloudFormation\n\n- Knowledge of ML or MLOps   orchestration tools such as, Airflow, Kubeflow,  or MLflow\n\n- Knowledge of distributed training, GPU optimization, or advanced model deployment patterns  \n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\n \n\nClearance:    \n\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><div><p><span><span>As an experienced engineer, you know that building reliable and scalable AI systems requires far more than just model development—it demands strong software engineering practices, automation, and seamless integration across complex environments. Your ability to design and<span> </span></span><span>maintain</span><span><span> </span>robust AI/ML pipelines, automate workflows, and integrate AI capabilities into production systems makes you an essential part of delivering resilient, mission-focused solutions. We need your technical<span> </span></span><span>expertise</span><span><span> </span>and problem‑solving mindset to support the development and operationalization of AI capabilities that directly enhance mission performance and decision‑making. As an AI and ML engineer on our national security team,<span> </span></span><span>you’ll</span><span><span> </span>build, test, deploy, and<span> </span></span><span>operate</span><span><span> software end</span></span><span>‑to‑end AI pipelines that keep mission systems running securely and efficiently.</span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p></p><p><span><span>In this role,<span> </span></span><span>you’ll</span><span><span> </span>guide the development of mission‑critical AI solutions by building reproducible pipelines, applying automation best practices, and introducing emerging tools that enhance performance and reliability.<span> </span></span><span>You’ll</span><span><span> </span>collaborate with a cross‑functional team of AI Model Engineers, Data Engineers, Cloud Architects, and ISSEs to align AI and ML workflows with infrastructure and security requirements, ensuring seamless integration into production and mission systems.<span> </span></span><span>You’ll</span><span><span> </span>contribute to solutions that<span> </span></span><span>optimize</span><span><span> </span>data flow, automate operational workflows, ensure monitoring and observability, and support resilient mission execution across hybrid compute environments. Your engineering skills and experience with modern AI and ML frameworks will help clients navigate evolving toolchains, deployment patterns, and operational considerations for scalable AI systems.</span></span><span> </span></p><p></p></div><div><p><span><span>Work with us to build reliable AI pipelines, modernize mission workflows, and define AI and ML strategy.</span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span><span>Join us. The world<span> </span></span><span>can’t</span><span><span> </span>wait. </span></span><span> </span></p></div><p></p><div><p><b><span>You Have:  </span></b><span><span> </span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><ul><li><p><span><span>6&#43; years of experience with software engineering </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with Python</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience developing and<span> </span></span><span>maintaining</span><span><span> </span>AI and ML pipelines for model training, validation, and deployment</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience integrating AI and ML capabilities into production systems and mission workflows</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience implementing monitoring and observability solutions for model performance, resource<span> </span></span><span>utilization</span><span>, and system health</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Knowledge of hybrid compute environments such as cloud and on‑prem</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Ability to automate workflows and build reproducible, scalable, and efficient ML and AI systems</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Ability to collaborate with cross‑functional teams, such as AI Model Engineers, Data Engineers, Cloud Architects, or ISSE, to align workflows with infrastructure and security requirement</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED and 6&#43; years of experience with­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­ software engineering or AI system development, or Bachelor’s degree and 4&#43; years of experience with software engineering or AI system development</span></p></li></ul><p></p></div><div><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:  </span></b><span> </span></p></div><div><ul><li><p><span><span>10&#43; years of experience with software engineering</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with Rust for systems‑level or high‑performance components</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience evaluating or adopting emerging AI and ML frameworks, libraries, or toolchains</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with containerization or orchestration technologies such as Docker or Kubernetes</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience in cloud services relevant to AI and ML such as AWS</span><span><span> </span>or</span><span><span> </span></span><span>Azure</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Knowledge of CI/CD for ML pipelines or infrastructure‑as‑code such as Terraform or CloudFormation</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Knowledge of ML or </span><span>MLOps<span> </span>orchestration tools such as, Airflow, Kubeflow,<span> or </span>MLflow</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Knowledge of distributed training, GPU optimization, or advanced model deployment patterns</span></span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></span></p></li></ul></div><div><p><span> </span></p></div><div><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><span><span> </span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></span></p></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Hampton-VA/AI-ML-Engineeer_R0242615","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Hampton-VA/AI-ML-Engineeer_R0242615","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c39092ecacbcf3de98f7849485f639ce250892ce46ddf439856c1ba5b070de51","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Hampton-VA/AI-ML-Engineeer_R0242615","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Hampton-VA/AI-ML-Engineeer_R0242615","locations":[{"label":"Hampton, VA"},{"label":"Norfolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242615","internal_job_id":"dfff4684f3361001f40ec00909d30000","first_published_at":"2026-07-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity:\nImagine using artificial intelligence (AI) to improve critical IT operations for integrated warfighting capabilities. As a DevOps engineer, you know how to create efficient and effective solutions so you can quickly deliver the best operational data. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation, and we’re looking for a DevOps engineer with knowledge of AIOps, ML Ops, model ops, and data ops to develop tools and get them into the hands of those who need them most. \n\nOn our team, you’ll streamline IT operations to enhance platform productivity to improve integrated warfighting capabilities including Agentic AI positioned as a critical enabler for next-gen autonomy and decision-support capabilities. Relate to AI enabled, policy controlled containerized application and data workload management and orchestration required for CDO-L and resilient capabilities.\n\nAs an experienced engineer, you know that building reliable and scalable AI systems requires strong software engineering practices, automation, and seamless integration across complex, secure environments. Your ability to design and maintain robust AI/ML pipelines, automate workflows, and integrate AI capabilities into production systems makes you an essential part of delivering resilient, mission-focused solutions. We need your technical expertise and problem‑solving mindset to support the development and operationalization of AI capabilities that directly enhance mission resilience, performance, and decision‑making.\n\nIn this role, you’ll guide the development of mission‑critical AI solutions by building reproducible pipelines, applying automation best practices, and introducing emerging tools that enhance performance and reliability. You’ll collaborate with others including AI Model Engineers, Data Engineers, Cloud Architects, and ISSEs to align AI and ML workflows with infrastructure and security requirements, ensuring seamless integration into production and mission systems. You’ll contribute to solutions that optimize resilience of warfighting capabilities including their data flows, operational workflow automation, workload environmental monitoring, workload management, and resilient mission execution across hybrid compute environments.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 5+ years of experience in the development of tools and processes to drive DevOps or DevSecOps maturity by automating builds, testing, monitoring, and pushing releases across environments\n\n- 5+ years of experience with scripting languages such as Python or Linux Shell Script and configuration management tools  \n\n- 5+ years of experience automating infrastructure provisioning, in the creation, and improvement of continuous automation across multiple technical stacks\n\n- 5+ years of experience with troubleshooting, triaging, and resolving issues with CI/CD pipeline failures or slowness, built using Kubernetes, Docker, or Jenkins\n\n- 5+ years of experience with AI/ML capabilities applied to policy controlled, workload management and orchestration including Zero Trust Containerized applications and data    \n\n- 5+ years of experience with troubleshooting, triaging, and resolving issues related to both open source and commercial tools in public cloud environments\n\n- Experience with artificial intelligence and machine learning frameworks for monitoring and optimization and containerization and container orchestration platforms and tools \n\n- Experience adding testing and security scans to pipelines\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree \n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform\n\n- Experience integrating AI systems architecture, AI platforms, or ML flow \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- ML, DevOps, or solution architecture certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b><br />Imagine using artificial intelligence (AI) to improve critical IT operations for integrated warfighting capabilities. As a DevOps engineer, you know how to create efficient and effective solutions so you can quickly deliver the best operational data. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation, and we’re looking for a DevOps engineer with knowledge of AIOps, ML Ops, model ops, and data ops to develop tools and get them into the hands of those who need them most. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll streamline IT operations to enhance platform productivity to improve<i><span class=\"emphasis-3\"> </span></i>integrated warfighting capabilities including<i><span class=\"emphasis-3\"> </span></i><span>Agentic AI positioned as a critical enabler for next-gen autonomy and decision-support capabilities. Relate to AI enabled, policy controlled containerized application and data workload management and orchestration required for CDO-L and resilient capabilities.</span></p><p></p><p>As an experienced engineer, you know that building reliable and scalable AI systems requires strong software engineering practices, automation, and seamless integration across complex, secure environments. Your ability to design and maintain robust AI/ML pipelines, automate workflows, and integrate AI capabilities into production systems makes you an essential part of delivering resilient, mission-focused solutions. We need your technical expertise and problem‑solving mindset to support the development and operationalization of AI capabilities that directly enhance mission resilience, performance, and decision‑making.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll guide the development of mission‑critical AI solutions by building reproducible pipelines, applying automation best practices, and introducing emerging tools that enhance performance and reliability. You’ll collaborate with others including AI Model Engineers, Data Engineers, Cloud Architects, and ISSEs to align AI and ML workflows with infrastructure and security requirements, ensuring seamless integration into production and mission systems. You’ll contribute to solutions that optimize resilience of warfighting capabilities including their data flows, operational workflow automation, workload environmental monitoring, workload management, and resilient mission execution across hybrid compute environments.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience in the development of tools and processes to drive DevOps or DevSecOps maturity by automating builds, testing, monitoring, and pushing releases across environments</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with scripting languages such as Python or Linux Shell Script and configuration management tools  </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience automating infrastructure provisioning, in the creation, and improvement of continuous automation across multiple technical stacks</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with troubleshooting, triaging, and resolving issues with CI/CD pipeline failures or slowness, built using Kubernetes, Docker, or Jenkins</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with AI/ML capabilities applied to policy controlled, workload management and orchestration including Zero Trust Containerized applications and data    </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with troubleshooting, triaging, and resolving issues related to both open source and commercial tools in public cloud environments</p></li><li><p>Experience with artificial intelligence and machine learning frameworks for monitoring and optimization and containerization and container orchestration platforms and tools </p></li><li><p>Experience adding testing and security scans to pipelines</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating AI systems architecture, AI platforms, or ML flow </p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>ML, DevOps, or solution architecture certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b><br />Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0236420","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0236420","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3c287da478aa8ba9c1df9f183c7ceb4b31e25b375f1a7175538d73bc931e06a9","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0236420","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/AI-ML-Engineer_R0236420","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0236420","internal_job_id":"9458e2704e7e1001f6082491a8140000","first_published_at":"2026-06-22","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support transforming the federal government with AI. As an AI Engineer on our national security team, you’ll build agentic systems, fine tune models, build RL environments, and make AI a reality for our clients.  \n\nIn this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI models and technologies. You’ll grow within a large community of AI engineers across the company and collaborate with product teams, data engineers, and government stakeholders to deliver world-class solutions to build agentic systems. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of AI algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for the intelligence community. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience working with LLMs, generative AI systems, or agentic frameworks \n\n- Knowledge of AI frameworks, supporting tools, and design patterns, such as LangGraph, MCP, or A2A \n\n- Ability to map AI solutions onto customer problems\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  \n\n- Bachelor's degree in a Technology field such as Computer Science or Statistics\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience training generative AI systems\n\n- Experience communicating technical solutions to non-technical stakeholders  \n\n- Experience deploying generative AI systems into production environments\n\n- Experience working in the Intelligence Community\n\n- Experience with a deep learning framework such as PyTorch or Keras\n\n- Knowledge of Python\n\n- Knowledge of security requirements for production code in government systems\n\n- Ability to translate general user requirements into actionable tasks\n\n- Master's degree in a Technology field preferred; Doctorate degree in a Technology field a plus\n\n- Cloud Certifications such as AWS Certified AI Practitioner Certification\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $55,200.00 to $126,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support transforming the federal government with AI. As an AI Engineer on our national security team, you’ll build agentic systems, fine tune models, build RL environments, and make AI a reality for our clients.  </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI models and technologies. You’ll grow within a large community of AI engineers across the company and collaborate with product teams, data engineers, and government stakeholders to deliver world-class solutions to build agentic systems. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of AI algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for the intelligence community. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience working with LLMs, generative AI systems, or agentic frameworks </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of AI frameworks, supporting tools, and design patterns, such as LangGraph, MCP, or A2A </p></li><li><p>Ability to map AI solutions onto customer problems</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a Technology field such as Computer Science or Statistics</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience training generative AI systems</p></li><li><p>Experience communicating technical solutions to non-technical stakeholders  </p></li><li><p>Experience deploying generative AI systems into production environments</p></li><li><p>Experience working in the Intelligence Community</p></li><li><p>Experience with a deep learning framework such as PyTorch or Keras</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Python</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of security requirements for production code in government systems</p></li><li><p>Ability to translate general user requirements into actionable tasks</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in a Technology field preferred; Doctorate degree in a Technology field a plus</p></li><li><p>Cloud Certifications such as AWS Certified AI Practitioner Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $55,200.00 to $126,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/AI-ML-Engineer_R0247603","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/AI-ML-Engineer_R0247603","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"452b30c4ded1e73b8205748d4ab7a451c7958a1efa39a4b8d306b3c30168e1e1","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/AI-ML-Engineer_R0247603","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/AI-ML-Engineer_R0247603","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"},{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247603","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a1002022ea1d9036a0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an machine learning engineer, you understand good software is more than just a good user experience. To compete in today’s technical landscape, mission-oriented machine learning solutions must be architected, designed, and built to handle fast-moving data, to seamlessly scale with infrastructure based on system usage, and to expand based on evolving mission requirements. We’re looking for an engineer like you to create artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) enabled solutions that help solve our toughest challenges facing the Defense and Intelligence sectors.\n\nOn our team, you’ll design, create, and implement complete AI systems that will transform client operations, increase data accessibility, and optimize AI and ML systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements. Additionally, you’ll deepen your skill set in areas like software engineering, machine learning operations (MLOps), and software deployment and integration into a variety of different mission environments.\n\nReady to transform the Defense and Intelligence sectors with software systems to aid data accessibility and AI and ML operationalization?\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience as a ML engineer, data scientist, analyst or researcher\n\n- 2+ years of experience working within data science or data research in a professional or academic environment, and training or deploying models across multiple modalities of data\n\n- Experience building production-grade ML solutions\n\n- Experience with programming, including ML frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, llama.cpp, or vLLM\n\n- Experience with project work in deep learning, computer vision, neural networks, NLP, or signal processing\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience working in cloud environments, including AWS and Azure\n\n- 2+ years of experience deploying and integrating production-grade ML models using tools, such as Docker and Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with client engagements, client-facing project work, and business development\n\n- Experience deploying and managing data brokering solutions, including Kafka, Red Panda, Confluent, and other related services \n\n- Ability to adapt in a rapidly changing environment\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Possession of excellent interpersonal, analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer<div><p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As an machine learning engineer, you understand good software is more than just a good user experience. To compete in today’s technical landscape, mission-oriented machine learning solutions must be architected, designed, and built to handle fast-moving data, to seamlessly scale with infrastructure based on system usage, and to expand based on evolving mission requirements. We’re looking for an engineer like you to create artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) enabled solutions that help solve our toughest challenges facing the Defense and Intelligence sectors.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll design, create, and implement complete AI systems that will transform client operations, increase data accessibility, and optimize AI and ML systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements. Additionally, you’ll deepen your skill set in areas like software engineering, machine learning operations (MLOps), and software deployment and integration into a variety of different mission environments.</p><p></p><p>Ready to transform the Defense and Intelligence sectors with software systems to aid data accessibility and AI and ML operationalization?</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience as a ML engineer, data scientist, analyst or researcher</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience working within data science or data research in a professional or academic environment, and training or deploying models across multiple modalities of data</p></li><li><p>Experience building production-grade ML solutions</p></li><li><p>Experience with programming, including ML frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, llama.cpp, or vLLM</p></li><li><p>Experience with project work in deep learning, computer vision, neural networks, NLP, or signal processing</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience working in cloud environments, including AWS and Azure</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience deploying and integrating production-grade ML models using tools, such as Docker and Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Experience with client engagements, client-facing project work, and business development</p></li><li><p>Experience deploying and managing data brokering solutions, including Kafka, Red Panda, Confluent, and other related services </p></li><li><p>Ability to adapt in a rapidly changing environment</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent interpersonal, analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills</p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Wharton-NJ/AI-ML-Engineer--Junior_R0245456","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Wharton-NJ/AI-ML-Engineer--Junior_R0245456","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3eb650fc081e2b610aaa68691c266f6027ee991894c4a00f27b1818bc877e8b5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer, Junior","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wharton-NJ/AI-ML-Engineer--Junior_R0245456","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wharton-NJ/AI-ML-Engineer--Junior_R0245456","locations":[{"label":"Wharton, NJ"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245456","internal_job_id":"d2fc07c00573100109743c88be800000","first_published_at":"2026-07-28","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer, Junior The Opportunity :\nAs a data techni cia n, you know that high‑quality labeled data is essential for training artifi cia l intelligence systems. Your ability to recognize patterns, follow detailed instructions, and maintain consistency across large volumes of information makes you an important part of building reliable AI‑enabled solutions. We need your attention to detail and willingness to learn to support mission‑focused data preparation work.\n\nAs part of our team, you’ll help prepare datasets by labeling images, tagging objects, and applying met adata that supports AI model development. You’ll grow your technical skill set as you learn how AI systems use labeled data and collaborate with engineers and analysts to ensure datasets are accurate, complete, and ready for future model training.\n\nWork with us to support real‑world missions through foundational AI data preparation.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience labeling or annotating data, including images or objects, to support data preparation workflows\n\n- Experience performing basic quality checks to ensure consistency and accuracy in labeled datasets\n\n- Knowledge of basic digital tools used for reviewing and labeling content\n\n- Knowledge of data organization practices, including categorizing and structuring information\n\n- Ability to follow detailed instructions and maintain high accuracy across repetitive tasks\n\n- Ability to identify and report data inconsistencies or unclear cases\n\n- Ability to learn new technical processes and tools over time\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience working with basic scripting or sof tware tools\n\n- Experience supporting teams in digital, analytical, or data‑driven environments\n\n- Knowledge of AI concepts or how training data supports model development\n\n- Knowledge of met adata tagging, object identification, or digital imaging\n\n- Ability to learn basic scripting or automation met hods over time\n\n- Ability to collaborate with technical teammates such as engineers or analysts\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $55,200.00 to $126,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer, Junior<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b><span>:</span></b></p><p>As a data techni<span>cia</span>n, you know that high‑quality labeled data is essential for training artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence systems. Your <span>ability to</span> recognize patterns, follow detailed instructions, and maintain consistency across large volumes of information makes you an important part of building reliable AI‑enabled solutions. We need your attention to detail and willingness to learn to support mission‑focused data preparation work.</p><p></p><p>As part of our team, you’ll help prepare datasets by labeling images, tagging objects, and applying <span>met</span>adata that supports AI model development. You’ll grow your technical skill set as you learn how AI systems use labeled data and collaborate with engineers and analysts to ensure datasets are accurate, complete, and ready for future model training.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to support real‑world missions through foundational AI data preparation.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> labeling or annotating data, including images or objects, to support data preparation workflows</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> performing basic quality checks to ensure consistency and accuracy in labeled datasets</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> basic digital tools used for reviewing and labeling content</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> data organization practices, including categorizing and structuring information</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> follow detailed instructions and maintain high accuracy across repetitive tasks</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> identify and report data inconsistencies or unclear cases</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> learn new technical processes and tools over time</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with basic scripting or <span>sof</span>tware tools</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> supporting teams in digital, analytical, or data‑driven environments</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AI concepts or how training data supports model development</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> <span>met</span>adata tagging, object identification, or digital imaging</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> learn basic scripting or automation <span>met</span>hods over time</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> collaborate with technical teammates such as engineers or analysts</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $55,200.00 to $126,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 27 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer--Mid_R0245169","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer--Mid_R0245169","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"39a7c8e6a577e4e4de603bf7ea6a38d4f5b624405da115910f64e5856982ce23","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AI/ML Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer--Mid_R0245169","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/AI-ML-Engineer--Mid_R0245169","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245169","internal_job_id":"c4c927081f051001a1ac6aba04f30000","first_published_at":"2026-07-23","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AI/ML Engineer, Mid The Opportunity: \nAs an AI/ML Engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge, curiosity, and drive for solving problems to support close to critical, close to mission challenges. As a machine learning engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, monitor, and maintain models that learn from data.  \n\nIn this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, software developers, data scientists, and mission stakeholders to deliver world-class solutions to creatively apply AI/ML solutions to solve cutting edge problems, triage large datasets. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience building and deploying AI/ML solutions into production\n\n- Experience working with LLMs, generative AI systems, or agentic frameworks\n\n- Experience with Python and object oriented programming\n\n- Knowledge of AI frameworks, supporting tools, and design patterns, such as LangGraph, MCP, or A2A \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience communicating technical solutions to non-technical stakeholders  \n\n- Experience deploying generative AI systems into production environments\n\n- Experience working in the Intelligence Community\n\n- Experience with a deep learning framework such as PyTorch or Keras\n\n- Knowledge of security requirements for production code in government systems\n\n- Ability to translate general user requirements into actionable tasks\n\n- Master's degree in a STEM field preferred; Doctorate degree in a STEM field a plus\n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AI/ML Engineer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As an AI/ML Engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge, curiosity, and drive for solving problems to support close to critical, close to mission challenges. As a machine learning engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, monitor, and maintain models that learn from data.  </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, software developers, data scientists, and mission stakeholders to deliver world-class solutions to creatively apply AI/ML solutions to solve cutting edge problems, triage large datasets. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience building and deploying AI/ML solutions into production</p></li><li><p>Experience working with LLMs, generative AI systems, or agentic frameworks</p></li><li><p>Experience with Python and object oriented programming</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of AI frameworks, supporting tools, and design patterns, such as LangGraph, MCP, or A2A </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience communicating technical solutions to non-technical stakeholders  </p></li><li><p>Experience deploying generative AI systems into production environments</p></li><li><p>Experience working in the Intelligence Community</p></li><li><p>Experience with a deep learning framework such as PyTorch or Keras</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of security requirements for production code in government systems</p></li><li><p>Ability to translate general user requirements into actionable tasks</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in a STEM field preferred; Doctorate degree in a STEM field a plus<span class=\"emphasis\"> </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance: </b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"56fef251f36757504bcccd45a61021c4aa0375c54abceb1bbd34f3524218f30f","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","locations":[{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244294","internal_job_id":"9aa9ab4a63ca1000c8ec958c0db10000","first_published_at":"2026-07-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support the U.S. Space Force under the U.S. Department of War. As an AI Solutions Engineer on our Defense Technology Group, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across sof tware development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerating the missions with AI tools.\n\nIn this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI technologies and emerging AI-native processes or workflows. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with full-stack sof tware engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and defense mission experts to deliver world-class solutions to deliver new sof tware capabilities to our customers with high velocity. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of Agentic workflows, AI / ML algorithms, full-stack development, DevSecOps, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for the U.S. Space Force.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience within machine learning, data science, data engineering, or software development\n\n- Experience with integration of LLMs or Agentic Workflows within sof tware stacks\n\n- Experience with the Agile sof tware development lifecycle and full-stack web application development\n\n- Knowledge of JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS\n\n- Ability to solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities\n\n- Secret clearance   \n\n- Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a Science or Mathematics field\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Knowledge of AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry\n\nClearance:   \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support the U.S. Space Force under the U.S. Department of War. As an AI Solutions Engineer on our Defense Technology Group, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across <span>sof</span>tware development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerating the missions with AI tools.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI technologies and emerging AI-native processes or workflows. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with full-stack <span>sof</span>tware engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and defense mission experts to deliver world-class solutions to deliver new <span>sof</span>tware capabilities to our customers with high velocity. Your skills and technical <span>experience</span> will help your clients navigate the landscape of Agentic workflows, AI<span>/</span>ML algorithms, full-stack development, DevSecOps, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for the U.S. Space Force.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience within machine learning, data science, data engineering, or software development</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with integration of LLMs or Agentic Workflows within <span>sof</span>tware stacks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with the Agile <span>sof</span>tware development lifecycle and full-stack web application development</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in Computer Science or a Science or Mathematics field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b>  </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span> </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence","Solutions Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Antonio-TX/AWS-Agentic-AI-Platform-Engineer_R0247584","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Antonio-TX/AWS-Agentic-AI-Platform-Engineer_R0247584","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"99cd5f1eb4589db9768213a04501a542cafe99c02182b3126f14d483a966fc0e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"AWS Agentic AI Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/AWS-Agentic-AI-Platform-Engineer_R0247584","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/AWS-Agentic-AI-Platform-Engineer_R0247584","locations":[{"label":"San Antonio, TX"},{"label":"Austin, TX"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247584","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a1001fb92242a6d300000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"AWS Agentic AI Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs an experience d AI / ML engineer, you know that machine learning and generative AI are critical to understanding and processing large, complex datasets. Your ability to apply statistical learning, large language models, retrieval techniques, and agentic workflow patterns makes you an integral part of delivering secure, customer-focused solutions. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to help mission organizations transform fragmented data and manual processes into t rus tworthy AI-enabled decision support and workflow automation. As an AI / ML engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain machine learning models and agentic applications that learn from data, retrieve governed knowledge, interact with approved tools and services, and support human decision-making.\n\nIn this role, you’ll own and help define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms, foundation models, retrieval architectures, and agent orchestration patterns. You’ll be part of a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, sof tware engineers, cloud and DevSecOps engineers, solutions architects, product owners, and mission subject matter experts to deliver secure AWS-based capabilities that process structured and unstructured data, automate complex workflows, and produce t race able outputs. Your skills and technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI / ML algorithms, tools, frameworks, evaluation met hods, and production deployment patterns.\n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI / ML strategy for national defense mission-support operations.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with AI / ML engineering, data science, sof tware engineering, data engineering, or cloud engineering\n\n- Experience developing AI / ML applications using Python\n\n- Experience developing agentic AI or large language model applications, retrieval-augmented generation systems, or predictive machine learning models\n\n- Experience integrating AI / ML capabilities with APIs, data stores, cloud services, or enterprise applications\n\n- Experience developing, deploying, or supporting applications on AWS\n\n- Knowledge of AI / ML evaluation met hods for model quality, retrieval relevance, task success, latency, cost, or system performance\n\n- Knowledge of sof tware engineering and DevSecOps practices, including version control, automated testing, CI / CD, containerization, and infrastructure as code\n\n- Ability to translate operational needs into testable technical requirements and collaborate with multidisciplinary engineering and mission teams\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience developing agentic AI applications using AWS Strands Agents, LangGraph, LangChain, LlamaIndex, or comparable frameworks\n\n- Experience with Amazon Bedrock, Amazon SageMaker AI, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Knowledge Bases for Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Bedrock Guardrails, or related AWS AI / ML services\n\n- Experience implementing retrieval-augmented generation, embeddings, vector search, reranking, knowledge graphs, Model Context Protocol, Agent-to-Agent communication, or structured tool-calling integrations\n\n- Experience developing Python APIs, microservices, or durable workflows using FastAPI, Pydantic, OpenAPI, Temporal, AWS Step Functions, Amazon EventBridge, or comparable technologies\n\n- Experience with Docker, Kubernetes, Amazon EKS, Amazon ECS, Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, AWS CDK, or CI / CD automation\n\n- Experience with MLOps or LLMOps, including automated evaluation, prompt or model versioning, observability, tracing, drift monitoring, or rollback controls\n\n- Experience supporting AWS GovCloud, FedRAMP High, DoD Impact Level 4 or 5, or another regulated or high-assurance cloud environment\n\n- Experience with computer vision, multimodal AI, geospatial analytics, graph neural networks, temporal or dynamic graph networks, network science, or so cia l network analysis\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- AWS AI / ML, Sof tware Development, Architecture, DevOps, Cloud Operations, or Security Certification or CompTIA Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"AWS Agentic AI Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d AI<span>/</span>ML engineer, you know that machine learning and generative AI are critical to understanding and processing large, complex datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> apply statistical learning, large language models, retrieval techniques, and agentic workflow patterns makes you an integral part of delivering secure, customer-focused solutions. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to help mission organizations transform fragmented data and manual processes into t<span>rus</span>tworthy AI-enabled decision support and workflow automation. As an AI<span>/</span>ML engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain machine learning models and agentic applications that learn from data, retrieve governed knowledge, interact with approved tools and services, and support human decision-making.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and help define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms, foundation models, retrieval architectures, and agent orchestration patterns. You’ll be part of a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, <span>sof</span>tware engineers, cloud and DevSecOps engineers, solutions architects, product owners, and mission subject matter experts to deliver secure AWS-based capabilities that process structured and unstructured data, automate complex workflows, and produce t<span>race</span>able outputs. Your skills and technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI<span>/</span>ML algorithms, tools, frameworks, evaluation <span>met</span>hods, and production deployment patterns.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI<span>/</span>ML strategy for national defense mission-support operations.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with AI<span>/</span>ML engineering, data science, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, data engineering, or cloud engineering</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing AI<span>/</span>ML applications using Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing agentic AI or large language model applications, retrieval-augmented generation systems, or predictive machine learning models</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating AI<span>/</span>ML capabilities with APIs, data stores, cloud services, or enterprise applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing, deploying, or supporting applications on AWS</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AI<span>/</span>ML evaluation <span>met</span>hods for model quality, retrieval relevance, task success, latency, cost, or system performance</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> <span>sof</span>tware engineering and DevSecOps practices, including version control, automated testing, CI<span>/</span>CD, containerization, and infrastructure as code</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> translate operational needs into testable technical requirements and collaborate with multidisciplinary engineering and mission teams</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing agentic AI applications using AWS Strands Agents, LangGraph, LangChain, LlamaIndex, or <span>comparable</span> frameworks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Amazon Bedrock, Amazon SageMaker AI, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Knowledge Bases for Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Bedrock Guardrails, or <span>related</span> AWS AI<span>/</span>ML services</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> implementing retrieval-augmented generation, embeddings, vector search, reranking, knowledge graphs, Model Context Protocol, Agent-to-Agent communication, or structured tool-calling integrations</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing Python APIs, microservices, or durable workflows using FastAPI, Pydantic, OpenAPI, Temporal, AWS Step Functions, Amazon EventBridge, or <span>comparable</span> technologies</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Docker, Kubernetes, Amazon EKS, Amazon ECS, Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, AWS CDK, or CI<span>/</span>CD automation</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with MLOps or LLMOps, including automated evaluation, prompt or model versioning, observability, tracing, drift monitoring, or rollback controls</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> supporting AWS GovCloud, FedRAMP High, DoD Impact Level 4 or 5, or another regulated or high-assurance cloud environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with computer vision, multimodal AI, geospatial analytics, graph neural networks, temporal or dynamic graph networks, network science, or so<span>cia</span>l network analysis</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>AWS AI<span>/</span>ML, <span>Sof</span>tware Development, Architecture, DevOps, Cloud Operations, or Security <span>Certification</span> or CompTIA Security&#43; <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/C2-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244268","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/C2-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244268","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"68be715f8408506fe4c629a2de0180afa4ec09297e4f3b171daee4e3c7f15b8f","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"C2 Systems Platform and Infrastructure Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/C2-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244268","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/C2-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244268","locations":[{"label":"Hanscom AFB, MA"},{"label":"Hampton, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244268","internal_job_id":"b3c781f660711000c43b2a49d5a90000","first_published_at":"2026-07-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"C2 Systems Platform and Infrastructure Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud”, but not everyone knows how. As an experience d cloud computing infrastructure architect, you know how to take advantage of cloud capabilities. Here, you’ll oversee our team of experience d professionals and use cutting-edge enterprise cloud platforms to guide your clients as they modernize their IT infrastructure and meet their most challenging missions. We’re looking for someone like you to help modernize solutions so warfighters stay safe. \n\nYou’ll collaborate closely with fellow cloud architects and engineers spe cia lizing in GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux to design, deploy, and harden the containerized foundation beneath next-generation C2 systems, from enterprise data center s to the tactical edge and cloud solution components. You’ll have the chance to broaden your experience within a DevOps framework to create and manage container apps and use products like Kubernetes to further the mission. With access to our internal sof tware, licenses, and environments, you’ll have the space and time to explore different ways of solving our clients’ problems, and you’ll partner with stakeholders and lead your team to deliver the right technical solutions. Whether modernizing legacy computing platforms and applications or creating new ones from scratch, you’ll have the latest tech and brightest teammates at your fingertips.  \n\nGrow your skills at the leading edge of innovation. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience operating Kubernetes at production scale, including cluster deployment, day-2 operations, upgrades, and security hardening\n- Experience with CI / CD and GitOps pipelines using tools such as GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux\n- Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code and configuration management using Terraform and Ansible\n- Experience implementing and operating an observability stack such as Pro met heus, Grafana, and ELK or OpenTele met ry\n- Experience designing and deploying systems in secure, air-gapped, or DDIL environments\n- Ability to translate mission and reliability requirements into resilient, automated platform designs\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree in CS or Engineering and 8+ years of experience in infrastructure or platform engineering, including technical leadership on production systems, or 12+ years of experience in infrastructure or platform engineering, including technical leadership on production systems, in lieu of a degree\n- DoD 8570 IAT Level II Security+ CE Certification\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with service mesh technologies such as Istio, Linkerd, or Consul, for traffic management, mTLS, and observability\n- Experience deploying and sustaining containerized platforms in DoD environments, including Platform One, Big Bang, or Iron Bank\n- Experience engineering for the tactical edge and hardening deployments for DDIL and disconnected operations\n- Experience with C2, ISR, or other mission-critical DoD systems and their operational constraints\n- Experience implementing DevSecOps practices, including container scanning, STIG compliance, and policy enforcement such as OPA or Gatekeeper, and Kyverno\n- Experience with secrets management and Zero T rus t patterns such as HashiCorp Vault and SPIFFE or SPIRE\n- Experience achieving and maintaining an Authority to Operate ( ATO ) , continuous ATO, or RMF accreditation\n- Secret clearance\n- Certified Kubernetes Administrator ( CKA ) Certification\n- AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Asso cia te or similar Cloud Certification\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,900.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"C2 Systems Platform and Infrastructure Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud”, but not everyone knows how. As an <span>experience</span>d cloud computing infrastructure architect, you know how to take advantage of cloud capabilities. Here, you’ll oversee our team of <span>experience</span>d professionals and use cutting-edge enterprise cloud platforms to guide your clients as they modernize their IT infrastructure and meet their most challenging missions. We’re looking for someone like you to help modernize solutions so warfighters stay safe. </p><p></p><p>You’ll collaborate closely with fellow cloud architects and engineers spe<span>cia</span>lizing in GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux to design, deploy, and harden the containerized foundation beneath next-generation C2 systems, from enterprise data <span>center</span>s to the tactical edge and cloud solution components. You’ll have the chance to broaden your <span>experience</span> within a DevOps framework to create and manage container apps and use products like Kubernetes to further the mission. With access to our internal <span>sof</span>tware, licenses, and environments, you’ll have the space and time to explore different ways of solving our clients’ problems, and you’ll partner with stakeholders and lead your team to deliver the right technical solutions. Whether modernizing legacy computing platforms and applications or creating new ones from scratch, you’ll have the latest tech and brightest teammates at your fingertips.  </p><p></p><p>Grow your skills at the leading edge of innovation. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> operating Kubernetes at production scale, including cluster deployment, day-2 operations, upgrades, and security hardening</li><li><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD and GitOps pipelines using tools such as GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure-as-Code and configuration management using Terraform and Ansible</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing and operating an observability stack such as Pro<span>met</span>heus, Grafana, and ELK or OpenTele<span>met</span>ry</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing and deploying systems in secure, air-gapped, or DDIL environments</li><li><span>Ability to</span> translate mission and reliability requirements into resilient, automated platform designs</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in CS or Engineering and 8&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in infrastructure or platform engineering, including technical leadership on production systems, or 12&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in infrastructure or platform engineering, including technical leadership on production systems, in lieu of a degree</li><li>DoD 8570 IAT Level II Security&#43; CE <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with service mesh technologies such as Istio, Linkerd, or Consul, for traffic management, mTLS, and observability</li><li><span>Experience</span> deploying and sustaining containerized platforms in DoD environments, including Platform One, Big Bang, or Iron Bank</li><li><span>Experience</span> engineering for the tactical edge and hardening deployments for DDIL and disconnected operations</li><li><span>Experience</span> with C2, ISR, <span>or other</span> mission-critical DoD systems and their operational constraints</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing DevSecOps practices, including container scanning, STIG compliance, and <span>policy</span> enforcement such as OPA or Gatekeeper, and Kyverno</li><li><span>Experience</span> with secrets management and Zero T<span>rus</span>t patterns such as HashiCorp Vault and SPIFFE or SPIRE</li><li><span>Experience</span> achieving and maintaining an Authority to Operate <span>(</span>ATO<span>)</span>, continuous ATO, or RMF accreditation</li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li>Certified Kubernetes Administrator <span>(</span>CKA<span>)</span> <span>Certification</span></li><li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Asso<span>cia</span>te or <span>similar</span> Cloud <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.  </p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,900.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Infrastructure Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Infrastructure","Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/Command---Control-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244276","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/Command---Control-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244276","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3c1d19347b143b059f277f3f4cb64d99021aba86dafb776b43c22ea762a7510b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Command & Control Systems Platform and Infrastructure Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/Command---Control-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244276","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Hanscom-AFB-MA/Command---Control-Systems-Platform-and-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0244276","locations":[{"label":"Hanscom AFB, MA"},{"label":"Hampton, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244276","internal_job_id":"9aa9ab4a63ca1000c5da4057fffd0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Command & Control Systems Platform and Infrastructure Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As an experience d cloud computing infrastructure architect, you know how to take advantage of cloud capabilities. Here, you’ll oversee our team of experience d professionals and use cutting-edge enterprise cloud platforms to guide your clients as they modernize their IT infrastructure and meet their most challenging missions. We’re looking for someone like you to help modernize our solution so the warfighters stay safe. \n\nYou’ll collaborate closely with fellow cloud architects and engineers spe cia lizing in GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux to design, deploy, and harden the containerized foundation beneath next-generation C2 systems — from enterprise data center s to the tactical edge and cloud solution components. You’ll have the chance to broaden your experience within a DevOps framework to create and manage container apps and use products like Kubernetes to further the mission. With access to our internal sof tware, licenses and environments, you’ll have the space and time to explore different ways of solving our clients’ problems, and you’ll partner with stakeholders and lead your team to deliver the right technical solutions. Whether modernizing legacy computing platforms and applications or creating new ones from scratch, you’ll have the latest tech and brightest teammates at your fingertips.\n\nGrow your skills at the leading edge of innovation. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 8+ years of experience in infrastructure or platform engineering, including technical leadership on production systems\n- Experience operating Kubernetes at production scale, including cluster deployment, day-2 operations, upgrades, and security hardening\n- Experience with CI / CD and GitOps pipelines using tools such as GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux\n- Experience with Infrastructure as Code and configuration management using Terraform and Ansible\n- Experience implementing and operating an observability stack such as Pro met heus, Grafana, and ELK or OpenTele met ry\n- Experience designing and deploying systems in secure, air-gapped, or DDIL environments\n- Ability to translate mission and reliability requirements into resilient, automated platform designs\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a technology field, or 6+ years of experience in designing, deploying, and maintaining mission‑critical C2 platforms and infrastructure in lieu of a degree\n- DoD 8570 IAT Level II Security+ CE certification\n  \nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with service mesh technologies, such as Istio, Linkerd, or Consul, for traffic management, mTLS, and observability\n- Experience deploying and sustaining containerized platforms in DoD environments such as Platform One, Big Bang, or Iron Bank\n- Experience engineering for the tactical edge and hardening deployments for DDIL and disconnected operations\n- Experience with C2, ISR, or other mission-critical DoD systems and their operational constraints\n- Experience implementing DevSecOps practices, including container scanning, policy enforcement, such as OPA, Gatekeeper, or Kyverno, and STIG compliance\n- Experience with secrets management and zero-t rus t patterns such as HashiCorp Vault or SPIFFE / SPIRE\n- Experience achieving and maintaining an Authority to Operate ( ATO ) , continuous ATO, or RMF accreditation\n- Secret clearance\n- Certified Kubernetes Administrator ( CKA ) certification\n- AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Asso cia te or equivalent cloud certification\n  \nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,900.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Command &amp; Control Systems Platform and Infrastructure Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As an <span>experience</span>d cloud computing infrastructure architect, you know how to take advantage of cloud capabilities. Here, you’ll oversee our team of <span>experience</span>d professionals and use cutting-edge enterprise cloud platforms to guide your clients as they modernize their IT infrastructure and meet their most challenging missions. We’re looking for someone like you to help modernize our solution so the warfighters stay safe. </p><p></p><p>You’ll collaborate closely with fellow cloud architects and engineers spe<span>cia</span>lizing in GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux to design, deploy, and harden the containerized foundation beneath next-generation C2 systems — from enterprise data <span>center</span>s to the tactical edge and cloud solution components. You’ll have the chance to broaden your <span>experience</span> within a DevOps framework to create and manage container apps and use products like Kubernetes to further the mission. With access to our internal <span>sof</span>tware, licenses and environments, you’ll have the space and time to explore different ways of solving our clients’ problems, and you’ll partner with stakeholders and lead your team to deliver the right technical solutions. Whether modernizing legacy computing platforms and applications or creating new ones from scratch, you’ll have the latest tech and brightest teammates at your fingertips.</p><p></p><p>Grow your <span>skills</span> at the leading edge of innovation. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li>8&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in infrastructure or platform engineering, including technical leadership on production systems</li><li><span>Experience</span> operating Kubernetes at production scale, including cluster deployment, day-2 operations, upgrades, and security hardening</li><li><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD and GitOps pipelines using tools such as GitLab CI, Jenkins, and ArgoCD or Flux</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure as Code and configuration management using Terraform and Ansible</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing and operating an observability stack such as Pro<span>met</span>heus, Grafana, and ELK or OpenTele<span>met</span>ry</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing and deploying systems in secure, air-gapped, or DDIL environments</li><li><span>Ability to</span> translate mission and reliability requirements into resilient, automated platform designs</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in Computer Science, Engineering, or a technology field, or 6&#43; years of experience in designing, deploying, and maintaining mission‑critical C2 platforms and infrastructure in lieu of a degree</li><li>DoD 8570 IAT Level II Security&#43; CE <span>certification</span></li></ul><p>  </p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with service mesh technologies, such as Istio, Linkerd, or Consul, for traffic management, mTLS, and observability</li><li><span>Experience</span> deploying and sustaining containerized platforms in DoD environments such as Platform One, Big Bang, or Iron Bank</li><li><span>Experience</span> engineering for the tactical edge and hardening deployments for DDIL and disconnected operations</li><li><span>Experience</span> with C2, ISR, <span>or other</span> mission-critical DoD systems and their operational constraints</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing DevSecOps practices, including container scanning, <span>policy</span> enforcement, such as OPA, Gatekeeper, or Kyverno, and STIG compliance</li><li><span>Experience</span> with secrets management and zero-t<span>rus</span>t patterns such as HashiCorp Vault or SPIFFE<span>/</span>SPIRE</li><li><span>Experience</span> achieving and maintaining an Authority to Operate <span>(</span>ATO<span>)</span>, continuous ATO, or RMF accreditation</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li>Certified Kubernetes Administrator <span>(</span>CKA<span>)</span> <span>certification</span></li><li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Asso<span>cia</span>te or <span>equivalent</span> cloud <span>certification</span></li></ul><p>  </p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,900.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Infrastructure Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Infrastructure","Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Cybersecurity-AI-ML-Engineer_R0243936","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Cybersecurity-AI-ML-Engineer_R0243936","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"f871b916f7de528c79a83a1444b6af8e4268a86e145350b99475e6691ebefe8e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cybersecurity AI/ML Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Cybersecurity-AI-ML-Engineer_R0243936","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Cybersecurity-AI-ML-Engineer_R0243936","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243936","internal_job_id":"186c347b6c0e1001562a141cfaf20000","first_published_at":"2026-07-08","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cybersecurity AI/ML Engineer The Opportunity :  \nAs a Cybersecurity AI/ML Engineer, you will operate as a hands-on technical contributor and engineering leader responsible for building, scaling, and operationalizing AI/ML systems that power Booz Allen's Cyber Operations teams. This role emphasizes production engineering and platform delivery, turning models, security telemetry, and analyst workflows into reliable, low-latency, observable services and pipelines that measurably improve prevention, detection, response, and recovery outcomes.\n\nYou will bridge ML engineering and security operations by translating models, threat models, and analyst needs into production-grade data and feature pipelines, training systems, inference services, and monitoring frameworks deployed across cloud, network, endpoint, identity, and application telemetry domains. You will originate, facilitate, and lead cross-functional efforts to mature AI-enabled cybersecurity capabilities, including real-time detection inference at scale, alert triage automation, LLM and agentic analyst tooling, and SOC platform integrations while guiding teams through MLSecOps, secure-AI engineering, and responsible AI practices.\n\nPerform code and architecture reviews, provide technical direction for complex ML systems initiatives, including SIEM, SOAR, and EDR ML integrations, cloud-native ML platforms for security, and GenAI services for analysts, and translate requirements into actionable, measurable implementation plans. Leverage strong software engineering, systems, and communication skills to assess complex security and platform problems, align technical and non-technical stakeholders, and drive decisions to closure in support of Booz Allen Hamilton's critical enterprise infrastructure, go-to-market platforms, and mission operations.\n\nThe ideal candidate for our Enterprise Cybersecurity team is technically inclined, intellectually curious, and adaptable, with a strong cyber-defense mindset. They thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment and are continuous learners who actively seek to understand complex challenges, ask thoughtful questions, and look beyond the obvious to identify innovative and effective ways of working. They bring a security-first perspective, analytical problem-solving skills, and the curiosity and aptitude to continuously evolve as threats, technologies, and mission needs change. This position is located in McLean, VA.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n- Design, build, and deploy production AI/ML services for cybersecurity, including supervised and unsupervised detection models, anomaly and behavioral analytics, NLP on security text, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) pipelines, agentic workflows, and LLM-assisted analyst tooling and own them end-to-end, data ingest → feature pipelines → training and tuning → packaging → deployment → serving → monitoring → retraining.\n\n- Engineer scalable batch and streaming data and feature pipelines over security telemetry including logs, EDR, network, identity, cloud, and threat intel with online and offline parity, feature stores, schema and contract management, and reproducible datasets that power detection, triage, and hunting use cases.\n\n- Build, harden, and operate ML platforms and inference services, including low-latency real-time scoring, batch inference, model packaging and containerization, autoscaling, canary and shadow deployments, observability, and rollback, to meet SOC throughput, latency, and reliability SLOs.\n\n- Apply secure-AI and MLSecOps engineering practices throughout the AI/ML lifecycle, including model and data protection, prompt and inference risk mitigation, evaluation against adversarial inputs such as evasion, poisoning, and prompt injection, model and dataset supply chain security, and responsible AI controls.\n\n- Integrate ML services and analytics into security tools and workflows such as SIEM, SOAR, EDR, IAM, or CSPM via APIs and event-driven architectures extending detection logic, enrichment, and response playbooks with custom ML/LLM capabilities where commercial tooling falls short.\n\n- Develop automation, scripting, and infrastructure-as-code (IaC) to enable repeatable, testable, and version-controlled ML pipelines, model deployments, and security data integrations across cloud and on-prem environments.\n\n- Collaborate across data science, platform, data, threat intelligence, and SOC operations teams to deliver end-to-end solutions, embed ML practices into DevSecOps and MLSecOps pipelines, and drive implementation through measurable operational outcomes.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience in machine learning engineering, software engineering for ML, or applied AI platform development\n\n- Experience building and operating production ML systems including cybersecurity or security operations\n\n- Experience developing, testing, and integrating ML services across security tools and platforms using APIs, automation, and workflow orchestration and applying AI and machine learning to cybersecurity use cases such as threat and anomaly detection, behavioral analytics, alert triage and prioritization, threat hunting support, analyst copilots, and response automation with measurable impact on SOC outcomes\n\n- Experience software engineering in Python for ML and security use cases, including production-quality code, design patterns, unit and integration testing, packaging, version control, CI/CD, Docker containerization, and container orchestration including Kubernetes\n\n- Experience working with the modern AI/ML stack, including PyTorch or TensorFlow, scikit-learn, Hugging Face, LangChain/LlamaIndex, agent frameworks, model serving frameworks, KServe, BentoML, Triton, Ray Serve, embedding-based retrieval, and vector databases such as pgvector, OpenSearch, Pinecone, and Milvus\n\n- Experience operationalizing AI/ML systems or MLOps, model versioning, experiment tracking, feature stores, evaluation harnesses, drift and quality monitoring, and CI/CD for models such as MLflow, Weights & Biases, SageMaker, Vertex AI, Azure ML, and Kubeflow\n\n- Knowledge of secure AI implementation practices and frameworks including model and data protection, prompt and inference risk, agent guardrails, evaluation against adversarial inputs, ML supply chain security, and governance controls aligned to NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM Top 10, and MITRE ATLAS\n\n- Knowledge of modern cybersecurity threats and attack patterns, including ransomware, insider threats, credential abuse, data exfiltration, and AI-enabled attack techniques such as prompt injection, model evasion, data poisoning, and model theft\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with programming or scripting languages used in ML, security, and automation environments such as Python, Go, Rust, SQL, PowerShell, and Bash\n\n- Experience designing, deploying, and maintaining enterprise-scale ML and security systems for sensitive or regulated environments including FedRAMP, IL4, IL5, HIPAA, and PCI\n\n- Experience designing and building agentic AI systems for security operations, multi-step reasoning, tool and function calling, retrieval pipelines, and human-in-the-loop workflows\n\n- Experience fine-tuning, distilling, quantizing, or serving LLMs and other models for domain-specific security tasks, including automated eval harnesses and red-teaming AI systems\n\n- Experience evaluating and integrating AI-enabled cybersecurity tooling such as AI-assisted SIEM, SOAR, UEBA, behavioral analytics, model-driven detection workflows into enterprise security operations via APIs and event-driven architectures\n\n- Experience designing and implementing AI/ML services and pipelines over enterprise security telemetry spanning network, endpoint, application, identity, and cloud environments\n\n- Knowledge of AI governance, model risk management, and policy controls aligned to enterprise and regulatory expectations for responsible AI use\n\n- Knowledge of data governance frameworks, data classification standards, and privacy regulations such as GDPR and CCPA\n\n- Knowledge of distributed data and streaming platforms, including Kafka, Kinesis, Spark, and Flink, database structures, data modeling fundamentals, and query optimization, including SQL and NoSQL\n\n- IT Engineering, ML, or Security Certifications such as AWS, GCP, Azure ML Engineer, CKAD, CKA, CISSP, CCSP, CDPSE, cloud security Certifications, or AI security Certifications such as ISC2 CAISS or IAPP AIGP Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cybersecurity AI/ML Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>:</b> </p><p>As a Cybersecurity AI/ML Engineer, you will operate as a hands-on technical contributor and engineering leader responsible for building, scaling, and operationalizing AI/ML systems that power Booz Allen&#39;s Cyber Operations teams. This role emphasizes production engineering and platform delivery, turning models, security telemetry, and analyst workflows into reliable, low-latency, observable services and pipelines that measurably improve prevention, detection, response, and recovery outcomes.</p><p></p><p>You will bridge ML engineering and security operations by translating models, threat models, and analyst needs into production-grade data and feature pipelines, training systems, inference services, and monitoring frameworks deployed across cloud, network, endpoint, identity, and application telemetry domains. You will originate, facilitate, and lead cross-functional efforts to mature AI-enabled cybersecurity capabilities, including real-time detection inference at scale, alert triage automation, LLM and agentic analyst tooling, and SOC platform integrations while guiding teams through MLSecOps, secure-AI engineering, and responsible AI practices.</p><p></p><p>Perform code and architecture reviews, provide technical direction for complex ML systems initiatives, including SIEM, SOAR, and EDR ML integrations, cloud-native ML platforms for security, and GenAI services for analysts, and translate requirements into actionable, measurable implementation plans. Leverage strong software engineering, systems, and communication skills to assess complex security and platform problems, align technical and non-technical stakeholders, and drive decisions to closure in support of Booz Allen Hamilton&#39;s critical enterprise infrastructure, go-to-market platforms, and mission operations.</p><p></p><p>The ideal candidate for our Enterprise Cybersecurity team is technically inclined, intellectually curious, and adaptable, with a strong cyber-defense mindset. They thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment and are continuous learners who actively seek to understand complex challenges, ask thoughtful questions, and look beyond the obvious to identify innovative and effective ways of working. They bring a security-first perspective, analytical problem-solving skills, and the curiosity and aptitude to continuously evolve as threats, technologies, and mission needs change. This position is located in McLean, VA.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>Design, build, and deploy production AI/ML services for cybersecurity, including supervised and unsupervised detection models, anomaly and behavioral analytics, NLP on security text, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) pipelines, agentic workflows, and LLM-assisted analyst tooling and own them end-to-end, data ingest → feature pipelines → training and tuning → packaging → deployment → serving → monitoring → retraining.</p></li><li><p>Engineer scalable batch and streaming data and feature pipelines over security telemetry including logs, EDR, network, identity, cloud, and threat intel with online and offline parity, feature stores, schema and contract management, and reproducible datasets that power detection, triage, and hunting use cases.</p></li><li><p>Build, harden, and operate ML platforms and inference services, including low-latency real-time scoring, batch inference, model packaging and containerization, autoscaling, canary and shadow deployments, observability, and rollback, to meet SOC throughput, latency, and reliability SLOs.</p></li><li><p>Apply secure-AI and MLSecOps engineering practices throughout the AI/ML lifecycle, including model and data protection, prompt and inference risk mitigation, evaluation against adversarial inputs such as evasion, poisoning, and prompt injection, model and dataset supply chain security, and responsible AI controls.</p></li><li><p>Integrate ML services and analytics into security tools and workflows such as SIEM, SOAR, EDR, IAM, or CSPM via APIs and event-driven architectures extending detection logic, enrichment, and response playbooks with custom ML/LLM capabilities where commercial tooling falls short.</p></li><li><p>Develop automation, scripting, and infrastructure-as-code (IaC) to enable repeatable, testable, and version-controlled ML pipelines, model deployments, and security data integrations across cloud and on-prem environments.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate across data science, platform, data, threat intelligence, and SOC operations teams to deliver end-to-end solutions, embed ML practices into DevSecOps and MLSecOps pipelines, and drive implementation through measurable operational outcomes.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience in machine learning engineering, software engineering for ML, or applied AI platform development</p></li><li><p>Experience building and operating production ML systems including cybersecurity or security operations</p></li><li><p>Experience developing, testing, and integrating ML services across security tools and platforms using APIs, automation, and workflow orchestration and applying AI and machine learning to cybersecurity use cases such as threat and anomaly detection, behavioral analytics, alert triage and prioritization, threat hunting support, analyst copilots, and response automation with measurable impact on SOC outcomes</p></li><li><p>Experience software engineering in Python for ML and security use cases, including production-quality code, design patterns, unit and integration testing, packaging, version control, CI/CD, Docker containerization, and container orchestration including Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Experience working with the modern AI/ML stack, including PyTorch or TensorFlow, scikit-learn, Hugging Face, LangChain/LlamaIndex, agent frameworks, model serving frameworks, KServe, BentoML, Triton, Ray Serve, embedding-based retrieval, and vector databases such as pgvector, OpenSearch, Pinecone, and Milvus</p></li><li><p>Experience operationalizing AI/ML systems or MLOps, model versioning, experiment tracking, feature stores, evaluation harnesses, drift and quality monitoring, and CI/CD for models such as MLflow, Weights &amp; Biases, SageMaker, Vertex AI, Azure ML, and Kubeflow</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of secure AI implementation practices and frameworks including model and data protection, prompt and inference risk, agent guardrails, evaluation against adversarial inputs, ML supply chain security, and governance controls aligned to NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM Top 10, and MITRE ATLAS</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modern cybersecurity threats and attack patterns, including ransomware, insider threats, credential abuse, data exfiltration, and AI-enabled attack techniques such as prompt injection, model evasion, data poisoning, and model theft</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with programming or scripting languages used in ML, security, and automation environments such as Python, Go, Rust, SQL, PowerShell, and Bash</p></li><li><p>Experience designing, deploying, and maintaining enterprise-scale ML and security systems for sensitive or regulated environments including FedRAMP, IL4, IL5, HIPAA, and PCI</p></li><li><p>Experience designing and building agentic AI systems for security operations, multi-step reasoning, tool and function calling, retrieval pipelines, and human-in-the-loop workflows</p></li><li><p>Experience fine-tuning, distilling, quantizing, or serving LLMs and other models for domain-specific security tasks, including automated eval harnesses and red-teaming AI systems</p></li><li><p>Experience evaluating and integrating AI-enabled cybersecurity tooling such as AI-assisted SIEM, SOAR, UEBA, behavioral analytics, model-driven detection workflows into enterprise security operations via APIs and event-driven architectures</p></li><li><p>Experience designing and implementing AI/ML services and pipelines over enterprise security telemetry spanning network, endpoint, application, identity, and cloud environments</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of AI governance, model risk management, and policy controls aligned to enterprise and regulatory expectations for responsible AI use</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of data governance frameworks, data classification standards, and privacy regulations such as GDPR and CCPA</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of distributed data and streaming platforms, including Kafka, Kinesis, Spark, and Flink, database structures, data modeling fundamentals, and query optimization, including SQL and NoSQL</p></li><li><p>IT Engineering, ML, or Security Certifications such as AWS, GCP, Azure ML Engineer, CKAD, CKA, CISSP, CCSP, CDPSE, cloud security Certifications, or AI security Certifications such as ISC2 CAISS or IAPP AIGP Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["ML Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","ML"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0238477","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0238477","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"767d3178e7ebf1e43bd2b8c080fa1c6c596a5079cec5501207f07a0b85d3ae1d","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0238477","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0238477","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0238477","internal_job_id":"01c8fe4d57e51001a08cb8c5d9300000","first_published_at":"2026-07-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Power Platform Developer The Opportunity:\nBuild business applications and dashboards using the Micro sof t Power Platform. Design intuitive Power Apps, automate workflows with Power Automate, and create actionable Power BI reports and dashboards. Guide stakeholders and create concise, collaborative documentation that supports iterative Agile delivery. Write custom code to create and deploy Power Platform solutions, as needed. Customize and brand Power Platform sites, configure workflows, and customize lists, pages, and forms using Power Platform. Support installation and configuration of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. Foster user adoption of Power Platform by demonstrating Power Platform features and technologies to clients and enabling the conversion of business requirements into solutions. Document system processes and procedures in a clear manner. Discuss requirements with clients and follow internal and client-specific protocols used to document and design Power Platform sites, templates, structure, and taxonomy develop ment required to develop and implement solutions using Power Platform Participate in all facets of the sof tware develop ment life cycle, including requirements solicitation and documentation, system and acceptance testing, and training, as needed.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience develop ing custom PowerApps applications\n- Experience working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations\n- Experience integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, and REST APIs\n- Ability to use Micro sof t Flow and Power Automate\n- Ability to design and implement Power BI dashboards, Power Automate, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows\n- Ability to work with general web technologies, including AngularJS, SPFX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and jQuery \n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with database modeling and concepts, Performance Points, Reporting Services, Business Data Catalogs, and Business Connectivity Services\n- Experience with Agile Sof tware Develop ment Life Cycle met hodology\n- Experience with Object-Oriented Programming concepts\n- Ability to work in a team environment and offer or support ideas\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Build business applications and dashboards using the Micro<span>sof</span>t Power Platform. Design intuitive Power Apps, automate workflows with Power Automate, and create actionable Power BI reports and dashboards. Guide stakeholders and create concise, collaborative documentation that supports iterative Agile delivery. Write custom code to create and deploy Power Platform solutions, as needed. Customize and brand Power Platform sites, configure workflows, and customize lists, pages, and forms using Power Platform. Support installation and configuration of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. Foster user adoption of Power Platform by demonstrating Power Platform features and technologies to clients and enabling the conversion of business requirements into solutions. Document system processes and procedures in a clear manner. Discuss requirements with clients and follow internal and client-specific protocols used to document and design Power Platform sites, templates, structure, and taxonomy <span>develop</span>ment required to <span>develop</span> and implement solutions using Power Platform Participate in all facets of the <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment life cycle, including requirements solicitation and documentation, system and acceptance testing, and training, as needed.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing custom PowerApps applications</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations</li><li><span>Experience</span> integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, and REST APIs</li><li><span>Ability to</span> use Micro<span>sof</span>t Flow and Power Automate</li><li><span>Ability to</span> design and implement Power BI dashboards, Power Automate, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with general web technologies, including AngularJS, SPFX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and jQuery </li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with database modeling and concepts, Performance Points, Reporting Services, Business Data Catalogs, and Business Connectivity Services</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>Sof</span>tware <span>Develop</span>ment Life Cycle <span>met</span>hodology</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Object-Oriented Programming concepts</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work in a team environment and offer or support ideas</li><li><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication <span>skills</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/SharePoint-Administrator-and-Power-Platform-Developer_R0244804","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/SharePoint-Administrator-and-Power-Platform-Developer_R0244804","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"44504e40efed1e63e71fc9bd180c48397694ee12272878aa591430b311184375","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/SharePoint-Administrator-and-Power-Platform-Developer_R0244804","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/SharePoint-Administrator-and-Power-Platform-Developer_R0244804","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"Atlanta, GA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244804","internal_job_id":"98fde5d94b9e1000b59331ff61f20000","first_published_at":"2026-07-28","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Power Platform Developer The Opportunity:\nIn this role, you will develop, improve, and support Power Apps and Power Automate solutions. You will work directly with a Power Platform Architect, following established solution architecture and best practices while turning clear requirements into well-designed, user-friendly applications and workflows.\n \nYour work will include managing SharePoint sites that support our applications and automations, maintaining existing lists, and ensuring data structures and permissions are correctly implemented. You will also assist with managing the Power Platform environment, including app permissions, environment access, and making sure solutions follow consistent governance standards. On a typical week, you might be building a new Canvas App, refining the user experience of an existing tool, troubleshooting an automation, updating SharePoint list schema, validating details with stakeholders, or exploring newer Power Platform capabilities, including Copilot. We are looking for someone who pays attention to detail, communicates well, and can work independently while staying connected to the team. This role requires someone who understands the business context and can deliver practical solutions that create real impact through both new development and ongoing enhancements.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 4+ years of experience in a professional work environment\n\n- 2+ years of experience with Power Apps\n\n- 2+ years of experience with Power Automate development work\n\n- 2+ years of experience integrating SharePoint Online with Power Platform Solutions  \n\n- Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination based on client requirements\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Microsoft Dataverse as a data source in Power Apps and Power Automate\n\n- Experience with Power BI, including report building and embedding in SharePoint or Power Apps\n\n- Experience with Copilot Studio\n\n- Experience with Power Platform AI Builder models\n\n- Experience with Power Pages\n\n- Possession of excellent communication skills\n\nVetting:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a government investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements of the U.S. government client.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>In this role, you will develop, improve, and support Power Apps and Power Automate solutions. You will work directly with a Power Platform Architect, following established solution architecture and best practices while turning clear requirements into well-designed, user-friendly applications and workflows.</p><p><span> </span></p><p>Your work will include managing SharePoint sites that support our applications and automations, maintaining existing lists, and ensuring data structures and permissions are correctly implemented. You will also assist with managing the Power Platform environment, including app permissions, environment access, and making sure solutions follow consistent governance standards. On a typical week, you might be building a new Canvas App, refining the user experience of an existing tool, troubleshooting an automation, updating SharePoint list schema, validating details with stakeholders, or exploring newer Power Platform capabilities, including Copilot. We are looking for someone who pays attention to detail, communicates well, and can work independently while staying connected to the team. This role requires someone who understands the business context and can deliver practical solutions that create real impact through both new development and ongoing enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience in a professional work environment </span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years</span> of <span>experience with Power Apps </span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with Power Automate development work</span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience integrating SharePoint Online with Power Platform Solutions  </span></p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination based on client requirements</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Microsoft Dataverse as a data source in Power Apps and Power Automate</p></li><li><p>Experience with Power BI, including report building and embedding in SharePoint or Power Apps</p></li><li><p>Experience with Copilot Studio</p></li><li><p>Experience with Power Platform AI Builder models</p></li><li><p>Experience with Power Pages</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent communication skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Vetting:</b><br />Applicants selected will be subject to a government investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements of the U.S. government client.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 27 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Norfolk-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0245702","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Norfolk-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0245702","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8506535b9709396caa198432221be034917395b3077541433429c50bcbc11e98","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Norfolk-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0245702","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Norfolk-VA/Power-Platform-Developer_R0245702","locations":[{"label":"Norfolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245702","internal_job_id":"d2fc07c005731001a90addad21300000","first_published_at":"2026-08-06","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Power Platform Developer The Opportunity: \nDesign, develop, and implement Power Platform solutions by using out-of-the-box features to create custom pages, site templates, features, and Web parts. Write custom code to create and deploy Power Platform solutions, as needed. Customize and brand SharePoint sites, configure workflows, and customize lists, pages, and forms using Power Platform. Support installation and configuration of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. Foster user adoption of Power Platform by demonstrating Power Platform features and technologies to clients and enabling the conversion of business requirements into solutions. Document system processes and procedures in a clear manner. Discuss requirements with clients and follow internal and client-specific protocols used to document and design Power Platform sites, templates, structure, and taxonomy development required to develop and implement solutions using Power Platform. Participate in all facets of the software development lifecycle, including requirements solicitation and documentation, system and acceptance testing, and training, as needed.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 3+ years of experience developing custom PowerApps applications\n\n- Experience working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations\n\n- Experience integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, and REST APIs\n\n- Ability to design and implement Power BI dashboards, Power Automate Flows, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Agile methodology, extreme programming, software engineering, product management, and software products \n\n- Experience with Java, Python, JavaScript, SQL, and PowerApps\n\n- Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization \n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Developer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Design, develop, and implement Power Platform solutions by using out-of-the-box features to create custom pages, site templates, features, and Web parts. Write custom code to create and deploy Power Platform solutions, as needed. Customize and brand SharePoint sites, configure workflows, and customize lists, pages, and forms using Power Platform. Support installation and configuration of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. Foster user adoption of Power Platform by demonstrating Power Platform features and technologies to clients and enabling the conversion of business requirements into solutions. Document system processes and procedures in a clear manner. Discuss requirements with clients and follow internal and client-specific protocols used to document and design Power Platform sites, templates, structure, and taxonomy development required to develop and implement solutions using Power Platform. Participate in all facets of the software development lifecycle, including requirements solicitation and documentation, system and acceptance testing, and training, as needed.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience developing custom PowerApps applications</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, and REST APIs</p></li><li><p>Ability to design and implement Power BI dashboards, Power Automate Flows, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Agile methodology, extreme programming, software engineering, product management, and software products </p></li><li><p>Experience with Java, Python, JavaScript, SQL, and PowerApps</p></li><li><p>Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization </p></li><li><p>Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 18 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Power-Platform-Developer_R0243995","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Power-Platform-Developer_R0243995","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"37b496f1615315828a99b2f3b10b4231404892aec9d2ced7138ad9c066129b49","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Power-Platform-Developer_R0243995","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Power-Platform-Developer_R0243995","locations":[{"label":"Uruma City, Okinawa"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243995","internal_job_id":"6e77dd6f4b62100166bbc897b6440000","first_published_at":"2026-08-25","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Power Platform Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a Power Platform Developer, you will design, develop, and implement solutions using out‑of‑the‑box capabilities to create custom pages, site templates, features, and web parts. You will also write custom code when needed to build and deploy advanced Power Platform solutions. In this role, you will customize and brand SharePoint sites, configure workflows, and tailor lists, pages, and forms to meet mission requirements. You will support the installation, configuration, and optimization of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. To drive user adoption, you will demonstrate platform features to clients and translate business needs into effective, scalable solutions. You will document system processes and procedures clearly and work closely with clients to gather requirements while following internal and client‑specific protocols for site design, structure, and taxonomy. Additionally, you will participate in all phases of the sof tware development lifecycle, including requirement elicitation, testing, deployment validation, and user training.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience developing custom PowerApps applications\n\n- 3+ years of experience working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations\n\n- 3+ years of experience integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, or REST APIs\n\n- 3+ years of experience using Micro sof t Flow and Power Automate\n\n- 3+ years of experience designing and implementing Power BI dashboards, Power Automate, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows\n\n- Experience working with general web technologies, including AngularJS, SPFX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, or jQuery \n\n- Experience with database modeling and concepts, performance points, reporting services, business data catalogs, and business connectivity services\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Associate's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 1+ years of experience working in sof tware development with foundational programming languages, technologies, tools, and web development\n\n- 1+ years of experience with Python, TypeScript, and Foundry AIP for application development\n\n- Experience managing a cross-functional team creating solutions to solve complex problems\n\n- Experience with SQL, Spark, Databricks, model hosting, or deployment specifics\n\n- Experience with Pipeline Builder for data ingestion and transformation\n\n- Experience with object-oriented programming concepts\n\n- Ability to work in a team environment and offer or support ideas\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- PL-900 Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a Power Platform Developer, you will design, develop, and implement solutions using out‑of‑the‑box capabilities to create custom pages, site templates, features, and web parts. You will also write custom code when needed to build and deploy advanced Power Platform solutions. In this role, you will customize and brand SharePoint sites, configure workflows, and tailor lists, pages, and forms to meet mission requirements. You will support the installation, configuration, and optimization of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. To drive user adoption, you will demonstrate platform features to clients and translate business needs into effective, scalable solutions. You will document system processes and procedures clearly and work closely with clients to gather requirements while following internal and client‑specific protocols for site design, structure, and taxonomy. Additionally, you will participate in all phases of the <span>sof</span>tware development lifecycle, including requirement elicitation, testing, deployment validation, and user training.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> developing custom PowerApps applications</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, or REST APIs</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> using Micro<span>sof</span>t Flow and Power Automate</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing and implementing Power BI dashboards, Power Automate, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with general web technologies, including AngularJS, SPFX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, or jQuery </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with database modeling and concepts, performance points, reporting services, business data catalogs, and business connectivity services</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Associate&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working in <span>sof</span>tware development with foundational programming languages, technologies, tools, and web development</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Python, TypeScript, and Foundry AIP for application development</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> managing a cross-functional team creating solutions to solve complex problems</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with SQL, Spark, Databricks, model hosting, or deployment specifics</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Pipeline Builder for data ingestion and transformation</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with object-oriented programming concepts</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work in a team environment and offer or support ideas</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>PL-900 <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"Japan","id":"8b705da2becf43cfaccc091da0988ab2"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
