nvironment\n\n- Knowledge of C++ fundamentals, including object-oriented programming, data types and structures, standard library, memory management, and design patterns\n\n- Ability to problem-solve and critically think through sof tware issues, including utilizing debuggers and testing infrastructure to troubleshoot issues\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with modeling and simulation frameworks, including AFSIM\n\n- Experience with large code bases and the complex code\n\n- Ability to work with technologies that support CI / CD development, including Git, Jira, and Bamboo\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"C++ Software Engineer, Mid<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Develop solution architecture <span>(</span>SA<span>)</span> and resolve complex issues in a variety of projects through the implementation of requirements analysis, expertise support, and project supervision. Apply basic principles, theories, and concepts, including limited industry knowledge. Solve routine problems of limited scope and complexity and refer more complex issues to higher levels. Work under direct supervision.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>3&#43; years of experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing C&#43;&#43; <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using Agile <span>met</span>hods</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems in a collaborative team environment</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> C&#43;&#43; fundamentals, including object-oriented programming, data types and structures, standard library, memory management, and design patterns</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> problem-solve and critically think through <span>sof</span>tware issues, including utilizing debuggers and testing infrastructure to troubleshoot issues</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with modeling and simulation frameworks, including AFSIM</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with large code bases and the complex code</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with technologies that support CI<span>/</span>CD development, including Git, Jira, and Bamboo</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Cloud-Developer-and-Customer-Support-Engineer_R0241200","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Cloud-Developer-and-Customer-Support-Engineer_R0241200","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8eca4a15e8c4d1da9cb3fed3fa34a1a48ccfb1d027168727a53391780348f077","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cloud Developer and Customer Support Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Cloud-Developer-and-Customer-Support-Engineer_R0241200","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Cloud-Developer-and-Customer-Support-Engineer_R0241200","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241200","internal_job_id":"768377881ab31000bedb0e8ba6780000","first_published_at":"2026-06-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cloud Developer and Customer Support Engineer The Opportunity:\nWould you like to implement innovative cloud computing solutions while directly supporting customers and helping them solve complex technical problems? Do you have a deep passion and desire to engineer and operate the company's advanced cloud computing infrastructure while providing exceptional customer support? This is an exciting opportunity to use the latest cloud computing technologies to help our customers supporting U.S. government agencies implement innovative cloud computing solutions, solve technical problems, and provide responsive and professional technical support.\n\nThe team is seeking a highly skilled and motivated cloud developer who combines strong technical development capabilities with excellent customer support skills. You should have a strong desire to build an operational excellence system, be adept at troubleshooting complex system solutions, have strong development skills, and understand Linux and Windows operating systems, networking fundamentals, and multiple AWS or Azure services. We need engineers who understand the big picture of PaaS infrastructure and can simplify solutions to complex problems, all the while ensuring that our tenants continue to have the best experience possible.\n\nAs a member of the team, you will serve as a technical point of contact, c ond ucting troubleshooting sessions, and providing timely resolutions to technical issues. You'll balance proactive development work with reactive customer support, ensuring customers receive prompt, professional, and effective technical assistance. You will be expected to understand customer issues, identify root causes, and dive deep to troubleshoot and fix issues. As an engineer, you'll build monitoring capabilities to investigate anomalies in those met rics in a timely manner and address them before they escalate into major problems. You'll also create and maintain technical documentation, runbooks, and knowledge base articles to help customers and improve team efficiency.\n\nThis role requires a balance of independent development work and collaborative customer support in a fast-paced environment where customer satisfaction is a top priority. You'll need flexibility to handle urgent customer issues while maintaining progress on development projects. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizen ship is required .\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n- Contribute to automation and infrastructure improvements based on customer feedback and support patterns.\n\n- Implement automation and IaC practices to streamline deployments, provisioning, and configuration management.\n\n- Evaluate and recommend cloud services, tools, and technologies to improve efficiency and enhance system capabilities.\n\n- Develop and maintain cloud infrastructure solutions using AWS, Azure, or GCP services.\n\n- Resp ond to customer support tickets and technical inquiries within defined SLAs.\n\n- Troubleshoot and resolve customer-reported issues, from simple configuration problems to complex system failures.\n\n- Collaborate with customers to understand their requirements and provide technical guidance.\n\n- Create and maintain technical documentation, runbooks, and knowledge base articles.\n\n- Monitor system health and proactively identify potential issues before they impact customers.\n\n- Participate in on-call rotation for critical customer support escalations.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Python and leveraging multiple services to build complex solutions with AWS or Azure\n\n- 2+ years of experience in customer-facing technical support or customer success roles\n\n- Experience with AWS or Azure services, Git, and IT systems engineering or administration, including Linux and Windows\n\n- Experience implementing automation and IaC practices to streamline deployments, provisioning, and configuration management\n\n- Experience evaluating and recommending cloud services, tools, and technologies to improve efficiency and enhance system capabilities, documenting solutions, creating knowledge base articles, and maintaining customer-facing documentation\n\n- Experience with incident management, escalation procedures, SLA adherence, and customer support tools, including ticketing systems such as ServiceNow, Zendesk, or Jira Service Management\n\n- Knowledge of multi-account or multi-tenant architecture\n\n- Ability to manage multiple customer support cases simultaneously while maintaining high service quality, explain technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and remain calm and professional under pressure\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\n- Certified AWS Solutions Architect or DevOps Engineer Certification\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience writing in IaC tools, such as AWS CloudFormation or Terraform\n\n- Experience with NIST standards, CI / CD, Agile or Scrum frameworks and practices, and containerization technologies such as Docker\n\n- Experience with customer support met rics and KPIs, including response time, resolution time, and customer satisfaction\n\n- Experience with remote support tools, screen-sharing platforms, customer onboarding, and technical enablement\n\n- Experience creating and delivering technical training or documentation for end users\n\n- Knowledge of ITIL or similar IT service management frameworks\n\n- Knowledge of Confluence, Jira, and Micro sof t Office suite\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Possession of excellent problem-solving skills\n\n- ITIL Foundation Certification and Certified AWS Security or Advanced Networking Spe cia lty Certification\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cloud Developer and Customer Support Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b><br />Would you like to implement innovative cloud computing solutions while directly supporting customers and helping them solve complex technical problems? Do you have a deep passion and desire to engineer and operate the company&#39;s advanced cloud computing infrastructure while providing exceptional customer support? This is an exciting opportunity to use the latest cloud computing technologies to help our customers supporting U.S. government agencies implement innovative cloud computing solutions, solve technical problems, and provide responsive and professional technical support.</p><p></p><p>The team is seeking a highly skilled and motivated cloud developer who combines strong technical development capabilities with excellent customer support skills. You should have a strong desire to build an operational excellence system, be adept at troubleshooting complex system solutions, have strong development skills, and understand Linux and Windows operating systems, networking fundamentals, and multiple AWS or Azure services. We need engineers who understand the big picture of PaaS infrastructure and can simplify solutions to complex problems, all the while ensuring that our tenants continue to have the best experience possible.</p><p></p><p>As a member of the team, you will serve as a technical point of contact, c<span>ond</span>ucting troubleshooting sessions, and providing timely resolutions to technical issues. You&#39;ll balance proactive development work with reactive customer support, ensuring customers receive prompt, professional, and effective technical assistance. You will be expected to understand customer issues, identify root causes, and dive deep to troubleshoot and fix issues. As an engineer, you&#39;ll build monitoring capabilities to investigate anomalies in those <span>met</span>rics in a timely manner and address them before they escalate into major problems. You&#39;ll also create and maintain technical documentation, runbooks, and knowledge base articles to help customers and improve team efficiency.</p><p></p><p>This role requires a balance of independent development work and collaborative customer support in a fast-paced environment where customer satisfaction is a top priority. You&#39;ll need flexibility to handle urgent customer issues while maintaining progress on development projects. <span>Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. </span><span>citizen</span><span>ship is required</span>.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On: </b></p><ul><li><p>Contribute to automation and infrastructure improvements based on customer feedback and support patterns.</p></li><li><p>Implement automation and IaC practices to streamline deployments, provisioning, and configuration management.</p></li><li><p>Evaluate and recommend cloud services, tools, and technologies to improve efficiency and enhance system capabilities.</p></li><li><p>Develop and maintain cloud infrastructure solutions using AWS, Azure, or GCP services.</p></li><li><p>Resp<span>ond</span> to customer support tickets and technical inquiries within defined SLAs.</p></li><li><p>Troubleshoot and resolve customer-reported issues, from simple configuration problems to complex system failures.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with customers to understand their requirements and provide technical guidance.</p></li><li><p>Create and maintain technical documentation, runbooks, and knowledge base articles.</p></li><li><p>Monitor system health and proactively identify potential issues before they impact customers.</p></li><li><p>Participate in on-call rotation for critical customer support escalations.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with Python and leveraging multiple services to build complex solutions with AWS or Azure</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in customer-facing technical support or customer success roles</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS or Azure services, Git, and IT systems engineering or administration, including Linux and Windows</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing automation and IaC practices to streamline deployments, provisioning, and configuration management</p></li><li><p>Experience evaluating and recommending cloud services, tools, and technologies to improve efficiency and enhance system capabilities, documenting solutions, creating knowledge base articles, and maintaining customer-facing documentation</p></li><li><p>Experience with incident management, escalation procedures, SLA adherence, and customer support tools, including ticketing systems such as ServiceNow, Zendesk, or Jira Service Management</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of multi-account or multi-tenant architecture</p></li><li><p>Ability to manage multiple customer support cases simultaneously while maintaining high service quality, explain technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and remain calm and professional under pressure</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li><li><p>Certified AWS Solutions Architect or DevOps Engineer Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience writing in IaC tools, such as AWS CloudFormation or Terraform</p></li><li><p>Experience with NIST standards, CI<span>/</span>CD, Agile or Scrum frameworks and practices, and containerization technologies such as Docker</p></li><li><p>Experience with customer support <span>met</span>rics and KPIs, including response time, resolution time, and customer satisfaction</p></li><li><p>Experience with <span>remote</span> support tools, screen-sharing platforms, customer onboarding, and technical enablement</p></li><li><p>Experience creating and delivering technical training or documentation for end users</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of ITIL or <span>similar</span> IT service management frameworks</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Confluence, Jira, and Micro<span>sof</span>t Office suite</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p>ITIL Foundation Certification and Certified AWS Security or Advanced Networking Spe<span>cia</span>lty Certification</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Cloud-Developer--Mid_R0236171","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Cloud-Developer--Mid_R0236171","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"448896511b8daeaa75ed12230b26c8b33b19ab50eda1afd336adde6cb2b11d83","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cloud Developer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Cloud-Developer--Mid_R0236171","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Cloud-Developer--Mid_R0236171","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"},{"label":"Charlottesville, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0236171","internal_job_id":"f21468196348100155672eb8d1b40000","first_published_at":"2026-08-07","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cloud Developer, Mid The Opportunity:  \nDoing DevSecOps well means development and automation. Making tasks repeatable and efficient across multiple environments requires Infrastructure as Code ( IAC ) , scripting, and sometimes writing applications. Our cloud service broker team is looking for a developer with a good understanding of Amazon Web Services ( AWS ) cloud infrastructure, containerization, and networking to make new cloud capabilities available in secure environments.\n\nIn this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you further your skill set and career. Work with us as we shape the next generation of DoD systems.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 7+ years of experience designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining systems in an enterprise-scale secure environment using Linux and Micro sof t platforms\n\n- 3+ years of experience with DevOps and cloud engineering using Infrastructure as Code ( IaC ) in AWS, Azure, and GCP using Terraform or CloudFormation, including hands-on development in GCP\n\n- 3+ years of experience with operational support activities such as system monitoring, incident response, logging or metrics configuration, and troubleshooting cloud workloads\n\n- 2+ years of experience using Golang, Python, SQL, Scala, or Java\n\n- Experience developing CI / CD pipelines to build, test, and deploy applications and infrastructure\n\n- Experience with networking fundamentals, including DNS, routing, switching, and load-balancing\n\n- Experience with containerization or orchestration using Kubernetes or Docker and Helm charts\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED and 8+ years of experience with sof tware engineering, or Bachelor's degree and 4+ years of experience with sof tware engineering\n\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 IAT Level II Certification within 30 days of start date\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with disa ster recovery services and concepts\n\n- Experience with GitLab, including automating DevSecOps pipeline processes in GitLab\n\n- Experience with migration of applications to the cloud\n\n- Ability to adapt to evolving requirements and deliver to project deadlines\n\n- TS / SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Information Technology\n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cloud Developer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>Doing DevSecOps well means development and automation. Making tasks repeatable and efficient across multiple environments requires Infrastructure as Code <span>(</span>IAC<span>)</span>, scripting, and sometimes writing applications. Our cloud service broker team is looking for a developer with a good understanding of Amazon Web Services <span>(</span>AWS<span>)</span> cloud infrastructure, containerization, and networking to make new cloud capabilities available in secure environments.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you further your skill set and career. Work with us as we shape the next generation of DoD systems.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>7&#43; years of experience designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining systems in an enterprise-scale secure environment using Linux and Micro<span>sof</span>t platforms</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with DevOps and cloud engineering using Infrastructure as Code <span>(</span>IaC<span>)</span> in AWS, Azure, and GCP using Terraform or CloudFormation, including hands-on development in GCP</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with operational support activities such as system monitoring, incident response, logging or metrics configuration, and troubleshooting cloud workloads</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience using Golang, Python, SQL, Scala, or Java</p></li><li><p>Experience developing CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines to build, test, and deploy applications and infrastructure</p></li><li><p>Experience with networking fundamentals, including DNS, routing, switching, and load-balancing</p></li><li><p>Experience with containerization or orchestration using Kubernetes or Docker and Helm charts</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED and 8&#43; years of experience with <span>sof</span>tware engineering, or Bachelor&#39;s degree and 4&#43; years of experience with <span>sof</span>tware engineering</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 IAT Level II Certification within 30 days of start date</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with <span>disa</span>ster recovery services and concepts</p></li><li><p>Experience with GitLab, including automating DevSecOps pipeline processes in GitLab</p></li><li><p>Experience with migration of applications to the cloud</p></li><li><p>Ability to adapt to evolving requirements and deliver to project deadlines</p></li><li><p>TS<span>/</span>SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Information Technology</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance: </b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 17 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Cloud-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0240283","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Cloud-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0240283","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"1d53cb9ccb1deb2a46766c2446d14e886dbdb244ecf7f1cd509792cff2c339db","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cloud Infrastructure Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Cloud-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0240283","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Cloud-Infrastructure-Engineer_R0240283","locations":[{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"},{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240283","internal_job_id":"d1c2b4334432100100b9c50f98e10000","first_published_at":"2026-08-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cloud Infrastructure Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As an experience d cloud computing infrastructure architect, you know how to take advantage of cloud capabilities. Here, you’ll oversee our team of experience d professionals and use cutting-edge enterprise cloud platforms to guide your clients as they modernize their IT infrastructure and meet their most challenging missions. That’s why we need you, an engineer who understands how data platforms, mission systems, hardware, sof tware, and Cloud-native capabilities fit together across classified environments to help us modernize IT systems supporting JWCC and C2E initiatives.\n\nYou’ll collaborate closely with fellow architects and engineers spe cia lizing in Classified System Platforms to build cloud solutions components. You’ll have the chance to broaden your experience within a DevOps framework to create and manage container apps and use products like Kubernetes to further the mission. With access to our internal support, you’ll have the space and time to explore different ways of solving our clients’ problems, and you’ll partner with stakeholders and lead your team to deliver the right technical solutions. Whether modernizing legacy computing platforms and applications or creating new ones from scratch, you’ll have the latest tech and brightest teammates at your fingertips. This position is located in Colorado Springs, CO or the Washington Met ro area.\n\nGrow your skills at the leading edge of innovation. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience with Cloud engineering, architecture, management, maintenance, and enhancement across enterprise environment\n\n- Experience working with Amazon Web Services ( AWS ) or Micro sof t Azure supporting enterprise-scale Cloud architecture and platform transformation\n\n- Experience designing, engineering, and deploying Cloud-native and hybrid environments supporting mission and data workloads\n\n- Experience working with networking, security groups, IAM, routing, and policy management in relation to Cloud resources across multiple operating systems, including UNIX, Linux, and Windows\n\n- Experience building and managing Cloud environments across multiple impact levels, regions, and providers\n\n- Experience supporting DoD or IC Cloud environments, security requirements, and certification frameworks\n\n- Experience with Infrastructure as Code ( IaC ) , automation, and configuration management tools\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- DoD 8570 Certification such as Security+ Certification\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with CI/CD pipeline solutions such as Jenkins, Bamboo, Travis CI, and GitLab\n\n- Experience with Kubernetes, containerization, and Cloud platform services\n\n- Experience building Cloud Data Plane and Mission Plane architectures\n\n- Knowledge of DoD accreditation and Cloud authorization processes\n\n- Ability to work through challenging security requirements and maintain compliance in classified environments\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\n- AWS or Azure Certification s\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cloud Infrastructure Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As an <span>experience</span>d cloud computing infrastructure architect, you know how to take advantage of cloud capabilities. Here, you’ll oversee our team of <span>experience</span>d professionals and use cutting-edge enterprise cloud platforms to guide your clients as they modernize their IT infrastructure and meet their most challenging missions. That’s why we need you, an engineer who understands how data platforms, mission systems, hardware, <span>sof</span>tware, and Cloud-native capabilities fit together across classified environments to help us modernize IT systems supporting JWCC and C2E initiatives.</p><p></p><p>You’ll collaborate closely with fellow architects and engineers spe<span>cia</span>lizing in Classified System Platforms to build cloud solutions components. You’ll have the chance to broaden your <span>experience</span> within a DevOps framework to create and manage container apps and use products like Kubernetes to further the mission. With access to our internal support, you’ll have the space and time to explore different ways of solving our clients’ problems, and you’ll partner with stakeholders and lead your team to deliver the right technical solutions. Whether modernizing legacy computing platforms and applications or creating new ones from scratch, you’ll have the latest tech and brightest teammates at your fingertips. This position is located in Colorado Springs, CO or the Washington <span>Met</span>ro area.</p><p></p><p>Grow your skills at the leading edge of innovation. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud engineering, architecture, management, maintenance, and enhancement across enterprise environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with Amazon Web Services <span>(</span>AWS<span>)</span> <span>or</span> Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure supporting enterprise-scale Cloud architecture and platform transformation</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing, engineering, and deploying Cloud-native and <span>hybrid</span> environments supporting mission and data workloads</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with networking, security groups, IAM, routing, and <span>policy</span> management in relation to Cloud resources across multiple operating systems, including UNIX, Linux, and Windows</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building and managing Cloud environments across multiple impact levels, regions, and providers</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> supporting DoD or IC Cloud environments, security requirements, and <span>certification</span> frameworks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure as Code <span>(</span>IaC<span>)</span>, automation, and configuration management tools</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li><li><p>DoD 8570 <span>Certification</span> such as Security&#43; <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with CI/CD pipeline solutions such as Jenkins, Bamboo, Travis CI, and GitLab</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Kubernetes, containerization, and Cloud platform services</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building Cloud Data Plane and Mission Plane architectures</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> DoD accreditation and Cloud authorization processes</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work through challenging security requirements and maintain compliance in classified environments</p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li><li><p>AWS or Azure <span>Certification</span>s</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Infrastructure Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Infrastructure"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Cloud-Software-Engineer_R0238011-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Cloud-Software-Engineer_R0238011-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"84794439b582f858bc30b9cd1cd848c56d248a7a6bbce89b13998d48d0ecc847","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cloud Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Cloud-Software-Engineer_R0238011-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Cloud-Software-Engineer_R0238011-1","locations":[{"label":"Fort Meade, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0238011","internal_job_id":"bd53c1c4c2e41001eefa10f729da0001","first_published_at":"2026-07-15","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cloud Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof t war e, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a seasoned developer like you with the expertise needed to build sof t war e and systems from vision to production-ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a lead full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll oversee a team as they learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- Experience developing sof t war e using Python or Java\n- Experience in data modeling, including normalization of data and working with met rics\n- Experience developing and maintaining web-based server applications and implementing algorithms that interface with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL\n- Experience developing task automation using AWS API\n- Experience with periodic or streaming data\n- Experience with Linux and shell scripting\n- Ability to design, develop, and implement data processing workflows\n- Ability to develop and optimize data structures within and between routines and for data storage and retrieval using JSON, YAML, or NoSQL Databases\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science field and 14+ years of experience with sof t war e engineering in a Linux environment, or 18+ years of experience with sof t war e engineering in a Linux environment in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with unstructured databases, including Mongo or Elasticsearch, and graph databases, including Neo4J\n- Experience with implementation of test environments for automated code validation\n- Experience working with containers\n- Experience developing CI / CD pipelines with GitLab CI\n- Experience with Infrastructure as Code ( IAC ) and tooling, including Terraform\n- Experience with mono-repo architecture and tooling\n- Experience with Web page design in JavaScript, Angular, or Python Shiny\n- Experience developing pipelines using the AWS API, to include Lambda and Step functions\n- Knowledge of network protocols such as NMP or BGP\n- Ability to work in an ambiguous, fast-paced, highly collaborative, and team-oriented environment and balance long- and short-term taskings\n\nClearance:  \n  Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,800.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cloud Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a seasoned developer like you with the expertise needed to build <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a lead full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll oversee a team as they learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> developing <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e using Python or Java</li><li><span>Experience</span> in data modeling, including normalization of data and working with <span>met</span>rics</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing and maintaining web-based server applications and implementing algorithms that interface with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing task automation using AWS API</li><li><span>Experience</span> with periodic or streaming data</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Linux and shell scripting</li><li><span>Ability to</span> design, develop, and implement data processing workflows</li><li><span>Ability to</span> develop and optimize data structures within and between routines and for data storage and retrieval using JSON, YAML, or NoSQL Databases</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in a Computer Science field and 14&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e engineering in a Linux environment, or 18&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e engineering in a Linux environment in lieu of a degree</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with unstructured databases, including Mongo or Elasticsearch, and graph databases, including Neo4J</li><li><span>Experience</span> with implementation of test environments for automated code validation</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with containers</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines with GitLab CI</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure as Code <span>(</span>IAC<span>)</span> and tooling, including Terraform</li><li><span>Experience</span> with mono-repo architecture and tooling</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Web page design in JavaScript, Angular, or Python Shiny</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing pipelines using the AWS API, to include Lambda and Step functions</li><li><span>Knowledge</span> of network protocols such as NMP or BGP</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work in an ambiguous, fast-paced, highly collaborative, and team-oriented environment and balance long- and short-term taskings</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p> <span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,800.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"26093b433ba1ab6bf0e14a5a067457ee3164ec126d944e0d1a35dbf37647b6eb","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"CMDB and Attack Surface Management Support - ServiceNow Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241487","internal_job_id":"7db64e3672d41001a727714da8fd0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"CMDB and Attack Surface Management Support - ServiceNow Developer The Opportunity:\nIn this role, you'll design and develop ServiceNow solutions that accelerate Booz Allen's CMDB practice and the Attack Surface Management initiatives that depend on it. With millions of CIs in scope, you'll build configured capability: Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items for CMDB requests, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation. You'll partner with the ServiceNow Platform Team, ITSM SMEs, and data source owners to convert CMDB-related initiative needs into working ServiceNow solutions, and you'll contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB priorities allow.\n\nYou'll be a key technical contributor on a team focused on bringing stakeholders together around CMDB data they can rely on and trust. You'll partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for platform-team refinement, and work with application and infrastructure SMEs to reconcile discovered CI data across sources. You'll develop the dashboards, reporting, and Service Catalog capabilities that the Attack Surface Management Working Group and similar CMDB-dependent initiatives need to inform security and operational prioritization. You'll work in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team, augmenting their delivery pipeline and converting initiative demand into ServiceNow-ready work. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n\nDevelopment:\n- Design, configure, and develop ServiceNow CMDB solutions including Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.\n\n- Build Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards that surface CI ownership, completeness, environment classification, health trends, and Attack Surface Management metrics for technical and executive audiences.\n\n- Develop and maintain the CMDB ServiceNow Workspace and Service Catalog items for CMDB-related requests, including new CI registration, ownership change, retirement, and data correction, including form design and the workflows that route them.\n\n- Contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB workload permits, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.\n\nAnalysis and Integration:\n- Monitor CMDB health and CI relationship health using ServiceNow KPIs, evaluate CI class and sub-class data quality, and perform trending analysis to identify where data quality gaps exist.\n\n- Partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for resolution and collaborate with application and infrastructure SMEs and data source owners to reconcile discovered CI data across sources and close data quality gaps at the source.\n\nTranslation and Backlog Support:\n- Translate CMDB-related initiative and governance needs, such as Attack Surface Management, Trusted Enterprise Transformation, and CMDB Health and Workspace governance into ServiceNow-ready business outcomes, requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, and UAT scenarios.\n\n- Support the CMDB enhancement backlog: intake, structure, prioritization support, dependency tracking, and readiness for ServiceNow Platform Team delivery.\n\n- Support implementation readiness for CMDB-related platform enhancements by validating data mappings, field requirements, reporting needs, and stakeholder acceptance through UAT.\n\nKnowledge Transfer:\n- Develop knowledge articles that help stakeholders self-serve and collaborate with other ITSM SMEs to contribute to the ongoing improvement of the CMDB practice.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n \nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience developing and implementing ServiceNow solutions, including configuration of forms, workflows, business rules, script includes, UI policies, and ACLs, including CMDB or CMDB-adjacent functions, such as ITSM, ITOM, or SecOps integration with CMDB\n\n- 3+ years of experience with ServiceNow CMDB operations, CI relationship health, and data quality, including accuracy, completeness, and consistency, with direct responsibility for CMDB data maintenance, quality checks, and remediation\n\n- 2+ years of experience with ServiceNow Discovery in an analyst capacity, including reviewing discovered CI data, identifying pattern or ingestion issues, and reconciling data from multiple sources\n\n- 2+ years of experience building Performance Analytics or Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards\n\n- 2+ years of experience developing ServiceNow Service Catalog items and workflows\n\n- Experience translating operational, security, or governance requirements into ServiceNow-ready user stories, acceptance criteria, dashboards, or UAT plans, and progressing them through Agile delivery, including backlog refinement and sprint planning in Jira or ServiceNow SPM\n\n- Experience with REST and JSON APIs, including with GraphQL\n\n- Experience with ITIL Configuration Management, CSDM framework, and CI lifecycle management principles\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Information Systems or Information Technology\n\n- ServiceNow Certified System Administrator (CSA) Certification and Certified Implementation Specialist – Data Foundations (CIS‑DF) CMDB and CSDM Certification\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience developing Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) rules, including identifier entries, reconciliation rules, and data source precedence for duplicate prevention\n\n- Experience integrating third-party data into the CMDB using Service Graph Connectors or Integration Hub\n\n- Experience with CI Class Manager for CI class, attribute, and relationship model configuration\n\n- Experience with ServiceNow Flow Designer, GlideAjax, and scripted REST APIs in production\n\n- Experience applying the Common Service Data Model (CSDM) methodology in production environments\n\n- Experience with vulnerability data sources integration through ServiceNow Vulnerability Response and vulnerability-to-CI reconciliation in the CMDB\n\n- Possession of strong written communication skills\n\n- ServiceNow Certified Application Developer (CAD) Certification\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"CMDB and Attack Surface Management Support - ServiceNow Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>In this role, you&#39;ll design and develop ServiceNow solutions that accelerate Booz Allen&#39;s CMDB practice and the Attack Surface Management initiatives that depend on it. With millions of CIs in scope, you&#39;ll build configured capability: Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items for CMDB requests, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation. You&#39;ll partner with the ServiceNow Platform Team, ITSM SMEs, and data source owners to convert CMDB-related initiative needs into working ServiceNow solutions, and you&#39;ll contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB priorities allow.</p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll be a key technical contributor on a team focused on bringing stakeholders together around CMDB data they can rely on and trust. You&#39;ll partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for platform-team refinement, and work with application and infrastructure SMEs to reconcile discovered CI data across sources. You&#39;ll develop the dashboards, reporting, and Service Catalog capabilities that the Attack Surface Management Working Group and similar CMDB-dependent initiatives need to inform security and operational prioritization. You&#39;ll work in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team, augmenting their delivery pipeline and converting initiative demand into ServiceNow-ready work. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On:</b></p><p></p><p><b>Development:</b></p><ul><li><p>Design, configure, and develop ServiceNow CMDB solutions including Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.</p></li><li><p>Build Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards that surface CI ownership, completeness, environment classification, health trends, and Attack Surface Management metrics for technical and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p>Develop and maintain the CMDB ServiceNow Workspace and Service Catalog items for CMDB-related requests, including new CI registration, ownership change, retirement, and data correction, including form design and the workflows that route them.</p></li><li><p>Contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB workload permits, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Analysis and Integration:</b></p><ul><li><p>Monitor CMDB health and CI relationship health using ServiceNow KPIs, evaluate CI class and sub-class data quality, and perform trending analysis to identify where data quality gaps exist.</p></li><li><p>Partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for resolution and collaborate with application and infrastructure SMEs and data source owners to reconcile discovered CI data across sources and close data quality gaps at the source.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Translation and Backlog Support:</b></p><ul><li><p>Translate CMDB-related initiative and governance needs, such as Attack Surface Management, Trusted Enterprise Transformation, and CMDB Health and Workspace governance into ServiceNow-ready business outcomes, requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, and UAT scenarios.</p></li><li><p>Support the CMDB enhancement backlog: intake, structure, prioritization support, dependency tracking, and readiness for ServiceNow Platform Team delivery.</p></li><li><p>Support implementation readiness for CMDB-related platform enhancements by validating data mappings, field requirements, reporting needs, and stakeholder acceptance through UAT.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Knowledge Transfer:</b></p><ul><li><p>Develop knowledge articles that help stakeholders self-serve and collaborate with other ITSM SMEs to contribute to the ongoing improvement of the CMDB practice.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p><span> </span></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience developing and implementing ServiceNow solutions, including configuration of forms, workflows, business rules, script includes, UI policies, and ACLs, including CMDB or CMDB-adjacent functions, such as ITSM, ITOM, or SecOps integration with CMDB</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with ServiceNow CMDB operations, CI relationship health, and data quality, including accuracy, completeness, and consistency, with direct responsibility for CMDB data maintenance, quality checks, and remediation</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with ServiceNow Discovery in an analyst capacity, including reviewing discovered CI data, identifying pattern or ingestion issues, and reconciling data from multiple sources</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience building Performance Analytics or Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience developing ServiceNow Service Catalog items and workflows</p></li><li><p>Experience translating operational, security, or governance requirements into ServiceNow-ready user stories, acceptance criteria, dashboards, or UAT plans, and progressing them through Agile delivery, including backlog refinement and sprint planning in Jira or ServiceNow SPM</p></li><li><p>Experience with REST and JSON APIs, including with GraphQL</p></li><li><p>Experience with ITIL Configuration Management, CSDM framework, and CI lifecycle management principles</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Information Systems or Information Technology</p></li><li><p>ServiceNow Certified System Administrator (CSA) Certification and Certified Implementation Specialist – Data Foundations (CIS‑DF) CMDB and CSDM Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p>Experience developing Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) rules, including identifier entries, reconciliation rules, and data source precedence for duplicate prevention</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating third-party data into the CMDB using Service Graph Connectors or Integration Hub</p></li><li><p>Experience with CI Class Manager for CI class, attribute, and relationship model configuration</p></li><li><p>Experience with ServiceNow Flow Designer, GlideAjax, and scripted REST APIs in production</p></li><li><p>Experience applying the Common Service Data Model (CSDM) methodology in production environments</p></li><li><p>Experience with vulnerability data sources integration through ServiceNow Vulnerability Response and vulnerability-to-CI reconciliation in the CMDB</p></li><li><p>Possession of strong written communication skills</p></li><li><p>ServiceNow Certified Application Developer (CAD) Certification</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226191-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226191-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"d2b7db283107051688f8bbc69db758df000353620a9c9867c54a904c0f9ced07","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"CNO Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226191-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226191-1","locations":[{"label":"Annapolis Junction, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0226191","internal_job_id":"0ed37d244bf8100200761475746b0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-23","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"CNO Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a computer network operations (CNO) specialist, you know that embedded and application developers, reverse engineers, and vulnerability analysts all play key roles in the CNO capability development life cycle. We’re looking for someone like you to flex your problem-solving prowess in a rapidly evolving systems security research and development environment.  \n\nAs a senior CNO capability development specialist on our team, you’ll support full project life cycles. Guiding an Agile team of professionals, you’ll manage reverse engineering and vulnerability analyses of various software problems. You’ll inform operational parameters for complex systems and leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning to influence the delivery of your work. Using your network operations expertise, you’ll determine what the art of the possible is and what can be done—and then you’ll bring it to life for your clients. \n\nHelp us combat the most advanced adversaries and defend national security.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 6+ years of experience in programming with object-oriented programming languages\n\n- 4+ years of experience with developing Windows applications using Visual Studio or .NET environments or developing UNIX applications using make files or a build environment\n\n- Experience with developing complex programs using C, C#, C++, or Java\n\n- Experience with implementing software life cycle management requirements, including design, develop, test, validate, or deploy\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science and 1+ year of experience with embedded development, or 4+ years of experience with embedded development in lieu of a degree\n\n  \nNice If You Have:    \n- 3+ years of experience with computer programming in C, C++, Python, Assembly, or PerlScript   \n\n- 2+ years of experience with computer engineering, computer science, electronic and electrical engineering, or applied mathematics   \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"CNO Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As a computer network operations (CNO) specialist, you know that embedded and application developers, reverse engineers, and vulnerability analysts all play key roles in the CNO capability development life cycle. We’re looking for someone like you to flex your problem-solving prowess in a rapidly evolving systems security research and development environment.  </p><p></p><p>As a senior CNO capability development specialist on our team, you’ll support full project life cycles. Guiding an Agile team of professionals, you’ll manage reverse engineering and vulnerability analyses of various software problems. You’ll inform operational parameters for complex systems and leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning to influence the delivery of your work. Using your network operations expertise, you’ll determine what the art of the possible is and what can be done—and then you’ll bring it to life for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Help us combat the most advanced adversaries and defend national security.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span>6&#43; years of experience in programming with object-oriented programming languages</span></p></li><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience with developing Windows applications using Visual Studio or .NET environments or developing UNIX applications using make files or a build environment</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with developing complex programs using C, C#, C&#43;&#43;, or Java</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with implementing software life cycle management requirements, including design, develop, test, validate, or deploy</span></p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science and 1&#43; year of experience with embedded development, or 4&#43; years of experience with embedded development in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p>  </p><p><b>Nice If You Have:    </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with computer programming in C, C&#43;&#43;, Python, Assembly, or PerlScript   </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with computer engineering, computer science, electronic and electrical engineering, or applied mathematics   </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226192","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226192","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"702569231a580aa66a6758296e2e78d891743e9b8a35e29f03c779ca223aa618","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"CNO Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226192","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226192","locations":[{"label":"Annapolis Junction, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0226192","internal_job_id":"0ed37d244bf8100200bbe55a6f890000","first_published_at":"2026-07-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"CNO Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a computer network operations (CNO) specialist, you know that embedded and application developers, reverse engineers, and vulnerability analysts all play key roles in the CNO capability development life cycle. We’re looking for someone like you to flex your problem-solving prowess in a rapidly evolving systems security research and development environment.  \n\nAs a senior CNO capability development specialist on our team, you’ll support full project life cycles. Guiding an Agile team of professionals, you’ll manage reverse engineering and vulnerability analyses of various software problems. You’ll inform operational parameters for complex systems and leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning to influence the delivery of your work. Using your network operations expertise, you’ll determine what the art of the possible is and what can be done—and then you’ll bring it to life for your clients. \n\nHelp us combat the most advanced adversaries and defend national security.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 6+ years of experience in programming with object-oriented programming languages\n\n- 4+ years of experience with developing Windows applications using Visual Studio or .NET environments or developing UNIX applications using make files or a build environment\n\n- Experience with developing complex programs using C, C#, C++, or Java\n\n- Experience with implementing software life cycle management requirements, including design, develop, test, validate, or deploy\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science and 1+ year of experience with embedded development, or 4+ years of experience with embedded development in lieu of a degree\n\n  \nNice If You Have:    \n- 3+ years of experience with computer programming in C, C++, Python, Assembly, or PerlScript   \n\n- 2+ years of experience with computer engineering, computer science, electronic and electrical engineering, or applied mathematics   \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"CNO Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As a computer network operations (CNO) specialist, you know that embedded and application developers, reverse engineers, and vulnerability analysts all play key roles in the CNO capability development life cycle. We’re looking for someone like you to flex your problem-solving prowess in a rapidly evolving systems security research and development environment.  </p><p></p><p>As a senior CNO capability development specialist on our team, you’ll support full project life cycles. Guiding an Agile team of professionals, you’ll manage reverse engineering and vulnerability analyses of various software problems. You’ll inform operational parameters for complex systems and leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning to influence the delivery of your work. Using your network operations expertise, you’ll determine what the art of the possible is and what can be done—and then you’ll bring it to life for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Help us combat the most advanced adversaries and defend national security.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span>6&#43; years of experience in programming with object-oriented programming languages</span></p></li><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience with developing Windows applications using Visual Studio or .NET environments or developing UNIX applications using make files or a build environment</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with developing complex programs using C, C#, C&#43;&#43;, or Java</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with implementing software life cycle management requirements, including design, develop, test, validate, or deploy</span></p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science and 1&#43; year of experience with embedded development, or 4&#43; years of experience with embedded development in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p>  </p><p><b>Nice If You Have:    </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with computer programming in C, C&#43;&#43;, Python, Assembly, or PerlScript   </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with computer engineering, computer science, electronic and electrical engineering, or applied mathematics   </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226193","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226193","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"dc7b2c1eb1720637e7674ee1295ab8568b04dd3ce4827caade72d0f91b9d240e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"CNO Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226193","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/CNO-Developer_R0226193","locations":[{"label":"Annapolis Junction, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0226193","internal_job_id":"0ed37d244bf81002017db86b84140000","first_published_at":"2026-07-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"CNO Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a computer network operations (CNO) specialist, you know that embedded and application developers, reverse engineers, and vulnerability analysts all play key roles in the CNO capability development life cycle. We’re looking for someone like you to flex your problem-solving prowess in a rapidly evolving systems security research and development environment.  \n\nAs a senior CNO capability development specialist on our team, you’ll support full project life cycles. Guiding an Agile team of professionals, you’ll manage reverse engineering and vulnerability analyses of various software problems. You’ll inform operational parameters for complex systems and leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning to influence the delivery of your work. Using your network operations expertise, you’ll determine what the art of the possible is and what can be done—and then you’ll bring it to life for your clients. \n\nHelp us combat the most advanced adversaries and defend national security.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 6+ years of experience in programming with object-oriented programming languages\n\n- 4+ years of experience with developing Windows applications using Visual Studio or .NET environments or developing UNIX applications using make files or a build environment\n\n- Experience with developing complex programs using C, C#, C++, or Java\n\n- Experience with implementing software life cycle management requirements, including design, develop, test, validate, or deploy\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science and 1+ year of experience with embedded development, or 4+ years of experience with embedded development in lieu of a degree\n\n  \nNice If You Have:    \n- 3+ years of experience with computer programming in C, C++, Python, Assembly, or PerlScript   \n\n- 2+ years of experience with computer engineering, computer science, electronic and electrical engineering, or applied mathematics   \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"CNO Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As a computer network operations (CNO) specialist, you know that embedded and application developers, reverse engineers, and vulnerability analysts all play key roles in the CNO capability development life cycle. We’re looking for someone like you to flex your problem-solving prowess in a rapidly evolving systems security research and development environment.  </p><p></p><p>As a senior CNO capability development specialist on our team, you’ll support full project life cycles. Guiding an Agile team of professionals, you’ll manage reverse engineering and vulnerability analyses of various software problems. You’ll inform operational parameters for complex systems and leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning to influence the delivery of your work. Using your network operations expertise, you’ll determine what the art of the possible is and what can be done—and then you’ll bring it to life for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Help us combat the most advanced adversaries and defend national security.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span>6&#43; years of experience in programming with object-oriented programming languages</span></p></li><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience with developing Windows applications using Visual Studio or .NET environments or developing UNIX applications using make files or a build environment</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with developing complex programs using C, C#, C&#43;&#43;, or Java</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with implementing software life cycle management requirements, including design, develop, test, validate, or deploy</span></p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science and 1&#43; year of experience with embedded development, or 4&#43; years of experience with embedded development in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p>  </p><p><b>Nice If You Have:    </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with computer programming in C, C&#43;&#43;, Python, Assembly, or PerlScript   </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with computer engineering, computer science, electronic and electrical engineering, or applied mathematics   </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matc