n- Apply deep learning approaches, including transformer‑based architectures such as DINO, CLIP, or SAM, to image understanding problems\n\n- Integrate classical estimation methods, such as Kalman‑family filters with modern deep learning workflows to support real‑time algorithm development\n\n- Contribute to GPU‑accelerated model development using CUDA, RAPIDS, or vendor‑provided inference runtimes\n\n- Collaborate with multidisciplinary engineering teams to test, refine, and operationalize computer vision models for constrained compute or real‑time environments\n\n- Support the implementation of microservice‑based inference pipelines or containerized model deployments under senior guidance\n\n- Contribute to the architecture and implementation of novel single and multi-sensor platform detection and tracking algorithms and track fusion of targets\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience developing computer vision algorithms for detection, tracking, or sensor‑based analytics in remote sensing or GEOINT‑relevant environments\n\n- 1+ years of experience applying deep learning to CV problems using transformer‑based, self‑supervised, or contrastive learning architectures, such as DINO, CLIP, or SAM\n\n- Experience building pipelines in Python or C++ for algorithm development, training, evaluation, or deployment\n\n- Experience with GPU‑accelerated workflows\n\n- Experience with classical tracking and estimation methods, such as Kalman or extended Kalman filters, supporting real‑time development needs\n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience in GPU programming, including CUDA or RAPIDs\n\n- Experience with developing synthetic modeling of Kinematic target features \n\n- Experience with AI‑augmented development workflows or agentic tools, such as Codex, Claude Code, or OpenCode or other multi-agent approach\n\n- Knowledge of modern software design patterns, including micro-service design and orchestration in Kubernetes deployment\n\n- Master’s degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, AI/ML, Physics, Mathematics or other related field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Computer Vision Software Engineer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity</b></p><p>Join a mission‑focused engineering team building advanced computer vision (CV), multi‑sensor fusion, and detection and tracking capabilities for remote sensing and GEOINT environments. As a Mid‑Level Computer Vision Engineer, you will design, implement, and optimize CV algorithms and deep learning pipelines, contributing to operational systems used across national security missions. You will work closely with senior engineers while owning well‑defined components of the technical solution.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On: </b></p><ul><li><p>Develop and implement computer vision algorithms for target detection, characterization, and tracking across single‑ and multi‑sensor data</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain model training, evaluation, and deployment pipelines in Python or C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p>Apply deep learning approaches, including transformer‑based architectures such as DINO, CLIP, or SAM, to image understanding problems</p></li><li><p>Integrate classical estimation methods, such as Kalman‑family filters with modern deep learning workflows to support real‑time algorithm development</p></li><li><p>Contribute to GPU‑accelerated model development using CUDA, RAPIDS, or vendor‑provided inference runtimes</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with multidisciplinary engineering teams to test, refine, and operationalize computer vision models for constrained compute or real‑time environments</p></li><li><p>Support the implementation of microservice‑based inference pipelines or containerized model deployments under senior guidance</p></li><li><p>Contribute to the architecture and implementation of novel single and multi-sensor platform detection and tracking algorithms and track fusion of targets</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience developing computer vision algorithms for detection, tracking, or sensor‑based analytics in remote sensing or GEOINT‑relevant environments</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience applying deep learning to CV problems using transformer‑based, self‑supervised, or contrastive learning architectures, such as DINO, CLIP, or SAM</p></li><li><p>Experience building pipelines in Python or C&#43;&#43; for algorithm development, training, evaluation, or deployment</p></li><li><p>Experience with GPU‑accelerated workflows</p></li><li><p>Experience with classical tracking and estimation methods, such as Kalman or extended Kalman filters, supporting real‑time development needs</p></li><li><p>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in GPU programming, including CUDA or RAPIDs</p></li><li><p>Experience with developing synthetic modeling of Kinematic target features </p></li><li><p>Experience with AI‑augmented development workflows or agentic tools, such as Codex, Claude Code, or OpenCode or other multi-agent approach</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modern software design patterns, including micro-service design and orchestration in Kubernetes deployment</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, AI/ML, Physics, Mathematics or other related field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Augusta-GA/Cyber-Training-Developer_R0246545","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Augusta-GA/Cyber-Training-Developer_R0246545","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"92b29c4be1a7bb30a781f203da121bec35d60683f1617c06c3d3a226dd11055e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cyber Training Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Augusta-GA/Cyber-Training-Developer_R0246545","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Augusta-GA/Cyber-Training-Developer_R0246545","locations":[{"label":"Augusta, GA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246545","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d010010cff6b3f22930000","first_published_at":"2026-08-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cyber Training Developer The Opportunity:\nDrive a multi-year technical training and assessment program. Leverage instructional systems design strategies and computer network operations experience to help magnify clients’ cyber training capabilities. Collaborate with military leadership, technical experts, and operational colleagues. Build, validate, implement, and evaluate critical training programs for advanced learners who are motivated to grow their skillset. Train developers as part of a collaborative multidisciplinary team producing highly sophisticated, technical, hands-on training solutions to meet the mission and time-critical needs of our client. Assist in providing classroom instruction that teaches assigned students in the manner described in the Program of Instruction. Utilize your operational experience to foster a team environment of learning, progress, and excellence and help us build the next generation of cyber warriors.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience in Computer Network Exploitation (CNE) or Offensive Cyberspace Operations (OCO)\n\n- 2+ years of experience with development, testing, management, operations, or training of networked hardware and software systems\n\n- Experience creating and configuring virtual hosts and networks using VMware in support of training content development or instructional scenarios\n\n- Experience with the development, deployment, operations, maintenance, training, or administration of Windows or Unix-based operating systems\n\n- Experience with assessing student understanding, skills, and abilities to gauge proficiency in the subject\n\n- Ability to translate complex concepts or data into graphically appealing and easy-to-understand presentations for a broad range of audiences\n\n- Ability to navigate in an ambiguous, matrixed environment with multiple stakeholders\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS Diploma/GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 2+ years of experience with teaching cyberspace operations in a formal classroom setting\n\n- Experience developing training evaluation metrics\n\n- Knowledge of commonly used software-programming languages such as, Python, PERL, shell scripting, or others\n\n- Ability to build consensus and effective cross-functional relationships\n\n- Ability to adapt content development and delivery to a variety of audiences\n\n- Possession of excellent oral and written communication skills\n\n- Possession of excellent organizational, project management, analytical, problem-solving, and client-management skills\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cyber Training Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Drive a multi-year technical training and assessment program. Leverage instructional systems design strategies and computer network operations experience to help magnify clients’ cyber training capabilities. Collaborate with military leadership, technical experts, and operational colleagues. Build, validate, implement, and evaluate critical training programs for advanced learners who are motivated to grow their skillset. Train developers as part of a collaborative multidisciplinary team producing highly sophisticated, technical, hands-on training solutions to meet the mission and time-critical needs of our client. Assist in providing classroom instruction that teaches assigned students in the manner described in the Program of Instruction. Utilize your operational experience to foster a team environment of learning, progress, and excellence and help us build the next generation of cyber warriors.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience in Computer Network Exploitation (CNE) or Offensive Cyberspace Operations (OCO)</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with development, testing, management, operations, or training of networked hardware and software systems</p></li><li><p>Experience creating and configuring virtual hosts and networks using VMware in support of training content development or instructional scenarios</p></li><li><p>Experience with the development, deployment, operations, maintenance, training, or administration of Windows or Unix-based operating systems</p></li><li><p>Experience with assessing student understanding, skills, and abilities to gauge proficiency in the subject</p></li><li><p>Ability to translate complex concepts or data into graphically appealing and easy-to-understand presentations for a broad range of audiences</p></li><li><p>Ability to navigate in an ambiguous, matrixed environment with multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>HS Diploma/GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with teaching cyberspace operations in a formal classroom setting</p></li><li><p>Experience developing training evaluation metrics</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of commonly used software-programming languages such as, Python, PERL, shell scripting, or others</p></li><li><p>Ability to build consensus and effective cross-functional relationships</p></li><li><p>Ability to adapt content development and delivery to a variety of audiences</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent oral and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent organizational, project management, analytical, problem-solving, and client-management skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Analytics-Platform-Engineer_R0237532","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Analytics-Platform-Engineer_R0237532","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"2cd3e9a81139ab21934a077b5e551b5860370511e20db4fcb1c3e54b77089587","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Analytics Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Analytics-Platform-Engineer_R0237532","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Analytics-Platform-Engineer_R0237532","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0237532","internal_job_id":"4541fb2b67011001fcb9cc9c262a0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Analytics Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience with data lake or analytics platforms\n\n- 1+ years of experience designing data pipeline architectures for security operations, including log collection, normalization, enrichment and routing\n\n- 1+ years of experience with defensive cyber operations, cybersecurity engineering or security platform architecture\n\n- Experience architecting detection engineering pipelines, threat hunting workflows or automated response capabilities\n\n- Experience deploying platforms across cloud, on-premises and disconnected environments\n\n- Knowledge of Zero Trust principles, DoD and IC Cybersecurity frameworks or federal compliance standards\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Windows or Linux administration activities\n\n- Experience with stream processing or data brokering platforms such as Cribl, Kafka, Logstash or Fluentd\n\n- Experience with threat detection or anomaly-based behavioral analysis\n\n- Experience with DevSecOps CI/CD pipelines in IL5, IL6 or IL7 environments\n\n- Experience with Python or scripting languages for security automation\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Analytics Platform Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with data lake or analytics platforms</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience designing data pipeline architectures for security operations, including log collection, normalization, enrichment and routing</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience with defensive cyber operations, cybersecurity engineering or security platform architecture</p></li><li><p>Experience architecting detection engineering pipelines, threat hunting workflows or automated response capabilities</p></li><li><p>Experience deploying platforms across cloud, on-premises and disconnected environments</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Zero Trust principles, DoD and IC Cybersecurity frameworks or federal compliance standards</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Windows or Linux administration activities</p></li><li><p>Experience with stream processing or data brokering platforms such as Cribl, Kafka, Logstash or Fluentd</p></li><li><p>Experience with threat detection or anomaly-based behavioral analysis</p></li><li><p>Experience with DevSecOps CI/CD pipelines in IL5, IL6 or IL7 environments</p></li><li><p>Experience with Python or scripting languages for security automation</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Alexandria-VA/Database-Developer--Mid_R0247319","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Alexandria-VA/Database-Developer--Mid_R0247319","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6c75020bb4800433588cd3d804009961d5a3dc77a6e8562a3e2fad0f76c42732","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Database Developer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Database-Developer--Mid_R0247319","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Database-Developer--Mid_R0247319","locations":[{"label":"Alexandria, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247319","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e100119ddcbaa95dd0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Database Developer, Mid The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for an Oracle Database Developer who also has experience working hand in hand with clients to develop impactful solutions. In this role you understand the system’s data, technology, and business rules. Your combination of people skills and technical knowledge provides the perfect combination to help clients define database requirements, identify needed system improvements, and overcome their most difficult challenges to achieve complete and accurate systems.\n\nOn our team, you’ll develop and maintain database features, custom reports, and queries in an agile environment. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. You’ll also understand the business and user needs clearly to be a key team member who helps fulfill these needs by creating deployable features. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop software, but drive the requirements to create a system, we need you on our team. \n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nWhat You'll Work On:\n- Collaborate with stakeholders to elicit and document business requirements and translate them for technical teams.\n\n- Analyze information to identify, plan, and design enhancements and modifications to an existing database application.\n\n- Design, develop, and modify database software including database structure, reports, views, and packages.\n\n- Develop RESTful services and APIs to share data across systems and organizations.\n\n- Modify templates and develop ETL scripts to load data into the database.\n\nYou Have: \n- 4+ years of experience developing database source code for software applications through the full software development lifecycle\n\n- 4+ years of experience with professional software development using Oracle, SQL, and PL/SQL\n\n- 4+ years of experience building and consuming RESTful APIs and webservices with attention to secure and efficient data exchange\n\n- 4+ years of experience working with Agile software development methodologies and stakeholders to elicit and document business requirements and translate them for technical teams\n\n- Experience with developing and maintaining custom reports and queries using PL or SQL\n\n- Experience in data analysis, data migrations, and data modeling\n\n- Experience with writing scripts to support DDL and DML operations and SQL database query optimization or performance tuning\n\n- Experience managing requirements within project tracking and collaboration tools such as Jira and Confluence\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or an analytical, scientific, or technical field\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience presenting to client teams\n\n- Experience with source control systems, including Git\n\n- Experience working with Oracle Spatial and geodatabases\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Database Developer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for an Oracle Database Developer who also has experience working hand in hand with clients to develop impactful solutions. In this role you understand the system’s data, technology, and business rules. Your combination of people skills and technical knowledge provides the perfect combination to help clients define database requirements, identify needed system improvements, and overcome their most difficult challenges to achieve complete and accurate systems.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll develop and maintain database features, custom reports, and queries in an agile environment. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. You’ll also understand the business and user needs clearly to be a key team member who helps fulfill these needs by creating deployable features. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop software, but drive the requirements to create a system, we need you on our team. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>Collaborate with stakeholders to elicit and document business requirements and translate them for technical teams.</p></li><li><p>Analyze information to identify, plan, and design enhancements and modifications to an existing database application.</p></li><li><p>Design, develop, and modify database software including database structure, reports, views, and packages.</p></li><li><p>Develop RESTful services and APIs to share data across systems and organizations.</p></li><li><p>Modify templates and develop ETL scripts to load data into the database.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>4&#43; years of experience developing database source code for software applications through the full software development lifecycle</p></li><li><p>4&#43; years of experience with professional software development using Oracle, SQL, and PL/SQL</p></li><li><p>4&#43; years of experience building and consuming RESTful APIs and webservices with attention to secure and efficient data exchange</p></li><li><p>4&#43; years of experience working with Agile software development methodologies and stakeholders to elicit and document business requirements and translate them for technical teams</p></li><li><p>Experience with developing and maintaining custom reports and queries using PL or SQL</p></li><li><p>Experience in data analysis, data migrations, and data modeling</p></li><li><p>Experience with writing scripts to support DDL and DML operations and SQL database query optimization or performance tuning</p></li><li><p>Experience managing requirements within project tracking and collaboration tools such as Jira and Confluence</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or an analytical, scientific, or technical field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience presenting to client teams</p></li><li><p>Experience with source control systems, including Git</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Oracle Spatial and geodatabases</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0242440","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0242440","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"a9605ebfb8f6870b4a37a1e4cba806875f1cf9f3f456b6f7021828e68df53a9a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"DevOps Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0242440","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0242440","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"Eglin AFB, FL"},{"label":"Hill AFB, UT"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242440","internal_job_id":"4ef4330bf513100151ba44cb245a0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"DevOps Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to make a difference? What if you could find a position that is tailor made for your mix of develop ment, engineering, and communication skills ? Efficient sof tware develop ment teams make the most of their time by limiting the activities that take develop ers away from writing their code. That’s why we need you, an experience d DevSecOps engineer, to help us shorten the time it takes to get critical tools develop ed and into the hands of digital citizen s and mission workers who need them to drive innovation in the nation.\n\nAs a DevSecOps engineer on our team, you’ll use your develop ment experience to streamline our sof tware develop ment lifecycle from requirements to monitoring in production. You’ll incorporate open-source tools, automation, and cloud resources to cut down on tedious, boring tasks and free up the team’s develop ers to do what they do best – innovate. You’ll implement continuous integration and delivery to limit manual testing and troubleshooting. This is an opportunity to build your experience in modern, cloud native sof tware develop ment.\n\nYou’ll work in a dynamic, large team environment supporting a large–scale government program, using next–gen tools, standards, and processes, including Kubernetes, GitLab CI, Ansible, CloudFormation, Terraform, Terragrunt, and Python. In this role, you’ll design and develop DevOps pipeline to drive rapid delivery of functionality using CI / CD tools like GitLab, Jenkins, Ansible, or AWS CodeDeploy. You’ll use state of the art diagnostic tools and monitoring systems to provide analysis on Web application errors, including the identification and investigation of application behavior through code and log analysis and business logic.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have :\n- 2+ years of experience in an Infrastructure, DevOps, or Site Reliability Engineer role\n- 2+ years of experience deploying containerized applications\n- 2+ years of experience with Amazon Web Services ( AWS )\n- Experience with Kubernetes\n- Experience with Agile met hods and practices\n- Experience with Infrastructure as Code, including Terraform, or Configuration as Code, including Ansible\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 IAT Level II or IAT Level III Certification within 30 days of hire date\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with AI / ML / LLM implementations \n- Experience with AI / ML / LLM security such as Hidden Layer\n- Experience automating, monitoring and troubleshooting Kubernetes clusters in a production environment\n- Experience with GitOps tooling including Flux or Argo CD and Kustomize\n- Experience implementing Cloud-Native solutions to accelerate application develop ment\n- Experience with Identity Authentication and Authorization, including Single-Sign-On, SAML, or OpenID\n- Knowledge of Linux or UNIX administration and automation\n- Bachelor's degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Statistics, or Engineering\n- AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Asso cia te Certification or AWS Certified Develop er - Asso cia te Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"DevOps Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to make a difference? What if you could find a position that is tailor made for your mix of <span>develop</span>ment, engineering, and communication <span>skills</span>? Efficient <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment teams make the most of their time by limiting the activities that take <span>develop</span>ers away from writing their code. That’s why we need you, an <span>experience</span>d DevSecOps engineer, to help us shorten the time it takes to get critical tools <span>develop</span>ed and into the hands of digital <span>citizen</span>s and mission workers who need them to drive innovation in the nation.</p><p></p><p>As a DevSecOps engineer on our team, you’ll use your <span>develop</span>ment <span>experience</span> to streamline our <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment lifecycle from requirements to monitoring in production. You’ll incorporate open-source tools, automation, and cloud resources to cut down on tedious, boring tasks and free up the team’s <span>develop</span>ers to do what they do best – innovate. You’ll implement continuous integration and delivery to limit manual testing and troubleshooting. This is an opportunity to build your <span>experience</span> in modern, cloud native <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment.</p><p></p><p>You’ll work in a dynamic, large team environment supporting a large–scale government program, using next–gen tools, standards, and processes, including Kubernetes, GitLab CI, Ansible, CloudFormation, Terraform, Terragrunt, and Python. In this role, you’ll design and <span>develop</span> DevOps pipeline to drive rapid delivery of functionality using CI<span>/</span>CD tools like GitLab, Jenkins, Ansible, or AWS CodeDeploy. You’ll use state of the art diagnostic tools and monitoring systems to provide analysis on Web application errors, including the identification and investigation of application behavior through code and log analysis and business logic.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have</span></b><span>:</span></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in an Infrastructure, DevOps, or Site Reliability Engineer role</li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> deploying containerized applications</li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Amazon Web Services <span>(</span>AWS<span>)</span></li><li><span>Experience</span> with Kubernetes</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hods and practices</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure as Code, including Terraform, or Configuration as Code, including Ansible</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></li><li><span>Ability to</span> obtain a DoD 8570 IAT Level II or IAT Level III <span>Certification</span> within 30 days of hire date</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with AI<span>/</span>ML<span>/</span>LLM implementations </li><li><span>Experience</span> with AI<span>/</span>ML<span>/</span>LLM security such as Hidden Layer</li><li><span>Experience</span> automating, monitoring and troubleshooting Kubernetes clusters in a production environment</li><li><span>Experience</span> with GitOps tooling including Flux or Argo CD and Kustomize</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing Cloud-Native solutions to accelerate application <span>develop</span>ment</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Identity Authentication and Authorization, including Single-Sign-On, SAML, or OpenID</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Linux or UNIX administration and automation</li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in CS, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Statistics, or Engineering</li><li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Asso<span>cia</span>te <span>Certification</span> or AWS Certified <span>Develop</span>er - Asso<span>cia</span>te <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0243162","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0243162","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"27b610576fabeaea79bcf58b64ccb748544d03b151b0404cfc93caea1f6bf2b9","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"DevOps Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0243162","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0243162","locations":[{"label":"Rome, NY"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243162","internal_job_id":"95d6bbf60dad1001f7cfd3433ab60000","first_published_at":"2026-06-26","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"DevOps Platform Engineer The Opportunity:  \nToday’s dynamic technology landscape demands constant and rapid innovation. To facilitate this transformation, we must ensure continuous integration and application development. That’s why we need an experience d DevOps engineer like you who’s eager to design, test, and program critical applications for our clients who need them most.\n\nAs a sof tware factory DevOps Platform Engineer on our team, you’ll support our sof tware development from requirements to testing in production. You’ll incorporate automation and cloud resources to minimize repetitive tasks and free up the team’s developers to do what they do best—innovate. You’ll work together with fellow professionals to implement continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) to limit manual testing and troubleshooting.\n\nThis is an opportunity to broaden your experience in sof tware engineering while helping to develop sof tware that will completely transform workflows and make a real impact. Here, we invest in technology, and we’ll invest in you. With access to continuing education resources, tuition assistance opportunities, and technology development programs, you’ll keep your skills sharp as you work at the leading edge of technology.\n\nWork with us as we build and test tools to transform the future.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience maintaining and deploying production-grade containerized applications through DevOps practices\n\n- Experience with CI / CD and developer workflow automation, including GitHub Actions, GitLab, GitBash, Git, AWS CodeStar, or CodePipeline\n\n- Experience with containerization, including Docker\n\n- Experience troubleshooting platform application deployments and configurations\n\n- Ability to work with IaC, including Terraform or Ansible\n\n- Ability to work with Cloud, including AWS or Azure\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Cloud and Network Security architecture, including least privilege in IAM, secrets management, Role-Based Access Control  ( RBAC ) , or Boundary Protection\n\n- Experience with concepts of Service Meshes such as Istio or AWS App Mesh\n\n- Experience with Pro met heus, Grafana, or Keycloak\n\n- Experience with Cloud-Native servers, Kubernetes platforms, and container registries\n\n- Experience with hardened AMIs and container images, including DoD STIGs or CIS Benchmarks\n\n- Experience with APM, including Datadog, New Relic, or Splunk\n\n- Experience in Rancher services, including RKE2\n\n- Experience with Identity Authentication and Authorization, including Single-Sign-On, SAML, or OpenID\n\n- Experience in Active Directory and GPO configuration and management\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"DevOps Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b> <br />Today’s dynamic technology landscape demands constant and rapid innovation. To facilitate this transformation, we must ensure continuous integration and application development. That’s why we need an <span>experience</span>d DevOps engineer like you who’s eager to design, test, and program critical applications for our clients who need them most.</p><p></p><p>As a <span>sof</span>tware factory DevOps Platform Engineer on our team, you’ll support our <span>sof</span>tware development from requirements to testing in production. You’ll incorporate automation and cloud resources to minimize repetitive tasks and free up the team’s developers to do what they do best—innovate. You’ll work together with fellow professionals to implement continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) to limit manual testing and troubleshooting.</p><p></p><p>This is an opportunity to broaden your <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering while helping to develop <span>sof</span>tware that will completely transform workflows and make a real impact. Here, we invest in technology, and we’ll invest in you. With access to continuing education resources, tuition assistance opportunities, and technology development programs, you’ll keep your skills sharp as you work at the leading edge of technology.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we build and test tools to transform the future.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> maintaining and deploying production-grade containerized applications through DevOps practices</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD and developer workflow automation, including GitHub Actions, GitLab, GitBash, Git, AWS CodeStar, or CodePipeline</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with containerization, including Docker</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> troubleshooting platform application deployments and configurations</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with IaC, including Terraform or Ansible</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with Cloud, including AWS or Azure</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud and Network Security architecture, including least privilege in IAM, secrets management, Role-Based Access Control <span>(</span>RBAC<span>)</span>, or Boundary Protection</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with concepts of Service Meshes such as Istio or AWS App Mesh</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Pro<span>met</span>heus, Grafana, or Keycloak</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud-Native servers, Kubernetes platforms, and container registries</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with hardened AMIs and container images, including DoD STIGs or CIS Benchmarks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with APM, including Datadog, New Relic, or Splunk</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in Rancher services, including RKE2</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Identity Authentication and Authorization, including Single-Sign-On, SAML, or OpenID</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in Active Directory and GPO configuration and management</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> TS/SCI<span> clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0247201","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0247201","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"60b5253956ea341d9216432707cdef9b4d2e5b7cf5d912a5388955868ab063c0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"DevOps Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0247201","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/DevOps-Platform-Engineer_R0247201","locations":[{"label":"Rome, NY"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247201","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d14610010375e5b179210000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"DevOps Platform Engineer The Opportunity:  \nToday’s dynamic technology landscape demands constant and rapid innovation. To facilitate this transformation, we must ensure continuous integration and application development. That’s why we need an experience d DevOps engineer like you who’s eager to design, test, and program critical applications for our clients who need them most.\n\nAs a sof tware factory DevOps Platform Engineer on our team, you’ll support our sof tware development from requirements to testing in production. You’ll incorporate automation and cloud resources to minimize repetitive tasks and free up the team’s developers to do what they do best—innovate. You’ll work together with fellow professionals to implement continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) to limit manual testing and troubleshooting.\n\nThis is an opportunity to broaden your experience in sof tware engineering while helping to develop sof tware that will completely transform workflows and make a real impact. Here, we invest in technology, and we’ll invest in you. With access to continuing education resources, tuition assistance opportunities, and technology development programs, you’ll keep your skills sharp as you work at the leading edge of technology.\n\nWork with us as we build and test tools to transform the future.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience maintaining and deploying production-grade containerized applications through DevOps practices\n\n- Experience with CI / CD and developer workflow automation, including GitHub Actions, GitLab, GitBash, Git, AWS CodeStar, or CodePipeline\n\n- Experience with containerization, including Docker\n\n- Experience troubleshooting platform application deployments and configurations\n\n- Ability to work with IaC, including Terraform or Ansible\n\n- Ability to work with Cloud, including AWS or Azure\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Cloud and Network Security architecture, including least privilege in IAM, secrets management, Role-Based Access Control  ( RBAC ) , or Boundary Protection\n\n- Experience with concepts of Service Meshes such as Istio or AWS App Mesh\n\n- Experience with Pro met heus, Grafana, or Keycloak\n\n- Experience with Cloud-Native servers, Kubernetes platforms, and container registries\n\n- Experience with hardened AMIs and container images, including DoD STIGs or CIS Benchmarks\n\n- Experience with APM, including Datadog, New Relic, or Splunk\n\n- Experience in Rancher services, including RKE2\n\n- Experience with Identity Authentication and Authorization, including Single-Sign-On, SAML, or OpenID\n\n- Experience in Active Directory and GPO configuration and management\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"DevOps Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b> <br />Today’s dynamic technology landscape demands constant and rapid innovation. To facilitate this transformation, we must ensure continuous integration and application development. That’s why we need an <span>experience</span>d DevOps engineer like you who’s eager to design, test, and program critical applications for our clients who need them most.</p><p></p><p>As a <span>sof</span>tware factory DevOps Platform Engineer on our team, you’ll support our <span>sof</span>tware development from requirements to testing in production. You’ll incorporate automation and cloud resources to minimize repetitive tasks and free up the team’s developers to do what they do best—innovate. You’ll work together with fellow professionals to implement continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) to limit manual testing and troubleshooting.</p><p></p><p>This is an opportunity to broaden your <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering while helping to develop <span>sof</span>tware that will completely transform workflows and make a real impact. Here, we invest in technology, and we’ll invest in you. With access to continuing education resources, tuition assistance opportunities, and technology development programs, you’ll keep your skills sharp as you work at the leading edge of technology.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we build and test tools to transform the future.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> maintaining and deploying production-grade containerized applications through DevOps practices</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD and developer workflow automation, including GitHub Actions, GitLab, GitBash, Git, AWS CodeStar, or CodePipeline</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with containerization, including Docker</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> troubleshooting platform application deployments and configurations</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with IaC, including Terraform or Ansible</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with Cloud, including AWS or Azure</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud and Network Security architecture, including least privilege in IAM, secrets management, Role-Based Access Control <span>(</span>RBAC<span>)</span>, or Boundary Protection</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with concepts of Service Meshes such as Istio or AWS App Mesh</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Pro<span>met</span>heus, Grafana, or Keycloak</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud-Native servers, Kubernetes platforms, and container registries</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with hardened AMIs and container images, including DoD STIGs or CIS Benchmarks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with APM, including Datadog, New Relic, or Splunk</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in Rancher services, including RKE2</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Identity Authentication and Authorization, including Single-Sign-On, SAML, or OpenID</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in Active Directory and GPO configuration and management</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> TS/SCI<span> clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/DevSecOps-Platform-Engineer_R0245768","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/DevSecOps-Platform-Engineer_R0245768","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"f0a9e9499e693156f5a83674925ad2a21a9d52d7b8b3ac9a4fe53ff4df286a85","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"DevSecOps Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/DevSecOps-Platform-Engineer_R0245768","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/DevSecOps-Platform-Engineer_R0245768","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245768","internal_job_id":"cc3e451c8bb71001ee5f4c6a81470000","first_published_at":"2026-07-31","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"DevSecOps Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nModernizing digital infrastructure in classified environments demands engineers who can build secure enterprise platforms, operate them reliably, and elevate the teams that depend on them. As a Senior DevSecOps Platform Engineer, you will design, deploy, and troubleshoot containerized systems in air-gapped environments, develop and optimize production CI / CD pipelines, author and refine Infrastructure-as-Code, and embed security, observability, and reliability into every layer of the delivery stack.\n\nYou’ll serve as a technical anchor for a cloud-focused DevOps team supporting the DoW, combining hands-on engineering expertise with a deliberate mentorship mission. You will coach active-duty military personnel and government civilians, lead technical exchanges and labs, and strengthen the organization’s ability to operate critical systems independently and sustainably.\n\nYou will also help drive early-stage artifi cia l intelligence ( AI ) adoption, including prototyping, evaluating AI-enabled capabilities, and responsibly applying AI / ML tooling within classified constraints. Your work will shape how the organization leverages automation, analytics, and modern platform engineering practices in highly restricted environments.\n\nOperate at the intersection of Kubernetes, cloud-native architectures, enterprise automation, and emerging AI technologies while helping develop the next generation of technical operators.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:\n- 8+ years of experience with IT, systems, or sof tware engineering\n- 5+ years of experience with DevOps or DevSecOps, building and operating production CI / CD pipelines\n- 3+ years of experience administering Kubernetes clusters in production, including lifecycle management and day‑2 operations\n- Experience developing Infrastructure-as-Code and configuration automation using Ansible and Terraform\n- Experience with Linux administration, including RHEL or Ubuntu, scripting with Python and Bash, AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud services, and cloud-native architectures\n- Experience supporting regulated environments such as the DoD or IC, including STIG automation, RMF or ATO processes, and air‑gapped constraints\n- Experience with basic AI prototyping, including LLM API use, RAG workflows, and automation assistants, and using AI-assisted engineering tools\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- HS diploma or GED\n- DoD 8140 or 8570 IAT Level II Certification such as Security+ CE Certification\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with DoD sof tware factory ecosystems, including Platform One, Big Bang, Iron Bank, and Kessel Run\n- Experience with observability stack, including Pro met heus, Grafana, and ELK or OpenSearch \n- Experience with service mesh and hardened platform services such as Istio, ArgoCD or Flux, and Harbor\n- Experience with network automation, including Nautobot or NetBox, Cisco automation, ServiceNow, and SolarWinds\n- Experience with Agile delivery, including Scrum or SAFe, and cross-functional teams\n- Cloud Certification s such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Certification\n- CKA, CKS, RHCSA, RHCE, Terraform Asso cia te, GitLab CI, or CISSP Certification s\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"DevSecOps Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Modernizing digital infrastructure in classified environments demands engineers who can build secure enterprise platforms, operate them reliably, and elevate the teams that depend on them. As a Senior DevSecOps Platform Engineer, you will design, deploy, and troubleshoot containerized systems in air-gapped environments, develop and optimize production CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines, author and refine Infrastructure-as-Code, and embed security, observability, and reliability into every layer of the delivery stack.</p><p></p><p>You’ll serve as a technical anchor for a cloud-focused DevOps team supporting the DoW, combining hands-on engineering expertise with a deliberate mentorship mission. You will coach active-duty military personnel and government civilians, lead technical exchanges and labs, and strengthen the organization’s <span>ability to</span> operate critical systems independently and sustainably.</p><p></p><p>You will also help drive early-stage artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence <span>(</span>AI<span>)</span> adoption, including prototyping, evaluating AI-enabled capabilities, and responsibly applying AI<span>/</span>ML tooling within classified constraints. Your work will shape how the organization leverages automation, analytics, and modern platform engineering practices in highly restricted environments.</p><p></p><p>Operate at the intersection of Kubernetes, cloud-native architectures, enterprise automation, and emerging AI technologies while helping develop the next generation of technical operators.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>8&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with IT, systems, or <span>sof</span>tware engineering</li><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with DevOps or DevSecOps, building and operating production CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> administering Kubernetes clusters in production, including lifecycle management and day‑2 operations</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing Infrastructure-as-Code and configuration automation using Ansible and Terraform</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Linux administration, including RHEL or Ubuntu, scripting with Python and Bash, AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud services, and cloud-native architectures</li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting regulated environments such as the DoD or IC, including STIG automation, RMF or ATO processes, and air‑gapped constraints</li><li><span>Experience</span> with basic AI prototyping, including LLM API use, RAG workflows, and automation assistants, and using AI-assisted engineering tools</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance </span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED </span></li><li>DoD 8140 or 8570 IAT Level II <span>Certification</span> such as Security&#43; CE Certification</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with DoD <span>sof</span>tware factory ecosystems, including Platform One, Big Bang, Iron Bank, and Kessel Run</li><li><span>Experience</span> with observability stack, including Pro<span>met</span>heus, Grafana, and ELK or OpenSearch </li><li><span>Experience</span> with service mesh and hardened platform services such as Istio, ArgoCD or Flux, and Harbor</li><li><span>Experience</span> with network automation, including Nautobot or NetBox, Cisco automation, ServiceNow, and SolarWinds</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile delivery, including Scrum or SAFe, and cross-functional teams</li><li>Cloud <span>Certification</span>s such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud <span>Certification</span></li><li>CKA, CKS, RHCSA, RHCE, Terraform Asso<span>cia</span>te, GitLab CI, or CISSP <span>Certification</span>s</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span> </p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 24 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Digital-Signal-Processing-Software-Engineer_R0244344-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Digital-Signal-Processing-Software-Engineer_R0244344-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"0457fd03e0930db16d67e55c5d3517aa6e8745a99f42b902af84b4b840a5a681","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Digital Signal Processing Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Digital-Signal-Processing-Software-Engineer_R0244344-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Digital-Signal-Processing-Software-Engineer_R0244344-1","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244344","internal_job_id":"b3c781f6607110010bf922b3e8bc0001","first_published_at":"2026-07-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Digital Signal Processing Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nUse tools, techniques, systems, and procedures for developing sof tware or analytic tools for wired or wireless transmission of signaling data. Apply leading-edge principles, theories, and concepts and contribute to the development of new principles and concepts. Work on unusually complex problems and provide highly innovative solutions. Operate with substantial latitude for unreviewed action or decision. Mentor or supervise employees in both company and technical competencies.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with sof tware development languages, including Python, C, or C++\n- Experience with digital signal processing algorithms or RF theory\n- Experience using Agile processes and tools, including Jira or Confluence\n- Ability to work in a team environment to brainstorm and innovate new ideas \n- ​ TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with firm ware development languages such as VHDL, Verilog, or CoreFire\n- Experience with machine learning packages and building and testing neural network architectures using TensorFlow, Keras, or PyTorch\n- Experience using version control, including GitHub\n- Experience using Linux systems\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Digital Signal Processing Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Use tools, techniques, systems, and procedures for developing <span>sof</span>tware or analytic tools for wired or wireless transmission of signaling data. Apply leading-edge principles, theories, and concepts and contribute to the development of new principles and concepts. Work on unusually complex problems and provide highly innovative solutions. Operate with substantial latitude for unreviewed action or decision. Mentor or supervise employees in both company and technical competencies.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of experience with <span>sof</span>tware development languages, including Python, C, or C&#43;&#43;</li><li>Experience with digital signal processing algorithms or RF theory</li><li>Experience using Agile processes and tools, including Jira or Confluence</li><li>Ability to work in a team environment to brainstorm and innovate new ideas </li><li>​<span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li>Experience with <span>firm</span>ware development languages such as VHDL, Verilog, or CoreFire</li><li>Experience with machine learning packages and building and testing neural network architectures using TensorFlow, Keras, or PyTorch</li><li>Experience using version control, including GitHub</li><li>Experience using Linux systems</li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Beavercreek-OH/Electronic-Warfare-Software-Engineer_R0235359","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Beavercreek-OH/Electronic-Warfare-Software-Engineer_R0235359","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c318c96004faccb6e15b32b91007c3234b50620a36ac44013fb0bcf9ca185921","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Electronic Warfare Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Electronic-Warfare-Software-Engineer_R0235359","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Electronic-Warfare-Software-Engineer_R0235359","locations":[{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0235359","internal_job_id":"74b696122b331000c68d547240a30000","first_published_at":"2026-06-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Electronic Warfare Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs an electrical engineer, you understand the workings behind complex systems. That knowledge is key when it comes to developing the next generation of Electronic Warfare technologies and solutions. We’re looking for an electrical engineer who can use their skills to provide the U.S. warfighter cutting edge capabilities in the management and dominance of the RF Spectrum.\n\nAt Booz Allen, you’ll use your engineering skills to transform Air Force. Our team analyzes the next generation of Electronic Warfare. That’s why we need you, an electrical engineer with a background in signal processing and sof tware development, to help us design and develop algorithms and sof tware for the characterization of a modern radar signal space. \n\nOn our team, you’ll utilize programming languages such as C or C++, MATLAB, and Python to perform analysis on signal processing and Electronic Warfare techniques. You’ll impact the Air Force by developing techniques, sof tware, and algorithms to shape the future of warfare. This is a chance to use your signal processing and programming skills while gaining experience in modern electronic warfare. \n\nTake on exciting challenges in the Air Force with us as we improve the Electronic Warfare environment for the warfighter.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\n You Have:\n- 2+ years of experience in electrical or design engineering, signal processing, or radar analysis\n\n- Experience in sof tware development\n\n- Knowledge of digital signal processing, C++, Python\n\n- Ability to work independently and as part of a group\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or Physics\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience in Agile sof tware development\n\n- Experience with statistical analysis, AI or ML, and mathematical optimization\n\n- Knowledge EW met hods and analysis, mission analysis, and signals analysis \n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering preferred; Doctorate degree in Electrical Engineering a plus\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Electronic Warfare Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As an electrical engineer, you understand the workings behind complex systems. That knowledge is key when it comes to developing the next generation of Electronic Warfare technologies and solutions. We’re looking for an electrical engineer who can use their skills to provide the U.S. warfighter cutting edge capabilities in the management and dominance of the RF Spectrum.</p><p></p><p>At Booz Allen, you’ll use your engineering skills to transform Air Force. Our team analyzes the next generation of Electronic Warfare. That’s why we need you, an electrical engineer with a background in signal processing and <span>sof</span>tware development, to help us design and develop algorithms and <span>sof</span>tware for the characterization of a modern radar signal space. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll utilize programming languages such as C or C&#43;&#43;, MATLAB, and Python to perform analysis on signal processing and Electronic Warfare techniques. You’ll impact the Air Force by developing techniques, <span>sof</span>tware, and algorithms to shape the future of warfare. This is a chance to use your signal processing and programming skills while gaining experience in modern electronic warfare. </p><p></p><p>Take on exciting challenges in the Air Force with us as we improve the Electronic Warfare environment for the warfighter.</p><p><br />Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p><br /><b> You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in electrical or design engineering, signal processing, or radar analysis</p></li><li><p>Experience in <span>sof</span>tware development</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of digital signal processing, C&#43;&#43;, Python</p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently and as part of a group</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or Physics</p></li></ul><p><br /><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in Agile <span>sof</span>tware development</p></li><li><p>Experience with statistical analysis, AI or ML, and mathematical optimization</p></li><li><p>Knowledge EW <span>met</span>hods and analysis, mission analysis, and signals analysis </p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering preferred; Doctorate degree in Electrical Engineering a plus</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Pensacola-FL/ELINT---EW-Curriculum-Developer_R0242409","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Pensacola-FL/ELINT---EW-Curriculum-Developer_R0242409","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5d6447a846d54af67830aa3da1523cd4a0c9b68ba6a155626136017f7531007e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"ELINT & EW Curriculum Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Pensacola-FL/ELINT---EW-Curriculum-Developer_R0242409","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Pensacola-FL/ELINT---EW-Curriculum-Developer_R0242409","locations":[{"label":"Pensacola, FL"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242409","internal_job_id":"9fe0da91f5e310011743d3cc47480000","first_published_at":"2026-08-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"ELINT & EW Curriculum Developer The Opportunity:  \nAssist in the implementation of emergent Intelligence Community ( IC ) training capabilities. Assist with training development functions and analysis of Department of Defense ( DoD ) and Joint training publications to identify potential revisions needed to legacy curriculum material. Work with key stakeholders to ensure training initiatives are embedded across institutional, operational, and self-development domains. Execute the implementation of training strategies and learning concepts. Collaborate with military and civilian stakeholders, technical experts, and operational colleagues. Build critical training materials for advanced learners who are motivated to grow their skills. Be part of a collaborative multidisciplinary team producing highly sophisticated, technical, and hands-on training solutions to meet the mission and time-critical needs of our client. Utilize your operational experience to foster a team environment of learning, progress, and excellence and help us build the next generation of IC experts.\n\nYou Have:     \n- Experience creating performance-based technical training, including practical applications and assessments to measure trainee performance and knowledge retention \n- Experience using Learning Management Systems ( LMS ) to develop, update, manage, and integrate training content \n- Knowledge of DoD and Navy guidance documents used in the development of task-based curriculum \n- Knowledge of learning tools and modalities, and measurement tools or met hods used to evaluate the effectiveness of instruction or training interventions \n- Ability to select teaching met hods appropriate for course audience \n- Ability to have interpersonal communications with civilian and military personnel, including verbal briefings or presentations, listening techniques, and developing written material such as technical reports documenting research and analysis performed \n- TS/SCI clearance \n- HS diploma or GED \n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $52,900.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"ELINT &amp; EW Curriculum Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>Assist in the implementation of emergent Intelligence Community <span>(</span>IC<span>)</span> training capabilities. Assist with training development functions and analysis of Department of Defense <span>(</span>DoD<span>)</span> and Joint training publications to identify potential revisions needed to legacy curriculum material. Work with key stakeholders to ensure training initiatives are embedded across institutional, operational, and self-development domains. Execute the implementation of training strategies and learning concepts. Collaborate with military and civilian stakeholders, technical experts, and operational colleagues. Build critical training materials for advanced learners who are motivated to grow their skills. Be part of a collaborative multidisciplinary team producing highly sophisticated, technical, and hands-on training solutions to meet the mission and time-critical needs of our client. Utilize your operational <span>experience</span> to foster a team environment of learning, progress, and excellence and help us build the next generation of IC experts.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>    </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> creating performance-based technical training, including practical applications and assessments to measure trainee performance and knowledge retention </li><li><span>Experience</span> using Learning Management Systems <span>(</span>LMS<span>)</span> to develop, update, manage, and integrate training content </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> DoD and Navy guidance documents used in the development of task-based curriculum </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> learning tools and modalities, and measurement tools or <span>met</span>hods used to evaluate the effectiveness of instruction or training interventions </li><li><span>Ability to</span> select teaching <span>met</span>hods appropriate for course audience </li><li><span>Ability to</span> have interpersonal communications with civilian and military personnel, including verbal briefings or presentations, listening techniques, and developing written material such as technical reports documenting research and analysis performed </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance </span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span> </p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $52,900.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 11 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0231944","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0231944","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"689f9ff697fafc94828093b04085ac7be15078483b6802c16c4c966d809738bc","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Embedded Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0231944","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0231944","locations":[{"label":"Annapolis Junction, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0231944","internal_job_id":"03b4cb5aa2f01000bab1a554cdb80000","first_published_at":"2026-06-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Embedded Developer The Opportunity:\nAs an embedded sof tware engineer, you know how to create and maintain cru cia l pieces of sof tware. You use your knowledge to write and optimize code that creates a bridge between pieces of sof tware, allowing them to communicate. We’re looking for an embedded sof tware engineer like you to develop technology for our clients’ most important mission-forward challenges.  \n\nAs an embedded sof tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll support the development of systems, sit es, and tools for our clients. Using the latest tools and technology, you’ll write, test, and edit code in support of the team’s overall results. You’ll strengthen your skills as you develop and reverse engineer sof tware that supports hardware functionality on a wide range of devices, as well as configure solutions based on the platform being used. You’ll partner with team leadership to troubleshoot and correct operational issues, as well as with cybersecurity spe cia lists to ensure that the sof tware you’re creating is secure.\n\nWork with us to expand your tech skills and make a meaningful difference.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 6+ years of experience with sof tware development using C\n- Experience with configuration, administration, and development with Virtual Environments such as VMWare, ESXi, or Open Stack\n- Experience with Linux Development\n- Experience with sof tware reverse engineering or debugging tools such as IDAPro, OllyDbg, or gdb\n- Experience with assembly languages development or reversing\n- Knowledge of low-level systems programming concepts\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with development on embedded platforms such as Unix, Android, and VxWorks\n- Experience with Open vSwitch, or QEMU\n- Experience with vulnerability analysis and exploit development\n- Experience with Python\n- Experience with Assembly\n- Experience with memory safe low-level programming such as Rus t\n- Knowledge of telecommunications\n\nClearance :\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Embedded Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know how to create and maintain cru<span>cia</span>l pieces of <span>sof</span>tware. You use your knowledge to write and optimize code that creates a bridge between pieces of <span>sof</span>tware, allowing them to communicate. We’re looking for an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to develop technology for our clients’ most important mission-forward challenges.  </p><p></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll support the development of systems, <span>sit</span>es, and tools for our clients. Using the latest tools and technology, you’ll write, test, and edit code in support of the team’s overall results. You’ll strengthen your skills as you develop and reverse engineer <span>sof</span>tware that supports hardware functionality on a wide range of devices, as well as configure solutions based on the platform being used. You’ll partner with team leadership to troubleshoot and correct operational issues, as well as with cybersecurity spe<span>cia</span>lists to ensure that the <span>sof</span>tware you’re creating is secure.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to expand your tech skills and make a meaningful difference.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware development using C</li><li><span>Experience</span> with configuration, administration, and development with Virtual Environments such as VMWare, ESXi, or Open Stack</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Linux Development</li><li><span>Experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware reverse engineering or debugging tools such as IDAPro, OllyDbg, or gdb</li><li><span>Experience</span> with assembly languages development or reversing</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> low-level systems programming concepts</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with development on embedded platforms such as Unix, Android, and VxWorks</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Open vSwitch, or QEMU</li><li><span>Experience</span> with vulnerability analysis and exploit development</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Assembly</li><li><span>Experience</span> with memory safe low-level programming such as <span>Rus</span>t</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> telecommunications</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance</span></b><b>:</b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0243402","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0243402","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"39c1dba6ce1adcd2457fb56e7700de6b3715f51c661e479b976289438f0841fe","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Embedded Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0243402","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Annapolis-Junction-MD/Embedded-Developer_R0243402","locations":[{"label":"Annapolis Junction, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243402","internal_job_id":"8f3baa969d4a100110c026e5604d0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Embedded Developer The Opportunity:\nAs an embedded sof tware engineer, you know how to create and maintain cru cia l pieces of sof tware. You use your knowledge to write and optimize code that creates a bridge between pieces of sof tware, allowing them to communicate. We’re looking for an embedded sof tware engineer like you to develop technology for our clients’ most important mission-forward challenges.  \n\nAs an embedded sof tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll support the development of systems, sit es, and tools for our clients. Using the latest tools and technology, you’ll write, test, and edit code in support of the team’s overall results. You’ll strengthen your skills as you develop and reverse engineer sof tware that supports hardware functionality on a wide range of devices, as well as configure solutions based on the platform being used. You’ll partner with team leadership to troubleshoot and correct operational issues, as well as with cybersecurity spe cia lists to ensure that the sof tware you’re creating is secure.\n\nWork with us to expand your tech skills and make a meaningful difference.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 6+ years of experience with sof tware development using C++ and Java\n\n- 6+ years of experience with s oftware system requirements analysis, design, development, integration, or testing\n\n- Experience with Python development\n\n- Experience with pytest\n\n- Experience with assembly languages development or reversing\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with software development experience using C\n\n- Experience with GIT repository, Maven, and Bamboo\n\n- Experience with Jenkins Scripting\n\n- Experience with Java GUI programming\n\n- Experience with XML and XLST\n\n- Experience with Unit test development using CppUnit, GMock, pytest or other similar software test frameworks\n\nClearance :\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Embedded Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know how to create and maintain cru<span>cia</span>l pieces of <span>sof</span>tware. You use your knowledge to write and optimize code that creates a bridge between pieces of <span>sof</span>tware, allowing them to communicate. We’re looking for an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to develop technology for our clients’ most important mission-forward challenges.  </p><p></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll support the development of systems, <span>sit</span>es, and tools for our clients. Using the latest tools and technology, you’ll write, test, and edit code in support of the team’s overall results. You’ll strengthen your skills as you develop and reverse engineer <span>sof</span>tware that supports hardware functionality on a wide range of devices, as well as configure solutions based on the platform being used. You’ll partner with team leadership to troubleshoot and correct operational issues, as well as with cybersecurity spe<span>cia</span>lists to ensure that the <span>sof</span>tware you’re creating is secure.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to expand your tech skills and make a meaningful difference.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware development using <span>C&#43;&#43; and Java</span></p></li><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with s<span>oftware system requirements analysis, design, development, integration, or testing </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with <span>Python development </span></p></li><li><p>Experience with pytest</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with assembly languages development or reversing</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with software development experience using C</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with GIT<span> repository, Maven, and Bamboo</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Jenkins Scripting</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Java<span> GUI programming</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with <span>XML and XLST</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with <span>Unit test development </span>using CppUnit, GMock, pytest or other similar software test frameworks</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance</span></b><b>:</b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0245751","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0245751","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6d5ca593451197f24a4eb773644f5cf7090211106c22d83a2387ab0708476889","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Embedded Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0245751","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0245751","locations":[{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245751","internal_job_id":"2b414f219eed1001bd7b5182cb930000","first_published_at":"2026-07-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Embedded Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAre you excited to apply RF quantum sensing technologies to critical national security missions? Your expertise in RF digital signal processing software development will be critical to integrate, test, and evaluate RF quantum sensing technologies. Apply core principles, theories, and concepts to provide effective solutions for practical applications. Solve complex technical problems and deliver innovative solutions. Operate with substantial independence and provide oversight or mentorship for your team’s technical competencies. Collaborate effectively with minimal supervision, overseeing and mentoring junior employees as needed.\n\nThis is a hands-on engineering role focused on embedded software, hardware-software integration, and system reliability. You will work across microcontrollers, device communications, motorized subsystems, sensors, and control logic that directly affect RF and quantum sensing system performance in production. The right candidate is comfortable debugging at every layer, from firmware behavior and electrical interfaces to system-level interactions in deployed hardware. This position is located in Colorado Springs, CO and requires laboratory work. This position requires the ability to travel up to 25% of the time.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 7+ years of experience with software development languages, including Python, C, or C++\n\n- Experience with the design, development, and testing of real-time software for microcontrollers interfacing with specialized hardware\n\n- Experience with digital signal processing (DSP) algorithms and RF theory, including building the front and back end of a spectrum analyzer\n\n- Experience using Agile processes and tools, including Jira or Confluence, and using version control, including GitHub\n\n- Experience using Windows and Linux systems; experience porting software from Windows to Linux, including compiling and cross-compiling libraries as needed\n\n- Experience developing software and firmware for embedded systems, such as SCPI, Ethernet, and Serial integration\n\n- Ability to work in a team environment to brainstorm and innovate new ideas\n\n- Ability to travel up to 25% of the time\n\n- Ability to obtain a TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Embedded Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>Are you excited to apply RF quantum sensing technologies to critical national security missions? Your expertise in RF digital signal processing software development will be critical to integrate, test, and evaluate RF quantum sensing technologies. Apply core principles, theories, and concepts to provide effective solutions for practical applications. Solve complex technical problems and deliver innovative solutions. Operate with substantial independence and provide oversight or mentorship for your team’s technical competencies. Collaborate effectively with minimal supervision, overseeing and mentoring junior employees as needed.</p><p></p><p>This is a hands-on engineering role focused on embedded software, hardware-software integration, and system reliability. You will work across microcontrollers, device communications, motorized subsystems, sensors, and control logic that directly affect RF and quantum sensing system performance in production. The right candidate is comfortable debugging at every layer, from firmware behavior and electrical interfaces to system-level interactions in deployed hardware. This position is located in Colorado Springs, CO and requires laboratory work. This position requires the ability to travel up to 25% of the time.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>7&#43; years of experience with software development languages, including Python, C, or C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p>Experience with the design, development, and testing of real-time software for microcontrollers interfacing with specialized hardware</p></li><li><p>Experience with digital signal processing (DSP) algorithms and RF theory, including building the front and back end of a spectrum analyzer</p></li><li><p>Experience using Agile processes and tools, including Jira or Confluence, and <span style=\"font-size:14px\">using version control, including GitHub</span></p></li><li><p>Experience using Windows and Linux systems; experience porting software from Windows to Linux, including compiling and cross-compiling libraries as needed</p></li><li><p>Experience developing software and firmware for embedded systems, such as SCPI, Ethernet, and Serial integration</p></li><li><p>Ability to work in a team environment to brainstorm and innovate new ideas</p></li><li><p>Ability to travel up to 25% of the time</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Huntsville-AL/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0244178","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Huntsville-AL/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0244178","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5a0bd259fa4af0a83f31d96be5b7495824f9b3de329dbca0efaf6bbe38f9007c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Embedded Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Huntsville-AL/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0244178","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Huntsville-AL/Embedded-Software-Engineer_R0244178","locations":[{"label":"Huntsville, AL"},{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"El Segundo, CA"},{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244178","internal_job_id":"6c9b0fa821f61000cecf8f745d7a0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Embedded Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs an embedded sof tware engineer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an engineer like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As an Embedded S of tware Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- Experience with sof tware engineering using Rus t, C, C++, or Python\n\n- Experience working in an agile development environment\n\n- Experience working within a CI / CD pipeline\n\n- Knowledge of AI-assisted sof tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns\n\n- Ability to effectively communicate, work independently and collaboratively on a cross-functional team, and demonstrate initiative to complete complex tasks to achieve program goals in a fast-paced environment\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience designing the architecture and containerized services with Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with secure coding practices and vulnerability remediation\n\n- Knowledge of Jira, Confluence, Git, and GitLab\n\n- Ability to display a personal or professional GitHub profile demonstrating projects\n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance \n\n- Secret clearance\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $52,900.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Embedded Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an engineer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p><br />This role is more than just coding. As an Embedded S<span>of</span>tware Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p><br />Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware engineering using <span>Rus</span>t, C, C&#43;&#43;, or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working in an agile development environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working within a CI<span>/</span>CD pipeline</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AI-assisted <span>sof</span>tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> effectively communicate, work independently and collaboratively on a cross-functional team, and demonstrate initiative to complete complex tasks to achieve program goals in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing the architecture and containerized services with Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with secure coding practices and vulnerability remediation</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> Jira, Confluence, Git, and GitLab</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> display a personal or professional GitHub profile demonstrating projects</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $52,900.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Agentic-AI-Engineer_R0247309","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Agentic-AI-Engineer_R0247309","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"506a3de5ee2a0f24fdf7d013166b15b6777ea2b442887840e72992d1abca9a89","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Enterprise Agentic AI Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Agentic-AI-Engineer_R0247309","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Agentic-AI-Engineer_R0247309","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247309","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d146100116b40856f6510000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Enterprise Agentic AI Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs an experience d engineer, you know that agentic AI is transforming how organizations operate, make decisions, and deliver outcomes at speed. Your ability to design and build practical agentic systems that turn manual workflows into AI-enabled solutions makes you an integral part of transforming Booz Allen’s enterprise business systems. We need your technical depth, product mindset, and problem-solving drive to support Project Keystone.\n\nProject Keystone is an enterprise-wide transformation initiative modernizing core business systems across Source‑to‑Pay ( S2P ) , Contract Lifecycle Management ( CLM ) , Enterprise Resource Planning ( ERP ) , and asso cia ted reporting and data workstreams. The program drives end‑to‑end process modernization by integrating platforms such as Icertis, Ivalua, and Costpoint to enable scalable, secure, and well‑governed digital capabilities. This effort underpins Booz Allen’s broader readiness strategy—enhancing organizational efficiency, strengthening user adoption, and enabling measurable business impact.\n\nYou will support complex workstreams spanning agentic AI prototyping, business process modernization, technology implementation, data, reporting, testing, change readiness, and stakeholder e nga gement. You will collaborate with program leaders, product owners, functional subject matter experts, technical teams, and business stakeholders to define requirements, coordinate delivery activities, and maintain alignment across interconnected initiatives.\n\nYou will be part of a high-performing, cross-functional team operating in a dynamic transformation environment where priorities may shift and multiple efforts run in parallel. Success in this role requires leadership, adaptability, clear communication, strong execution, and ownership of outcomes from planning through implementation. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.\n\nWork with us to modernize critical enterprise capabilities and help shape the future of how Booz Allen operates.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 5+ years of experience supporting enterprise transformation, technology modernization, AI-enabled solutions, program delivery, or business process improvement initiatives\n- 3+ years of experience supporting AI, machine learning, intelligent automation, data analytics, or emerging technology initiatives\n- 3+ years of experience gathering, analyzing, and translating business needs into requirements, implementation plans, and actionable recommendations\n- 1+ years of experience designing, develop ing, evaluating, or implementing agentic AI applications in prototype or production environments\n- Experience coordinating activities across process design, system implementation, data, reporting, testing, deployment, or organizational readiness workstreams\n- Experience implementing agent orchestration frameworks, and designing and implementing agent loops, tool-calling workflows, and multi-agent interaction patterns\n- Knowledge of LLM platforms and providers, including OpenAI and Databricks\n- Knowledge of prompt engineering techniques for reliability, controllability, and task performance\n- Knowledge of MCP usage and develop ment, including integration of external tools and capabilities\n- Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science, Sof tware Engineering, Data Science, Artifi cia l Intelligence, or technology field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience supporting large-scale enterprise transformation or technology modernization programs\n- Experience supporting ERP, procurement, contract management, finance, or back-office transformation initiatives\n- Experience with enterprise platforms such as Icertis, Ivalua, or Costpoint\n- Experience applying Agile, hybrid , or traditional program and project management met hodologies\n- Experience supporting user acceptance testing, deployment planning, operational readiness, training, communications, or organizational change management\n- Master’s degree\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Enterprise Agentic AI Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d engineer, you know that agentic AI is transforming how organizations operate, make decisions, and deliver outcomes at speed. Your <span>ability to</span> design and build practical agentic systems that turn manual workflows into AI-enabled solutions makes you an integral part of transforming Booz Allen’s enterprise business systems. We need your technical depth, product mindset, and problem-solving drive to support Project Keystone.</p><p></p><p>Project Keystone is an enterprise-wide transformation initiative modernizing core business systems across Source‑to‑Pay <span>(</span>S2P<span>)</span>, Contract Lifecycle Management <span>(</span>CLM<span>)</span>, Enterprise Resource Planning <span>(</span>ERP<span>)</span>, and asso<span>cia</span>ted reporting and data workstreams. The program drives end‑to‑end process modernization by integrating platforms such as Icertis, Ivalua, and Costpoint to enable scalable, secure, and well‑governed digital capabilities. This effort underpins Booz Allen’s broader readiness strategy—enhancing organizational efficiency, strengthening user adoption, and enabling measurable business impact.</p><p></p><p>You will support complex workstreams spanning agentic AI prototyping, business process modernization, technology implementation, data, reporting, testing, change readiness, and stakeholder e<span>nga</span>gement. You will collaborate with program leaders, product owners, functional subject matter experts, technical teams, and business stakeholders to define requirements, coordinate delivery activities, and maintain alignment across interconnected initiatives.</p><p></p><p>You will be part of a high-performing, cross-functional team operating in a dynamic transformation environment where priorities may shift and multiple efforts run in parallel. Success in this role requires leadership, adaptability, clear communication, strong execution, and ownership of outcomes from planning through implementation. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to modernize critical enterprise capabilities and help shape the future of how Booz Allen operates.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> supporting enterprise transformation, technology modernization, AI-enabled solutions, program delivery, or business process improvement initiatives</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> supporting AI, machine learning, intelligent automation, data analytics, or emerging technology initiatives</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> gathering, analyzing, and translating business needs into requirements, implementation plans, and actionable recommendations</li><li>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, <span>develop</span>ing, evaluating, or implementing agentic AI applications in prototype or production environments</li><li><span>Experience</span> coordinating activities across process design, system implementation, data, reporting, testing, deployment, or organizational readiness workstreams</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing agent orchestration frameworks, and designing and implementing agent loops, tool-calling workflows, and multi-agent interaction patterns</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> LLM platforms and providers, including OpenAI and Databricks</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> prompt engineering techniques for reliability, controllability, and task performance</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> MCP usage and <span>develop</span>ment, including integration of external tools and capabilities</li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in a Computer Science, <span>Sof</span>tware Engineering, Data Science, Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence, or technology field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> supporting large-scale enterprise transformation or technology modernization programs</li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting ERP, procurement, contract management, finance, or back-office transformation initiatives</li><li><span>Experience</span> with enterprise platforms such as Icertis, Ivalua, or Costpoint</li><li><span>Experience</span> applying Agile, <span>hybrid</span>, or traditional program and project management <span>met</span>hodologies</li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting user acceptance testing, deployment planning, operational readiness, training, communications, or organizational change management</li><li><span>Master’s degree</span></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["AI Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Integration-Developer_R0246906","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Integration-Developer_R0246906","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7b7cc8212de6fffc6b57ada8f7ae7947527c38c790ce80e60f090a9ac022b520","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Enterprise Integration Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Integration-Developer_R0246906","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Integration-Developer_R0246906","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246906","internal_job_id":"e534098ad7cc1001ad4349fed8f80000","first_published_at":"2026-08-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Enterprise Integration Developer The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to improve how enterprise systems work together for employees and agents? As an Enterprise Integration Developer, you understand the importance of connecting applications, data, and workflows in a way that is reliable and maintainable.\n\nOn our team, you’ll support the design and development of integration solutions that connect core business systems, internal platforms, and emerging AI-enabled services. Your work will focus on building cross-application workflows, automation, and reusable integration services across the enterprise. You’ll work with technologies such as Mule Sof t Anypoint Platform, REST APIs, messaging and event platforms, and cloud services such as AWS and Azure, to develop and support integrations in production. You’ll collaborate with architects, engineers, platform owners, and business stakeholders to implement solutions aligned to business processes and operational needs.\n\nIn this role, you’ll help improve data flow across systems and contribute to automation and integration solutions that support internal operations. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizen ship is required .\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience building or supporting enterprise integrations or APIs\n- Experience integrating enterprise SaaS platforms, internal applications, or legacy systems using APIs or messaging patterns\n- Experience working with REST APIs and common integration patterns, including synchronous and asynchronous\n- Experience working in cloud environments such as AWS or Azure, and supporting deployment of integration solutions\n- Experience with CI / CD pipelines and automated testing practices for integration services\n- Knowledge of integration security fundamentals, including authentication and secure API usage\n- Ability to work from technical designs and business requirements to develop, test, and support integration solutions\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 1+ years of experience with the Mule Sof t Anypoint Platform\n- Experience with automated integration testing tools such as MUnit\n- Experience using AI-assisted development tools such as GitHub Copilot or Cursor\n- Experience integrating AI or LLM-based services into enterprise workflows\n- Experience with event streaming platforms such as Kafka or Azure Event Grid\n- Mule Sof t Certified Developer Certification\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Enterprise Integration Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to improve how enterprise systems work together for employees and agents? As an Enterprise Integration Developer, you understand the importance of connecting applications, data, and workflows in a way that is reliable and maintainable.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll support the design and development of integration solutions that connect core business systems, internal platforms, and emerging AI-enabled services. Your work will focus on building cross-application workflows, automation, and reusable integration services across the enterprise. You’ll work with technologies such as Mule<span>Sof</span>t Anypoint Platform, REST APIs, messaging and event platforms, and cloud services such as AWS and Azure, to develop and support integrations in production. You’ll collaborate with architects, engineers, platform owners, and business stakeholders to implement solutions aligned to business processes and operational needs.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll help improve data flow across systems and contribute to automation and integration solutions that support internal operations. <span>Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. </span><span>citizen</span><span>ship is required</span>.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> building or supporting enterprise integrations or APIs</li><li><span>Experience</span> integrating enterprise SaaS platforms, internal applications, or legacy systems using APIs or messaging patterns</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with REST APIs and common integration patterns, including synchronous and asynchronous</li><li><span>Experience</span> working in cloud environments such as AWS or Azure, and supporting deployment of integration solutions</li><li><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines and automated testing practices for integration services</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> integration security fundamentals, including authentication and secure API usage</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work from technical designs and business requirements to develop, test, and support integration solutions</li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with the Mule<span>Sof</span>t Anypoint Platform</li><li><span>Experience</span> with automated integration testing tools such as MUnit</li><li><span>Experience</span> using AI-assisted development tools such as GitHub Copilot or Cursor</li><li><span>Experience</span> integrating AI or LLM-based services into enterprise workflows</li><li><span>Experience</span> with event streaming platforms such as Kafka or Azure Event Grid</li><li>Mule<span>Sof</span>t Certified Developer <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 11 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Workflow-Software-Engineer--Mid_R0246798","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Workflow-Software-Engineer--Mid_R0246798","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c77faf45ba6abd8723172888177d75822c8385ba38fb97fe45f173c81c8b8488","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Enterprise Workflow Software Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Workflow-Software-Engineer--Mid_R0246798","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Enterprise-Workflow-Software-Engineer--Mid_R0246798","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Reston, VA"},{"label":"Herndon, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246798","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d010015de318cde6980000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Enterprise Workflow Software Engineer, Mid The Opportunity:\nAs a full stack develop er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a develop er like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production-ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a full stack develop er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution develop ed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience designing, modifying, develop ing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications  \n- 2+ years of experience with sof tware develop ment using basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web develop ment stacks\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications \n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions \n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment \n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor's degree or 5+ years of experience in sof tware engineering in lieu of a degree \n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Agile met hodology, extreme programming, sof tware engineering, product management, and sof tware products \n- Experience with enterprise workflow, such as, Salesforce, or IT management sof tware such as ServiceNow\n- Experience with a Cloud such as AWS, OCI, or Azure\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Enterprise Workflow Software Engineer, Mid<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full stack <span>develop</span>er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a <span>develop</span>er like you with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a full stack <span>develop</span>er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution <span>develop</span>ed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, <span>develop</span>ing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications  </li><li>2&#43; years of experience with <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment using basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web <span>develop</span>ment stacks</li><li><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications </li><li><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to <span>develop</span> complete solutions </li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> or 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering in lieu of a degree </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology, extreme programming, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, product management, and <span>sof</span>tware products </li><li><span>Experience</span> with enterprise workflow, such as, Salesforce, or IT management <span>sof</span>tware such as ServiceNow</li><li><span>Experience</span> with a Cloud such as AWS, OCI, or Azure</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/EPM-Cloud-Application-Developer_R0245800","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/EPM-Cloud-Application-Developer_R0245800","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8bc60538e5879e0d1e6b6fd6c27a8436441a80b2889169c17307e7afa0bf50d1","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"EPM Cloud Application Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/EPM-Cloud-Application-Developer_R0245800","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/EPM-Cloud-Application-Developer_R0245800","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245800","internal_job_id":"adece80c64641001a21cef69bbbc0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-06","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"EPM Cloud Application Developer The Opportunity:  \nLead the requirements gathering, development, and delivery of solution‑driven applications using Oracle Enterprise Planning and Budgeting Cloud Services (EPBCS) within EPM Cloud. Manage full life‑cycle development for planning applications, including defining and documenting business requirements, designing key processes, building rules and Essbase calculations, and establishing robust data sourcing strategies. Provide ongoing user support through training, documentation, and best‑practice guidance. Ensure adherence to testing, governance, and code‑promotion standards while actively monitoring system performance, data integrity, quality, and security controls. Use strong analytical, critical‑thinking, and debugging skills to identify, troubleshoot, and resolve system or process issues.\n\nEnhance planning and forecasting capabilities by incorporating AI‑powered methods such as machine learning-based predictive forecasting, anomaly detection, and intelligent data validation. Design automation solutions that leverage AI to streamline data processing, improve forecast accuracy, and reduce manual workload across planning cycles. Collaborate regularly with management, colleagues, and cross‑functional partners to deliver project updates, recommend improvements, and present new development and AI‑driven capabilities that support strategic decision‑making.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience with development for Hyperion planning\n\n- Experience with full life cycle project management and development, including requirement gathering, design, development, testing, rollout, and implementation\n\n- Experience driving client and peer relationships and facilitating information-gathering sessions to elicit requirements using multiple methods\n\n- Experience with Oracle EPM AI Agents, including enabling, implementing, and monitoring AI capabilities within the platform\n\n- Experience incorporating AI‑powered methods such as machine learning-based predictive forecasting, anomaly detection, and intelligent data validation\n\n- Experience performing detailed analysis and research, managing deadlines across multiple deliverables, and creating detailed project documentation, including discussions, considerations, and requirements\n\n- Experience quickly learning new EPM software tools and developing integration and deployment strategies\n\n- Experience applying logical and critical thinking to address and process system issues and troubleshoot bugs\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Government Cost Accounting and Forward Pricing Rate Proposals\n\n- Experience with managing applications that meet Sarbanes Oxley SOX or process and access controls\n\n- Knowledge of Databricks\n\n- Knowledge of basic ETL concepts\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"EPM Cloud Application Developer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b> </p><div><p>Lead the requirements gathering, development, and delivery of solution‑driven applications using Oracle Enterprise Planning and Budgeting Cloud Services (EPBCS) within EPM Cloud. Manage full life‑cycle development for planning applications, including defining and documenting business requirements, designing key processes, building rules and Essbase calculations, and establishing robust data sourcing strategies. Provide ongoing user support through training, documentation, and best‑practice guidance. Ensure adherence to testing, governance, and code‑promotion standards while actively monitoring system performance, data integrity, quality, and security controls. Use strong analytical, critical‑thinking, and debugging skills to identify, troubleshoot, and resolve system or process issues.</p><p></p><p>Enhance planning and forecasting capabilities by incorporating AI‑powered methods such as machine learning-based predictive forecasting, anomaly detection, and intelligent data validation. Design automation solutions that leverage AI to streamline data processing, improve forecast accuracy, and reduce manual workload across planning cycles. Collaborate regularly with management, colleagues, and cross‑functional partners to deliver project updates, recommend improvements, and present new development and AI‑driven capabilities that support strategic decision‑making.</p><p></p></div><p><span>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait. </span></p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43;<span> years of experience with development for Hyperion planning </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with full life cycle project management and development, including requirement gathering, design, development, testing, rollout, and implementation</span></p></li><li><p>Experience driving client and peer relationships and facilitating information-gathering sessions to elicit requirements using multiple methods</p></li><li><p>Experience with Oracle EPM AI Agents, including enabling, implementing, and monitoring AI capabilities within the platform</p></li><li><p>Experience incorporating AI‑powered methods such as machine learning-based predictive forecasting, anomaly detection, and intelligent data validation</p></li><li><p>Experience performing detailed analysis and research, managing deadlines across multiple deliverables, and creating detailed project documentation, including discussions, considerations, and requirements</p></li><li><p>Experience quickly learning new EPM software tools and developing integration and deployment strategies</p></li><li><p>Experience applying logical and critical thinking to address and process system issues and troubleshoot bugs</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with Government Cost Accounting and Forward Pricing Rate Proposals </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with managing applications that meet Sarbanes Oxley SOX or process and access controls</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of Databricks</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of basic ETL concepts </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 18 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Beavercreek-OH/FPGA-Developer_R0239364","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Beavercreek-OH/FPGA-Developer_R0239364","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"ee2b22b3857c7a6637bfd9b6c25c33e84eebf16dc7bf6296a21532c036dc8cbc","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"FPGA Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/FPGA-Developer_R0239364","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/FPGA-Developer_R0239364","locations":[{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"},{"label":"Wright Patterson AFB, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0239364","internal_job_id":"d5333478233a10015baa46fd01f40000","first_published_at":"2026-06-02","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"FPGA Developer The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big‑picture thinking to make an impact on national defense? You understand your client’s environment and how to develop the right systems to support their mission. Your ability to translate real‑world needs into technical specifications makes you a key contributor to delivering client‑focused engineering solutions.\n\nAs an experienced electrical engineer with a background in Field Programmable Gate Array (FPGA) design, you will help solve complex challenges that drive the development of next‑generation satellite systems. You will take on a hands‑on role in designing, implementing, and testing FPGA‑based processing architectures, while enhancing these systems through advanced technology solutions that meet demanding space and mission requirements.\n\nYou’ll apply your expertise while providing guidance to a cross-domain team focused on digital design, verification, and system integration. In this role, you will collaborate closely across engineering disciplines to ensure seamless integration of FPGA designs into spacecraft subsystems. Through this work, you will help translate system‑level requirements into robust hardware implementations that enable reliable on‑orbit performance.\n\nJoin our team and help shape the future of resilient space systems in support of national security.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience using Vivado for embedded system design\n\n- Experience with Digital Signal Processing mathematics and implementing algorithms in synthesizable HDL\n\n- Experience with scientific analysis software, such as MATLAB\n\n- Experience with benchtop equipment, including oscilloscopes, spectrum analyzers, arbitrary waveform generators, and vector signal generators\n\n- Knowledge of commercial RF and digital component and assembly distributors for rapid prototyping\n\n- Knowledge of wideband RF signal acquisition and generation, as well as FPGA development processes\n\n- Knowledge of RF signal propagation chain configurations\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering or Computer Engineering and 7+ years of experience in digital design through HDL and schematic layout, or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering or Computer Engineering and 5+ years of experience in digital design through HDL and schematic layout\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with FPGA development tools, such as AMD Vitis or Intel Quartus\n\n- Experience with EDA tools for HDL and RTL simulation, such as ModelSim, Questa, Xcelium, VCS, or Aldec\n\n- Knowledge of satellite requirements and design\n\n- Knowledge of space‑specific requirements, including system hardening\n\n- Knowledge of RADAR and Electronic Attack (EA) and Electronic Support (ES) concepts\n\n- Knowledge of embedded Linux and RTOS development, including U‑Boot, Yocto, BitBake, OpenEmbedded, or device tree components\n\n- Doctorate degree in Electrical Engineering or Computer Engineering\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"FPGA Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p><span>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big‑picture thinking to make an impact on national defense? You understand your client’s environment and how to develop the right systems to support their mission. Your ability to translate real‑world needs into technical specifications makes you a key contributor to delivering client‑focused engineering solutions.</span></p><p></p><p><span>As an experienced electrical engineer with a background in Field Programmable Gate Array (FPGA) design, you will help solve complex challenges that drive the development of next‑generation satellite systems. You will take on a hands‑on role in designing, implementing, and testing FPGA‑based processing architectures, while enhancing these systems through advanced technology solutions that meet demanding space and mission requirements.</span></p><p></p><p><span>You’ll apply your expertise while providing guidance to a cross-domain team focused on digital design, verification, and system integration. In this role, you will collaborate closely across engineering disciplines to ensure seamless integration of FPGA designs into spacecraft subsystems. Through this work, you will help translate system‑level requirements into robust hardware implementations that enable reliable on‑orbit performance.</span></p><p></p><p><span>Join our team and help shape the future of resilient space systems in support of national security.</span></p><p></p><p><span>Join us. The world can’t wait.</span></p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience using Vivado for embedded system design</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Digital Signal Processing mathematics and implementing algorithms in synthesizable HDL</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with scientific analysis software, such as MATLAB</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with benchtop equipment, including oscilloscopes, spectrum analyzers, arbitrary waveform generators, and vector signal generators</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of commercial RF and digital component and assembly distributors for rapid prototyping</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of wideband RF signal acquisition and generation, as well as FPGA development processes</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of RF signal propagation chain configurations</span></p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering or Computer Engineering and 7&#43; years of experience in digital design through HDL and schematic layout, or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering or Computer Engineering and 5&#43; years of experience in digital design through HDL and schematic layout</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with FPGA development tools, such as AMD Vitis or Intel Quartus</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with EDA tools for HDL and RTL simulation, such as ModelSim, Questa, Xcelium, VCS, or Aldec</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of satellite requirements and design</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of space‑specific requirements, including system hardening</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of RADAR and Electronic Attack (EA) and Electronic Support (ES) concepts</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of embedded Linux and RTOS development, including U‑Boot, Yocto, BitBake, OpenEmbedded, or device tree components</span></p></li><li><p><span>Doctorate degree in Electrical Engineering or Computer Engineering</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Front-End-Developer_R0243843","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Front-End-Developer_R0243843","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4cea5fc1fde49c8ff0677c939a5c12fd7a442b723d62bd9d94dcdfa549f599ee","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Front End Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Front-End-Developer_R0243843","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Front-End-Developer_R0243843","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243843","internal_job_id":"9b5fc83f94a31000cb10b7ec780b0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-06","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Front End Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a full stack develop er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a develop er like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production-ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a full stack develop er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution develop ed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience develop ing web applications using JavaScript or TypeScript with frameworks such as Angular, React, or Vue\n- Experience with Develop ment in Node.JS\n- Experience with usability analysis, automated testing develop ment, such as unit testing and E2E\n- Experience collaborating closely with sof tware develop ment teams\n- Experience in creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment\n- Ability to switch between programming languages and learn new ones as needed\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- HS diploma or GED\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 Security+ or CISSP Certification within 30 days of start date\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with ArcGIS JavaScript or geospatial web develop ment\n- Experience with Java Spring Framework\n- Experience with testing frameworks such as Jasmine, Karma, or Selenium\n- Experience scripting in Bash or Perl in Linux environments\n- Experience with JavaScript visualization libraries such as D3, Leaflet, or AG Grid\n- Experience with information security practices\n- Experience with Agile or Kanban  develop ment met hodologies\n- Knowledge of  JIRA, Confluence, Git, GitHub, or GitLab\n- Knowledge of standards across JavaScript, JSON, REST, CORS, Web architecture, and HTTP\n- Ability to work with geospatial tools, including ArcGIS\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Front End Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full stack <span>develop</span>er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a <span>develop</span>er like you with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a full stack <span>develop</span>er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution <span>develop</span>ed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing web applications using JavaScript or TypeScript with frameworks such as Angular, React, or Vue</li><li><span>Experience</span> with <span>Develop</span>ment in Node.JS</li><li><span>Experience</span> with usability analysis, automated testing <span>develop</span>ment, such as unit testing and E2E</li><li><span>Experience</span> collaborating closely with <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment teams</li><li><span>Experience</span> in creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment</li><li><span>Ability to</span> switch between programming languages and learn new ones as needed</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li><li><span>Ability to</span> obtain a DoD 8570 Security&#43; or CISSP <span>Certification</span> within 30 days of start date</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with ArcGIS JavaScript or geospatial web <span>develop</span>ment</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Java Spring Framework</li><li><span>Experience</span> with testing frameworks such as Jasmine, Karma, or Selenium</li><li><span>Experience</span> scripting in Bash or Perl in Linux environments</li><li><span>Experience</span> with JavaScript visualization libraries such as D3, Leaflet, or AG Grid</li><li><span>Experience</span> with information security practices</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile or Kanban <span>develop</span>ment <span>met</span>hodologies</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> JIRA, Confluence, Git, GitHub, or GitLab</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> standards across JavaScript, JSON, REST, CORS, Web architecture, and HTTP</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with geospatial tools, including ArcGIS</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
