rate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and product owners to deliver world-class solutions to implement a wide variety of AI use cases. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks.\n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for national security.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with artifi cia l intelligence, data science, sof tware engineering, or machine learning engineering, including developing and deploying models\n\n- Experience with generative and agentic AI technologies such as LLMs, MCP, LangChain, or LangGraph\n\n- Experience developing code using a common programming language, including Python, C++, Rus t, or Java\n\n- Experience with deep learning, computer vision, or generative AI\n\n- Experience with data handling and model development\n\n- Ability to solve client issues and problems\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Python coding and libraries, including scikit-learn, TensorFlow, or PyTorch\n\n- Experience with supervised and unsupervised learning\n\n- Experience leveraging AI productivity tools for coding using tools such as Cursor\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Machine Learning Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d AI and ML engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support innovation across the DoD market. As a machine learning engineer on our defense technology team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data. </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by implementing AI that enables faster mission success. You’ll be part of a large community of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and product owners to deliver world-class solutions to implement a wide variety of AI use cases. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for national security.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence, data science, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, or machine learning engineering, including developing and deploying models</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with generative and agentic AI technologies such as LLMs, MCP, LangChain, or LangGraph</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing code using a common programming language, including Python, C&#43;&#43;, <span>Rus</span>t, or Java</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with deep learning, computer vision, or generative AI</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data handling and model development</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> solve client issues and problems</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Python coding and libraries, including scikit-learn, TensorFlow, or PyTorch</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with supervised and unsupervised learning</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> leveraging AI productivity tools for coding using tools such as Cursor</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Machine Learning"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Machine Learning"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Aurora-CO/Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0246351","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Aurora-CO/Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0246351","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e1caca41337017439470783140e6b1b54f8a5ff51feb992e03499f1723042053","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Machine Learning Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aurora-CO/Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0246351","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aurora-CO/Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0246351","locations":[{"label":"Aurora, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246351","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a10010adc528e6dd10000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Machine Learning Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support the space industry. As a machine learning engineer on our space team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.  \n\nIn this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data scientists, physicists, and systems engineers to deliver world-class solutions to develop agentic AI solutions. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define ML strategy for intelligence community space projects.\n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience with operationalizing software in the cloud such as AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google\n\n- Experience with Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with data science or machine learning\n\n- Knowledge of python, java, or c++ programming\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with machine learning operations pipelines\n\n- Ability to deploy software into a production environment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\n- Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Machine Learning Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support the space industry. As a machine learning engineer on our space team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.  </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data scientists, physicists, and systems engineers to deliver world-class solutions to develop agentic AI solutions. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define ML strategy for intelligence community space projects.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with operationalizing software in the cloud such as AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google</p></li><li><p>Experience with Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Experience with data science or machine learning</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of python, java, or c&#43;&#43; programming</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with machine learning operations pipelines</p></li><li><p>Ability to deploy software into a production environment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field</p></li><li><p>Security&#43; Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Machine Learning"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Machine Learning"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Medical-Robotics-Embodied-AI-Advisor_R0246496","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Medical-Robotics-Embodied-AI-Advisor_R0246496","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5f56b73f4db6a2b0a8df119d5769dc6075ff187c18f2cb3d977720279f8b9688","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Medical-Robotics-Embodied-AI-Advisor_R0246496","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Medical-Robotics-Embodied-AI-Advisor_R0246496","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246496","internal_job_id":"83b83551a7591001041e876757470000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor The Opportunity:  \nTo achieve an organization’s mission, leaders need strong team members who can create processes, communicate requirements, and develop innovative solutions throughout the execution of the mission. Whether completing an immediate task, recognizing a process gap, recommending a solution, or flexing to support an immerging requirement, our clients need someone who can help manage operations while managing responses to external inquiries in a timely manner. That is why we need an experience d Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor like you to provide technical expertise and project development for emerging opportunities within healthcare.\n\nAs part of our team, you'll serve as a strategic technical advisor to the Advanced Research Projects Agency for Health ( ARPA-H ) , helping conceptualize, create, and execute advanced government-funded research and development programs to accelerate better health outcomes for everyone. You’ll work with world-class scientists and engineers to support the development of high-impact solutions to society's most challenging health problems. You’ll leverage your technical expertise to provide strategic assessments of new technologies in support to senior ARPA-H decision-makers. You’ll maintain responsibility for producing and presenting findings and recommendations to a team of colleagues and clients on the feasibility and potential impact of future research programs, assisting with the management of current programs, and facilitating commer cia lization of successfully developed technologies. \n\nYou'll serve as a Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor helping clients to develop stakeholder management strategies, establish new business processes, and complete research and analysis to determine viable solutions. You will be responsible for managing incoming requirements, facilitating e nga gements within offices and across the agency, and being readily available to shift your focus to fulfill emerging client requests. Your attention to detail, flexibility, communication skills, understanding of the client's mission, and problem-solving will enable the mission's success.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n- Analyze and develop reports on the state-of-the-art for embodied surgical AI and related spaces.\n- Support strategy development and program execution for embodied surgical AI and related initiatives.\n- Evaluate the conceptual and technical soundness of research programs spanning embodied surgical AI and other AI applications in the health space.\n- Assist in defining program goals, technical milestones, budget s, and performer expectations for high-impact scientific initiatives.\n- Conduct technical reviews of performer progress to ensure alignment with ARPA-H objectives.\n- Interact with clients, government offi cia ls, and other executives in various sectors.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience supporting and advising government leadership or federal research programs\n- Knowledge of AI, machine learning, and robotics, including in areas of imitation learning, medical robotics control systems, foundation models for physical AI, or world modeling\n- Ability to manage budget s, technical milestones, and multidisciplinary research efforts across multi-site or multi-performer programs\n- Ability to travel up to 25% of the time\n- Master’s degree in Engineering\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with AI systems that are physically integrated into surgical robots or operating environments\n- Experience in the health, medical, or biological sciences spaces\n- Experience operating within a government environment\n- Experience supporting senior federal leaders\n- Ability to manage multiple priorities at once\n- Possession of strong communication skills\n- Doctorate degree in Health or Biological Sciences\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>To achieve an organization’s mission, leaders need strong team members who can create processes, communicate requirements, and develop innovative solutions throughout the execution of the mission. Whether completing an immediate task, recognizing a process gap, recommending a solution, or flexing to support an immerging requirement, our clients need someone who can help manage operations while managing responses to external inquiries in a timely manner. That is why we need an <span>experience</span>d Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor like you to provide technical expertise and project development for emerging opportunities within healthcare.</p><p></p><p>As part of our team, you&#39;ll serve as a strategic technical advisor to the Advanced Research Projects Agency for Health <span>(</span>ARPA-H<span>)</span>, helping conceptualize, create, and execute advanced government-funded research and development programs to accelerate better health outcomes for everyone. You’ll work with world-class scientists and engineers to support the development of high-impact solutions to society&#39;s most challenging health problems. You’ll leverage your technical expertise to provide strategic assessments of new technologies in support to senior ARPA-H decision-makers. You’ll maintain responsibility for producing and presenting findings and recommendations to a team of colleagues and clients on the feasibility and potential impact of future research programs, assisting with the management of <span>current</span> programs, and facilitating commer<span>cia</span>lization of successfully developed technologies. </p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll serve as a Medical Robotics Embodied AI Advisor helping clients to develop stakeholder management strategies, establish new business processes, and complete research and analysis to determine viable solutions. You will be responsible for managing incoming requirements, facilitating e<span>nga</span>gements within offices and across the agency, and being readily available to shift your focus to fulfill emerging client requests. Your attention to detail, flexibility, communication skills, understanding of the client&#39;s mission, and problem-solving will enable the mission&#39;s success.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li>Analyze and develop reports on the state-of-the-art for embodied surgical AI and <span>related</span> spaces.</li><li>Support strategy development and program execution for embodied surgical AI and <span>related</span> initiatives.</li><li>Evaluate the conceptual and technical soundness of research programs spanning embodied surgical AI <span>and other</span> AI applications in the health space.</li><li>Assist in defining program goals, technical milestones, <span>budget</span>s, and performer expectations for high-impact scientific initiatives.</li><li>Conduct technical reviews of performer progress to ensure alignment with ARPA-H objectives.</li><li>Interact with clients, government offi<span>cia</span>ls, <span>and other</span> executives in various sectors.</li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> supporting and advising government leadership or federal research programs</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> AI, machine learning, and robotics, including in areas of imitation learning, medical robotics control systems, foundation models for physical AI, or world modeling</li><li><span>Ability to</span> manage <span>budget</span>s, technical milestones, and multidisciplinary research efforts across multi-site or multi-performer programs</li><li><span>Ability to</span> travel up to 25% of the time</li><li><span>Master’s degree</span> in Engineering</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with AI systems that are physically integrated into surgical robots or operating environments</li><li><span>Experience</span> in the health, medical, or biological sciences spaces</li><li><span>Experience</span> operating within a government environment</li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting senior federal leaders</li><li><span>Ability to</span> manage multiple priorities at once</li><li><span>Possession of</span> strong communication skills</li><li><span>Doctorate degree</span> in Health or Biological Sciences</li></ul><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Robotics"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Bethesda-MD/Microsoft-Dynamics-Developer_R0243848","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Bethesda-MD/Microsoft-Dynamics-Developer_R0243848","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"566faf65d0e0455e1b2336de1999f5d72bcac17d2c1049685002eec25ff14106","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Microsoft Dynamics Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Bethesda-MD/Microsoft-Dynamics-Developer_R0243848","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Bethesda-MD/Microsoft-Dynamics-Developer_R0243848","locations":[{"label":"Bethesda, MD"},{"label":"Silver Spring, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243848","internal_job_id":"9aa9ab4a63ca1000be56bbeb1c470000","first_published_at":"2026-07-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Microsoft Dynamics Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a Dynamics 365 Contact Center Developer, you will design, configure, and extend Microsoft Customer Service and Omnichannel capabilities, while integrating modern AI and Copilot features that enhance routing, case handling, agent assist, and customer experience. You’ll build and optimize core customer service workflows, Dataverse components, routing logic, and agent workspace experiences that support multi‑tier contact center operations across the enterprise.\n\nYou’ll also help shape the contact center of the future by incorporating genera AI into day‑to‑day service delivery. This includes building AI‑assisted experiences, controlled topics, intent models, knowledge grounding, conversation summarization, and automation patterns that improve agent efficiency and reduce operational burden.\n\nYou’ll work with analysts, contact center SMEs, architects, and data teams to translate operational requirements into scalable CRM configuration, AI‑enabled workflows, and compliant implementation patterns. Your combined CRM and AI expertise will accelerate modernization and elevate the service experience across Centers.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience configuring Dynamics 365 Customer Service or Omnichannel, including forms, views, business rules, SLAs, queues, routing, and case processes\n\n- 5+ years of experience designing or enhancing applications using Power Platform, including Dataverse, model‑driven apps, Power Pages, and canvas apps\n\n- Experience configuring or extending Dataverse tables, relationships, security roles, automation, or workflows\n\n- Experience implementing routing rules, workstreams, session templates, agent‑workspace components, or interaction handling workflows\n\n- Experience working with business stakeholders to document requirements, map customer service workflows, and design optimized processes\n\n- Experience with Power Automate or tools to support automation, integrations, or process orchestration\n\n- Ability to work within Agile delivery teams to design, configure, test, and validate CRM and AI‑enabled capabilities\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Copilot Studio, conversational AI, intent classification, agent assist prompts, adaptive cards, or generative orchestration\n\n- Experience building AI‑enabled workflows such as interaction summaries, recommended actions, knowledge grounding, or automated routing suggestions\n\n- Experience designing customer‑experience journeys or optimizing contact center workflows using AI insights or automation\n\n- Experience with additional coding languages or integration patterns such as JavaScript or APIs\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Microsoft Dynamics Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As a Dynamics 365 Contact Center Developer, you will design, configure, and extend Microsoft Customer Service and Omnichannel capabilities, while integrating modern AI and Copilot features that enhance routing, case handling, agent assist, and customer experience. You’ll build and optimize core customer service workflows, Dataverse components, routing logic, and agent workspace experiences that support multi‑tier contact center operations across the enterprise.</p><p></p><p>You’ll also help shape the contact center of the future by incorporating genera AI into day‑to‑day service delivery. This includes building AI‑assisted experiences, controlled topics, intent models, knowledge grounding, conversation summarization, and automation patterns that improve agent efficiency and reduce operational burden.</p><p></p><p>You’ll work with analysts, contact center SMEs, architects, and data teams to translate operational requirements into scalable CRM configuration, AI‑enabled workflows, and compliant implementation patterns. Your combined CRM and AI expertise will accelerate modernization and elevate the service experience across Centers.</p><p></p><p><span>Join us. The world can’t wait.</span></p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience configuring Dynamics 365 Customer Service or Omnichannel, including forms, views, business rules, SLAs, queues, routing, and case processes</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience designing or enhancing applications using Power Platform, including Dataverse, model‑driven apps, Power Pages, and canvas apps</p></li><li><p>Experience configuring or extending Dataverse tables, relationships, security roles, automation, or workflows</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing routing rules, workstreams, session templates, agent‑workspace components, or interaction handling workflows</p></li><li><p>Experience working with business stakeholders to document requirements, map customer service workflows, and design optimized processes</p></li><li><p>Experience with Power Automate or tools to support automation, integrations, or process orchestration</p></li><li><p>Ability to work within Agile delivery teams to design, configure, test, and validate CRM and AI‑enabled capabilities</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Copilot Studio, conversational AI, intent classification, agent assist prompts, adaptive cards, or generative orchestration</p></li><li><p>Experience building AI‑enabled workflows such as interaction summaries, recommended actions, knowledge grounding, or automated routing suggestions</p></li><li><p>Experience designing customer‑experience journeys or optimizing contact center workflows using AI insights or automation</p></li><li><p>Experience with additional coding languages or integration patterns such as JavaScript or APIs</p></li></ul><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"249d47fc302465d1c0db53b706c2a28bb766401344ac7cf3c0e831554afa9049","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","locations":[{"label":"Suffolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245326","internal_job_id":"d2fc07c005731000ba994c4e71360000","first_published_at":"2026-07-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nYou will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.\n\nAs part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with developing software in Java, C++, C, and or C#\n\n- Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows\n\n- Experience working in Linux environments\n\n- Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol\n\n- Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling & Simulation (M&S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization\n\n- Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems\n\n- Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases\n\n- Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&S tools\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations\n\n- Experience with TAK products\n\n- Experience working within the SOF communities\n\n- Experience building and managing containers\n\n- Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines\n\n- Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools\n\n- Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><div><p>You will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.</p><p></p><p>As part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&amp;S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.</p></div><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with developing software in Java, C&#43;&#43;, C, and or C#</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working in Linux environments</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling &amp; Simulation (M&amp;S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&amp;S tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with TAK products</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within the SOF communities</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building and managing containers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"aa40d42ade35a95b76ea43a8f300c7d83de898f57c979fb78bee3dfa17c91275","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","locations":[{"label":"Suffolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245332","internal_job_id":"45e74e1697ae1000b8495c2bbcc00000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nYou will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.\n\nAs part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait. \n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with developing software in Java, C++, C, or C#\n\n- Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows\n\n- Experience working in Linux environments\n\n- Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol\n\n- Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling & Simulation (M&S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization\n\n- Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems\n\n- Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases\n\n- Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&S tools\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations\n\n- Experience with TAK products\n\n- Experience working within the SOF communities\n\n- Experience building and managing containers\n\n- Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines\n\n- Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools\n\n- Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><div><p>You will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.</p><p></p><p>As part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&amp;S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.</p></div><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with developing software in Java, C&#43;&#43;, C, or C#</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working in Linux environments</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling &amp; Simulation (M&amp;S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&amp;S tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with TAK products</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within the SOF communities</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building and managing containers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Beavercreek-OH/Modeling-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0246853","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Beavercreek-OH/Modeling-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0246853","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c9f8a11186da64acd781f4394c97b9ae76410ec93a8bc431828d753b740d5bea","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Modeling and Simulation Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Modeling-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0246853","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Modeling-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0246853","locations":[{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246853","internal_job_id":"83b83551a759100177e1441e4b490000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Modeling and Simulation Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAs a sof tware engineer, you know that good sof tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. You need the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for a sof tware engineer like you to develop efficient and effective sof tware, from vision to production-ready systems, in an exciting, agile environment. \n\nAs a sof tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to deliver complete end-to-end solutions to your clients. Using your sof tware engineering expertise, you’ll analyze the environment to ensure that your team’s solutions consider the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. You’ll sharpen your skills as you master new tools and techniques while helping to identify and implement system improvements.\n\nWork with us as we develop systems to create change for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience designing, modifying, develop ing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications using Agile met hods    \n\n- 3+ years of experience working with C++ \n\n- Experience with modeling and simulation frameworks\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications\n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems in a collaborative team environment \n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with Simulation Models, including Radar, Sensors, or Aircraft\n\n- Experience with pre- or post-processing scripting for large data sets \n\n- Experience with Modeling and Simulation frameworks, such as AFSIM, EAAGLES, FLAMES or Simulation Engines, such as Unreal and RavEngine\n\n- Experience with Agile met hodology, extreme programming, sof tware engineering, product management, and sof tware products \n\n- Experience with Data Modeling Architecture\n\n- Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization\n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Modeling and Simulation Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As a <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know that good <span>sof</span>tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. You need the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to <span>develop</span> a user-focused solution. We’re looking for a <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to <span>develop</span> efficient and effective <span>sof</span>tware, from vision to production-ready systems, in an exciting, agile environment. </p><p></p><p>As a <span>sof</span>tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to deliver complete end-to-end solutions to your clients. Using your <span>sof</span>tware engineering expertise, you’ll analyze the environment to ensure that your team’s solutions consider the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. You’ll sharpen your <span>skills</span> as you master new tools and techniques while helping to identify and implement system improvements.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we <span>develop</span> systems to create change for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, <span>develop</span>ing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using Agile <span>met</span>hods    </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working with C&#43;&#43; </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with modeling and simulation frameworks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems in a collaborative team environment </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Simulation Models, including Radar, Sensors, or Aircraft</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with pre- or post-processing scripting for large data sets </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Modeling and Simulation frameworks, such as AFSIM, EAAGLES, FLAMES or Simulation Engines, such as Unreal and RavEngine</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology, extreme programming, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, product management, and <span>sof</span>tware products </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Data Modeling Architecture</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Manassas-VA/Modernization-Software-Engineer_R0241651","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Manassas-VA/Modernization-Software-Engineer_R0241651","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"de49645ed82290f5729f82dc388ad425dc75ad6d21ef0f256c927aec3ec9ea31","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Modernization Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Manassas-VA/Modernization-Software-Engineer_R0241651","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Manassas-VA/Modernization-Software-Engineer_R0241651","locations":[{"label":"Manassas, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241651","internal_job_id":"2aa713bd94ca1000c9db393bbb8f0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-08","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Modernization Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nAre you a driven software developer ready to modernize mission-critical systems that directly impact national defense? As a software engineer, you’ll contribute to transforming legacy code into robust, scalable solutions that help ensure Navy combat systems remain effective. If you’re looking for the chance to make a difference, we need you on our team. This role is more than just coding. You’ll work on a small, embedded software development team that performs hands-on analysis of legacy system complexity, deployment of advanced development tools, and integration of modernized solutions. As an experienced software engineer, you’ll engage with the client daily to execute targeted enhancements.\n \nWork with us as we develop systems to create change for the better.\n \nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of software development in Rust and C or C++, including complexity analysis, integration testing, and debugging in a professional environment\n\n- Experience with containerization such as Docker or Kubernetes, and CI/CD\n\n- Knowledge of Linux and Windows environments, and networking fundamentals and tools such as Git, SSH, PuTTY, or CLI\n\n- Knowledge of foundational software engineering principles such as modularity, memory management, design patterns, code review, or documentation\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Python\n\n- Experience in modernizing legacy code\n\n- Experience with Navy acoustic or sonar systems, or other real-time signal processing\n\n- Knowledge of modern streaming platforms such as Kafka or Redpanda\n\n- Ability to display interest in applying AI-forward approaches to developer workflows such as hosting LLMs, vector databases, or LangChain\n\n- Secret clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Modernization Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Are you a driven software developer ready to modernize mission-critical systems that directly impact national defense? As a software engineer, you’ll contribute to transforming legacy code into robust, scalable solutions that help ensure Navy combat systems remain effective. If you’re looking for the chance to make a difference, we need you on our team. This role is more than just coding. You’ll work on a small, embedded software development team that performs hands-on analysis of legacy system complexity, deployment of advanced development tools, and integration of modernized solutions. As an experienced software engineer, you’ll engage with the client daily to execute targeted enhancements.<br /> </p><p>Work with us as we develop systems to create change for the better.<br /> </p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of software development in Rust and C or C&#43;&#43;, including complexity analysis, integration testing, and debugging in a professional environment</p></li><li><p>Experience with containerization such as Docker or Kubernetes, and CI/CD</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Linux and Windows environments, and networking fundamentals and tools such as Git, SSH, PuTTY, or CLI</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of foundational software engineering principles such as modularity, memory management, design patterns, code review, or documentation</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Python</p></li><li><p>Experience in modernizing legacy code</p></li><li><p>Experience with Navy acoustic or sonar systems, or other real-time signal processing</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modern streaming platforms such as Kafka or Redpanda</p></li><li><p>Ability to display interest in applying AI-forward approaches to developer workflows such as hosting LLMs, vector databases, or LangChain</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"05845875721a301e52af7c1923d6073c8e69cf9f8a72aa09d50938b363bb79a2","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Node.js Developer SME","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Herndon, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246020","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb40100111be97b511970000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Node.js Developer SME The Opportunity:  \nAs an expert Node.js developer, you know that a good site or system needs the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for an experienced back-end-focused developer with the software engineering skills it takes to identify potential risks, contribute to solution development, and create efficient and effective systems for our clients. \n\nAs a developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to deliver solutions. Using your software engineering experience, you’ll work with the development team to create custom tools, systems, and sites with consistent performance and scalability. \n\nIn this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you further your skillset and career. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.   \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience implementing, maintaining, and supporting agile software development\n\n- 5+ years of experience developing web applications\n\n- 2+ years of experience with Node.js software development\n\n- 2+ years of experience with TypeScript\n\n- Experience developing Linux-based systems in AWS\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree or 7+ years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree \n\n Nice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Angular\n\n- Experience with ElasticSearch\n\n- Experience with MongoDB\n\n- Experience with Redis\n\n- Experience with AWS\n\n- Experience with DevOps, CI/CD, and IaC\n\n- Experience with designing, implementing, and deploying microservices\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Node.js Developer SME<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As an expert Node.js developer, you know that a good site or system needs the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for an experienced back-end-focused developer with the software engineering skills it takes to identify potential risks, contribute to solution development, and create efficient and effective systems for our clients. </p><p></p><p>As a developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to deliver solutions. Using your software engineering experience, you’ll work with the development team to create custom tools, systems, and sites with consistent performance and scalability. </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you further your skillset and career. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.   </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience implementing, maintaining, and supporting agile software development</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience developing web applications</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Node.js software development</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with TypeScript</p></li><li><p>Experience developing Linux-based systems in AWS</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree or 7&#43; years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b> Nice If You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p>Experience with Angular</p></li><li><p>Experience with ElasticSearch</p></li><li><p>Experience with MongoDB</p></li><li><p>Experience with Redis</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS</p></li><li><p>Experience with DevOps, CI/CD, and IaC</p></li><li><p>Experience with designing, implementing, and deploying microservices</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Rockville-MD/OpenText-Content-Server-Developer_R0244080","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Rockville-MD/OpenText-Content-Server-Developer_R0244080","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9d209c1ba12c46acf546fb5dd1ee56ac61f18ca882959f69bcd734747e124ab2","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"OpenText Content Server Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rockville-MD/OpenText-Content-Server-Developer_R0244080","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rockville-MD/OpenText-Content-Server-Developer_R0244080","locations":[{"label":"Rockville, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244080","internal_job_id":"2adb8a04dcd21001b24c9b6290a40000","first_published_at":"2026-07-09","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"OpenText Content Server Developer The Opportunity:\nAs an embedded sof tware engineer, you know how to create and maintain cru cia l pieces of sof tware. You use your knowledge to write and optimize code that creates a bridge between pieces of sof tware, allowing them to communicate. We’re looking for an experience d embedded sof tware engineer like you to develop technology for our clients’ most important mission-forward challenges.  \n\nAs a senior embedded sof tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll support the develop ment of systems, sites, and tools for our clients. Using the latest tools and technology, you’ll write, test, and edit code in support of the team’s overall results. You’ll expand your skills as you develop and reverse engineer sof tware that supports hardware functionality on a wide range of devices, as well as configure solutions based on the platform being used. You’ll work with other team leaders to troubleshoot and correct operational issues, as well as with cybersecurity spe cia lists to ensure that the sof tware you’re creating is secure.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience with OpenText Content Server versions 16.x or 22.x\n- Experience configuring and customizing OpenText Content Server, including OScript module develop ment, workflows, forms, and Content Server Web Services such as SOAP or REST\n- Experience integrating OpenText with external systems using APIs, middleware, or enterprise service bus patterns\n- Experience develop ing technical documentation, migration strategies, implementation roadmaps, test plans, and deployment artifacts\n- Experience supporting secure, large-scale enterprise environments, ideally in federal or regulated industries\n- Experience with authentication or authorization frameworks such as SAML, OAuth, or LDAP / A, and with SQL databases, such as Oracle or SQL Server, system logs analysis, and performance tuning\n- Experience with OScript, WebReports, SmartUI or REST API extensions, Content Server administration, and module customization\n- Ability to develop automation, met adata models, and governance-enabling features that improve retrieval, classification, and lifecycle management of enterprise content\n- Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination based on client requirements\n- HS diploma or GED\n​\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with OpenText platforms such as AppWorks, Core Share, Extended ECM, or Documentum\n- Knowledge of cloud platforms such as Azure, AWS, or GovCloud equivalents\n- Possession of strong communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills\n- OpenText Content Server, AWS, or Azure certification s\n\nVetting:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a government investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements of the U.S. government client .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"OpenText Content Server Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know how to create and maintain cru<span>cia</span>l pieces of <span>sof</span>tware. You use your knowledge to write and optimize code that creates a bridge between pieces of <span>sof</span>tware, allowing them to communicate. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to <span>develop</span> technology for our clients’ most important mission-forward challenges.  </p><p></p><p>As a senior embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll support the <span>develop</span>ment of systems, sites, and tools for our clients. Using the latest tools and technology, you’ll write, test, and edit code in support of the team’s overall results. You’ll expand your <span>skills</span> as you <span>develop</span> and reverse engineer <span>sof</span>tware that supports hardware functionality on a wide range of devices, as well as configure solutions based on the platform being used. You’ll work with other team leaders to troubleshoot and correct operational issues, as well as with cybersecurity spe<span>cia</span>lists to ensure that the <span>sof</span>tware you’re creating is secure.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with OpenText Content Server versions 16.x or 22.x</li><li><span>Experience</span> configuring and customizing OpenText Content Server, including OScript module <span>develop</span>ment, workflows, forms, and Content Server Web Services such as SOAP or REST</li><li><span>Experience</span> integrating OpenText with external systems using APIs, middleware, or enterprise service bus patterns</li><li><span>Experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing technical documentation, migration strategies, implementation roadmaps, test plans, and deployment artifacts</li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting secure, large-scale enterprise environments, ideally in federal or regulated industries</li><li><span>Experience</span> with authentication or authorization frameworks such as SAML, OAuth, or LDAP<span>/</span>A, and with SQL databases, such as Oracle or SQL Server, system logs analysis, and performance tuning</li><li><span>Experience</span> with OScript, WebReports, SmartUI or REST API extensions, Content Server administration, and module customization</li><li><span>Ability to</span> <span>develop</span> automation, <span>met</span>adata models, and governance-enabling features that improve retrieval, classification, and lifecycle management of enterprise content</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination based on client requirements</span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li></ul><p>​</p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with OpenText platforms such as AppWorks, Core Share, Extended ECM, or Documentum</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> cloud platforms such as Azure, AWS, or GovCloud equivalents</li><li><span>Possession of</span> strong communication, analytical, and problem-solving <span>skills</span></li><li>OpenText Content Server, AWS, or Azure <span>certification</span>s</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Vetting:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a government investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements of the U.S. government client</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Platform-Engineer_R0240174-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Platform-Engineer_R0240174-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e8c143462f3d34de7cf8cdf58b5f33134602cf9a7438db58d1f33b75cd5a36f2","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Platform-Engineer_R0240174-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Platform-Engineer_R0240174-1","locations":[{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240174","internal_job_id":"4281f7c3ce06100208312d9590010000","first_published_at":"2026-06-22","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nJoin a mission focused team supporting the modernization, automation, and secure delivery of enterprise software capabilities for the Department of Defense. As a Platform Engineer, you will help design, develop, and enhance a modern application platform leveraging‑ Kubernetes, container services, and DevSecOps pipelines. You will collaborate with software developers, system administrators, and security professionals to streamline delivery, improve automation, and mature platform services supporting continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD).\n\nYou will apply hands-on experience with modern developer tooling, container orchestration, infrastructure automation, and RMF-aligned best practices to strengthen platform reliability and developer experience across the organization. This role also provides opportunities to lead small teams, mentor junior engineers, and help define platform standards, processes, and technical direction.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with DoD RMF or STIGs\n\n- Experience with automation, including Git workflows, package and dependency management, and scripting\n\n- Experience researching tools and contributing to platform development, including processes, standards, and procedures\n\n- Experience optimizing CI/CD workflows, including build and package automation, pipeline tooling integration, and secure delivery processes\n\n- Experience with developer and platform tooling, such as Git, Bitbucket, Bamboo, Jenkins, Harbor, Nexus, or Jira\n\n- Experience with containerized applications, including deployment automation using YAML, and with Unix Shell scripting or command-line tooling\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience contributing to Agile-based team ceremonies and workflows\n\n- Ability to enhance developer workflows and overall developer experience\n\n- Ability to manage multiple priorities and resolve technical challenges efficiently\n\n- Possession of strong problem solving, deconfliction, and issue resolution skills\n\n- Possession of strong verbal and written communication skills\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Platform Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p><span>Join a mission focused team supporting the modernization, automation, and secure delivery of enterprise software capabilities for the Department of Defense. As a Platform Engineer, you will help design, develop, and enhance a modern application platform leveraging‑ Kubernetes, container services, and DevSecOps pipelines. You will collaborate with software developers, system administrators, and security professionals to streamline delivery, improve automation, and mature platform services supporting continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD).</span></p><p></p><p><span>You will apply hands-on experience with modern developer tooling, container orchestration, infrastructure automation, and RMF-aligned best practices to strengthen platform reliability and developer experience across the organization. This role also provides opportunities to lead small teams, mentor junior engineers, and help define platform standards, processes, and technical direction.</span></p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with DoD RMF or STIGs</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with automation, including Git workflows, package and dependency management, and scripting</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience researching tools and contributing to platform development, including processes, standards, and procedures</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience optimizing CI/CD workflows, including build and package automation, pipeline tooling integration, and secure delivery processes</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with developer and platform tooling, such as Git, Bitbucket, Bamboo, Jenkins, Harbor, Nexus, or Jira</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with containerized applications, including deployment automation using YAML, and </span><span>with Unix Shell scripting or command-line tooling</span></p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience contributing to Agile-based team ceremonies and workflows</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to enhance developer workflows and overall developer experience</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to manage multiple priorities and resolve technical challenges efficiently</span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of strong problem solving, deconfliction, and issue resolution skills</span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of strong verbal and written communication skills</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b><br />Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret<span class=\"emphasis-3\"> </span>clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245676","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245676","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"34ddcb68554bcd4d95ed9dccd016846e2e35bb6a4f12956078e325ff15901bb3","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245676","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245676","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245676","internal_job_id":"fe4132e52a9210019dff276d107b0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud”, but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop , manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management sof tware to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. \n\nAs a Platform Engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with current container sof tware to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform experience , you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are met throughout the containerization process.\n\nYou’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the develop ment of critical cloud platforms.\n\nWork with us to use cloud platform technology for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with sof tware develop ment or programming in a DevOps environment   \n\n- 1+ years of experience with automation tools, including Terraform, Ansible, CloudFormation, or Puppet  \n\n- Experience with Kubernetes\n\n- Knowledge of architecting and deploying applications on Amazon Web Services ( AWS ) or Micro sof t Azure\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 Security+ or CISSP Certification within 30 days of start date\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience managing Git-based version control systems and continuous integration and continuous delivery ( CI / CD )  pipelines, including GitLab and GitHub  \n\n- Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code environments, including activities around the automated server or network configurations, large-scale sof tware deployments, or monitoring and testing such as CI / CD\n\n- Experience provisioning and managing infrastructure and applications in cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform ( GCP )   \n\n- Experience with system integration using a variety of protocols, including JSON, REST, and XML  \n\n- Experience with scripting in Bash, PowerShell, Python, Groovy, or Ruby  \n\n- Experience leveraging JSON, YAML, or XML for configuration  \n\n- Bachelor's degree in STEM\n\n- Agile, DevOps, or Cloud Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud”, but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to <span>develop</span>, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to <span>develop</span> container management <span>sof</span>tware to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. <br /><br />As a Platform Engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical <span>skills</span> to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your <span>skills</span> using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with <span>current</span> container <span>sof</span>tware to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform <span>experience</span>, you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are <span>met</span> throughout the containerization process.</p><p></p><p>You’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps <span>skills</span> while supporting the <span>develop</span>ment of critical cloud platforms.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use cloud platform technology for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment or programming in a DevOps environment   </p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with automation tools, including Terraform, Ansible, CloudFormation, or Puppet  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> architecting and deploying applications on Amazon Web Services <span>(</span>AWS<span>)</span> or Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> obtain a DoD 8570 Security&#43; or CISSP <span>Certification</span> within 30 days of start date</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> managing Git-based version control systems and continuous integration and continuous delivery <span>(</span>CI<span>/</span>CD<span>)</span> pipelines, including GitLab and GitHub  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure-as-Code environments, including activities around the automated server or network configurations, large-scale <span>sof</span>tware deployments, or monitoring and testing such as CI<span>/</span>CD</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> provisioning and managing infrastructure and applications in cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform <span>(</span>GCP<span>)</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with system integration using a variety of protocols, including JSON, REST, and XML  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with scripting in Bash, PowerShell, Python, Groovy, or Ruby  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> leveraging JSON, YAML, or XML for configuration  </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in STEM</p></li><li><p>Agile, DevOps, or Cloud <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245680","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245680","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e8467e00e69433d2b5775fd9176b0ed460d417782df723e94412c24c0d8d4be5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245680","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0245680","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245680","internal_job_id":"2b414f219eed1001adac0c3049540000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a platform developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an experience d developer like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production-ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a platform developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications using Agile met hods  \n- 2+ years of experience with automation tools, including Terraform, Ansible, CloudFormation, or Puppet \n- Experience with Agile met hodology\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n- Knowledge of architecting and deploying applications on Amazon Web Services ( AWS ) or Micro sof t Azure\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- HS diploma or GED\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 Security+ or CISSP Certification within 30 days of start date\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience managing Git-based version control systems and continuous integration and continuous delivery ( CI / CD ) pipelines, including GitLab and GitHub \n- Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code environments, including activities around the automated server or network configurations, large-scale sof tware deployments, or monitoring and testing such as CI / CD\n- Experience provisioning and managing infrastructure and applications in cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform ( GCP )  \n- Experience with system integration using a variety of protocols, including JSON, REST, and XML \n- Experience with scripting in Bash, PowerShell, Python, Groovy, or Ruby \n- Experience leveraging JSON, YAML, or XML for configuration \n- Secret clearance \n- Agile Certification\n- DevOps Certification\n- Cloud Certification\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a platform developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d developer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a platform developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using Agile <span>met</span>hods  </li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with automation tools, including Terraform, Ansible, CloudFormation, or Puppet </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> architecting and deploying applications on Amazon Web Services <span>(</span>AWS<span>)</span> or Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li><li><span>Ability to</span> obtain a DoD 8570 Security&#43; or CISSP <span>Certification</span> within 30 days of start date</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> managing Git-based version control systems and continuous integration and continuous delivery <span>(</span>CI<span>/</span>CD<span>)</span> pipelines, including GitLab and GitHub </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure-as-Code environments, including activities around the automated server or network configurations, large-scale <span>sof</span>tware deployments, or monitoring and testing such as CI<span>/</span>CD</li><li><span>Experience</span> provisioning and managing infrastructure and applications in cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform <span>(</span>GCP<span>)</span> </li><li><span>Experience</span> with system integration using a variety of protocols, including JSON, REST, and XML </li><li><span>Experience</span> with scripting in Bash, PowerShell, Python, Groovy, or Ruby </li><li><span>Experience</span> leveraging JSON, YAML, or XML for configuration </li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li>Agile <span>Certification</span></li><li>DevOps <span>Certification</span></li><li>Cloud <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0247028","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0247028","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"584b0159fb2d759bcb1bf981a5aec9127669ef73e067a7e8bcab0896200387b5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0247028","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0247028","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"},{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247028","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d01001ed916398b0f20000","first_published_at":"2026-08-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management sof tware to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. \n\nAs a Platform Engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with current container sof tware to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform experience , you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are met throughout the containerization process.\n\nYou’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the development of critical cloud platforms.\n\nWork with us to use cloud platform technology for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with sof tware development or programming in a DevOps environment   \n\n- 1+ years of experience with automation tools, including Terraform, Ansible, CloudFormation, or Puppet  \n\n- Experience with Kubernetes\n\n- Knowledge of architecting and deploying applications on Amazon Web Services ( AWS ) or Micro sof t Azure\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 Security+ or CISSP Certification within 30 days of start date\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience managing Git-based version control systems and CI / CD pipelines, including GitLab and GitHub  \n\n- Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code environments, including activities around the automated server or network configurations, large-scale sof tware deployments, or monitoring and testing such as CI / CD\n\n- Experience provisioning and managing infrastructure and applications in cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform ( GCP )   \n\n- Experience with system integration using a variety of protocols, including JSON, REST, and XML  \n\n- Experience with scripting in Bash, PowerShell, Python, Groovy, or Ruby  \n\n- Experience leveraging JSON, YAML, or XML for configuration  \n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\n- Agile, DevOps, or Cloud Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management <span>sof</span>tware to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. <br /><br />As a Platform Engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with <span>current</span> container <span>sof</span>tware to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform <span>experience</span>, you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are <span>met</span> throughout the containerization process.</p><p></p><p>You’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the development of critical cloud platforms.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use cloud platform technology for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware development or programming in a DevOps environment   </p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with automation tools, including Terraform, Ansible, CloudFormation, or Puppet  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> architecting and deploying applications on Amazon Web Services <span>(</span>AWS<span>)</span> or Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> obtain a DoD 8570 Security&#43; or CISSP <span>Certification</span> within 30 days of start date</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> managing Git-based version control systems and CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines, including GitLab and GitHub  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Infrastructure-as-Code environments, including activities around the automated server or network configurations, large-scale <span>sof</span>tware deployments, or monitoring and testing such as CI<span>/</span>CD</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> provisioning and managing infrastructure and applications in cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform <span>(</span>GCP<span>)</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with system integration using a variety of protocols, including JSON, REST, and XML  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with scripting in Bash, PowerShell, Python, Groovy, or Ruby  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> leveraging JSON, YAML, or XML for configuration  </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</p></li><li><p>Agile, DevOps, or Cloud <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 10 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0242482","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0242482","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"43f6fcd3181f272c1217aa43be7ec837926135cf4f49cdc4ff5e3af70d419423","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0242482","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Platform-Engineer_R0242482","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242482","internal_job_id":"dfff4684f336100158702bd9ca9d0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a Platform Engineer, you’ll help build and operate the foundational infrastructure behind an enterprise Digital Twin and modeling and simulation platform. You’ll support containerized platforms and deployment pipelines that enable real-time visualization, simulation, and analytics across hybrid cloud and on-prem environments.\n\nHere, you’ll work alongside senior platform, DevOps, and application engineers in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment. You’ll gain hands-on experience supporting systems operating under DoD security and ATO constraints while learning how large-scale digital platforms are built and sustained.\n\nYou’ll be building and sustaining critical systems and will have the opportunity to work side by side with our partners to ensure that we keep our platforms reliable, secure, and scalable.\n\nWork with us to use cloud platform technology for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience working with containerized applications or platforms\n- 5+ years of experience with Kubernetes fundamentals\n- 5+ years of experience with Docker or OCI containers\n- Experience working in Linux-based environments\n- Knowledge of IaC tools such as Terraform or Helm\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience supporting hybrid cloud or on-prem deployments\n- Knowledge of regulated, government, or DoD environments\n- Knowledge of container hardening or secure baseline concepts\n- Secret clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a Platform Engineer, you’ll help build and operate the foundational infrastructure behind an enterprise Digital Twin and modeling and simulation platform. You’ll support containerized platforms and deployment pipelines that enable real-time visualization, simulation, and analytics across <span>hybrid</span> cloud and on-prem environments.</p><p><br />Here, you’ll work alongside senior platform, DevOps, and application engineers in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment. You’ll gain hands-on <span>experience</span> supporting systems operating under DoD security and ATO constraints while learning how large-scale digital platforms are built and sustained.</p><p></p><p>You’ll be building and sustaining critical systems and will have the opportunity to work side by side with our partners to ensure that we keep our platforms reliable, secure, and scalable.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use cloud platform technology for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working with containerized applications or platforms</li><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Kubernetes fundamentals</li><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Docker or OCI containers</li><li><span>Experience</span> working in Linux-based environments</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> IaC tools such as Terraform or Helm</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> supporting <span>hybrid</span> cloud or on-prem deployments</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> regulated, government, or DoD environments</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> container hardening or secure baseline concepts</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Quantum-Algorithms-Developer_R0244204","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Quantum-Algorithms-Developer_R0244204","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"42b0acd79f04afa55dd08c062eeb5b48e6c5c123e1f4e9c6b8ecba2ae4410ad6","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Quantum Algorithms Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Quantum-Algorithms-Developer_R0244204","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Quantum-Algorithms-Developer_R0244204","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"},{"label":"Annapolis Junction, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244204","internal_job_id":"b3c781f660711001f0178bd796330000","first_published_at":"2026-07-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Quantum Algorithms Developer The Opportunity :\nAre you fascinated by the possibilities of quantum technology? Do you want to transform its potential into reality? Are you passionate about collaboration and eager to build partnerships that drive innovation? We have an opportunity for you to leverage your scientific and technical expertise to advance quantum computing. In this role, you leverage your existing software development expertise to create programs that scale to meet the demands of AI and Quantum Computing.\n\nWhat You’ll Do :\n- Work closely with customers to understand their needs and provide direct quantum support in a laboratory or agile sof t war e development environment.\n\n- Apply your expertise in sof t war e engineering for problem-solving, design, development, and maintenance of cutting-edge quantum systems.\n\n- Identify and grow technical collaborations that form the foundation of engineering advancements.\n\n- Identify new growth areas for our quantum and artifi cia l intelligence businesses and build MVPs that excite customers.\n\n- Leverage principles of software development to build frameworks and programs that can take advantage of the latest and most appropriate computational resources for the customer's use case.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience in software development or quantum algorithms\n\n- Experience in laboratory or Agile software development environments\n\n- Experience with quantum algorithms, quantum software development, or quantum computing applications\n\n- Experience with Python, C, C++, or Rust\n\n- Knowledge of quantum computing hardware, control electronics, and environmental control requirements\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Physics, Computer Science, Electrical or Mechanical Engineering\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience managing teams of scientists, engineers, or developers\n\n- Experience in quantum materials, qubit control, or quantum information science, demonstrated through professional experience or publications\n\n- Experience performing research in quantum mechanics and the quantum effects that enable quantum computing, quantum sensing, or quantum networking\n\n- Possession of excellent collaboration skills across different technical backgrounds\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills, to communicate complex concepts\n\n- Master's degree in Physics, Computer Science, Electrical or Mechanical Engineering preferred; Doctorate degree in Physics, Material Science, or Mechanical or Electrical Engineering a plus\n\n- Quantum Materials-, Qubit Control-, or Quantum Information Science- related Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Quantum Algorithms Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>:</b></p><p>Are you fascinated by the possibilities of quantum technology? Do you want to transform its potential into reality? Are you passionate about collaboration and eager to build partnerships that drive innovation? We have an opportunity for you to leverage your scientific and technical expertise to advance quantum computing. In this role, you leverage your existing software development expertise to create programs that scale to meet the demands of AI and Quantum Computing.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Do</b><b>:</b></p><ul><li><p>Work closely with customers to understand their needs and provide direct quantum support in a laboratory or agile <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development environment.</p></li><li><p>Apply your expertise in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e engineering for problem-solving, design, development, and maintenance of cutting-edge quantum systems.</p></li><li><p>Identify and grow technical collaborations that form the foundation of engineering advancements.</p></li><li><p>Identify new growth areas for our quantum and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence businesses and build MVPs that excite customers.</p></li><li><p>Leverage principles of software development to build frameworks and programs that can take advantage of the latest and most appropriate computational resources for the customer&#39;s use case.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience in software development or quantum algorithms</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience in laboratory or Agile software development environments</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with quantum algorithms, quantum software development, or quantum computing applications</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Python, C, C&#43;&#43;, or Rust</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of quantum computing hardware, control electronics, and environmental control requirements</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Physics, Computer Science, Electrical or Mechanical Engineering</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience managing teams of scientists, engineers, or developers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience in quantum materials, qubit control, or quantum information science, demonstrated through professional experience or publications</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience performing research in quantum mechanics and the quantum effects that enable quantum computing, quantum sensing, or quantum networking</span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of excellent collaboration skills across different technical backgrounds</span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills, to communicate complex concepts</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree in Physics, Computer Science, Electrical or Mechanical Engineering preferred; Doctorate degree in Physics, Material Science, or Mechanical or Electrical Engineering a plus</span></p></li><li><p><span>Quantum Materials-, Qubit Control-, or Quantum Information Science- related Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["quant","software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Real-Time-Software-Engineer_R0247301","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Real-Time-Software-Engineer_R0247301","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4b2f2b76158151111587a3070656602cf89f7575456ef15faa8a442e4d0ef0dc","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Real-Time Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Real-Time-Software-Engineer_R0247301","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Real-Time-Software-Engineer_R0247301","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247301","internal_job_id":"71f630993997100115dbe7a3ebd50000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Real-Time Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAre you excited to apply RF theory to critical national security missions? Your expertise in RF digital signal processing software development will be critical to integrate, test, and evaluate RF software applications. Apply core principles, theories, and concepts to provide effective solutions for practical applications. Solve complex technical problems and deliver innovative solutions. Operate with substantial independence and provide oversight or mentorship for your team’s technical competencies. Collaborate effectively with minimal supervision, overseeing and mentoring junior employees as needed.\n\nThis is a hands-on engineering role focused on real-time software, including embedded systems, distributed systems, and hardware-software integration. You will work across software applications for RF applications which require and understanding of embedded software, firmware, distributed software, and machine learning to successfully execute. You will be debugging at every layer, from software behavior to system-level interactions in deployed hardware.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 6+ years of experience with software development languages, including Python, C, or C++\n\n- Experience with the design, development, and testing of real-time software\n\n- Experience with microservice architectures and tools such as Kubernetes or Docker, and optimizing applications for distributed environments\n\n- Experience using Agile processes and tools, including Jira or Confluence, and using version control, including GitHub\n\n- Experience developing software and firmware for embedded systems, such as SCPI, Ethernet, and Serial integration\n\n- Ability to work in a team environment to brainstorm and innovate new ideas\n\n- Ability to obtain a TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience leading and managing small to medium-sized engineering, integration, and testing projects\n\n- Experience using Windows and Linux systems; experience porting software from Windows to Linux, including compiling and cross-compiling libraries as needed\n\n- Experience with UI development, including Javascript, Rust, Angular, React\n\n- Experience with machine learning packages and building and testing neural network architectures using TensorFlow, Keras, or PyTorch\n\n- Experience with firmware development languages such as VHDL, Verilog, or CoreFire\n\n- Experience with RF theory, software defined radios, Low noise amplifiers\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master's degree in a STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Real-Time Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>Are you excited to apply RF theory to critical national security missions? Your expertise in RF digital signal processing software development will be critical to integrate, test, and evaluate RF software applications. Apply core principles, theories, and concepts to provide effective solutions for practical applications. Solve complex technical problems and deliver innovative solutions. Operate with substantial independence and provide oversight or mentorship for your team’s technical competencies. Collaborate effectively with minimal supervision, overseeing and mentoring junior employees as needed.</p><p></p><p>This is a hands-on engineering role focused on real-time software, including embedded systems, distributed systems, and hardware-software integration. You will work across software applications for RF applications which require and understanding of embedded software, firmware, distributed software, and machine learning to successfully execute. You will be debugging at every layer, from software behavior to system-level interactions in deployed hardware.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>6&#43; years of experience with software development languages, including Python, C, or C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p>Experience with the design, development, and testing of real-time software</p></li><li><p>Experience with microservice architectures and tools such as Kubernetes or Docker, and optimizing applications for distributed environments</p></li><li><p>Experience using Agile processes and tools, including Jira or Confluence, and using version control, including GitHub</p></li><li><p>Experience developing software and firmware for embedded systems, such as SCPI, Ethernet, and Serial integration</p></li><li><p>Ability to work in a team environment to brainstorm and innovate new ideas</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience leading and managing small to medium-sized engineering, integration, and testing projects</p></li><li><p>Experience using Windows and Linux systems; experience porting software from Windows to Linux, including compiling and cross-compiling libraries as needed</p></li><li><p>Experience with UI development, including Javascript, Rust, Angular, React</p></li><li><p>Experience with machine learning packages and building and testing neural network architectures using TensorFlow, Keras, or PyTorch</p></li><li><p>Experience with firmware development languages such as VHDL, Verilog, or CoreFire</p></li><li><p>Experience with RF theory, software defined radios, Low noise amplifiers</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Huntsville-AL/Reinforcement-Learning-AI-Engineer_R0245112","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Huntsville-AL/Reinforcement-Learning-AI-Engineer_R0245112","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"d410a4234a4402e83e52251f3f21f262b2176f467dbd8d09052220e04b213339","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Reinforcement Learning AI Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Huntsville-AL/Reinforcement-Learning-AI-Engineer_R0245112","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Huntsville-AL/Reinforcement-Learning-AI-Engineer_R0245112","locations":[{"label":"Huntsville, AL"},{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"El Segundo, CA"},{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245112","internal_job_id":"c4c927081f0510015c040507a7170000","first_published_at":"2026-08-05","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Reinforcement Learning AI Engineer The Opportunity:\nAre you an innovative and experience d artifi cia l intelligence ( AI ) developer spe cia lizing in reinforcement learning? Utilize your expertise in AI, data science, and machine learning (ML) engineering to train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data to drive real-world mission critical impact. You will collaborate with dynamic teams to translate reinforcement learning research into operational capability and production-grade code, bringing significant technological advancements that drive mission success.\n\nYou’ll join a growing community of ML engineers focused on delivering products and solutions to our customers’ most challenging problems. You’ll collaborate with a team of dedicated space, military, intelligence, engineering, and AI professionals to deliver cutting-edge solutions to solve issues of national importance.\n\nWhat You'll Work On:\n- Design, implement, and train reinforcement learning ( RL ) and multi-agent reinforcement learning ( MARL ) algorithms for complex decision-making problems.\n\n- Develop scalable training pipelines using Python and modern ML frameworks.\n\n- Build and evaluate agents in simulated environments using Gym or PettingZoo, high-fidelity simulators, or custom environments.\n\n- Apply RL techniques such as policy optimization, value-based learning, model-based RL, and imitation learning.\n\n- Collaborate with domain experts to define reward structures, constraints, and evaluation met rics aligned with mission objectives.\n\n- Implement distributed training workflows leveraging cloud compute, containerization, and orchestration technologies.\n\n- Transition trained models into production systems, following strong sof tware engineering best practices.\n\n- Contribute to system architecture and performance optimization in Python with opportunities to extend into C++ or Rus t for high-performance components. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience developing and training RL agents\n\n- Experience with AI, data science, ML engineering, or sof tware engineering\n\n- Experience with Gym or PettingZoo interfaces\n\n- Experience with ML frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or JAX\n\n- Experience developing technical solutions using Rus t, Python, or C++\n\n- Knowledge of RL and artifi cia l neural networks\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a CS, AI, or Engineering field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience applying RL to autonomy, control systems, or mission-scale\n\n- Experience with MARL\n\n- Experience with AFSIM or other high-fidelity simulation environments\n\n- Experience with embedded systems programming in Rus t, C, or C++\n\n- Experience in GPU programming, including CUDA or RAPID\n\n- Experience developing in-space solutions\n\n- Knowledge of modern sof tware design patterns, including microservice design and orchestration in Kubernetes deployment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master’s degree in CS, AI, Engineering, or a related field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Reinforcement Learning AI Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Are you an innovative and <span>experience</span>d artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence <span>(</span>AI<span>)</span> developer spe<span>cia</span>lizing in reinforcement learning? Utilize your expertise in AI, data science, and machine learning (ML) engineering to train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data to drive real-world mission critical impact. You will collaborate with dynamic teams to translate reinforcement learning research into operational capability and production-grade code, bringing significant technological advancements that drive mission success.</p><p></p><p>You’ll join a growing community of ML engineers focused on delivering products and solutions to our customers’ most challenging problems. You’ll collaborate with a team of dedicated space, military, intelligence, engineering, and AI professionals to deliver cutting-edge solutions to solve issues of national importance.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>Design, implement, and train reinforcement learning <span>(</span>RL<span>)</span> and multi-agent reinforcement learning <span>(</span>MARL<span>)</span> algorithms for complex decision-making problems.</p></li><li><p>Develop scalable training pipelines using Python and modern ML frameworks.</p></li><li><p>Build and evaluate agents in simulated environments using Gym or PettingZoo, high-fidelity simulators, or custom environments.</p></li><li><p>Apply RL techniques such as <span>policy</span> optimization, value-based learning, model-based RL, and imitation learning.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with domain experts to define reward structures, constraints, and evaluation <span>met</span>rics aligned with mission objectives.</p></li><li><p>Implement distributed training workflows leveraging cloud compute, containerization, and orchestration technologies.</p></li><li><p>Transition trained models into production systems, following strong <span>sof</span>tware engineering best practices.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to system architecture and performance optimization in Python with opportunities to extend into C&#43;&#43; or <span>Rus</span>t for high-performance components. </p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> developing and training RL agents</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI, data science, ML engineering, or <span>sof</span>tware engineering</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Gym or PettingZoo interfaces</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with ML frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or JAX</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing technical solutions using <span>Rus</span>t, Python, or C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> RL and artifi<span>cia</span>l neural networks</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a CS, AI, or Engineering field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> applying RL to autonomy, control systems, or mission-scale</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with MARL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AFSIM <span>or other</span> high-fidelity simulation environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with embedded systems programming in <span>Rus</span>t, C, or C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in GPU programming, including CUDA or RAPID</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing in-space solutions</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> modern <span>sof</span>tware design patterns, including microservice design and orchestration in Kubernetes deployment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span> in CS, AI, Engineering, or a <span>related</span> field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 19 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["AI Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0242684","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0242684","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"627b0cffbadc0ff18ebb2382e0503e0e227f521bc42e28a9c03ca7c628b877f9","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Remote Sensing Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0242684","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0242684","locations":[{"label":"Dayton, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242684","internal_job_id":"f4d78b1c63961000c0300f74b3e90000","first_published_at":"2026-06-22","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Remote Sensing Software Engineer The Opportunity\nAt Booz Allen, you’ll join a team using advanced imaging, physics-based modeling, and AI / ML to solve some of the nation’s most compelling Space Domain Awareness ( SDA ) and remote sensing challenges. You’ll contribute to the design and develop ment of high-fidelity processing pipelines that transform raw sensor data into insight.\n\nYou’ll join a collaborative technical delivery team where you’ll contribute to secure, reliable, user centric tools that accelerate mission outcomes.\n\nWhat You'll Do:\n- Develop sof tware tools for radio met ric modeling and satellite observation geo met ry\n- Implement imaging and signal processing workflows including motion compe nsa tion, multi-frame alignment, and super-resolution\n- Build ML enabled detection, anomaly identification, and object classification modules using operational EO / IR and synthetic datasets\n- Design scientific Python pipelines, such as NumPy, OpenCV, Astropy, or SciPy, for real time and batch processing\n- Support orbital modeling tasks, such as SGP4, TLE ingestion, or basic pose estimation\n- Conduct imagery preprocessing such as radio met ric calibration, artifact correction, and multi-frame filtering\n- Maintain reproducible environments using GitLab, containers, and experiment-tracking tools\n- Collaborate with astrodynamics SMEs, operations personnel, and ML engineers to deliver integrated mission capabilities\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- 4+ years of experience with remote sensing, image processing, or GEOINT data exploitation\n- Experience designing, modifying, develop ing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications using agile met hods\n- Experience with Python and scientific Python packages such as NumPy, SciPy, OpenCV, or xarray\n- Experience with basic orbital mechanics\n- Experience with ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow\n- Experience with large sensor datasets such as HDF5 or cloud object storage\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n- Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with administration of continuous integration / continuous deployment ( CI / CD ) pipelines using Kubernetes, Docker, or Jenkins\n- Experience with sensor phenomenology, radio met ric calibration, or remote sensing interpretation\n- Experience with super-resolution, deblurring, spectral exploitation, or resolved feature extraction\n- Experience with uncertainty quantification, Kalman filtering, or tracking algorithms\n- Experience with AI augmented develop ment workflows or agentic tools\n- Experience with GitLab based CI / CD workflows\n- Master’s degree in an engineering field, or Physics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a related STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Remote Sensing Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity </b></p><p>At Booz Allen, you’ll join a team using advanced imaging, physics-based modeling, and AI<span>/</span>ML to solve some of the nation’s most compelling Space Domain Awareness <span>(</span>SDA<span>)</span> and <span>remote</span> sensing challenges. You’ll contribute to the design and <span>develop</span>ment of high-fidelity processing pipelines that transform raw sensor data into insight.</p><p></p><p>You’ll join a collaborative technical delivery team where you’ll contribute to secure, reliable, user centric tools that accelerate mission outcomes.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Do: </b></p><ul><li><span>Develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware tools for radio<span>met</span>ric modeling and satellite observation geo<span>met</span>ry</li><li>Implement imaging and signal processing workflows including motion compe<span>nsa</span>tion, multi-frame alignment, and super-resolution</li><li>Build ML enabled detection, anomaly identification, and object classification modules using operational EO<span>/</span>IR and synthetic datasets</li><li>Design scientific Python pipelines, such as NumPy, OpenCV, Astropy, or SciPy, for real time and batch processing</li><li>Support orbital modeling tasks, such as SGP4, TLE ingestion, or basic pose estimation</li><li>Conduct imagery preprocessing such as radio<span>met</span>ric calibration, artifact correction, and multi-frame filtering</li><li>Maintain reproducible environments using GitLab, containers, and experiment-tracking tools</li><li>Collaborate with astrodynamics SMEs, operations personnel, and ML engineers to deliver integrated mission capabilities</li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:  </span></b></p><ul><li>4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>remote</span> sensing, image processing, or GEOINT data exploitation</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, <span>develop</span>ing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using agile <span>met</span>hods</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python and scientific Python packages such as NumPy, SciPy, OpenCV, or xarray</li><li><span>Experience</span> with basic orbital mechanics</li><li><span>Experience</span> with ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow</li><li><span>Experience</span> with large sensor datasets such as HDF5 or cloud object storage</li><li><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:  </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with administration of continuous integration<span>/</span>continuous deployment <span>(</span>CI<span>/</span>CD<span>)</span> pipelines using Kubernetes, Docker, or Jenkins</li><li><span>Experience</span> with sensor phenomenology, radio<span>met</span>ric calibration, or <span>remote</span> sensing interpretation</li><li><span>Experience</span> with super-resolution, deblurring, spectral exploitation, or resolved feature extraction</li><li><span>Experience</span> with uncertainty quantification, Kalman filtering, or tracking algorithms</li><li><span>Experience</span> with AI augmented <span>develop</span>ment workflows or agentic tools</li><li><span>Experience</span> with GitLab based CI<span>/</span>CD workflows</li><li><span>Master’s degree</span> in an engineering field, or Physics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a <span>related</span> STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0243285-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0243285-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"51e4596dadc6c8ed24a7cd5f94907127dfad74b04c0f7e943602eabd0e012a35","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Remote Sensing Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0243285-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Remote-Sensing-Software-Engineer_R0243285-1","locations":[{"label":"Dayton, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243285","internal_job_id":"8f3baa969d4a1000c54a987e9c630001","first_published_at":"2026-06-29","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Remote Sensing Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAt Booz Allen, you’ll join a team using advanced imaging, physics-based modeling, and AI / ML to solve some of the nation’s most compelling Space Domain Awareness ( SDA ) and remote sensing challenges. You’ll contribute to the design and development of high-fidelity processing pipelines that transform raw sensor data into insight.\n\nYou’ll join a collaborative technical delivery team where you’ll contribute to secure, reliable, and user-centric tools that accelerate mission outcomes.\n\nWhat You'll Do:\n- Develop sof tware tools for radio met ric modeling and satellite observation geo met ry.\n- Implement imaging and signal processing workflows, including motion compe nsa tion, multi-frame alignment, and super-resolution.\n- Build ML-enabled detection, anomaly identification, and object classification modules using operational EO / IR and synthetic datasets.\n- Design scientific Python pipelines such as NumPy, OpenCV, Astropy, or SciPy, for real time and batch processing.\n- Support orbital modeling tasks such as SGP4, TLE ingestion, or basic pose estimation.\n- Conduct imagery preprocessing such as radio met ric calibration, artifact correction, and multi-frame filtering.\n- Maintain reproducible environments using GitLab, containers, and experiment-tracking tools.\n- Collaborate with astrodynamics SMEs, operations personnel, and ML engineers to deliver integrated mission capabilities.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- 4+ years of experience with remote sensing, image processing, or GEOINT data exploitation\n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications using Agile met hods\n- Experience with Python and scientific Python packages such as NumPy, SciPy, OpenCV, or xarray\n- Experience with basic orbital mechanics\n- Experience with ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow\n- Experience with large sensor datasets such as HDF5 or cloud object storage\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n- Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with administration of continuous integration or continuous deployment ( CI / CD ) pipelines using Kubernetes, Docker, or Jenkins\n- Experience with sensor phenomenology, radio met ric calibration, or remote sensing interpretation\n- Experience with super-resolution, deblurring, spectral exploitation, or resolved feature extraction\n- Experience with uncertainty quantification, Kalman filtering, or tracking algorithms\n- Experience with AI-augmented development workflows or agentic tools\n- Experience with GitLab-based CI / CD workflows\n- Master’s degree in Physics, Mathematics, CS, or a related STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Remote Sensing Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>At Booz Allen, you’ll join a team using advanced imaging, physics-based modeling, and AI<span>/</span>ML to solve some of the nation’s most compelling Space Domain Awareness <span>(</span>SDA<span>)</span> and <span>remote</span> sensing challenges. You’ll contribute to the design and development of high-fidelity processing pipelines that transform raw sensor data into insight.</p><p></p><p>You’ll join a collaborative technical delivery team where you’ll contribute to secure, reliable, and user-centric tools that accelerate mission outcomes.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Do: </b></p><ul><li>Develop <span>sof</span>tware tools for radio<span>met</span>ric modeling and satellite observation geo<span>met</span>ry.</li><li>Implement imaging and signal processing workflows, including motion compe<span>nsa</span>tion, multi-frame alignment, and super-resolution.</li><li>Build ML-enabled detection, anomaly identification, and object classification modules using operational EO<span>/</span>IR and synthetic datasets.</li><li>Design scientific Python pipelines such as NumPy, OpenCV, Astropy, or SciPy, for real time and batch processing.</li><li>Support orbital modeling tasks such as SGP4, TLE ingestion, or basic pose estimation.</li><li>Conduct imagery preprocessing such as radio<span>met</span>ric calibration, artifact correction, and multi-frame filtering.</li><li>Maintain reproducible environments using GitLab, containers, and experiment-tracking tools.</li><li>Collaborate with astrodynamics SMEs, operations personnel, and ML engineers to deliver integrated mission capabilities.</li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:  </span></b></p><ul><li>4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>remote</span> sensing, image processing, or GEOINT data exploitation</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using Agile <span>met</span>hods</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python and scientific Python packages such as NumPy, SciPy, OpenCV, or xarray</li><li><span>Experience</span> with basic orbital mechanics</li><li><span>Experience</span> with ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow</li><li><span>Experience</span> with large sensor datasets such as HDF5 or cloud object storage</li><li><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:  </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with administration of continuous integration or continuous deployment <span>(</span>CI<span>/</span>CD<span>)</span> pipelines using Kubernetes, Docker, or Jenkins</li><li><span>Experience</span> with sensor phenomenology, radio<span>met</span>ric calibration, or <span>remote</span> sensing interpretation</li><li><span>Experience</span> with super-resolution, deblurring, spectral exploitation, or resolved feature extraction</li><li><span>Experience</span> with uncertainty quantification, Kalman filtering, or tracking algorithms</li><li><span>Experience</span> with AI-augmented development workflows or agentic tools</li><li><span>Experience</span> with GitLab-based CI<span>/</span>CD workflows</li><li><span>Master’s degree</span> in Physics, Mathematics, CS, or a <span>related</span> STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"]