ion impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience in sof t war e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications\n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience operating within an Agile environment\n\n- Experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes\n\n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof t war e programming applications\n\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n\n- Experience working within a Cloud Solution Provider ( CSP ) , including AWS, Azure, or Google\n\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.js\n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>t<span>war</span>e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p></p><p>You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p></p><p>This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating within an Agile environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud Solution Provider <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span>, including AWS, Azure, or Google</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.js</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"30add4012979708f7253adfb2d4f2e743619b5618961fba4963ef07a15dfe9a7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241095","internal_job_id":"31e03fc9eb56100166962c758e7c0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Sof tware Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build sof tware that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the sof tware developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb race s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building sof tware that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience in sof tware development with programming languages such as Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n- 3+ years of experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools such as Docker or Kubernetes\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n- Experience working within a Cloud Service Provider ( CSP ) such as AWS, Azure, or Google\n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n- Top Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree and 5+ years of experience in sof tware engineering, or 10+ years of experience in sof tware engineering in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience in an Agile environment\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.JS\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance :  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>tware Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>tware that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>tware developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p><br />You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p><br />This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>tware that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware development with programming languages such as Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools such as Docker or Kubernetes</li><li><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</li><li><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud <span>Service Provider</span> <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span> such as AWS, Azure, or Google</li><li><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> and 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, or 10&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering in lieu of a degree</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> in an Agile environment</li><li><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</li><li><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.JS</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Master’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance</span></b><span>:</span> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"1b66868b6a9d22ad13ff25c0f34e78c87cea2d762ea4762697cea039e6ac62d7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244279","internal_job_id":"6c9b0fa821f61000c4e8c0c1251d0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Sof t war e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build sof t war e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the sof t war e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb race s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building sof t war e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience in sof t war e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications\n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience operating within an Agile environment\n\n- Experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes\n\n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof t war e programming applications\n\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n\n- Experience working within a Cloud Solution Provider ( CSP ) , including AWS, Azure, or Google\n\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.js\n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>t<span>war</span>e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p></p><p>You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p></p><p>This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating within an Agile environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud Solution Provider <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span>, including AWS, Azure, or Google</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.js</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"840c25d796f478dfb5311f0d5b329f8270c407fa73099a1b3991bbfff8d39759","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246016","internal_job_id":"adece80c64641001129b1291e4160000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Software Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build software that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the software developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, embraces innovation, and understands the responsibility of building software that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 8+ years of experience in DevSecOps with a major Cloud Service Provider, such as AWS, Azure, GCP, or Oracle, within the government\n\n- Experience building and supporting CI/CD pipelines using tools such as Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or GitLab CI\n\n- Experience with version control tools, including Git, including branching strategies and workflow management\n\n- Experience with container technologies such as Docker or ECS\n\n- Experience with RHEL\n\n- Experience with collaboration and project tracking tools such as Confluence and Jira\n\n- Experience programming in Java, Python, or Bash\n\n- Knowledge of aws-cli and azure-cli, secure software development practices, IAM, secrets management, and cloud security principles\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Jenkins or GitLab administration, including developing and maintaining custom pipeline configurations on self‑hosted infrastructure\n\n- Knowledge of Microservice architectures, including Cloud Native stacks, such as Kubernetes or OpenShift, or Cloud centric design using AWS Lambda functions\n\n- Knowledge of developing an enterprise level CI/CD pipeline that delivers products from development to production\n\n- Master’s degree\n\n- AWS Solution Architecture Certification, Azure Architecture Certification or AWS Certified Developer Associate Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a Software Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build software that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the software developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p></p><p>You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p></p><p>This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, embraces innovation, and understands the responsibility of building software that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>8&#43; years of experience in DevSecOps with a major Cloud Service Provider, such as AWS, Azure, GCP, or Oracle, within the government</p></li><li><p>Experience building and supporting CI/CD pipelines using tools such as Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or GitLab CI</p></li><li><p>Experience with version control tools, including Git, including branching strategies and workflow management</p></li><li><p>Experience with container technologies such as Docker or ECS</p></li><li><p>Experience with RHEL</p></li><li><p>Experience with collaboration and project tracking tools such as Confluence and Jira</p></li><li><p>Experience programming in Java, Python, or Bash</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of aws-cli and azure-cli, secure software development practices, IAM, secrets management, and cloud security principles</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Jenkins or GitLab administration, including developing and maintaining custom pipeline configurations on self‑hosted infrastructure</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Microservice architectures, including Cloud Native stacks, such as Kubernetes or OpenShift, or Cloud centric design using AWS Lambda functions</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of developing an enterprise level CI/CD pipeline that delivers products from development to production</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree</p></li><li><p>AWS Solution Architecture Certification, Azure Architecture Certification or AWS Certified Developer Associate Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247521","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247521","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3f722e0ba17127c3cfe18e424b045095989a338a973bfe4e63c8184e4ae099c0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247521","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247521","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Aurora, CO"},{"label":"Herndon, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247521","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a1001b5e4f5b1ad2a0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAs a back-end developer, you know that a good site or system needs the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for a back-end developer with the software engineering skills it takes to help identify potential risks, contribute to solution development, and create efficient and effective systems for our clients. \n\nAs a back-end developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to help deliver solutions. Using your software engineering knowledge, you’ll work with and learn from the development team to create custom tools, systems, and sites with consistent performance and scalability. \n\nIn this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you sharpen your skillset and grow your career. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience with Java\n\n- Experience in working with microservices and containerization technologies, including Docker and Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with backend frameworks, such as Spring Framework or Spring Boot\n\n- Experience with API development, including REST architectural style\n\n- Experience with integration and development tools, including AWS, Bitbucket, or Jenkins\n\n- Experience with supporting systems engineering efforts in system design, solution engineering, and software development\n\n- Experience with Linux OS and Command Line Interface\n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 Compliant Certification, including Security+ or CISSP, within 6 months of start date\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Open Systems Architecture design principles\n\n- Experience with DevOps technologies\n\n- Experience with CI/CD technologies, including Ansible, Jenkins, and Git\n\n- Experience with Agile development or Scrum\n\n- Knowledge of non-relational databases, including MongoDB\n\n- Knowledge of Apache NiFi and Kafka\n\n- Ability to work in a fast-paced and collaborative team environment\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Security+ CE, SSCP, CCNA-Security, or GSEC Certification\n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<div><p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As a back-end developer, you know that a good site or system needs the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for a back-end developer with the software engineering skills it takes to help identify potential risks, contribute to solution development, and create efficient and effective systems for our clients. </p><p></p><p>As a back-end developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to help deliver solutions. Using your software engineering knowledge, you’ll work with and learn from the development team to create custom tools, systems, and sites with consistent performance and scalability. </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you sharpen your skillset and grow your career. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with Java</p></li><li><p>Experience in working with microservices and containerization technologies, including Docker and Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Experience with backend frameworks, such as Spring Framework or Spring Boot</p></li><li><p>Experience with API development, including REST architectural style</p></li><li><p>Experience with integration and development tools, including AWS, Bitbucket, or Jenkins</p></li><li><p>Experience with supporting systems engineering efforts in system design, solution engineering, and software development</p></li><li><p>Experience with Linux OS and Command Line Interface</p></li><li><p>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a DoD 8570 Compliant Certification, including Security&#43; or CISSP, within 6 months of start date</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Open Systems Architecture design principles</p></li><li><p>Experience with DevOps technologies</p></li><li><p>Experience with CI/CD technologies, including Ansible, Jenkins, and Git</p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile development or Scrum</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of non-relational databases, including MongoDB</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Apache NiFi and Kafka</p></li><li><p>Ability to work in a fast-paced and collaborative team environment</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Security&#43; CE, SSCP, CCNA-Security, or GSEC Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance: </b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p></div>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/Software-Engineer_R0247395","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/Software-Engineer_R0247395","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"0238f6bddb8dd70fca8dd77b898b03d15f41e5b5149d4fa2d35b38213de4b63a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Software-Engineer_R0247395","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Software-Engineer_R0247395","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247395","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a10015c613e125ca40000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a full-stack developer, you will maintain and execute a network of simulators and modeling capabilities focused on providing rehearsal and exercise capabilities for various units. These simulators are in different locations throughout the country, and the client’s engineering team is responsible for managing the network, maintaining an Authority to Connect (ATO), improving system design and architecture, tier 1-3 troubleshooting during operations, hardware installs, lifecycle management, software releases and deployment, new features, and innovation.\n\nThe software engineering team works on compiling and running from the provided source code, setting up their CI/CD pipeline, breaking down operational requirements for the simulator into manageable tasks or features in JIRA, implementing the tasks or features with various programming languages, assisting in innovation initiatives for the program, improving their skills and knowledge through training opportunities, integrating with other applications and simulations, and creating or improving upon their development environment.\n\nAs a Software Engineer, you will be operating on an Agile Scrum team and are expected to have daily communication. This job requires personnel who are skilled and effective programmers that can provide onsite support when needed. You will have a lot of growth opportunities within the program and areas for innovation on simulation systems.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience with Java, C++, or C#\n\n- Experience working on simulation systems\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications \n\n- Experience with administration of CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins or GitHub actions\n\n- Knowledge of Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol\n\n- TS/SCI clearance \n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with Python, JavaScript, or SQL\n\n- Experience in virtualization\n\n- Experience in DevSecOps\n\n- Experience working with JIRA\n\n- Experience with Kubernetes\n\n- Knowledge of MVRsimulation's Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG)\n\n- Knowledge of BSI's software MACE\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As a full-stack developer, you will maintain and execute a network of simulators and modeling capabilities focused on providing rehearsal and exercise capabilities for various units. These simulators are in different locations throughout the country, and the client’s engineering team is responsible for managing the network, maintaining an Authority to Connect (ATO), improving system design and architecture, tier 1-3 troubleshooting during operations, hardware installs, lifecycle management, software releases and deployment, new features, and innovation.</p><p></p><p>The software engineering team works on compiling and running from the provided source code, setting up their CI/CD pipeline, breaking down operational requirements for the simulator into manageable tasks or features in JIRA, implementing the tasks or features with various programming languages, assisting in innovation initiatives for the program, improving their skills and knowledge through training opportunities, integrating with other applications and simulations, and creating or improving upon their development environment.</p><p></p><p>As a Software Engineer, you will be operating on an Agile Scrum team and are expected to have daily communication. This job requires personnel who are skilled and effective programmers that can provide onsite support when needed. You will have a lot of growth opportunities within the program and areas for innovation on simulation systems.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b>   </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with Java, C&#43;&#43;, or C#</p></li><li><p>Experience working on simulation systems</p></li><li><p>Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications </p></li><li><p>Experience with administration of CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins or GitHub actions</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b>   </p><ul><li><p>Experience with Python, JavaScript, or SQL</p></li><li><p>Experience in virtualization</p></li><li><p>Experience in DevSecOps</p></li><li><p>Experience working with JIRA</p></li><li><p>Experience with Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of MVRsimulation&#39;s Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG)</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of BSI&#39;s software MACE</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Lexington-MA/Software-Engineer_R0246686","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Lexington-MA/Software-Engineer_R0246686","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"39f4d55c0c66e7d452e1584bc930020e749f3c345cda7d482332fb75b4d24f43","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-MA/Software-Engineer_R0246686","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-MA/Software-Engineer_R0246686","locations":[{"label":"Lexington, MA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246686","internal_job_id":"e534098ad7cc10011b3dec57f7450000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a software engineer, you know that great software isn’t just built—it’s crafted. It’s more than an elegant UI or a clean data model, and it’s the integration of intuitive interfaces, robust backend systems, scalable APIs, and resilient infrastructure. At Booz Allen, we’re looking for a software engineer who’s passionate about building impactful solutions end-to-end, from whiteboard to production.\n\nIn this role, you’ll work in a fast-paced, agile environment alongside a team of mission-driven engineers, designers, and analysts. You’ll contribute to solutions that matter—whether it’s streamlining internal tools or building new products that serve national security missions. You’ll apply modern engineering practices, use the latest open-source frameworks, and continuously sharpen your technical toolkit. You’ll engage directly with stakeholders, write clean, maintainable code, and help shape the technical strategy and delivery approach for your team.\n\nWe value engineers who are curious, collaborative, and eager to contribute. Whether you’re deep in code or in a design session, your ideas will help shape solutions that drive real change.\n\nWork with us to build mission-ready systems that make a difference.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience designing, developing, modifying, or implementing software applications\n\n- 2+ years of experience with common programming languages or web development stacks\n\n- Experience writing, maintaining, or enhancing source code for production-level software\n\n- Experience working within Agile teams using Scrum, Kanban, or XP methodologies\n\n- Experience solving complex technical problems in collaborative, cross-functional environments\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with gathering business requirements and translating them into scalable technical solutions\n\n- Experience with Java, Python, JavaScript, React, Node.js, C#, .NET, PHP, C, C++, or Drupal\n\n- Experience working with DevOps pipelines and CI/CD tools, such as Jenkins, GitLab, Docker, or Kubernetes\n\n- Knowledge of integrating automated tests and quality checks into development workflows\n\n- Secret clearance\n\nClearance\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As a software engineer, you know that great software isn’t just built—it’s crafted. It’s more than an elegant UI or a clean data model, and it’s the integration of intuitive interfaces, robust backend systems, scalable APIs, and resilient infrastructure. At Booz Allen, we’re looking for a software engineer who’s passionate about building impactful solutions end-to-end, from whiteboard to production.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll work in a fast-paced, agile environment alongside a team of mission-driven engineers, designers, and analysts. You’ll contribute to solutions that matter—whether it’s streamlining internal tools or building new products that serve national security missions. You’ll apply modern engineering practices, use the latest open-source frameworks, and continuously sharpen your technical toolkit. You’ll engage directly with stakeholders, write clean, maintainable code, and help shape the technical strategy and delivery approach for your team.</p><p></p><p>We value engineers who are curious, collaborative, and eager to contribute. Whether you’re deep in code or in a design session, your ideas will help shape solutions that drive real change.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to build mission-ready systems that make a difference.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience designing, developing, modifying, or implementing software applications</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with common programming languages or web development stacks</p></li><li><p>Experience writing, maintaining, or enhancing source code for production-level software</p></li><li><p>Experience working within Agile teams using Scrum, Kanban, or XP methodologies</p></li><li><p>Experience solving complex technical problems in collaborative, cross-functional environments</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with gathering business requirements and translating them into scalable technical solutions</p></li><li><p>Experience with Java, Python, JavaScript, React, Node.js, C#, .NET, PHP, C, C&#43;&#43;, or Drupal</p></li><li><p>Experience working with DevOps pipelines and CI/CD tools, such as Jenkins, GitLab, Docker, or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of integrating automated tests and quality checks into development workflows</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance</b><br />Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Software-Engineer_R0243159","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Software-Engineer_R0243159","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"528c4ae7e40c3e9cabe483af990f339d8a748a21c1f8dca367e67a56f4d3ba74","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Software-Engineer_R0243159","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Software-Engineer_R0243159","locations":[{"label":"Lexington Park, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243159","internal_job_id":"f4d78b1c63961001f776a3985b690000","first_published_at":"2026-06-26","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop software, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a developer like you with the skills needed to develop software and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing software programming applications  \n\n- 2+ years of experience with software development using basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web development stacks including C#, C, C++, .NET, or JavaScript \n\n- Experience with Agile methodology\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications \n\n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions \n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment \n\n- Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor's degree or 5+ years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree \n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Java, React, NodeJS, or Database\n\n- Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization \n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance \n\n- Top Secret clearance \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop software, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a developer like you with the skills needed to develop software and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing software programming applications  </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with software development using basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web development stacks including C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, .NET, or JavaScript </p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile methodology</p></li><li><p>Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications </p></li><li><p>Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions </p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree or 5&#43; years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Java, React, NodeJS, or Database</p></li><li><p>Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization </p></li><li><p>Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247155","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247155","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"51a1e220563bc842fca17d2f64354d94ba065578c40d18c1bccb92ea70aba806","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247155","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247155","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247155","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1000c43db509cd5f0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAs an AI sof tware engineer, you know that good sof tware is more than just a nice-looking interface plus data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation and we’re looking for a sof tware engineer like you to create artifi cia l intelligence and machine learning solutions that help solve industry's toughest problems.\n\nHere, you’ll lead a team as they create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nYou will architect the patterns, templates, and automation that empower teams across the enterprise to start projects quickly while meeting the highest standards for security, compliance, and delivery excellence without sacrificing developer velocity.\n\nWhat You'll Work On:\n- ​Design and implement a repeatable, automated process to create new GitHub organizations pre-configured for secure sof tware delivery.\n\n- Configure default repository, branch, and team settings aligned with applicable security standards such as SLSA Level 3 and NIST Secure Sof tware Development Framework ( SSDF ) .\n\n- Establish governance controls, access management patterns, and audit logging capabilities to ensure compliance at scale.\n\n- Create and maintain reusable GitHub Actions workflows and pipeline components for common sof tware delivery scenarios.\n\n- Integrate code scanning, dependency scanning, artifact signing, provenance generation, and release workflows into the default templates.\n\n- Ensure CI / CD workflows produce cryptographically verifiable build artifacts compliant with SLSA provenance requirements.\n\n- Implement organization-wide enforcement of branch protection rules, mandatory reviews, security scanning, and secrets detection.\n\n- Integrate GitHub Advanced Security features into templates to enforce code scanning, Dependabot alerts, and secret scanning by default.\n\n- Automate compliance evidence collection for internal audits and external frameworks such as SOC 2, FedRAMP, or CMMC.\n\n- Develop tooling such as Terraform, GitHub CLI, REST, or GraphQL APIs to provision and configure GitHub orgs at scale.\n\n- Integrate GitHub org provisioning into enterprise onboarding workflows.\n\n- Establish guardrails that allow autonomy for product teams while maintaining enterprise security baselines.\n\n- Stay ahead of evolving sof tware supply chain security requirements.\n\n- Recommend and implement improvements for developer experience , security posture, and operational efficiency.\n\n- Mentor engineering teams on secure sof tware development and delivery practices.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have :\n- 4+ years of experience with sof tware engineering, DevSecOps, or platform engineering\n\n- Experience with GitHub Actions, reusable workflows, and pipeline security controls\n\n- Experience with scripting and programming such as Python or Go for automation and tooling\n\n- Experience with IaC tools\n\n- Knowledge of secure sof tware supply chain principles, SLSA, SSDF, and NIST 800-218\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have :\n- Experience in a large, regulated environment such as DoD, FedRAMP, CMMC, SOX, or HIPAA\n\n- Experience with GitHub Enterprise administration at scale\n\n- Experience with SBOM standards such as Sigstore and Cosign\n\n- Experience with multi-org governance, cross-repo code reuse, and enterprise-scale GitHub migration and modernization\n\n- Experience with container security, policy -as-code such as OPA or Kyverno, and compliance automation tooling\n\n- Knowledge of OpenSSF best practices and secure sof tware maturity models\n\n- Possession of excellent interpersonal and communication skills to communicate with engineering and leadership stakeholders\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b> <br />As an AI <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know that good <span>sof</span>tware is more than just a nice-looking interface plus data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation and we’re looking for a <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to create artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence and machine learning solutions that help solve industry&#39;s toughest problems.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll lead a team as they create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>You will architect the patterns, templates, and automation that empower teams across the enterprise to start projects quickly while meeting the highest standards for security, compliance, and delivery excellence without sacrificing developer velocity.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>​Design and implement a repeatable, automated process to create new GitHub organizations pre-configured for secure <span>sof</span>tware delivery.</p></li><li><p>Configure default repository, branch, and team settings aligned with <span>applicable</span> security standards such as SLSA Level 3 and NIST Secure <span>Sof</span>tware Development Framework <span>(</span>SSDF<span>)</span>.</p></li><li><p>Establish governance controls, access management patterns, and audit logging capabilities to ensure compliance at scale.</p></li><li><p>Create and maintain reusable GitHub Actions workflows and pipeline components for common <span>sof</span>tware delivery scenarios.</p></li><li><p>Integrate code scanning, dependency scanning, artifact signing, provenance generation, and release workflows into the default templates.</p></li><li><p>Ensure CI<span>/</span>CD workflows produce cryptographically verifiable build artifacts compliant with SLSA provenance requirements.</p></li><li><p>Implement organization-wide enforcement of branch protection rules, mandatory reviews, security scanning, and secrets detection.</p></li><li><p>Integrate GitHub Advanced Security features into templates to enforce code scanning, Dependabot alerts, and secret scanning by default.</p></li><li><p>Automate compliance evidence collection for internal audits and external frameworks such as SOC 2, FedRAMP, or CMMC.</p></li><li><p>Develop tooling such as Terraform, GitHub CLI, REST, or GraphQL APIs to provision and configure GitHub orgs at scale.</p></li><li><p>Integrate GitHub org provisioning into enterprise onboarding workflows.</p></li><li><p>Establish guardrails that allow autonomy for product teams while maintaining enterprise security baselines.</p></li><li><p>Stay ahead of evolving <span>sof</span>tware supply chain security requirements.</p></li><li><p>Recommend and implement improvements for developer <span>experience</span>, security posture, and operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p>Mentor engineering teams on secure <span>sof</span>tware development and delivery practices.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have</span></b><span>:</span></p><ul><li><p>4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware engineering, DevSecOps, or platform engineering</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with GitHub Actions, reusable workflows, and pipeline security controls</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with scripting and programming such as Python or Go for automation and tooling</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with IaC tools</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> secure <span>sof</span>tware supply chain principles, SLSA, SSDF, and NIST 800-218</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have</span></b><span>:</span></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> in a large, regulated environment such as DoD, FedRAMP, CMMC, SOX, or HIPAA</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with GitHub Enterprise administration at scale</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with SBOM standards such as Sigstore and Cosign</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with multi-org governance, cross-repo code reuse, and enterprise-scale GitHub migration and modernization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with container security, <span>policy</span>-as-code such as OPA or Kyverno, and compliance automation tooling</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> OpenSSF best practices and secure <span>sof</span>tware maturity models</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent interpersonal and communication skills to communicate with engineering and leadership stakeholders</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247157","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247157","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7666fa0ddc9000128a7b9234c1eea9f2945e4abaf97ea1f8c948dba683103a5a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247157","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247157","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247157","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d1461000c4d0941151380000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAs an AI sof tware engineer, you know that good sof tware is more than just a nice-looking interface + data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation and we’re looking for a sof tware engineer like you to create artifi cia l intelligence and machine learning solutions that help solve industry's toughest problems.\n\nHere, you’ll lead a team as they create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nYou will architect the patterns, templates, and automation that empower teams across the enterprise to start projects quickly while meeting the highest standards for security, compliance, and delivery excellence without sacrificing develop er velocity.\n\nWhat You'll Do :\n- ​Design and implement a repeatable, automated process to create new GitHub organizations pre-configured for secure sof tware delivery.\n\n- Configure default repository, branch, and team settings aligned with SLSA Level 3, NIST Secure Sof tware Develop ment Framework ( SSDF ) , and other applicable security standards.\n\n- Establish governance controls, access management patterns, and audit logging capabilities to ensure compliance at scale.\n\n- Create and maintain reusable GitHub Actions workflows and pipeline components for common sof tware delivery scenarios.\n\n- Integrate code scanning, dependency scanning, artifact signing, provenance generation, and release workflows into the default templates.\n\n- Ensure CI / CD workflows produce cryptographically verifiable build artifacts compliant with SLSA provenance requirements.\n\n- Implement organization-wide enforcement of branch protection rules, mandatory reviews, security scanning, and secrets detection.\n\n- Integrate GitHub Advanced Security features into templates to enforce code scanning, Dependabot alerts, and secret scanning by default.\n\n- Automate compliance evidence collection for internal audits and external frameworks such as SOC 2, FedRAMP, or CMMC.\n\n- Develop tooling such as Terraform, GitHub CLI, REST, or GraphQL APIs to provision and configure GitHub orgs at scale.\n\n- Integrate GitHub org provisioning into enterprise onboarding workflows.\n\n- Establish guardrails that allow autonomy for product teams while maintaining enterprise security baselines.\n\n- Stay ahead of evolving sof tware supply chain security requirements.\n\n- Recommend and implement improvements for develop er experience , security posture, and operational efficiency.\n\n- Mentor engineering teams on secure sof tware develop ment and delivery practices.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have :\n- 7+ years of experience with sof tware engineering, DevSecOps, or platform engineering\n\n- Experience with GitHub Enterprise administration at scale\n\n- Experience with GitHub Actions, reusable workflows, and pipeline security controls\n\n- Experience with scripting and programming, such as Python or Go, for automation and tooling\n\n- Experience with IaC tools, such as Terraform and Pulumi, and API-driven configuration management\n\n- Experience with SBOM standards, such as SPDX and CycloneDX, and artifact signing, such as Sigstore and Cosign\n\n- Knowledge of secure sof tware supply chain principles, SLSA, SSDF, and NIST 800-218\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have :\n- Experience in a large, regulated environment, such as DoD, FedRAMP, CMMC, SOX, or HIPAA\n\n- Experience with multi-org governance, cross-repo code reuse, and enterprise-scale GitHub migration and modernization\n\n- Experience with container security, policy -as-code, such as OPA or Kyverno, and compliance automation tooling\n\n- Knowledge of OpenSSF best practices and secure sof tware maturity models\n\n- Possession of strong interpersonal and communication skills to communicate with engineering and leadership stakeholders\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,800.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b> <br />As an AI <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know that good <span>sof</span>tware is more than just a nice-looking interface &#43; data. Today, you need to <span>develop</span> user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation and we’re looking for a <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to create artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence and machine learning solutions that help solve industry&#39;s toughest problems.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll lead a team as they create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize client systems. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>You will architect the patterns, templates, and automation that empower teams across the enterprise to start projects quickly while meeting the highest standards for security, compliance, and delivery excellence without sacrificing <span>develop</span>er velocity.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Do</b>:</p><ul><li><p>​Design and implement a repeatable, automated process to create new GitHub organizations pre-configured for secure <span>sof</span>tware delivery.</p></li><li><p>Configure default repository, branch, and team settings aligned with SLSA Level 3, NIST Secure <span>Sof</span>tware <span>Develop</span>ment Framework <span>(</span>SSDF<span>)</span>, <span>and other</span> <span>applicable</span> security standards.</p></li><li><p>Establish governance controls, access management patterns, and audit logging capabilities to ensure compliance at scale.</p></li><li><p>Create and maintain reusable GitHub Actions workflows and pipeline components for common <span>sof</span>tware delivery scenarios.</p></li><li><p>Integrate code scanning, dependency scanning, artifact signing, provenance generation, and release workflows into the default templates.</p></li><li><p>Ensure CI<span>/</span>CD workflows produce cryptographically verifiable build artifacts compliant with SLSA provenance requirements.</p></li><li><p>Implement organization-wide enforcement of branch protection rules, mandatory reviews, security scanning, and secrets detection.</p></li><li><p>Integrate GitHub Advanced Security features into templates to enforce code scanning, Dependabot alerts, and secret scanning by default.</p></li><li><p>Automate compliance evidence collection for internal audits and external frameworks such as SOC 2, FedRAMP, or CMMC.</p></li><li><p><span>Develop</span> tooling such as Terraform, GitHub CLI, REST, or GraphQL APIs to provision and configure GitHub orgs at scale.</p></li><li><p>Integrate GitHub org provisioning into enterprise onboarding workflows.</p></li><li><p>Establish guardrails that allow autonomy for product teams while maintaining enterprise security baselines.</p></li><li><p>Stay ahead of evolving <span>sof</span>tware supply chain security requirements.</p></li><li><p>Recommend and implement improvements for <span>develop</span>er <span>experience</span>, security posture, and operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p>Mentor engineering teams on secure <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment and delivery practices.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have</span></b><span>:</span></p><ul><li><p>7&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware engineering, DevSecOps, or platform engineering</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with GitHub Enterprise administration at scale</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with GitHub Actions, reusable workflows, and pipeline security controls</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with scripting and programming, such as Python or Go, for automation and tooling</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with IaC tools, such as Terraform and Pulumi, and API-driven configuration management</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with SBOM standards, such as SPDX and CycloneDX, and artifact signing, such as Sigstore and Cosign</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge</span> of secure <span>sof</span>tware supply chain principles, SLSA, SSDF, and NIST 800-218</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have</span></b><span>:</span></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> in a large, regulated environment, such as DoD, FedRAMP, CMMC, SOX, or HIPAA</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with multi-org governance, cross-repo code reuse, and enterprise-scale GitHub migration and modernization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with container security, <span>policy</span>-as-code, such as OPA or Kyverno, and compliance automation tooling</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge</span> of OpenSSF best practices and secure <span>sof</span>tware maturity models</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> strong interpersonal and communication <span>skills</span> to communicate with engineering and leadership stakeholders</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,800.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247280","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247280","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"a02cff4a4de9b5eebe37bba77107d563c1161825bb9e50045277105707a61e6b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247280","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247280","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247280","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e10010cc8aa2179ff0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nWe're looking for a passionate, full-stack sof tware engineer to work with a fast-paced, highly collaborative sof tware develop ment team building and launching capability for Enterprise web-based systems in the Cybersecurity field. You'll have the opportunity to work on automation of nation-level, mission-critical security processes, workflows, and sensor data in risk management, compliance, vulnerability management, and continuous monitoring. \n\nYou'll be responsible for breaking down customer requirements and designing solutions to complex business rules. You'll develop robust, secure, performant, production-grade features, test system functionality, and document functionality. You'll leverage your technical expertise in web technologies, configuration management, sof tware, and data to modernize and re-factor traditional web application components.\n\nYou’ll use your communication skills to work with a team of analysts and engineers to build, test, and operate system capabilities. You should have expertise with full-stack web application develop ment, an understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented design principles, and be able to learn new languages, technologies, and codebases quickly. You should be able to work independently on features while collaborating with a team to review code and solve problems.\n\nWork with us as we build capabilities to change Cybersecurity for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with requirements, develop ment, and testing of complex web application features\n\n- 2+ years of experience with object-oriented programming such as C# or Java\n\n- 2+ years of experience with web develop ment languages, including HTML, CSS, or JavaScript, such as jQuery or Vue\n\n- 2+ years of experience with high-scale relational databases in production such as SQL Server or PostgreSQL\n\n- Experience with Cloud, Containers, System Administration AWS or Azure, Docker or Kubernetes, and Windows Server\n\n- Knowledge of web technologies, applications, sof tware systems and networks, and sof tware security\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with C#, NET Core, Web API, IIS, MVC, and LINQ or Entity Framework\n\n- Experience with CI / CD tools such as Jenkins or GitHub Actions\n\n- Experience with scripting languages such as PowerShell or Python\n\n- Experience with pub or sub tools such as RabbitMQ or Kafka\n\n- Experience modernizing sof tware such as migration to React or Vue\n\n- Experience migrating traditional web applications to Cloud, such as Azure or AWS\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree\n\n- DoD 8570 IAT II Certification , such as Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>We&#39;re looking for a passionate, full-stack <span>sof</span>tware engineer to work with a fast-paced, highly collaborative <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment team building and launching capability for Enterprise web-based systems in the Cybersecurity field. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to work on automation of nation-level, mission-critical security processes, workflows, and sensor data in risk management, compliance, vulnerability management, and continuous monitoring. </p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll be responsible for breaking down customer requirements and designing solutions to complex business rules. You&#39;ll <span>develop</span> robust, secure, performant, production-grade features, test system functionality, and document functionality. You&#39;ll leverage your technical expertise in web technologies, configuration management, <span>sof</span>tware, and data to modernize and re-factor traditional web application components.</p><p></p><p>You’ll use your communication <span>skills</span> to work with a team of analysts and engineers to build, test, and operate system capabilities. You should have expertise with full-stack web application <span>develop</span>ment, an understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented design principles, and be able to learn new languages, technologies, and codebases quickly. You should be able to work independently on features while collaborating with a team to review code and solve problems.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we build capabilities to change Cybersecurity for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with requirements, <span>develop</span>ment, and testing of complex web application features</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with object-oriented programming such as C# or Java</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with web <span>develop</span>ment languages, including HTML, CSS, or JavaScript, such as jQuery or Vue</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with high-scale relational databases in production such as SQL Server or PostgreSQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud, Containers, System Administration AWS or Azure, Docker or Kubernetes, and Windows Server</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of web technologies, applications, <span>sof</span>tware systems and networks, and <span>sof</span>tware security</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, NET Core, Web API, IIS, MVC, and LINQ or Entity Framework</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD tools such as Jenkins or GitHub Actions</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with scripting languages such as PowerShell or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with pub or sub tools such as RabbitMQ or Kafka</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> modernizing <span>sof</span>tware such as migration to React or Vue</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> migrating traditional web applications to Cloud, such as Azure or AWS</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span></p></li><li><p>DoD 8570 IAT II <span>Certification</span>, such as Security&#43; Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>; <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247283-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247283-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"1db55196b6da8fda4ccef13024c9faa3838d7d6f2ba85f3bc0d390d6fe34cbdd","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247283-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247283-1","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247283","internal_job_id":"71f63099399710010cf32122e9ce0001","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nWe're looking for a passionate, full-stack sof tware engineer to work with a fast-paced, highly collaborative sof tware develop ment team building and launching capability for Enterprise web-based systems in the Cybersecurity field. You'll have the opportunity to work on automation of nation-level, mission-critical security processes, workflows, and sensor data in risk management, compliance, vulnerability management, and continuous monitoring. \n\nYou'll be responsible for breaking down customer requirements and designing solutions to complex business rules. You'll develop robust, secure, performant, production-grade features, test system functionality, and document functionality. You'll leverage your technical expertise in web technologies, configuration management, sof tware, and data to modernize and re-factor traditional web application components.\n\nYou’ll use your communication skills to work with a team of analysts and engineers to build, test, and operate system capabilities. You should have expertise with full-stack web application develop ment, an understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented design principles, and be able to learn new languages, technologies, and codebases quickly. You should be able to work independently on features while collaborating with a team to review code and solve problems.\n\nWork with us as we build capabilities to change Cybersecurity for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with requirements, develop ment, and testing of complex web application features\n\n- 2+ years of experience with object-oriented programming such as C# or Java\n\n- 2+ years of experience with web develop ment languages, including HTML, CSS, or JavaScript, such as jQuery or Vue\n\n- 2+ years of experience with high-scale relational databases in production such as SQL Server or PostgreSQL\n\n- Experience with Cloud, Containers, System Administration AWS or Azure, Docker or Kubernetes, and Windows Server\n\n- Knowledge of web technologies, applications, sof tware systems and networks, and sof tware security\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with C#, NET Core, Web API, IIS, MVC, and LINQ or Entity Framework\n\n- Experience with CI / CD tools such as Jenkins or GitHub Actions\n\n- Experience with scripting languages such as PowerShell or Python\n\n- Experience with pub or sub tools such as RabbitMQ or Kafka\n\n- Experience modernizing sof tware such as migration to React or Vue\n\n- Experience migrating traditional web applications to Cloud, such as Azure or AWS\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree\n\n- DoD 8570 IAT II Certification , such as Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>We&#39;re looking for a passionate, full-stack <span>sof</span>tware engineer to work with a fast-paced, highly collaborative <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment team building and launching capability for Enterprise web-based systems in the Cybersecurity field. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to work on automation of nation-level, mission-critical security processes, workflows, and sensor data in risk management, compliance, vulnerability management, and continuous monitoring. </p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll be responsible for breaking down customer requirements and designing solutions to complex business rules. You&#39;ll <span>develop</span> robust, secure, performant, production-grade features, test system functionality, and document functionality. You&#39;ll leverage your technical expertise in web technologies, configuration management, <span>sof</span>tware, and data to modernize and re-factor traditional web application components.</p><p></p><p>You’ll use your communication <span>skills</span> to work with a team of analysts and engineers to build, test, and operate system capabilities. You should have expertise with full-stack web application <span>develop</span>ment, an understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented design principles, and be able to learn new languages, technologies, and codebases quickly. You should be able to work independently on features while collaborating with a team to review code and solve problems.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we build capabilities to change Cybersecurity for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with requirements, <span>develop</span>ment, and testing of complex web application features</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with object-oriented programming such as C# or Java</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with web <span>develop</span>ment languages, including HTML, CSS, or JavaScript, such as jQuery or Vue</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with high-scale relational databases in production such as SQL Server or PostgreSQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud, Containers, System Administration AWS or Azure, Docker or Kubernetes, and Windows Server</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of web technologies, applications, <span>sof</span>tware systems and networks, and <span>sof</span>tware security</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, NET Core, Web API, IIS, MVC, and LINQ or Entity Framework</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD tools such as Jenkins or GitHub Actions</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with scripting languages such as PowerShell or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with pub or sub tools such as RabbitMQ or Kafka</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> modernizing <span>sof</span>tware such as migration to React or Vue</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> migrating traditional web applications to Cloud, such as Azure or AWS</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span></p></li><li><p>DoD 8570 IAT II <span>Certification</span>, such as Security&#43; Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>; <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247287","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247287","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5f3378a9af05f6ed9c98835831d1fc37234421f46d4f9b30e6eb028c67a52a7d","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247287","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Software-Engineer_R0247287","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247287","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1001104b8168bb9d0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nWe're looking for a passionate, full-stack sof tware engineer to work with a fast-paced, highly collaborative sof tware develop ment team building and launching capability for Enterprise web-based systems in the Cybersecurity field. You'll have the opportunity to work on automation of nation-level, mission-critical security processes, workflows, and sensor data in risk management, compliance, vulnerability management, and continuous monitoring. \n\nYou'll be responsible for breaking down customer requirements and designing solutions to complex business rules. You'll develop robust, secure, performant, production-grade features, test system functionality, and document functionality. You'll leverage your technical expertise in web technologies, configuration management, sof tware, and data to modernize and re-factor traditional web application components.\n\nYou’ll use your communication skills to work with a team of analysts and engineers to build, test, and operate system capabilities. You should have expertise with full-stack web application develop ment, an understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented design principles, and be able to learn new languages, technologies, and codebases quickly. You should be able to work independently on features while collaborating with a team to review code and solve problems.\n\nWork with us as we build capabilities to change Cybersecurity for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with requirements, develop ment, and testing of complex web application features\n\n- 2+ years of experience with object–oriented programming such as C# or Java\n\n- 2+ years of experience with web develop ment languages, including HTML, CSS, or Javascript, such as jQuery or Vue\n\n- 2+ years of experience with high-scale relational databases in production such as SQL Server or PostgreSQL\n\n- Experience with Cloud, Containers, System Administration AWS or Azure, Docker or Kubernetes, and Windows Server\n\n- Knowledge of web technologies, applications, sof tware systems and networks, and sof tware security\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with C#, NET Core, Web API, IIS, MVC, and LINQ or Entity Framework\n\n- Experience with CI / CD tools such as Jenkins or Github Actions\n\n- Experience with Scripting languages such as PowerShell or Python\n\n- Experience with pub or sub tools such as RabbitMQ or Kafka\n\n- Experience modernizing sof tware such as migration to React or Vue\n\n- Experience migrating traditional web applications to Cloud, such as Azure or AWS\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree\n\n- DoD 8570 IAT II Certification , such as Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>We&#39;re looking for a passionate, full-stack <span>sof</span>tware engineer to work with a fast-paced, highly collaborative <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment team building and launching capability for Enterprise web-based systems in the Cybersecurity field. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to work on automation of nation-level, mission-critical security processes, workflows, and sensor data in risk management, compliance, vulnerability management, and continuous monitoring. </p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll be responsible for breaking down customer requirements and designing solutions to complex business rules. You&#39;ll <span>develop</span> robust, secure, performant, production-grade features, test system functionality, and document functionality. You&#39;ll leverage your technical expertise in web technologies, configuration management, <span>sof</span>tware, and data to modernize and re-factor traditional web application components.</p><p></p><p>You’ll use your communication <span>skills</span> to work with a team of analysts and engineers to build, test, and operate system capabilities. You should have expertise with full-stack web application <span>develop</span>ment, an understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented design principles, and be able to learn new languages, technologies, and codebases quickly. You should be able to work independently on features while collaborating with a team to review code and solve problems.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we build capabilities to change Cybersecurity for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with requirements, <span>develop</span>ment, and testing of complex web application features</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with object–oriented programming such as C# or Java</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with web <span>develop</span>ment languages, including HTML, CSS, or Javascript, such as jQuery or Vue</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with high-scale relational databases in production such as SQL Server or PostgreSQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cloud, Containers, System Administration AWS or Azure, Docker or Kubernetes, and Windows Server</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of web technologies, applications, <span>sof</span>tware systems and networks, and <span>sof</span>tware security</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, NET Core, Web API, IIS, MVC, and LINQ or Entity Framework</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD tools such as Jenkins or Github Actions</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Scripting languages such as PowerShell or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with pub or sub tools such as RabbitMQ or Kafka</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> modernizing <span>sof</span>tware such as migration to React or Vue</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> migrating traditional web applications to Cloud, such as Azure or AWS</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span></p></li><li><p>DoD 8570 IAT II <span>Certification</span>, such as Security&#43; Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>; <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243190","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243190","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9680e88adcf3cd76dce21907266d835551d42a8e2f6e59b9b452b4fedcd51903","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243190","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243190","locations":[{"label":"Rome, NY"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243190","internal_job_id":"b497c26d3cec1001fe48c13c45770000","first_published_at":"2026-06-26","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will have a positive impact? As a sof tware develop er on our team, you can solve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a dynamic, Agile environment. We’re looking for someone with the skills needed to develop and improve technology from vision to production-ready systems.\n   \nThis role is more than just coding. We need a Sof tware Engineer who will use their passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. Using a variety of technical skills , you’ll work with the develop ment team to create technical solutions for our clients. You’ll analyze the needs and the environment to help make sure the solution the team develop s considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Join us as we develop systems to change the world for the better.\n \nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n   \nYou Have:\n- Experience with Python, Golang, Java, C, C++, Spring, React.js, Node.js, or Angular.js   \n- Experience using Micro sof t Office, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint   \n- Knowledge of systems develop ment lifecycle met hodologies and activities   \n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance    \n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Knowledge of Agile develop ment   \n- Knowledge of Cloud platforms and operating systems   \n- Knowledge of databases, including SQL or Oracle   \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b><br />Are you looking for an opportunity to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will have a positive impact? As a <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>er on our team, you can solve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a dynamic, Agile environment. We’re looking for someone with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> and improve technology from vision to production-ready systems.<br />   <br />This role is more than just coding. We need a <span>Sof</span>tware Engineer who will use their passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. Using a variety of technical <span>skills</span>, you’ll work with the <span>develop</span>ment team to create technical solutions for our clients. You’ll analyze the needs and the environment to help make sure the solution the team <span>develop</span>s considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Join us as we <span>develop</span> systems to change the world for the better.<br /> <br />Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.<br />   <br /><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Python, Golang, Java, C, C&#43;&#43;, Spring, React.js, Node.js, or Angular.js   </li><li><span>Experience</span> using Micro<span>sof</span>t Office, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint   </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> systems <span>develop</span>ment lifecycle <span>met</span>hodologies and activities   </li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span>   </li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Agile <span>develop</span>ment   </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Cloud platforms and operating systems   </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> databases, including SQL or Oracle   </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243328","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243328","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"2c4b43acb66564cf23520735f1c800a434f4b3dfd6f921b3197d73d0016a2c52","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243328","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rome-NY/Software-Engineer_R0243328","locations":[{"label":"Rome, NY"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243328","internal_job_id":"a47d725a43b91000cbab4fd48e490000","first_published_at":"2026-06-29","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a full-stack develop er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an experience d develop er like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production-ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack develop er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution develop ed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.    \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- 3+ years of experience with sof tware engineering in a professional work environment\n\n- Experience with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web develop ment stacks including C#, C, C++, .NET, or JavaScript   \n\n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions   \n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment \n\n- Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor's degree in CS or Computer Engineering\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with Java, React, NodeJS, or Database  \n\n- Experience with Linux at the systems-level, including systems, networking, filesystems such as overlays or tmpfs, and containers under the hood\n\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n\n- Experience using Rus t or modern C++ in production  \n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance \n\nClearance:    \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full-stack <span>develop</span>er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d <span>develop</span>er like you with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack <span>develop</span>er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution <span>develop</span>ed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.    </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware engineering in a professional work environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web <span>develop</span>ment stacks including C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, .NET, or JavaScript   </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to <span>develop</span> complete solutions   </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance </span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in CS or Computer Engineering</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Java, React, NodeJS, or Database  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux at the systems-level, including systems, networking, filesystems such as overlays or tmpfs, and containers under the hood</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> using <span>Rus</span>t or modern C&#43;&#43; in production  </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b>   </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
