e suggestions for improvement. You’ll help our team and clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience with sof tware engineering using Rus t, C, or C++\n\n- Experience building and operating production-grade full-stack applications\n\n- Experience designing the architecture and containerized services with Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with AI-assisted sof tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns, to increase delivery velocity responsibly\n\n- Experience developing sof tware within an Agile framework and DevSecOps infrastructure as part of a Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment ( CI / CD ) pipeline\n\n- Knowledge of authentication, authorization, and security best practices\n\n- Ability to effectively communicate, work independently and collaboratively on a cross-functional team, and demonstrate initiative to complete complex tasks to achieve program goals in a fast-paced environment\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in CS or Engineering and 5+ years of experience in sof tware development, or 7+ years of experience in  sof tware development in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with PyO3 for Rus t-Python interoperability and building Python extensions in  Rus t\n\n- Experience with code quality and static analysis tools such as SonarQube, Clippy, cargo-deny, or cargo-audit\n\n- Experience with secure coding practices and vulnerability remediation\n\n- Knowledge of Systems Modeling Language  ( SysML ) , DoD Architecture Framework ( DoDAF ) , and Unified Architecture Framework ( UAF )\n\n- Ability to display a personal or professional GitHub profile demonstrating projects\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Space System Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an engineer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As an embedded <span>sof</span>tware engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You will lead a team of <span>sof</span>tware engineers to help them develop professionally, review their work, and provide suggestions for improvement. You’ll help our team and clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware engineering using <span>Rus</span>t, C, or C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building and operating production-grade full-stack applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing the architecture and containerized services with Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI-assisted <span>sof</span>tware development tools and practices such as code copilots, automated tests, or secure-by-design patterns, to increase delivery velocity responsibly</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing <span>sof</span>tware within an Agile framework and DevSecOps infrastructure as part of a Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment <span>(</span>CI<span>/</span>CD<span>)</span> pipeline</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> authentication, authorization, and security best practices</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> effectively communicate, work independently and collaboratively on a cross-functional team, and demonstrate initiative to complete complex tasks to achieve program goals in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in CS or Engineering and 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware development, or 7&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware development in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with PyO3 for <span>Rus</span>t-Python interoperability and building Python extensions in <span>Rus</span>t</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with code quality and static analysis tools such as SonarQube, Clippy, cargo-deny, or cargo-audit</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with secure coding practices and vulnerability remediation</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> Systems Modeling Language <span>(</span>SysML<span>)</span>, DoD Architecture Framework <span>(</span>DoDAF<span>)</span>, and Unified Architecture Framework <span>(</span>UAF<span>)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> display a personal or professional GitHub profile demonstrating projects</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Benning-GA/Special-Missions-Software-Engineer_R0242585","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Benning-GA/Special-Missions-Software-Engineer_R0242585","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"01af829d2eee8489fea5811ed610a8cc33ce1e72970dfcf7284eb56fb784ac4c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Special Missions Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Benning-GA/Special-Missions-Software-Engineer_R0242585","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Benning-GA/Special-Missions-Software-Engineer_R0242585","locations":[{"label":"Fort Benning, GA"},{"label":"Virginia Beach, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242585","internal_job_id":"6a5039c1aed41001b21b24c39ae40000","first_published_at":"2026-07-02","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Special Missions Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs a full-stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an experience d developer like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications using Agile met hods  \n\n- Experience in sof tware development with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web development stacks\n\n- Experience with Palantir Foundry\n\n- Experience with Agile met hodology, extreme programming, sof tware engineering, product management, and sof tware products \n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications \n\n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions \n\n- Ability to travel up to 25% of the time\n\n- Ability to travel OCONUS up to 25% of the time\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization \n\n- Experience with Java, Python, C#, C / C++, .NET, JavaScript, React, NodeJS, PHP, or Drupal \n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Special Missions Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a full-stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d developer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using Agile <span>met</span>hods  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware development with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web development stacks</p></li><li><p>Experience with Palantir Foundry</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology, extreme programming, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, product management, and <span>sof</span>tware products </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> travel up to 25% of the time</p></li><li><p>Ability to travel OCONUS up to 25% of the time</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Java, Python, C#, C<span>/</span>C&#43;&#43;, .NET, JavaScript, React, NodeJS, PHP, or Drupal </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Lexington-MA/TAK-Developer_R0242139","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Lexington-MA/TAK-Developer_R0242139","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4e6fa931c4c14b64fadcf2704d20325907a89312f0fe8ef73b505e9b541af48a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"TAK Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-MA/TAK-Developer_R0242139","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-MA/TAK-Developer_R0242139","locations":[{"label":"Lexington, MA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242139","internal_job_id":"1076cb28ebff100203ef2ce876f30000","first_published_at":"2026-06-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"TAK Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop  sof tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an  experience d developer like you with the skills needed to develop  sof tware and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a senior full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the  current  architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience in sof tware programming with object-oriented languages, including Java, Kotlin, or JavaScript\n\n- 3+ years of experience with Python for backend services, data processing, or automation\n\n- Experience with relational databases and SQL, including MySQL or PostgreSQL\n\n- Experience with Cursor-on-Target ( CoT ) and geospatial data formats such as KML and GeoJSON\n\n- Experience with Linux server administration and containerization such as Docker\n\n- Experience provisioning and managing virtualized or cloud infrastructure such as AWS EC2, Azure, vSphere, or Kubernetes\n\n- Knowledge of the Tactical Assault Kit ( TAK ) ecosystem, including ATAK plugin development\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree , or 8+ years of experience in sof tware development in lieu of a degree \n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience developing Android applications and with the Andriod SDK\n\n- Experience with mobile technologies, including cellular and wireless\n\n- Experience with WinTAK, TAK X, and TAK Server\n\n- Experience with the ATAK-CIV SDK and Gradle-based plugin builds\n\n- Experience with message brokers or pub-sub such as NATS, MQTT, or ActiveMQ\n\n- Experience with gRPC or protobuf for service-to-service communication\n\n- Knowledge of DevOps, continuous integration, and continuous deployment \n\n- Knowledge of shell scripting and automation \n\n- Ability to debug, troubleshoot, monitor, and maintain the operation of application code \n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ;   Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"TAK Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>tware, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d developer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a senior full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware programming with object-oriented languages, including Java, Kotlin, or JavaScript</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Python for backend services, data processing, or automation</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with relational databases and SQL, including MySQL or PostgreSQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Cursor-on-Target <span>(</span>CoT<span>)</span> and geospatial data formats such as KML and GeoJSON</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux server administration and containerization such as Docker</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> provisioning and managing virtualized or cloud infrastructure such as AWS EC2, Azure, vSphere, or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> the Tactical Assault Kit <span>(</span>TAK<span>)</span> ecosystem, including ATAK plugin development</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span>, or 8&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware development in lieu of a degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing Android applications and with the Andriod SDK</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with mobile technologies, including cellular and wireless</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with WinTAK, TAK X, and TAK Server</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with the ATAK-CIV SDK and Gradle-based plugin builds</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with message brokers or pub-sub such as NATS, MQTT, or ActiveMQ</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with gRPC or protobuf for service-to-service communication</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> DevOps, continuous integration, and continuous deployment </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> shell scripting and automation </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> debug, troubleshoot, monitor, and maintain the operation of application code </p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247381","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247381","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"db0b7a329fe4a5e195f9649c64094755ade6bdd5f4039a3a75dc993f5c4145df","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"TAK Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247381","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247381","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247381","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a1001563567bcbff80000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"TAK Developer The Opportunity: \nAs a full-stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast and agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof t war e, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an experience d developer like you with the skills needed to develop sof t war e and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience in sof t war e programming with object-oriented languages, including Java and Kotlin\n\n- 2+ years of experience with development with TAK Server plugins\n\n- 2+ years of experience with the Tactical Assault Kit ( TAK ) ecosystem\n\n- Experience with Mission Data Packages\n\n- Experience with Geo Servers\n\n- Experience with on-device database management using SQLite\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with development in the Android Tactical Assault Kit ( ATAK ) sof t war e development kit\n\n- Experience developing native Android applications\n\n- Experience profiling UI, memory, and concurrency on Android\n\n- Experience with Android distributions and sof t war e developmental kits\n\n- Experience with mobile technologies, including cellular and wireless\n\n- Experience with WinTAK and TAK X\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"TAK Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a full-stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast and agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d developer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming with object-oriented languages, including Java and Kotlin</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with development with TAK Server plugins</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with the Tactical Assault Kit <span>(</span>TAK<span>)</span> ecosystem</p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Mission Data Packages</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Geo Servers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with on-device database management using SQLite</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with development in the Android Tactical Assault Kit <span>(</span>ATAK<span>)</span> <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development kit</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing native Android applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> profiling UI, memory, and concurrency on Android</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Android distributions and <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developmental kits</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with mobile technologies, including cellular and wireless</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with WinTAK and TAK X</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247485-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247485-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5c84a7c21182087a4868f4fcf5d83bdbc463385d18aff1a48db6afc17147a9bd","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"TAK Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247485-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/TAK-Developer_R0247485-1","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247485","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a100119b79e75b2f20000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"TAK Developer The Opportunity: \nAs a full-stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast and agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof t war e, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an experience d developer like you with the skills needed to develop sof t war e and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience in sof t war e programming, including C and C++\n\n- Experience with the Tactical Assault Kit ( TAK ) ecosystem\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with development in the Android Tactical Assault Kit ( ATAK ) sof t war e development kit\n\n- Experience with development with TAK Server plugins\n\n- Experience developing native Android applications\n\n- Experience profiling UI, memory, and concurrency on Android\n\n- Experience with Android distributions and sof t war e developmental kits\n\n- Experience Mission Data Packages\n\n- Experience with Geo Servers\n\n- Experience with on-device database management using SQLitev\n\n- Experience with mobile technologies, including cellular and wireless\n\n- Experience with WinTAK and TAK X\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"TAK Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a full-stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast and agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e, but to create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for an <span>experience</span>d developer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a senior full-stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to master new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming, including C and C&#43;&#43;</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with the Tactical Assault Kit <span>(</span>TAK<span>)</span> ecosystem</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with development in the Android Tactical Assault Kit <span>(</span>ATAK<span>)</span> <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development kit</p></li><li><p><span>Experience with development with TAK Server plugins</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing native Android applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> profiling UI, memory, and concurrency on Android</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Android distributions and <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developmental kits</p></li><li><p><span>Experience Mission Data Packages</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Geo Servers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with on-device database management using SQLitev</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with mobile technologies, including cellular and wireless</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with WinTAK and TAK X</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/North-Charleston-SC/Technical-Instructor---Course-Developer_R0247515","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/North-Charleston-SC/Technical-Instructor---Course-Developer_R0247515","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"28653a7f59ef5974db6c7b9bb498d6c3aad1387619808c68bdca4a5a276419ce","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Technical Instructor & Course Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/North-Charleston-SC/Technical-Instructor---Course-Developer_R0247515","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/North-Charleston-SC/Technical-Instructor---Course-Developer_R0247515","locations":[{"label":"North Charleston, SC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247515","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1001b9790316c4a40000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Technical Instructor & Course Developer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen Hamilton seeks a Technical Instructor & Course Developer to revise, maintain, and deliver technical curriculum for Air Traffic Control (ATC) training. This role focuses on developing instructional materials for electronics, weapons systems, and related ATC disciplines, integrating computer-based tools and graphics, and facilitating a range of course formats to ensure Navy personnel receive mission-ready training. The candidate will demonstrate effective classroom techniques, develop new teaching methods, and support curriculum innovation. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.\n\nHow You'll Contribute:\n- Revise and maintain ATC technical curriculum in alignment with client requirements.\n\n- Develop technical course content for electronics, weapons systems, and related areas, using computers for drafting and graphics integration.\n\n- Deliver instructor-led, computer-based, and simulator-based courses, including short technical sessions for Navy personnel.\n\n- Incorporate new curriculum into existing programs and adapt materials to reflect training needs and operational changes.\n\n- Demonstrate professional classroom techniques and develop alternative teaching methods to enhance learning outcomes.\n\n- Act as testing officer, conducting test analysis and supporting the revision of assessments and evaluation tools.\n\n- Draft, edit, and update technical documents, procedures, and guidelines for ATC systems.\n\n- Conduct research to establish training needs and develop effective training programs.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 8+ years of experience in ATC instruction or course development, including hands-on technical training and curriculum delivery\n\n- Experience in researching, establishing training needs, and developing training programs for Navy or service equivalent operational environments\n\n- Experience in training, training development, or instructional support\n\n- Experience developing training solutions for technical or operational environments\n\n- Experience drafting technical procedures, guidelines, and instructional documentation for ATC equipment or systems\n\n- Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams and technical stakeholders\n\n- Knowledge of learning principles, adult learning concepts, and instructional design theories\n\n- Ability to revise technical curriculum and implement new instructional methods\n\n- Ability to draft, edit, and update technical and instructional documents with accuracy and clarity\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience as a military instructor\n\n- Experience supporting Air Traffic Control, C4I, or another technical operational field\n\n- Experience with Navy, Marine Corps, or Army formal training development or instruction\n\n- Experience using AIM2 and Content Planning Module (CPM) for Navy curriculum management\n\n- Experience supporting military technical training environments\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in Education, Instructional Design, Psychology, Curriculum Development, or a related field\n\n- Possession of excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Technical Instructor &amp; Course Developer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Booz Allen Hamilton seeks a Technical Instructor &amp; Course Developer to revise, maintain, and deliver technical curriculum for Air Traffic Control (ATC) training. This role focuses on developing instructional materials for electronics, weapons systems, and related ATC disciplines, integrating computer-based tools and graphics, and facilitating a range of course formats to ensure Navy personnel receive mission-ready training. The candidate will demonstrate effective classroom techniques, develop new teaching methods, and support curriculum innovation. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.</p><p></p><p><b>How You&#39;ll Contribute:</b></p><ul><li><p>Revise and maintain ATC technical curriculum in alignment with client requirements.</p></li><li><p>Develop technical course content for electronics, weapons systems, and related areas, using computers for drafting and graphics integration.</p></li><li><p>Deliver instructor-led, computer-based, and simulator-based courses, including short technical sessions for Navy personnel.</p></li><li><p>Incorporate new curriculum into existing programs and adapt materials to reflect training needs and operational changes.</p></li><li><p>Demonstrate professional classroom techniques and develop alternative teaching methods to enhance learning outcomes.</p></li><li><p>Act as testing officer, conducting test analysis and supporting the revision of assessments and evaluation tools.</p></li><li><p>Draft, edit, and update technical documents, procedures, and guidelines for ATC systems.</p></li><li><p>Conduct research to establish training needs and develop effective training programs.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>8&#43; years of experience in ATC instruction or course development, including hands-on technical training and curriculum delivery</p></li><li><p>Experience in researching, establishing training needs, and developing training programs for Navy or service equivalent operational environments</p></li><li><p>Experience in training, training development, or instructional support</p></li><li><p>Experience developing training solutions for technical or operational environments</p></li><li><p>Experience drafting technical procedures, guidelines, and instructional documentation for ATC equipment or systems</p></li><li><p>Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams and technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of learning principles, adult learning concepts, and instructional design theories</p></li><li><p>Ability to revise technical curriculum and implement new instructional methods</p></li><li><p>Ability to draft, edit, and update technical and instructional documents with accuracy and clarity</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience as a military instructor</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting Air Traffic Control, C4I, or another technical operational field</p></li><li><p>Experience with Navy, Marine Corps, or Army formal training development or instruction</p></li><li><p>Experience using AIM2 and Content Planning Module (CPM) for Navy curriculum management</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting military technical training environments</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in Education, Instructional Design, Psychology, Curriculum Development, or a related field</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Test-Automation-Software-Engineer_R0246604","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Test-Automation-Software-Engineer_R0246604","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6e50b81e7389be77ae574d89d7c0b5b9fd950cd5d10879101e3319a577a1c068","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Test Automation Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Test-Automation-Software-Engineer_R0246604","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Test-Automation-Software-Engineer_R0246604","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246604","internal_job_id":"e596be2e738310010c42076c69a60000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Test Automation Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAre you looking for an opportunity to leverage your Software Engineering expertise in a high impact role? We’re rapidly building and launch capability for Enterprise-web based systems in the Cybersecurity field. We need a Software Engineer in Test Automation to transform the way we execute quality assurance.\n\nYou’ll be responsible for understanding system functionality and test cases in-depth to design, implement, and advance software test automation capability. You’ll analyze existing test automation software against the latest industry advancements in technology, to design and recommend new solutions. You’ll determine test cases and rapidly implement software to improve automated coverage as a software engineer in test. You’ll operationalize automation across a team of developers, manual testers, and automated testers.\n\nYou should have a background in software engineering and be able to learn new languages and technologies. You should have expertise in software engineering and quality assurance of complex web applications. You should be able to design technical solutions, make recommendations, and collaborate with testing and development teams.\n\nJoin us as we launch next generation Cybersecurity products.\n\nThe world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience on web application development teams fielding production systems\n\n- 3+ years of experience with programming, including Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, C# or .NET\n\n- 3+ years of experience with Agile development tools, including Git, Jira, or Wikis\n\n- Experience with test frameworks, including Selenium or Playwright\n\n- Experience with web-based user interfaces, REST APIs, and databases\n\n- Experience with test automation in CI/CD, including Jenkins or Github Actions\n\n- Knowledge of complex web-based application functions, modules, integrations, or data\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with SQL, Windows Server, IIS, Containers, and Linux\n\n- Experience with DevSecOps and GitOps\n\n- Experience with Security tools, including Github CodeQL or Static Code Analysis\n\n- Master's Degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.   \n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Test Automation Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to leverage your Software Engineering expertise in a high impact role? We’re rapidly building and launch capability for Enterprise-web based systems in the Cybersecurity field. We need a Software Engineer in Test Automation to transform the way we execute quality assurance.</p><p></p><p>You’ll be responsible for understanding system functionality and test cases in-depth to design, implement, and advance software test automation capability. You’ll analyze existing test automation software against the latest industry advancements in technology, to design and recommend new solutions. You’ll determine test cases and rapidly implement software to improve automated coverage as a software engineer in test. You’ll operationalize automation across a team of developers, manual testers, and automated testers.</p><p></p><p>You should have a background in software engineering and be able to learn new languages and technologies. You should have expertise in software engineering and quality assurance of complex web applications. You should be able to design technical solutions, make recommendations, and collaborate with testing and development teams.</p><p></p><p>Join us as we launch next generation Cybersecurity products.</p><p></p><p>The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience on web application development teams fielding production systems</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with programming, including Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, C# or .NET</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with Agile development tools, including Git, Jira, or Wikis</p></li><li><p>Experience with test frameworks, including Selenium or Playwright</p></li><li><p>Experience with web-based user interfaces, REST APIs, and databases</p></li><li><p>Experience with test automation in CI/CD, including Jenkins or Github Actions</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of complex web-based application functions, modules, integrations, or data</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with SQL, Windows Server, IIS, Containers, and Linux</p></li><li><p>Experience with DevSecOps and GitOps</p></li><li><p>Experience with Security tools, including Github CodeQL or Static Code Analysis</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s Degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.   </p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Training-Developer_R0245085","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Training-Developer_R0245085","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"ffc719530f22212100b7adc5d0b1cefc69b540e876fee47d6ae04f5187f3cbc8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Training Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Training-Developer_R0245085","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Training-Developer_R0245085","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245085","internal_job_id":"55fd93ad348410016350159796fe0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Training Developer The Opportunity:\nConstructing a compelling course that teaches critical tradecraft requires a real passion for understanding the needs of your client. We have an opportunity for a training developer who is committed to crafting effective training for a critical program.\n\nOn our team, you’ll work with SMEs and product owners to capture your client’s training needs and advise them on the right learning solution to help them accomplish their mission. Putting the learner at the center of the training experience, you’ll design training material and performance support tools. You’ll build training material with curriculum developers and SMEs.\n\nYou’ll use your te chn ical skills, creativity, and experience to produce new ideas to develop an e nga ging, interactive learning experience on screen or in a classroom. You’ll recommend cutting-edge multimedia te chn ologies and strategies, including blended learning to build a successful learning environment. You know communication is key, so you’ll meet with SMEs throughout the process to discuss learning material and incorporate feedback. To ensure your solution is hitting the mark, you’ll collect and analyze results using evaluation methodologies such as the Kirkpatrick Model, then fine tune your training for maximum impact. This is a chance to use your deep understanding of training methodologies to build a creative learning experience that will e nga ge students.\n\nJoin us as we improve national security through learner-centered instructional design.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience with adult learning theory and instructional te chn ologies\n\n- 3+ years of experience with the DoD or IC\n\n- 2+ years of experience with technical training development, including training for technical systems\n\n- Experience authoring instructional materials, learning objectives, and knowledge and performance tests\n\n- Experience facilitating or instructing material\n\n- Experience with competency frameworks\n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Human-Centered Design\n\n- Experience with eLearning te chn ologies\n\n- Experience integrating training into Learning or Knowledge Management Systems\n\n- Experience c ond ucting computer-based training, including building curriculum and reference materials\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Learning or Instructional Design\n\n- Human-Centered Design Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Training Developer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Constructing a compelling course that teaches critical tradecraft requires a real passion for understanding the needs of your client. We have an opportunity for a training developer who is committed to crafting effective training for a critical program.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll work with SMEs and product owners to capture your client’s training needs and advise them on the right learning solution to help them accomplish their mission. Putting the learner at the center of the training experience, you’ll design training material and performance support tools. You’ll build training material with curriculum developers and SMEs.</p><p></p><p>You’ll use your te<span>chn</span>ical skills, creativity, and experience to produce new ideas to develop an e<span>nga</span>ging, interactive learning experience on screen or in a classroom. You’ll recommend cutting-edge multimedia te<span>chn</span>ologies and strategies, including blended learning to build a successful learning environment. You know communication is key, so you’ll meet with SMEs throughout the process to discuss learning material and incorporate feedback. To ensure your solution is hitting the mark, you’ll collect and analyze results using evaluation methodologies such as the Kirkpatrick Model, then fine tune your training for maximum impact. This is a chance to use your deep understanding of training methodologies to build a creative learning experience that will e<span>nga</span>ge students.</p><p></p><p>Join us as we improve national security through learner-centered instructional design.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with adult learning theory and instructional te<span>chn</span>ologies</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with the DoD or IC</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with technical training development, including training for technical systems</p></li><li><p>Experience authoring instructional materials, learning objectives, and knowledge and performance tests</p></li><li><p>Experience facilitating or instructing material</p></li><li><p>Experience with competency frameworks</p></li><li><p><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Human-Centered Design</p></li><li><p>Experience with eLearning te<span>chn</span>ologies</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating training into Learning or Knowledge Management Systems</p></li><li><p>Experience c<span>ond</span>ucting computer-based training, including building curriculum and reference materials</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Learning or Instructional Design</p></li><li><p>Human-Centered Design Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Huntsville-AL/UAV-Software-Engineer_R0241711","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Huntsville-AL/UAV-Software-Engineer_R0241711","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"fb8be5788f7e4fd1cb838c4f013b827b7e934193a300ee5f34ec1fe63bd59e40","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"UAV Embedded Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Huntsville-AL/UAV-Software-Engineer_R0241711","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Huntsville-AL/UAV-Software-Engineer_R0241711","locations":[{"label":"Huntsville, AL"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241711","internal_job_id":"1076cb28ebff1000bb435a0137690000","first_published_at":"2026-06-15","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"UAV Embedded Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nBooz Allen is building the next generation of tactical robotic systems for defense, national security, and public safety missions, establishing a new center of engineering excellence to design and deliver an entirely new class of mission‑ready platforms. We focus on delivering real systems with real capabilities, grounded in operator‑centered design, rapid field‑driven iteration, and U.S.-based manufacturing. As an embedded software engineer, you understand how to create and maintain the critical software that enables these systems to function, writing and optimizing code that bridges hardware and software, enabling reliable communication and performance.\n\nWe are entering a new phase of growth and seeking a highly skilled Senior Embedded Engineer to help shape the next wave of autonomous, semi‑autonomous, and precision‑flight systems. In this role, you will support system architecture , parts selection , validation test design , and full hardware‑software development cycles across multiple product lines. You’ll write, test, and refine embedded code, reverse engineer software to support hardware functionality, configure solutions across various platforms, and collaborate with cybersecurity specialists to ensure secure and resilient systems. You’ll also work closely with technical leads to troubleshoot operational issues and support field deployments, contributing directly to the systems that protect our service members, communities, and country.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with embedded Software support for development of PX4-based UAV systems and ground control stations (GCS)\n\n- 2+ years of experience with C++ based software development to modify or augment the PX4 flight controller and develop applications for the PX4 hardware\n\n- 2+ years of experience with UAV control and monitoring through the development of dashboards, interfaces, telemetry displays, and configuration in C++ with the Qt framework\n\n- 2+ years of experience with hardware abstraction layers, middleware components, and interface elements using MAVLink\n\n- Knowledge of SIL and HIL testing of UAV systems and components\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree or 5+ years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree  \n\nNice If You Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with computer vision, such as OpenCV, camera models, and camera calibrations\n\n- 2+ years of experience working with UAS platforms and PX4-based flight controllers\n\n- 2+ years of experience working with software containerization methods and utilities such as Docker and Docker-compose\n\n- Experience leading software development efforts following DevOps principles, including Agile, CI/CD, and test-driven development, and using automation tools, including pipelines and runners\n\n- Experience briefing DoD leaders and customers, and collecting requirements for defense missions\n\n- Experience with Universal Command and Control Interface (UCI) for UAS and Open Mission Systems (OMS)\n\n- Experience with QGroundControl\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master’s degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Robotics preferred; Doctorate degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Robotics a plus\n\n- FAA Small UAS Part 107 Remote Pilot Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"UAV Embedded Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p><span>Booz Allen is building the next generation of tactical robotic systems for defense, national security, and public safety missions, establishing a new center of engineering excellence to design and deliver an entirely new class of mission‑ready platforms. We focus on delivering real systems with real capabilities, grounded in operator‑centered design, rapid field‑driven iteration, and U.S.-based manufacturing. As an embedded software engineer, you understand how to create and maintain the critical software that enables these systems to function, writing and optimizing code that bridges hardware and software, enabling reliable communication and performance. </span></p><p></p><p><span>We are entering a new phase of growth and seeking a highly skilled Senior Embedded Engineer to help shape the next wave of autonomous, semi‑autonomous, and precision‑flight systems. In this role, you will support <span>system architecture</span>, <span>parts selection</span>, <span>validation test design</span>, and full hardware‑software development cycles across multiple product lines. You’ll write, test, and refine embedded code, reverse engineer software to support hardware functionality, configure solutions across various platforms, and collaborate with cybersecurity specialists to ensure secure and resilient systems. You’ll also work closely with technical leads to troubleshoot operational issues and support field deployments, contributing directly to the systems that protect our service members, communities, and country. </span></p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with embedded Software support for development of PX4-based UAV systems and ground control stations (GCS)</span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with C&#43;&#43; based software development to modify or augment the PX4 flight controller and develop applications for the PX4 hardware</span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with UAV control and monitoring through the development of dashboards, interfaces, telemetry displays, and configuration in C&#43;&#43; with the Qt framework</span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with hardware abstraction layers, middleware components, and interface elements using MAVLink</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of SIL and HIL testing of UAV systems and components</span></p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree or 5&#43; years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with computer vision, such as OpenCV, camera models, and camera calibrations</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience working with UAS platforms and PX4-based flight controllers</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience working with software containerization methods and utilities such as Docker and Docker-compose</p></li><li><p>Experience leading software development efforts following DevOps principles, including Agile, CI/CD, and test-driven development, and using automation tools, including pipelines and runners</p></li><li><p>Experience briefing DoD leaders and customers, and collecting requirements for defense missions</p></li><li><p>Experience with Universal Command and Control Interface (UCI) for UAS and Open Mission Systems (OMS)</p></li><li><p>Experience with QGroundControl</p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Robotics preferred; Doctorate degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Robotics a plus</p></li><li><p>FAA Small UAS Part 107 Remote Pilot Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/University--Software-Engineer_R0241736","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/University--Software-Engineer_R0241736","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"14699c8c171a69cb3d196f588053e2607757e0bbce03b9ae8d7ee89eb7f53edf","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"University, Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/University--Software-Engineer_R0241736","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/University--Software-Engineer_R0241736","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241736","internal_job_id":"8d303c4688181001634f0028a2c20000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"University, Software Engineer The Opportunity:  \nAre you looking for an opportunity to not just develop software, but to help create a system that will have a positive impact? As a Software Engineer on our team, you can solve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a dynamic, agile environment. We’re looking for someone with the skills needed to develop and improve technology from vision to production-ready system.  \n  \nThis role is more than just coding. We need a Software Engineer who will use their passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. Using a variety of technical skills, you’ll work with the development team to create technical solutions for our clients. You’ll analyze the needs and the environment to help make sure the solution the team develops considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Join us as we develop systems to change the world for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n  \nYou Have:    \n- Experience with programming languages or frameworks, including Python, GoLang, Java, C, C++, Spring, React.js, Node.js, or Angular.js  \n\n- Experience with using Microsoft Office, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint   \n\n- Knowledge of systems development life cycle methodologies and associated activities   \n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance   \n\n- Scheduled to obtain a Bachelor's degree by Winter 2026\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Knowledge of Agile development  \n\n- Knowledge of Cloud platforms and operating systems  \n\n- Knowledge of databases, including SQL or Oracle  \n\n- Pursuing a Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Computer Information Systems, IT, or a related field preferred\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $53,000.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.\n\nURT1","description_html":"University, Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b><br />Are you looking for an opportunity to not just develop software, but to help create a system that will have a positive impact? As a Software Engineer on our team, you can solve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a dynamic, agile environment. We’re looking for someone with the skills needed to develop and improve technology from vision to production-ready system.  <br />  <br />This role is more than just coding. We need a Software Engineer who will use their passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. Using a variety of technical skills, you’ll work with the development team to create technical solutions for our clients. You’ll analyze the needs and the environment to help make sure the solution the team develops considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Join us as we develop systems to change the world for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.<br />  </p><p><b>You Have:  </b> </p><ul><li><p>Experience with programming languages or frameworks, including Python, GoLang, Java, C, C&#43;&#43;, Spring, React.js, Node.js, or Angular.js  </p></li><li><p>Experience with using Microsoft Office, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint   </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of systems development life cycle methodologies and associated activities   </p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance   </p></li><li><p>Scheduled to obtain a Bachelor&#39;s degree by Winter 2026</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Knowledge of Agile development  </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Cloud platforms and operating systems  </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of databases, including SQL or Oracle  </p></li><li><p>Pursuing a Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Computer Information Systems, IT, or a related field preferred</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:  </b><br />Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $53,000.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>URT1","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Graphic-Designer--Mid_R0245443","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Graphic-Designer--Mid_R0245443","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4380ef68602c546db5fe6f90f32894859c3202660b82c96bf3f4b60c8124f4d3","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Web Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Graphic-Designer--Mid_R0245443","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Graphic-Designer--Mid_R0245443","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245443","internal_job_id":"45e74e1697ae1001067fb5ae6ddf0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Web Developer The Opportunity:\nPerform as a Web Developer and Designer for corporate communications and websites using design principles, an exceptional eye for detail, and a passion for producing creative and impactful visual materials that support the client’s mission and enhance brand identity. Apply web development and design skills to create a wide range of deliverables, including SharePoint pages and potentially logos, publications, presentations, multimedia products, and videos, while ensuring compliance with Section 508 accessibility standards. Leverage design principles such as typography, hierarchy, and visual balance to craft visually appealing assets that align with organizational branding and messaging, ensuring consistency across all materials. Manage multiple work assignments by applying accuracy, time management, and problem-solving skills in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Work collaboratively within a team of designers, engage with senior designers for feedback, and collaborate with stakeholders to conceptualize project requirements and deliver solutions that effectively communicate government or defense-sector priorities.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience in web development and SharePoint development\n\n- Experience with Section 508 compliance for designing and developing accessible products\n\n- Experience with SharePoint and Microsoft Office Suite programs, including PowerPoint and Word\n\n- Experience facilitating client-facing discussions to interpret workforce messaging, display data visually, and conceptualize analytic ideas\n\n- Ability to collaborate with stakeholders to define project requirements and deliver design outcomes that align with mission-focused goals\n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience supporting intelligence analysts and senior-level or executive staff with tailored graphic design solutions\n\n- Experience with design tools such as Adobe Creative Cloud, InDesign, Photoshop, and Illustrator\n\n- Experience working within the government or defense sectors\n\n- Knowledge of DoD or Intelligence Community (IC) processes and requirements\n\n- Ability to set expectations, define project timelines, and deliver quality products with minimal supervision or oversight\n\n- Ability to collaborate effectively within cross-functional teams in a dynamic environment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ;   TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $53,000.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Web Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p><span>Perform as a Web Developer and Designer for corporate communications and websites using design principles, an exceptional eye for detail, and a passion for producing creative and impactful visual materials that support the client’s mission and enhance brand identity. Apply web development and design skills to create a wide range of deliverables, including SharePoint pages and potentially logos, publications, presentations, multimedia products, and videos, while ensuring compliance with Section 508 accessibility standards. Leverage design principles such as typography, hierarchy, and visual balance to craft visually appealing assets that align with organizational branding and messaging, ensuring consistency across all materials. Manage multiple work assignments by applying accuracy, time management, and problem-solving skills in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Work collaboratively within a team of designers, engage with senior designers for feedback, and collaborate with stakeholders to conceptualize project requirements and deliver solutions that effectively communicate government or defense-sector priorities.</span></p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience in web development and SharePoint development</p></li><li><p>Experience with Section 508 compliance for designing and developing accessible products</p></li><li><p>Experience with SharePoint and Microsoft Office Suite programs, including PowerPoint and Word</p></li><li><p>Experience facilitating client-facing discussions to interpret workforce messaging, display data visually, and conceptualize analytic ideas</p></li><li><p>Ability to collaborate with stakeholders to define project requirements and deliver design outcomes that align with mission-focused goals</p></li><li><p>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p><br /><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>Experience supporting intelligence analysts and senior-level or executive staff with tailored graphic design solutions</p></li><li><p>Experience with design tools such as Adobe Creative Cloud, InDesign, Photoshop, and Illustrator</p></li><li><p>Experience working within the government or defense sectors</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of DoD or Intelligence Community (IC) processes and requirements</p></li><li><p>Ability to set expectations, define project timelines, and deliver quality products with minimal supervision or oversight</p></li><li><p>Ability to collaborate effectively within cross-functional teams in a dynamic environment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $53,000.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Web-Developer--Mid_R0246297","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Web-Developer--Mid_R0246297","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9206560673525b5ab07d768c241fe57d62dbcb3e135703025462a41115702f81","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Web Developer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Web-Developer--Mid_R0246297","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Web-Developer--Mid_R0246297","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246297","internal_job_id":"f43e8f6091f81001fff75daebfaa0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-07","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Web Developer, Mid The Opportunity:\nLeads the design, development, implementation and maintenance of a major website. Applies advanced skills, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develops innovative solutions to complex problems. Works without considerable direction. Mentors and may supervise team members.\n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience of developing websites or web applications \n\n- 5+ years of experience using JavaScript and PHP \n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or reviewing, generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications or software\n\n- Knowledge of database systems and MySQL\n\n- Ability to work across both front‑end and back‑end development, including user interfaces, middleware, services, and APIs, to deliver complete solutions\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or Software Engineering or 8+ years of experience in Web Development or Software Engineering in lieu of a degree \n\nNice If You Have:     \n- Experience using content management systems, such as Joomla\n\n- Experience with AWS\n\n- Experience project management tools such as Jira or Confluence\n\n- Experience with front‑end frameworks and fundamentals, such as HTML, CSS, responsive design, and accessibility\n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment\n\n- Knowledge of CMS plug-ins and extensions\n\n- Knowledge of building, enhancing, web application, or API \n\n- Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $55,200.00 to $126,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Web Developer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Leads the design, development, implementation and maintenance of a major website. Applies advanced skills, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develops innovative solutions to complex problems. Works without considerable direction. Mentors and may supervise team members.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b>   </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience of developing websites or web applications </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience using JavaScript and PHP </p></li><li><p>Experience writing source code for new applications or reviewing, generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications or software</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of database systems and MySQL</p></li><li><p>Ability to work across both front‑end and back‑end development, including user interfaces, middleware, services, and APIs, to deliver complete solutions</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science or Software Engineering or 8&#43; years of experience in Web Development or Software Engineering in lieu of a degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b>    </p><ul><li><p>Experience using content management systems, such as Joomla</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS</p></li><li><p>Experience project management tools such as Jira or Confluence</p></li><li><p>Experience with front‑end frameworks and fundamentals, such as HTML, CSS, responsive design, and accessibility</p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of CMS plug-ins and extensions</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of building, enhancing, web application, or API </p></li><li><p>Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $55,200.00 to $126,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 17 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Wireless-Infrstructure-Engineer--Junior_R0246947","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Wireless-Infrstructure-Engineer--Junior_R0246947","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"43f5840c5fcf0b84d2533d2c6005fc0a9603729103dbc6265b51362d8166c6fe","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Wireless Infrastructure Engineer, Junior","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Wireless-Infrstructure-Engineer--Junior_R0246947","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Wireless-Infrstructure-Engineer--Junior_R0246947","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246947","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d1461000c57d1c43f23b0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Wireless Infrastructure Engineer, Junior The Opportunity:\nA well-designed IT infrastructure is critical to move data and enable organizations to achieve their missions, but how can an organization make sure their network will fit their current and evolving needs? Crafting the right network, with the right equipment and software, requires a combination of technical skill and careful planning. That’s why we need you.\n\nAs an IT infrastructure engineer on our team, you’ll help develop IT systems prototypes and experiment with emerging IT and 5G wireless technology to support critical mission use cases. You’ll work with clients and a varied team of technologists to learn the strategic goals and operational needs that shape the IT requirements. You’ll then have the opportunity to plan and implement IT infrastructure components. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms, to supporting the prototyping of solutions, you’ll put your hardware and software talents to good use. This is your chance to grow your skills in IT system planning, configuration, scripting, 5G, and cloud technologies while continuing to grow your network engineering experience.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 1+ years of experience with IT infrastructure systems \n\n- 1+ years of experience with network design and integration of network technologies\n\n- Experience implementing, configuring, and operating virtualization solutions, including VMware\n\n- Experience in container technology, including Docker, and container orchestration, including Kubernetes\n\n- Knowledge of CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, GitLab CI, or GitHub Actions\n\n- Ability to implement, configure, and operate servers, including Windows and Linux\n\n- Ability to develop technical briefs and convey technical concepts to a varied audience\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Knowledge of networking concepts and principles\n\n- Knowledge of cloud concepts and principles\n\n- Knowledge of wireless networks\n\n- Knowledge of cellular communication networks, including 4G and 5G\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Microsoft Certified Administrator or RHCS Certification\n\n- CCNA, CCNP, or 5G Certifications\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $53,000.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Wireless Infrastructure Engineer, Junior<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>A well-designed IT infrastructure is critical to move data and enable organizations to achieve their missions, but how can an organization make sure their network will fit their current and evolving needs? Crafting the right network, with the right equipment and software, requires a combination of technical skill and careful planning. That’s why we need you.</p><p></p><p>As an IT infrastructure engineer on our team, you’ll help develop IT systems prototypes and experiment with emerging IT and 5G wireless technology to support critical mission use cases. You’ll work with clients and a varied team of technologists to learn the strategic goals and operational needs that shape the IT requirements. You’ll then have the opportunity to plan and implement IT infrastructure components. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms, to supporting the prototyping of solutions, you’ll put your hardware and software talents to good use. This is your chance to grow your skills in IT system planning, configuration, scripting, 5G, and cloud technologies while continuing to grow your network engineering experience.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>1&#43; years of experience with IT infrastructure systems </p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience with network design and integration of network technologies</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing, configuring, and operating virtualization solutions, including VMware</p></li><li><p>Experience in container technology, including Docker, and container orchestration, including Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, GitLab CI, or GitHub Actions</p></li><li><p>Ability to implement, configure, and operate servers, including Windows and Linux</p></li><li><p>Ability to develop technical briefs and convey technical concepts to a varied audience</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Knowledge of networking concepts and principles</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of cloud concepts and principles</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of wireless networks</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of cellular communication networks, including 4G and 5G</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Microsoft Certified Administrator or RHCS Certification</p></li><li><p>CCNA, CCNP, or 5G Certifications</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $53,000.00 to $108,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Infrastructure Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Infrastructure"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
